window.READ_BOOKS=window.READ_BOOKS||{};window.READ_BOOKS["the-great-gatsby"]={"id":"the-great-gatsby","title":"The Great Gatsby","titleZh":"了不起的盖茨比","author":"F. Scott Fitzgerald","translatorZh":"李继宏","sourceEn":"Project Gutenberg #64317","hasZh":true,"chapters":[{"id":"front","n":null,"title":"Dedication","titleZh":null,"paragraphs":[{"en":"Once again to Zelda","sentences":[{"en":"Once again to Zelda","zh":"那就戴上金帽吧，假如能够感动她，假如你能为她起舞，那也为她起舞吧，直到她感动地说：“爱人，戴金帽的、跳舞的爱人，我必须拥有你！”——托马斯·帕克·邓维利尔斯","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Then wear the gold hat, if that will move her; If you can bounce high, bounce for her too, Till she cry “Lover, gold-hatted, high-bouncing lover, I must have you!”","sentences":[{"en":"Then wear the gold hat, if that will move her; If you can bounce high, bounce for her too, Till she cry “Lover, gold-hatted, high-bouncing lover, I must have you!”","zh":"那就戴上金帽吧，假如能够感动她，假如你能为她起舞，那也为她起舞吧，直到她感动地说：“爱人，戴金帽的、跳舞的爱人，我必须拥有你！”——托马斯·帕克·邓维利尔斯","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Thomas Parke d’Invilliers","sentences":[{"en":"Thomas Parke d’Invilliers","zh":"那就戴上金帽吧，假如能够感动她，假如你能为她起舞，那也为她起舞吧，直到她感动地说：“爱人，戴金帽的、跳舞的爱人，我必须拥有你！”——托马斯·帕克·邓维利尔斯","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-1","n":1,"title":"Chapter I","titleZh":"第一章","paragraphs":[{"en":"In my younger and more vulnerable years my father gave me some advice that I’ve been turning over in my mind ever since.","sentences":[{"en":"In my younger and more vulnerable years my father gave me some advice that I’ve been turning over in my mind ever since.","zh":"在我年纪更轻、见识更浅时，父亲曾给我一个忠告，它至今仍在我脑海萦绕。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Whenever you feel like criticizing anyone,” he told me, “just remember that all the people in this world haven’t had the advantages that you’ve had.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Whenever you feel like criticizing anyone,” he told me, “just remember that all the people in this world haven’t had the advantages that you’ve had.”","zh":"“每当你要批评别人，”他告诉我，“要记住，世上不是每个人都有你这么好的条件。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He didn’t say any more, but we’ve always been unusually communicative in a reserved way, and I understood that he meant a great deal more than that. In consequence, I’m inclined to reserve all judgements, a habit that has opened up many curious natures to me and also made me the victim of not a few veteran bores. The abnormal mind is quick to detect and attach itself to this quality when it appears in a normal person, and so it came about that in college I was unjustly accused of being a politician, because I was privy to the secret griefs of wild, unknown men. Most of the confidences were unsought—frequently I have feigned sleep, preoccupation, or a hostile levity when I realized by some unmistakable sign that an intimate revelation was quivering on the horizon; for the intimate revelations of young men, or at least the terms in which they express them, are usually plagiaristic and marred by obvious suppressions. Reserving judgements is a matter of infinite hope. I am still a little afraid of missing something if I forget that, as my father snobbishly suggested, and I snobbishly repeat, a sense of the fundamental decencies is parcelled out unequally at birth.","sentences":[{"en":"He didn’t say any more, but we’ve always been unusually communicative in a reserved way, and I understood that he meant a great deal more than that.","zh":"他的话到此为止，但我们向来话虽不多，心意却是相通，我能明白他的言下之意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In consequence, I’m inclined to reserve all judgements, a habit that has opened up many curious natures to me and also made me the victim of not a few veteran bores.","zh":"自那以后，我从不随便评判别人。这种习惯使我见识了许多古怪的性格，也让我领教了不少极其无聊的人物。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The abnormal mind is quick to detect and attach itself to this quality when it appears in a normal person, and so it came about that in college I was unjustly accused of being a politician, because I was privy to the secret griefs of wild, unknown men.","zh":"如果正常人有这种脾气，心理异常的人很快会察觉到，并前来纠缠不清；所以上大学时，有人错怪我像个政客，因为甚至连有些冒失的陌生人也会来找我诉说心事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Most of the confidences were unsought—frequently I have feigned sleep, preoccupation, or a hostile levity when I realized by some unmistakable sign that an intimate revelation was quivering on the horizon; for the intimate revelations of young men, or at least the terms in which they express them, are usually plagiaristic and marred by obvious suppressions.","zh":"我并不想知道他们的隐私——如果按照以往的经验，发现有人就要向我倾吐衷情，我通常会假装睡觉、忙碌或者心不在焉。因为这些年轻人的衷情，至少是用来表达它们的言语，每每并不由衷，而且总是欲说还休。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Reserving judgements is a matter of infinite hope.","zh":"不去评判别人就是对别人怀有无限的希望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am still a little afraid of missing something if I forget that, as my father snobbishly suggested, and I snobbishly repeat, a sense of the fundamental decencies is parcelled out unequally at birth.","zh":"我父亲那句话好像有点瞧不起人，我的转述也显得很势利，但其实他想说的是，基本的道德观念并非与生俱来、人人皆有的东西。现在我仍然牢记这个道理，以免误会别人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And, after boasting this way of my tolerance, I come to the admission that it has a limit. Conduct may be founded on the hard rock or the wet marshes, but after a certain point I don’t care what it’s founded on. When I came back from the East last autumn I felt that I wanted the world to be in uniform and at a sort of moral attention forever; I wanted no more riotous excursions with privileged glimpses into the human heart. Only Gatsby, the man who gives his name to this book, was exempt from my reaction—Gatsby, who represented everything for which I have an unaffected scorn. If personality is an unbroken series of successful gestures, then there was something gorgeous about him, some heightened sensitivity to the promises of life, as if he were related to one of those intricate machines that register earthquakes ten thousand miles away. This responsiveness had nothing to do with that flabby impressionability which is dignified under the name of the “creative temperament”—it was an extraordinary gift for hope, a romantic readiness such as I have never found in any other person and which it is not likely I shall ever find again. No—Gatsby turned out all right at the end; it is what preyed on Gatsby, what foul dust floated in the wake of his dreams that temporarily closed out my interest in the abortive sorrows and short-winded elations of men.","sentences":[{"en":"And, after boasting this way of my tolerance, I come to the admission that it has a limit.","zh":"如此自夸宽厚待人之后，必须承认的是，我的宽厚也有个限度。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Conduct may be founded on the hard rock or the wet marshes, but after a certain point I don’t care what it’s founded on.","zh":"别人的行为或有磐石般靠得住的基础，或有烂泥般靠不住的理由，可是一旦过分到某种程度，我也就不管背后的原因了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When I came back from the East last autumn I felt that I wanted the world to be in uniform and at a sort of moral attention forever; I wanted no more riotous excursions with privileged glimpses into the human heart.","zh":"去年秋天我从东部回来后，我恨不得世人全都穿上军装，永远向道德立正致敬；我再也不要参加各种乱七八糟的活动，再也不要窥见人们的内心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Only Gatsby, the man who gives his name to this book, was exempt from my reaction—Gatsby, who represented everything for which I have an unaffected scorn.","zh":"只有盖茨比例外。这本书是以盖茨比命名的，他曾经象征着我厌憎的一切。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If personality is an unbroken series of successful gestures, then there was something gorgeous about him, some heightened sensitivity to the promises of life, as if he were related to one of those intricate machines that register earthquakes ten thousand miles away.","zh":"倘使人格是许多连续不断的成功行动，那么他身上自有雍容华贵的气派，他对生活的各种前景也敏感得如同一台能够测知万里之外地震的精密仪器。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This responsiveness had nothing to do with that flabby impressionability which is dignified under the name of the “creative temperament”—it was an extraordinary gift for hope, a romantic readiness such as I have never found in any other person and which it is not likely I shall ever find again.","zh":"这种敏锐并非那种被冠以“天才气质”美誉的多愁善感，而是一种永不言弃的乐观心态，一种罗曼蒂克的随机应变，是我在别人身上未曾发现、以后也很可能不会再见到的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No—Gatsby turned out all right at the end; it is what preyed on Gatsby, what foul dust floated in the wake of his dreams that temporarily closed out my interest in the abortive sorrows and short-winded elations of men.","zh":"是的——盖茨比其实完全没有问题，使我暂时对人世徒劳之悲哀和易逝之欢欣丧失兴趣的，是盖茨比身边那些食客，是那阵在他的梦想破灭之后飘散的污浊灰尘。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"My family have been prominent, well-to-do people in this Middle Western city for three generations. The Carraways are something of a clan, and we have a tradition that we’re descended from the Dukes of Buccleuch, but the actual founder of my line was my grandfather’s brother, who came here in fifty-one, sent a substitute to the Civil War, and started the wholesale hardware business that my father carries on today.","sentences":[{"en":"My family have been prominent, well-to-do people in this Middle Western city for three generations.","zh":"我的家族在这座中西部城市已经兴旺发达了三代人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The Carraways are something of a clan, and we have a tradition that we’re descended from the Dukes of Buccleuch, but the actual founder of my line was my grandfather’s brother, who came here in fifty-one, sent a substitute to the Civil War, and started the wholesale hardware business that my father carries on today.","zh":"卡拉威家族算得上是名门望族，我们家历来自称是伯克禄公爵的后裔，但一世祖实际上是我祖父的兄长。他在1851年来到此地，南北战争时派人替他去打仗，并做起了我父亲如今经营的五金批发生意。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I never saw this great-uncle, but I’m supposed to look like him—with special reference to the rather hard-boiled painting that hangs in father’s office. I graduated from New Haven in 1915, just a quarter of a century after my father, and a little later I participated in that delayed Teutonic migration known as the Great War. I enjoyed the counter-raid so thoroughly that I came back restless. Instead of being the warm centre of the world, the Middle West now seemed like the ragged edge of the universe—so I decided to go East and learn the bond business. Everybody I knew was in the bond business, so I supposed it could support one more single man. All my aunts and uncles talked it over as if they were choosing a prep school for me, and finally said, “Why—ye-es,” with very grave, hesitant faces. Father agreed to finance me for a year, and after various delays I came East, permanently, I thought, in the spring of twenty-two.","sentences":[{"en":"I never saw this great-uncle, but I’m supposed to look like him—with special reference to the rather hard-boiled painting that hangs in father’s office.","zh":"我从未见过这位祖伯父，但据说我长得很像他——证据就是父亲办公室挂着的那幅面无表情的画像。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I graduated from New Haven in 1915, just a quarter of a century after my father, and a little later I participated in that delayed Teutonic migration known as the Great War.","zh":"我从纽黑文毕业是在1915年，距我父亲从那毕业正好四分之一世纪。不久之后，我参加了那场受阻的条顿大迁徙，也就是所谓的世界大战。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I enjoyed the counter-raid so thoroughly that I came back restless.","zh":"我经历过非常激动人心的反攻大战，所以回乡后反倒待不住。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of being the warm centre of the world, the Middle West now seemed like the ragged edge of the universe—so I decided to go East and learn the bond business.","zh":"中西部不再是温暖的世界中心，现在它像是荒凉的宇宙边缘——于是我决定到东部去学习债券生意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everybody I knew was in the bond business, so I supposed it could support one more single man.","zh":"我认识的人都在从事债券交易，所以我认为这行业再养活一个人应该没问题。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All my aunts and uncles talked it over as if they were choosing a prep school for me, and finally said, “Why—ye-es,” with very grave, hesitant faces.","zh":"我的叔伯姑姨商量了很久，仿佛是要为我挑选某个预科学校，最后他们带着沉重、勉强的表情说：“嗯…那好吧。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Father agreed to finance me for a year, and after various delays I came East, permanently, I thought, in the spring of twenty-two.","zh":"父亲同意资助我一年，经过几番耽搁，1922年春天，我怀着一去不返的心情，启程来到东部。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The practical thing was to find rooms in the city, but it was a warm season, and I had just left a country of wide lawns and friendly trees, so when a young man at the office suggested that we take a house together in a commuting town, it sounded like a great idea. He found the house, a weather-beaten cardboard bungalow at eighty a month, but at the last minute the firm ordered him to Washington, and I went out to the country alone. I had a dog—at least I had him for a few days until he ran away—and an old Dodge and a Finnish woman, who made my bed and cooked breakfast and muttered Finnish wisdom to herself over the electric stove.","sentences":[{"en":"The practical thing was to find rooms in the city, but it was a warm season, and I had just left a country of wide lawns and friendly trees, so when a young man at the office suggested that we take a house together in a commuting town, it sounded like a great idea.","zh":"按理说，我应该在市区找个房间寄宿，但那时天气暖和，而我又刚离开碧草如茵、绿树婆娑的故乡，所以当有个年轻同事说他想和我到郊区合租一套别墅时，我很高兴地答应了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He found the house, a weather-beaten cardboard bungalow at eighty a month, but at the last minute the firm ordered him to Washington, and I went out to the country alone.","zh":"房子是他找的，是一座久经风霜的单层木板房，月租八十元。但公司临时派他去华盛顿，我就独自住到了郊外。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had a dog—at least I had him for a few days until he ran away—and an old Dodge and a Finnish woman, who made my bed and cooked breakfast and muttered Finnish wisdom to herself over the electric stove.","zh":"我拥有一条狗（至少拥有了好几天，然后它跑掉了）、一辆旧道奇和一个芬兰女佣。她会打扫房间、准备早餐，还会在电炉边自言自语地咕哝着芬兰人的道理。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was lonely for a day or so until one morning some man, more recently arrived than I, stopped me on the road.","sentences":[{"en":"It was lonely for a day or so until one morning some man, more recently arrived than I, stopped me on the road.","zh":"起初两天我很孤单，第三天早上，有个比我更晚搬来的人在路上把我拦下。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How do you get to West Egg village?” he asked helplessly.","sentences":[{"en":"“How do you get to West Egg village?” he asked helplessly.","zh":"“请问西卵怎么走？”他无助地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I told him. And as I walked on I was lonely no longer. I was a guide, a pathfinder, an original settler. He had casually conferred on me the freedom of the neighbourhood.","sentences":[{"en":"I told him.","zh":"我告诉了他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as I walked on I was lonely no longer.","zh":"我继续往前走，再也不觉得孤单了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was a guide, a pathfinder, an original settler.","zh":"我已经是指路人，是拓荒者，是原住民。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had casually conferred on me the freedom of the neighbourhood.","zh":"他无意间让我对这个地方感到亲切而自在起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And so with the sunshine and the great bursts of leaves growing on the trees, just as things grow in fast movies, I had that familiar conviction that life was beginning over again with the summer.","sentences":[{"en":"And so with the sunshine and the great bursts of leaves growing on the trees, just as things grow in fast movies, I had that familiar conviction that life was beginning over again with the summer.","zh":"眼看阳光明媚，周边林木的枝头倏忽长满了树叶，就像电影里情节推进那么快，我心里深深地相信，新的生活必将随着夏天的来临而开始。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was so much to read, for one thing, and so much fine health to be pulled down out of the young breath-giving air. I bought a dozen volumes on banking and credit and investment securities, and they stood on my shelf in red and gold like new money from the mint, promising to unfold the shining secrets that only Midas and Morgan and Maecenas knew. And I had the high intention of reading many other books besides. I was rather literary in college—one year I wrote a series of very solemn and obvious editorials for the Yale News—and now I was going to bring back all such things into my life and become again that most limited of all specialists, the “well-rounded man.” This isn’t just an epigram—life is much more successfully looked at from a single window, after all.","sentences":[{"en":"There was so much to read, for one thing, and so much fine health to be pulled down out of the young breath-giving air.","zh":"首先，需要阅读的书很多，这种让人振奋的新生活中有待我去吸收的养分也很多。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I bought a dozen volumes on banking and credit and investment securities, and they stood on my shelf in red and gold like new money from the mint, promising to unfold the shining secrets that only Midas and Morgan and Maecenas knew.","zh":"我买了十几本有关银行业务、信用贷款、证券投资的书，那些红皮烫金的图书摆在书架上，就像新铸的钱币，准备向我揭晓唯有迈达斯、摩根和梅塞纳斯才了解的金光闪闪的秘密。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And I had the high intention of reading many other books besides.","zh":"我还下定决心要读许多别的书。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was rather literary in college—one year I wrote a series of very solemn and obvious editorials for the Yale News—and now I was going to bring back all such things into my life and become again that most limited of all specialists, the “well-rounded man.”","zh":"上大学时，我算是文艺青年，曾替《耶鲁校报》写过许多非常严肃却见识浅陋的社论。现在我准备重拾这些东西，再次成为所有专家中最浅薄的那种，也就是所谓的“通才”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This isn’t just an epigram—life is much more successfully looked at from a single window, after all.","zh":"这倒不是刻薄的俏皮话——毕竟，真正的一技之长会让生活成功得多。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was a matter of chance that I should have rented a house in one of the strangest communities in North America. It was on that slender riotous island which extends itself due east of New York—and where there are, among other natural curiosities, two unusual formations of land. Twenty miles from the city a pair of enormous eggs, identical in contour and separated only by a courtesy bay, jut out into the most domesticated body of salt water in the Western hemisphere, the great wet barnyard of Long Island Sound. They are not perfect ovals—like the egg in the Columbus story, they are both crushed flat at the contact end—but their physical resemblance must be a source of perpetual wonder to the gulls that fly overhead. To the wingless a more interesting phenomenon is their dissimilarity in every particular except shape and size.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a matter of chance that I should have rented a house in one of the strangest communities in North America.","zh":"巧合的是，我租住的这个地方，属于北美洲最奇怪的社区之列。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was on that slender riotous island which extends itself due east of New York—and where there are, among other natural curiosities, two unusual formations of land.","zh":"它坐落在纽约以东一个细长而多姿多彩的海岛上。这海岛除了许多自然奇观，还有两片形状罕见的土地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Twenty miles from the city a pair of enormous eggs, identical in contour and separated only by a courtesy bay, jut out into the most domesticated body of salt water in the Western hemisphere, the great wet barnyard of Long Island Sound.","zh":"这两个地方离市区二十英里，活像一对巨大的鸡蛋，轮廓并无二致，中间只隔着一片优美的海湾，伸入西半球最宜人的海面——长岛海湾那大片的水域。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They are not perfect ovals—like the egg in the Columbus story, they are both crushed flat at the contact end—but their physical resemblance must be a source of perpetual wonder to the gulls that fly overhead.","zh":"它们的轮廓倒不是完美的椭圆，而是像哥伦布的鸡蛋，连接陆地的部分都被压扁了，但它们外观的相似之处，肯定会让在上空翱翔的海鸥惊奇不已。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To the wingless a more interesting phenomenon is their dissimilarity in every particular except shape and size.","zh":"对于身无双翼的人类来说，更有趣的现象是，除了形状和大小，它们竟然别无相似之处。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I lived at West Egg, the—well, the less fashionable of the two, though this is a most superficial tag to express the bizarre and not a little sinister contrast between them. My house was at the very tip of the egg, only fifty yards from the Sound, and squeezed between two huge places that rented for twelve or fifteen thousand a season. The one on my right was a colossal affair by any standard—it was a factual imitation of some Hôtel de Ville in Normandy, with a tower on one side, spanking new under a thin beard of raw ivy, and a marble swimming pool, and more than forty acres of lawn and garden. It was Gatsby’s mansion. Or, rather, as I didn’t know Mr. Gatsby, it was a mansion inhabited by a gentleman of that name. My own house was an eyesore, but it was a small eyesore, and it had been overlooked, so I had a view of the water, a partial view of my neighbour’s lawn, and the consoling proximity of millionaires—all for eighty dollars a month.","sentences":[{"en":"I lived at West Egg, the—well, the less fashionable of the two, though this is a most superficial tag to express the bizarre and not a little sinister contrast between them.","zh":"我住的是西卵，它，怎么说呢，它没有东卵那么时髦，但这是最肤浅的比较，不足以表明两者之间那种怪诞而又有点邪恶的差异。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My house was at the very tip of the egg, only fifty yards from the Sound, and squeezed between two huge places that rented for twelve or fifteen thousand a season.","zh":"我的房子位于西卵的顶端，离海湾只有五十码，被夹在两座每季度租金一万二到一万五千美元的大别墅之间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The one on my right was a colossal affair by any standard—it was a factual imitation of some Hôtel de Ville in Normandy, with a tower on one side, spanking new under a thin beard of raw ivy, and a marble swimming pool, and more than forty acres of lawn and garden.","zh":"左边那座是标准的豪宅——它的外观完全照搬诺曼底市政大楼，边上有座崭新的塔楼，其上攀援着稀稀疏疏的常春藤，还有个游泳池，以及超过四十英亩的草坪和花园。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Gatsby’s mansion.","zh":"它就是盖茨比的公馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Or, rather, as I didn’t know Mr. Gatsby, it was a mansion inhabited by a gentleman of that name.","zh":"或者更准确地说，它是一个姓盖茨比的绅士居住的公馆，因为我并不认识那人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My own house was an eyesore, but it was a small eyesore, and it had been overlooked, so I had a view of the water, a partial view of my neighbour’s lawn, and the consoling proximity of millionaires—all for eighty dollars a month.","zh":"我自己的房子很寒碜，但它寒碜得很不起眼，向来无人注意，所以我才有幸住进这座海景别墅，得以欣赏邻居的部分草坪，还能聊以与豪门巨富比邻自慰——这一切只要每月八十元。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Across the courtesy bay the white palaces of fashionable East Egg glittered along the water, and the history of the summer really begins on the evening I drove over there to have dinner with the Tom Buchanans. Daisy was my second cousin once removed, and I’d known Tom in college. And just after the war I spent two days with them in Chicago.","sentences":[{"en":"Across the courtesy bay the white palaces of fashionable East Egg glittered along the water, and the history of the summer really begins on the evening I drove over there to have dinner with the Tom Buchanans.","zh":"优美的港湾对面，沿着海岸排开的，便是东卵那些时髦漂亮的白色房子。有一天，我开车到那边和汤姆·布坎南夫妇共进晚餐，于是这个夏天的故事真正地开始了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy was my second cousin once removed, and I’d known Tom in college.","zh":"黛熙是我的远房亲戚，而汤姆是我在大学认识的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And just after the war I spent two days with them in Chicago.","zh":"战争结束后不久，我曾在芝加哥和他们相处过两天。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her husband, among various physical accomplishments, had been one of the most powerful ends that ever played football at New Haven—a national figure in a way, one of those men who reach such an acute limited excellence at twenty-one that everything afterward savours of anticlimax. His family were enormously wealthy—even in college his freedom with money was a matter for reproach—but now he’d left Chicago and come East in a fashion that rather took your breath away: for instance, he’d brought down a string of polo ponies from Lake Forest. It was hard to realize that a man in my own generation was wealthy enough to do that.","sentences":[{"en":"Her husband, among various physical accomplishments, had been one of the most powerful ends that ever played football at New Haven—a national figure in a way, one of those men who reach such an acute limited excellence at twenty-one that everything afterward savours of anticlimax.","zh":"黛熙的丈夫擅长各种体育运动，他是纽黑文橄榄球史上最出色的防守端锋，某种程度上算是全国知名人物。像他这种人，年仅二十一岁便在某个领域登上最高峰，随后只能不停地走下坡路了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His family were enormously wealthy—even in college his freedom with money was a matter for reproach—but now he’d left Chicago and come East in a fashion that rather took your breath away: for instance, he’d brought down a string of polo ponies from Lake Forest.","zh":"他的家族富可敌国，他上大学时挥金如土，曾引来不少非议。现在他离开芝加哥来到东部，搬家的排场之大足以让你瞠目结舌，例如，他居然把许多马球马从森林湖运过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was hard to realize that a man in my own generation was wealthy enough to do that.","zh":"我很难想象竟然有同龄人会富裕到这种程度。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Why they came East I don’t know. They had spent a year in France for no particular reason, and then drifted here and there unrestfully wherever people played polo and were rich together. This was a permanent move, said Daisy over the telephone, but I didn’t believe it—I had no sight into Daisy’s heart, but I felt that Tom would drift on forever seeking, a little wistfully, for the dramatic turbulence of some irrecoverable football game.","sentences":[{"en":"Why they came East I don’t know.","zh":"至于他们为何来到东部，我并不知情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had spent a year in France for no particular reason, and then drifted here and there unrestfully wherever people played polo and were rich together.","zh":"他们先前漫无目的地在法国住了一年，然后东游西逛，到处找其他有钱人打马球。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This was a permanent move, said Daisy over the telephone, but I didn’t believe it—I had no sight into Daisy’s heart, but I felt that Tom would drift on forever seeking, a little wistfully, for the dramatic turbulence of some irrecoverable football game.","zh":"这次来是准备定居了，黛熙在电话里说，但我不信——我不知道黛熙是怎么想的，但我觉得汤姆会永远飘荡下去，不无惆怅地寻找那种已经不可复得的、过去参加橄榄球比赛时才会有的狂热激情。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And so it happened that on a warm windy evening I drove over to East Egg to see two old friends whom I scarcely knew at all. Their house was even more elaborate than I expected, a cheerful red-and-white Georgian Colonial mansion, overlooking the bay. The lawn started at the beach and ran towards the front door for a quarter of a mile, jumping over sundials and brick walks and burning gardens—finally when it reached the house drifting up the side in bright vines as though from the momentum of its run. The front was broken by a line of French windows, glowing now with reflected gold and wide open to the warm windy afternoon, and Tom Buchanan in riding clothes was standing with his legs apart on the front porch.","sentences":[{"en":"And so it happened that on a warm windy evening I drove over to East Egg to see two old friends whom I scarcely knew at all.","zh":"于是在某个有风但闷热的黄昏，我驱车前往东卵，去探望这两个我根本所知无多的老朋友。他们的房子甚至比我预想的还要华美。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Their house was even more elaborate than I expected, a cheerful red-and-white Georgian Colonial mansion, overlooking the bay.","zh":"那是一座赏心悦目、红白相间的华厦，典型的乔治王时期殖民主义风格，前方就是海湾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The lawn started at the beach and ran towards the front door for a quarter of a mile, jumping over sundials and brick walks and burning gardens—finally when it reached the house drifting up the side in bright vines as though from the momentum of its run.","zh":"草坪从沙滩开始，跑过四分之一英里，来到前门，跳过日晷、砖径和几个万紫千红的花园，抵达墙角之后，仿佛借助奔跑的势头，变成常春藤继续往墙上冲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The front was broken by a line of French windows, glowing now with reflected gold and wide open to the warm windy afternoon, and Tom Buchanan in riding clothes was standing with his legs apart on the front porch.","zh":"房子正面有一排落地玻璃窗，在金色斜晖的照耀之下闪闪发亮，敞开着迎接午后暖煦的和风。汤姆·布坎南穿着骑马的服装，叉开双腿，站在门廊里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He had changed since his New Haven years. Now he was a sturdy straw-haired man of thirty, with a rather hard mouth and a supercilious manner. Two shining arrogant eyes had established dominance over his face and gave him the appearance of always leaning aggressively forward. Not even the effeminate swank of his riding clothes could hide the enormous power of that body—he seemed to fill those glistening boots until he strained the top lacing, and you could see a great pack of muscle shifting when his shoulder moved under his thin coat. It was a body capable of enormous leverage—a cruel body.","sentences":[{"en":"He had changed since his New Haven years.","zh":"他的模样变得跟在纽黑文时不同。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now he was a sturdy straw-haired man of thirty, with a rather hard mouth and a supercilious manner.","zh":"如今他已到而立之年，身材壮硕，头发灰黄，嘴角下垂，神态显得很倨傲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Two shining arrogant eyes had established dominance over his face and gave him the appearance of always leaning aggressively forward.","zh":"他脸上最引人关注的是那双明亮的眼睛，闪烁着傲慢的光彩，总是一副咄咄逼人的样子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Not even the effeminate swank of his riding clothes could hide the enormous power of that body—he seemed to fill those glistening boots until he strained the top lacing, and you could see a great pack of muscle shifting when his shoulder moved under his thin coat.","zh":"甚至连那套华丽得有点女人气的骑马服也遮盖不住他魁梧的身材——他的小腿将那双油光发亮的长筒皮靴绷得紧紧的，每当他的肩膀在薄薄的上衣里面挪动，你能看到肌肉的抖动——那蛮横的身材。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was a body capable of enormous leverage—a cruel body.","zh":"甚至连那套华丽得有点女人气的骑马服也遮盖不住他魁梧的身材——他的小腿将那双油光发亮的长筒皮靴绷得紧紧的，每当他的肩膀在薄薄的上衣里面挪动，你能看到肌肉的抖动——那蛮横的身材。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His speaking voice, a gruff husky tenor, added to the impression of fractiousness he conveyed. There was a touch of paternal contempt in it, even toward people he liked—and there were men at New Haven who had hated his guts.","sentences":[{"en":"His speaking voice, a gruff husky tenor, added to the impression of fractiousness he conveyed.","zh":"他说话的声音既粗又重，而且会给人一种这人性情非常暴躁的印象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a touch of paternal contempt in it, even toward people he liked—and there were men at New Haven who had hated his guts.","zh":"他还总是带着长辈教训晚辈的口吻，哪怕是对他喜欢的人也是如此——当年在纽黑文，讨厌他这副德性的人可不在少数。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Now, don’t think my opinion on these matters is final,” he seemed to say, “just because I’m stronger and more of a man than you are.” We were in the same senior society, and while we were never intimate I always had the impression that he approved of me and wanted me to like him with some harsh, defiant wistfulness of his own.","sentences":[{"en":"“Now, don’t think my opinion on these matters is final,” he seemed to say, “just because I’m stronger and more of a man than you are.”","zh":"“喏，别只是因为我比你强壮，比你更像男子汉，”他当年总是这么说，“就觉得我对这些事情的看法是不容辩驳的定论。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We were in the same senior society, and while we were never intimate I always had the impression that he approved of me and wanted me to like him with some harsh, defiant wistfulness of his own.","zh":"我们同属一个高级联谊会，虽然彼此的关系不算亲近，但我向来觉得他是很欣赏我的，而且怀着他自己那种急躁而又骄矜的热切心情，希望我也会喜欢他。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We talked for a few minutes on the sunny porch.","sentences":[{"en":"We talked for a few minutes on the sunny porch.","zh":"我们在阳光灿烂的门廊里寒暄了几分钟。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got a nice place here,” he said, his eyes flashing about restlessly.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got a nice place here,” he said, his eyes flashing about restlessly.","zh":"“我这个地方不错吧，”他说，眼珠子滴溜溜地到处看。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Turning me around by one arm, he moved a broad flat hand along the front vista, including in its sweep a sunken Italian garden, a half acre of deep, pungent roses, and a snub-nosed motorboat that bumped the tide offshore.","sentences":[{"en":"Turning me around by one arm, he moved a broad flat hand along the front vista, including in its sweep a sunken Italian garden, a half acre of deep, pungent roses, and a snub-nosed motorboat that bumped the tide offshore.","zh":"他用一只手搭着我，让我转了个身，另外那只巨大而扁平的手掌朝前一摆，示意我看眼前的景物：一座下沉式的意大利风格花园，半英亩花香浓郁的深色玫瑰花，以及海边一艘随着浪花起伏的平头汽艇。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It belonged to Demaine, the oil man.” He turned me around again, politely and abruptly. “We’ll go inside.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It belonged to Demaine, the oil man.”","zh":"“这里原来的主人是德梅恩，那个石油大亨，”他又把我转了回来，礼貌但突兀地说，“我们进去吧。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He turned me around again, politely and abruptly.","zh":"“这里原来的主人是德梅恩，那个石油大亨，”他又把我转了回来，礼貌但突兀地说，“我们进去吧。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“We’ll go inside.”","zh":"“这里原来的主人是德梅恩，那个石油大亨，”他又把我转了回来，礼貌但突兀地说，“我们进去吧。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We walked through a high hallway into a bright rosy-coloured space, fragilely bound into the house by French windows at either end. The windows were ajar and gleaming white against the fresh grass outside that seemed to grow a little way into the house. A breeze blew through the room, blew curtains in at one end and out the other like pale flags, twisting them up toward the frosted wedding-cake of the ceiling, and then rippled over the wine-coloured rug, making a shadow on it as wind does on the sea.","sentences":[{"en":"We walked through a high hallway into a bright rosy-coloured space, fragilely bound into the house by French windows at either end.","zh":"我们穿过高高的门厅，来到明艳的玫瑰色客厅，客厅很雅致，两端是落地窗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The windows were ajar and gleaming white against the fresh grass outside that seemed to grow a little way into the house.","zh":"两扇玻璃窗都开着，映照着户外绿油油的草地，显得那些草儿好像长到厅里来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A breeze blew through the room, blew curtains in at one end and out the other like pale flags, twisting them up toward the frosted wedding-cake of the ceiling, and then rippled over the wine-coloured rug, making a shadow on it as wind does on the sea.","zh":"和风穿堂而过，将一边的窗帘吹进来，又将一边的窗帘吹出去，让白旗般的窗帘飘向婚礼蛋糕似的天花板，然后拂过酒红色的地毯，在其上留下波浪起伏的影子，宛如劲风刮过海面。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The only completely stationary object in the room was an enormous couch on which two young women were buoyed up as though upon an anchored balloon. They were both in white, and their dresses were rippling and fluttering as if they had just been blown back in after a short flight around the house. I must have stood for a few moments listening to the whip and snap of the curtains and the groan of a picture on the wall. Then there was a boom as Tom Buchanan shut the rear windows and the caught wind died out about the room, and the curtains and the rugs and the two young women ballooned slowly to the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"The only completely stationary object in the room was an enormous couch on which two young women were buoyed up as though upon an anchored balloon.","zh":"客厅里唯一完全静止的东西是一套巨大的沙发，上面坐着两个年轻女子，那模样仿佛是坐在落地的大气球上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were both in white, and their dresses were rippling and fluttering as if they had just been blown back in after a short flight around the house.","zh":"两人都穿着白色的衣服，裙子不停地波动、轻摆，似乎她们刚刚乘坐气球环绕屋子归来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I must have stood for a few moments listening to the whip and snap of the curtains and the groan of a picture on the wall.","zh":"我不由呆呆地站住了，耳边尽是窗帘的沙沙响和墙上一幅挂画的呻吟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then there was a boom as Tom Buchanan shut the rear windows and the caught wind died out about the room, and the curtains and the rugs and the two young women ballooned slowly to the floor.","zh":"然后突然传来砰砰的响声，原来是汤姆·布坎南关上了后窗，于是客厅中的风渐渐平息，而窗帘、地毯和那两个年轻女子也终于慢慢地降落到地面。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The younger of the two was a stranger to me. She was extended full length at her end of the divan, completely motionless, and with her chin raised a little, as if she were balancing something on it which was quite likely to fall. If she saw me out of the corner of her eyes she gave no hint of it—indeed, I was almost surprised into murmuring an apology for having disturbed her by coming in.","sentences":[{"en":"The younger of the two was a stranger to me.","zh":"那个年纪较轻的女孩我并不认识。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was extended full length at her end of the divan, completely motionless, and with her chin raised a little, as if she were balancing something on it which was quite likely to fall.","zh":"她平躺在贵妃榻上，纹丝不动，下巴微微翘起，仿佛上面有东西就要掉下来，而她正在努力让其保持平衡似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If she saw me out of the corner of her eyes she gave no hint of it—indeed, I was almost surprised into murmuring an apology for having disturbed her by coming in.","zh":"她眼珠转都不转一下，似乎没有看到我进来。其实我反倒很吃惊，差点嗫嚅地为我的到来打扰了她而道歉。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The other girl, Daisy, made an attempt to rise—she leaned slightly forward with a conscientious expression—then she laughed, an absurd, charming little laugh, and I laughed too and came forward into the room.","sentences":[{"en":"The other girl, Daisy, made an attempt to rise—she leaned slightly forward with a conscientious expression—then she laughed, an absurd, charming little laugh, and I laughed too and came forward into the room.","zh":"另外那女子就是黛熙了，她作势要站起来——身体稍微前倾，装出诚恳的表情——然后她轻轻地笑了，那笑声既古怪又迷人，我也笑起来，举步走进客厅。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m p-paralysed with happiness.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m p-paralysed with happiness.”","zh":"“我高兴得呆掉了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She laughed again, as if she said something very witty, and held my hand for a moment, looking up into my face, promising that there was no one in the world she so much wanted to see. That was a way she had. She hinted in a murmur that the surname of the balancing girl was Baker. (I’ve heard it said that Daisy’s murmur was only to make people lean toward her; an irrelevant criticism that made it no less charming.)","sentences":[{"en":"She laughed again, as if she said something very witty, and held my hand for a moment, looking up into my face, promising that there was no one in the world she so much wanted to see.","zh":"她又笑起来，仿佛适才说的那句话非常聪明似的。她握着我的手，盯着我的脸看，装出一副全世界她最想看到的人就是我的样子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That was a way she had.","zh":"这是她惯用的伎俩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She hinted in a murmur that the surname of the balancing girl was Baker.","zh":"她轻声细语地说，那个下巴顶着东西的女孩姓贝克。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"(I’ve heard it said that Daisy’s murmur was only to make people lean toward her; an irrelevant criticism that made it no less charming.)","zh":"（我曾听人说，黛熙说话很小声，是为了让人靠近她；这句无关的闲话并没有减少黛熙这种说话方式的魅力。）","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At any rate, Miss Baker’s lips fluttered, she nodded at me almost imperceptibly, and then quickly tipped her head back again—the object she was balancing had obviously tottered a little and given her something of a fright. Again a sort of apology arose to my lips. Almost any exhibition of complete self-sufficiency draws a stunned tribute from me.","sentences":[{"en":"At any rate, Miss Baker’s lips fluttered, she nodded at me almost imperceptibly, and then quickly tipped her head back again—the object she was balancing had obviously tottered a little and given her something of a fright.","zh":"反正贝克小姐的嘴唇是动了几下，几乎看不出来地朝我点点头，然后赶紧让她的头回到原位——她下巴顶着的那样东西显然歪了一点，把她吓坏了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Again a sort of apology arose to my lips.","zh":"我又差点脱口说出道歉的话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Almost any exhibition of complete self-sufficiency draws a stunned tribute from me.","zh":"对这种我行我素、旁若无人的气概，我向来是既震惊又敬佩的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I looked back at my cousin, who began to ask me questions in her low, thrilling voice. It was the kind of voice that the ear follows up and down, as if each speech is an arrangement of notes that will never be played again. Her face was sad and lovely with bright things in it, bright eyes and a bright passionate mouth, but there was an excitement in her voice that men who had cared for her found difficult to forget: a singing compulsion, a whispered “Listen,” a promise that she had done gay, exciting things just a while since and that there were gay, exciting things hovering in the next hour.","sentences":[{"en":"I looked back at my cousin, who began to ask me questions in her low, thrilling voice.","zh":"我回过头来看着我表妹，她随即用低微而诱人的声音问东问西。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the kind of voice that the ear follows up and down, as if each speech is an arrangement of notes that will never be played again.","zh":"那是让人侧耳倾听的嗓音，仿佛每句话都是人间能得几回闻的天籁之声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her face was sad and lovely with bright things in it, bright eyes and a bright passionate mouth, but there was an excitement in her voice that men who had cared for her found difficult to forget: a singing compulsion, a whispered “Listen,” a promise that she had done gay, exciting things just a while since and that there were gay, exciting things hovering in the next hour.","zh":"她的表情忧伤又可爱，还有着明媚的双眸和明艳的嘴巴，但最让人兴奋的还是她的声音，足以令在乎她的人永生难忘：那是低吟浅唱，也是窃窃私语，暗示着她刚刚做完欢乐轻快的事，而且接下来还有欢乐轻快的事。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I told her how I had stopped off in Chicago for a day on my way East, and how a dozen people had sent their love through me.","sentences":[{"en":"I told her how I had stopped off in Chicago for a day on my way East, and how a dozen people had sent their love through me.","zh":"我跟她说，前来东部途中，我在芝加哥停留了一天，有十来个人托我问候她。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do they miss me?” she cried ecstatically.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do they miss me?” she cried ecstatically.","zh":"“他们很想念我吧？”她欣喜若狂地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The whole town is desolate. All the cars have the left rear wheel painted black as a mourning wreath, and there’s a persistent wail all night along the north shore.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The whole town is desolate.","zh":"“整座城市弥漫着伤感。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the cars have the left rear wheel painted black as a mourning wreath, and there’s a persistent wail all night along the north shore.”","zh":"所有轿车都把左后边的车轮涂黑了表示哀伤，北郊的悲泣声彻夜不停啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How gorgeous! Let’s go back, Tom. Tomorrow!” Then she added irrelevantly: “You ought to see the baby.”","sentences":[{"en":"“How gorgeous!","zh":"“太好啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let’s go back, Tom.","zh":"我们回去吧，汤姆，明天就走！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Tomorrow!”","zh":"我们回去吧，汤姆，明天就走！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she added irrelevantly: “You ought to see the baby.”","zh":"然后她前言不搭后语地说，“你应该看看我的宝贝。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’d like to.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’d like to.”","zh":"“好啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s asleep. She’s three years old. Haven’t you ever seen her?”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s asleep.","zh":"“她睡着啦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She’s three years old.","zh":"她今年三岁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Haven’t you ever seen her?”","zh":"你没有见过她吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Never.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Never.”","zh":"“没有。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, you ought to see her. She’s—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you ought to see her.","zh":"“嗯，你应该见见她。她…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She’s—”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom Buchanan, who had been hovering restlessly about the room, stopped and rested his hand on my shoulder.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom Buchanan, who had been hovering restlessly about the room, stopped and rested his hand on my shoulder.","zh":"刚才片刻不停地在客厅里走来走去的汤姆·布坎南停下脚步，把手搭在我肩膀上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What you doing, Nick?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What you doing, Nick?”","zh":"“尼克，你做什么工作呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m a bond man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m a bond man.”","zh":"“我是搞债券的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who with?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who with?”","zh":"“跟谁搞啊？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I told him.","sentences":[{"en":"I told him.","zh":"我跟他说了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Never heard of them,” he remarked decisively.","sentences":[{"en":"“Never heard of them,” he remarked decisively.","zh":"“没听说过这几个人嘛，”他言之凿凿地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"This annoyed me.","sentences":[{"en":"This annoyed me.","zh":"这让我很恼火。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You will,” I answered shortly. “You will if you stay in the East.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You will,” I answered shortly.","zh":"“你会听说的，”我没好气地回答，“如果你在东部住下来，你会听说的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You will if you stay in the East.”","zh":"“你会听说的，”我没好气地回答，“如果你在东部住下来，你会听说的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, I’ll stay in the East, don’t you worry,” he said, glancing at Daisy and then back at me, as if he were alert for something more. “I’d be a God damned fool to live anywhere else.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I’ll stay in the East, don’t you worry,” he said, glancing at Daisy and then back at me, as if he were alert for something more.","zh":"“哦，我会在东部住下来的，你别担心，”他说，先瞟了黛熙一眼，又看着我，生怕说错话似的，“我要住到别的地方去，那才是大傻瓜呢。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’d be a God damned fool to live anywhere else.”","zh":"“哦，我会在东部住下来的，你别担心，”他说，先瞟了黛熙一眼，又看着我，生怕说错话似的，“我要住到别的地方去，那才是大傻瓜呢。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At this point Miss Baker said: “Absolutely!” with such suddenness that I started—it was the first word she had uttered since I came into the room. Evidently it surprised her as much as it did me, for she yawned and with a series of rapid, deft movements stood up into the room.","sentences":[{"en":"At this point Miss Baker said: “Absolutely!” with such suddenness that I started—it was the first word she had uttered since I came into the room.","zh":"这时贝克小姐说：“绝对的啦！”这句突如其来的话把我吓了一跳——这是我走进客厅以来她说的第一句话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Evidently it surprised her as much as it did me, for she yawned and with a series of rapid, deft movements stood up into the room.","zh":"显然这句话也把她自己吓到了，因为她打着哈欠，通过一系列灵巧而迅速的动作站了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m stiff,” she complained, “I’ve been lying on that sofa for as long as I can remember.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m stiff,” she complained, “I’ve been lying on that sofa for as long as I can remember.”","zh":"“我浑身都僵啦，”她抱怨说，“我都忘记在沙发上躺了有多久。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t look at me,” Daisy retorted, “I’ve been trying to get you to New York all afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t look at me,” Daisy retorted, “I’ve been trying to get you to New York all afternoon.”","zh":"“别看着我，”黛熙反驳说，“我整个下午都在劝你到纽约去。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, thanks,” said Miss Baker to the four cocktails just in from the pantry. “I’m absolutely in training.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, thanks,” said Miss Baker to the four cocktails just in from the pantry.","zh":"“我不喝，谢谢啦，”贝克小姐对着佣人刚从厨房端进来的四杯鸡尾酒说，“我可是遵纪守法的良民。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m absolutely in training.”","zh":"“我不喝，谢谢啦，”贝克小姐对着佣人刚从厨房端进来的四杯鸡尾酒说，“我可是遵纪守法的良民。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her host looked at her incredulously.","sentences":[{"en":"Her host looked at her incredulously.","zh":"“我不喝，谢谢啦，”贝克小姐对着佣人刚从厨房端进来的四杯鸡尾酒说，“我可是遵纪守法的良民。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You are!” He took down his drink as if it were a drop in the bottom of a glass. “How you ever get anything done is beyond me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are!”","zh":"她的男主人不解地看着她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He took down his drink as if it were a drop in the bottom of a glass.","zh":"“是吗！”他举起杯子一饮而尽，“那我真不懂你那些事是怎么办成的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“How you ever get anything done is beyond me.”","zh":"“是吗！”他举起杯子一饮而尽，“那我真不懂你那些事是怎么办成的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I looked at Miss Baker, wondering what it was she “got done.” I enjoyed looking at her. She was a slender, small-breasted girl, with an erect carriage, which she accentuated by throwing her body backward at the shoulders like a young cadet. Her grey sun-strained eyes looked back at me with polite reciprocal curiosity out of a wan, charming, discontented face. It occurred to me now that I had seen her, or a picture of her, somewhere before.","sentences":[{"en":"I looked at Miss Baker, wondering what it was she “got done.”","zh":"我望着贝克小姐，心里奇怪她“办成”了什么事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I enjoyed looking at her.","zh":"她是个苗条的平胸少女，昂首挺胸地站着，姿势很像年轻的军校学生。她的眼睛半眯着，显然经常在阳光下活动。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was a slender, small-breasted girl, with an erect carriage, which she accentuated by throwing her body backward at the shoulders like a young cadet.","zh":"她是个苗条的平胸少女，昂首挺胸地站着，姿势很像年轻的军校学生。她的眼睛半眯着，显然经常在阳光下活动。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her grey sun-strained eyes looked back at me with polite reciprocal curiosity out of a wan, charming, discontented face.","zh":"这双灰色的眼睛好奇地看着我，苍白而迷人的脸庞上满是不高兴的神色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It occurred to me now that I had seen her, or a picture of her, somewhere before.","zh":"这时我才想起来我曾在别处见过她，或者她的照片。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You live in West Egg,” she remarked contemptuously. “I know somebody there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You live in West Egg,” she remarked contemptuously.","zh":"“你住在西卵吧，”她轻蔑地说，“那边有个人我认识。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I know somebody there.”","zh":"“你住在西卵吧，”她轻蔑地说，“那边有个人我认识。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t know a single—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t know a single—”","zh":"“我谁也不认识…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You must know Gatsby.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You must know Gatsby.”","zh":"“你肯定认识盖茨比。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Gatsby?” demanded Daisy. “What Gatsby?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Gatsby?” demanded Daisy.","zh":"“盖茨比？”黛熙迫不及待地问，“哪个盖茨比？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What Gatsby?”","zh":"“盖茨比？”黛熙迫不及待地问，“哪个盖茨比？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Before I could reply that he was my neighbour dinner was announced; wedging his tense arm imperatively under mine, Tom Buchanan compelled me from the room as though he were moving a checker to another square.","sentences":[{"en":"Before I could reply that he was my neighbour dinner was announced; wedging his tense arm imperatively under mine, Tom Buchanan compelled me from the room as though he were moving a checker to another square.","zh":"我还没来得及说他是我的邻居，佣人就宣布晚餐开始了。汤姆·布坎南强行将他结实的手臂插到我腋下，拖着我往客厅外面走，仿佛他正要将棋子移到另外一格似的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Slenderly, languidly, their hands set lightly on their hips, the two young women preceded us out on to a rosy-coloured porch, open toward the sunset, where four candles flickered on the table in the diminished wind.","sentences":[{"en":"Slenderly, languidly, their hands set lightly on their hips, the two young women preceded us out on to a rosy-coloured porch, open toward the sunset, where four candles flickered on the table in the diminished wind.","zh":"两位苗条的年轻女子慵懒地把手轻轻放在腰上，领着我们走到客厅外玫瑰色的门廊。沐浴着晚照的门廊摆着餐桌，上面点着四支蜡烛，烛火在微风中摇曳。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why candles?” objected Daisy, frowning. She snapped them out with her fingers. “In two weeks it’ll be the longest day in the year.” She looked at us all radiantly. “Do you always watch for the longest day of the year and then miss it? I always watch for the longest day in the year and then miss it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why candles?” objected Daisy, frowning.","zh":"“干吗点蜡烛呀？”黛熙皱着眉抗议。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She snapped them out with her fingers.","zh":"她用手指把蜡烛捏熄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“In two weeks it’ll be the longest day in the year.”","zh":"“再过两个星期，就是一年中白天最长的日子啦，”她容光焕发地看着我们说，“你们会期盼一年中白天最长的日子，等它来临时却忘记了吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"She looked at us all radiantly.","zh":"“再过两个星期，就是一年中白天最长的日子啦，”她容光焕发地看着我们说，“你们会期盼一年中白天最长的日子，等它来临时却忘记了吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Do you always watch for the longest day of the year and then miss it?","zh":"“再过两个星期，就是一年中白天最长的日子啦，”她容光焕发地看着我们说，“你们会期盼一年中白天最长的日子，等它来临时却忘记了吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"I always watch for the longest day in the year and then miss it.”","zh":"我总是期盼这个日子，然后到了那天又会忘记。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We ought to plan something,” yawned Miss Baker, sitting down at the table as if she were getting into bed.","sentences":[{"en":"“We ought to plan something,” yawned Miss Baker, sitting down at the table as if she were getting into bed.","zh":"“我们应该找点事做，”贝克小姐打着哈欠说，她虽然坐在餐桌旁边，却是一副就要睡觉的样子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right,” said Daisy. “What’ll we plan?” She turned to me helplessly: “What do people plan?”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right,” said Daisy.","zh":"“好吧，”黛熙说，“我们做什么好呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What’ll we plan?”","zh":"“好吧，”黛熙说，“我们做什么好呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She turned to me helplessly: “What do people plan?”","zh":"她无可奈何地看着我。“大家做什么好呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Before I could answer her eyes fastened with an awed expression on her little finger.","sentences":[{"en":"Before I could answer her eyes fastened with an awed expression on her little finger.","zh":"我尚未回答，她的眼睛忽又惊讶地看着她的小指头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look!” she complained; “I hurt it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look!” she complained; “I hurt it.”","zh":"“看啊！”她抱怨说，“我把它弄伤了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We all looked—the knuckle was black and blue.","sentences":[{"en":"We all looked—the knuckle was black and blue.","zh":"我们都看过去——指节有点淤青。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You did it, Tom,” she said accusingly. “I know you didn’t mean to, but you did do it. That’s what I get for marrying a brute of a man, a great, big, hulking physical specimen of a—”","sentences":[{"en":"“You did it, Tom,” she said accusingly.","zh":"“你干的好事，汤姆，”她责怪地说，“我知道你不是故意的，但这是你造成的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I know you didn’t mean to, but you did do it.","zh":"“你干的好事，汤姆，”她责怪地说，“我知道你不是故意的，但这是你造成的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"That’s what I get for marrying a brute of a man, a great, big, hulking physical specimen of a—”","zh":"我真是命苦呀，嫁给这个粗鲁的男人，又壮又高又粗又笨的…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I hate that word ‘hulking,’ ” objected Tom crossly, “even in kidding.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I hate that word ‘hulking,’ ” objected Tom crossly, “even in kidding.”","zh":"“我讨厌你说我又粗又笨，”汤姆立刻抗议，“哪怕是在开玩笑。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hulking,” insisted Daisy.","sentences":[{"en":"“Hulking,” insisted Daisy.","zh":"“我讨厌你说我又粗又笨，”汤姆立刻抗议，“哪怕是在开玩笑。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Sometimes she and Miss Baker talked at once, unobtrusively and with a bantering inconsequence that was never quite chatter, that was as cool as their white dresses and their impersonal eyes in the absence of all desire. They were here, and they accepted Tom and me, making only a polite pleasant effort to entertain or to be entertained. They knew that presently dinner would be over and a little later the evening too would be over and casually put away. It was sharply different from the West, where an evening was hurried from phase to phase towards its close, in a continually disappointed anticipation or else in sheer nervous dread of the moment itself.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes she and Miss Baker talked at once, unobtrusively and with a bantering inconsequence that was never quite chatter, that was as cool as their white dresses and their impersonal eyes in the absence of all desire.","zh":"“你就是又粗又笨，”黛熙毫不示弱。有时候她和贝克小姐同时开口，漫不经心地说着无关紧要的玩笑话，而且也绝不会彼此争执，口气冷冷淡淡的，如同她们的白色裙子和漠然的、没有任何情欲的眼睛。她们愿意坐下来，也不反感汤姆和我，礼貌地说说笑笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were here, and they accepted Tom and me, making only a polite pleasant effort to entertain or to be entertained.","zh":"“你就是又粗又笨，”黛熙毫不示弱。有时候她和贝克小姐同时开口，漫不经心地说着无关紧要的玩笑话，而且也绝不会彼此争执，口气冷冷淡淡的，如同她们的白色裙子和漠然的、没有任何情欲的眼睛。她们愿意坐下来，也不反感汤姆和我，礼貌地说说笑笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They knew that presently dinner would be over and a little later the evening too would be over and casually put away.","zh":"但她们知道这顿晚餐终究会结束，片刻之后，今晚的欢聚也将会告终，她们对此并不在乎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was sharply different from the West, where an evening was hurried from phase to phase towards its close, in a continually disappointed anticipation or else in sheer nervous dread of the moment itself.","zh":"这种态度跟西部截然不同，那边的人们夜里聚会时，总是热切地倾谈着，自始至终不会冷场，无论他们是感到越来越失望，或者非常不愿意曲终人散的时刻来临。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You make me feel uncivilized, Daisy,” I confessed on my second glass of corky but rather impressive claret. “Can’t you talk about crops or something?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You make me feel uncivilized, Daisy,” I confessed on my second glass of corky but rather impressive claret.","zh":"“你让我觉得自己很不文明耶，黛熙，”我喝下第二杯混杂着软木塞的气息然而口感很好的红酒，然后说，“你就不能聊聊庄稼或者其他我能听懂的话题吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Can’t you talk about crops or something?”","zh":"“你让我觉得自己很不文明耶，黛熙，”我喝下第二杯混杂着软木塞的气息然而口感很好的红酒，然后说，“你就不能聊聊庄稼或者其他我能听懂的话题吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I meant nothing in particular by this remark, but it was taken up in an unexpected way.","sentences":[{"en":"I meant nothing in particular by this remark, but it was taken up in an unexpected way.","zh":"其实我只是随口说说，但汤姆却以我意想不到的方式把话头接了过去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Civilization’s going to pieces,” broke out Tom violently. “I’ve gotten to be a terrible pessimist about things. Have you read The Rise of the Coloured Empires by this man Goddard?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Civilization’s going to pieces,” broke out Tom violently.","zh":"“文明即将破灭啦，”汤姆大声地说，“我现在对很多事情都感到极其悲观。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ve gotten to be a terrible pessimist about things.","zh":"“文明即将破灭啦，”汤姆大声地说，“我现在对很多事情都感到极其悲观。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Have you read The Rise of the Coloured Empires by this man Goddard?”","zh":"你看过《有色帝国的崛起》吗？是个叫高达德的家伙写的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why, no,” I answered, rather surprised by his tone.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, no,” I answered, rather surprised by his tone.","zh":"“没看过呢，”我说。他的口气让我相当意外。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, it’s a fine book, and everybody ought to read it. The idea is if we don’t look out the white race will be—will be utterly submerged. It’s all scientific stuff; it’s been proved.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, it’s a fine book, and everybody ought to read it.","zh":"“嗯，那绝对是好书，大家都应该读一读。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The idea is if we don’t look out the white race will be—will be utterly submerged.","zh":"作者认为，如果我们不小心提防，白种人将会…将会彻底沉沦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s all scientific stuff; it’s been proved.”","zh":"书里全是科学性的材料，这种说法是有凭有据的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Tom’s getting very profound,” said Daisy, with an expression of unthoughtful sadness. “He reads deep books with long words in them. What was that word we—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Tom’s getting very profound,” said Daisy, with an expression of unthoughtful sadness.","zh":"“汤姆最近变得非常学究气，”黛熙说，不期然地露出悲伤的表情，“他读了很多有大量长句的图书。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He reads deep books with long words in them.","zh":"“汤姆最近变得非常学究气，”黛熙说，不期然地露出悲伤的表情，“他读了很多有大量长句的图书。","scope":"group"},{"en":"What was that word we—”","zh":"有句话怎么说来着，我们…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, these books are all scientific,” insisted Tom, glancing at her impatiently. “This fellow has worked out the whole thing. It’s up to us, who are the dominant race, to watch out or these other races will have control of things.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, these books are all scientific,” insisted Tom, glancing at her impatiently.","zh":"“这些书都是讲科学的，”汤姆不耐烦地瞟了她一眼，固执地说，“这家伙提出了整套理论。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“This fellow has worked out the whole thing.","zh":"“这些书都是讲科学的，”汤姆不耐烦地瞟了她一眼，固执地说，“这家伙提出了整套理论。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s up to us, who are the dominant race, to watch out or these other races will have control of things.”","zh":"我们这些占据统治地位的人种必须小心行事，否则其他人种就会取得控制权。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ve got to beat them down,” whispered Daisy, winking ferociously toward the fervent sun.","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ve got to beat them down,” whispered Daisy, winking ferociously toward the fervent sun.","zh":"“我们得把他们打趴了，”黛熙轻轻地说，对着火红的斜阳猛眨眼。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You ought to live in California—” began Miss Baker, but Tom interrupted her by shifting heavily in his chair.","sentences":[{"en":"“You ought to live in California—” began Miss Baker, but Tom interrupted her by shifting heavily in his chair.","zh":"“你们应该住到加利福尼亚去…”贝克小姐试图插嘴，但汤姆坐在椅子上重重地挪了挪身体，打断了她。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This idea is that we’re Nordics. I am, and you are, and you are, and—” After an infinitesimal hesitation he included Daisy with a slight nod, and she winked at me again. “—And we’ve produced all the things that go to make civilization—oh, science and art, and all that. Do you see?”","sentences":[{"en":"“This idea is that we’re Nordics.","zh":"“我们属于北欧民族，我，你，你，还有…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am, and you are, and you are, and—” After an infinitesimal hesitation he included Daisy with a slight nod, and she winked at me again.","zh":"”他略微迟疑，随即点点头，把黛熙也囊括在内，而黛熙又朝我眨起眼睛来，“…你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“—And we’ve produced all the things that go to make civilization—oh, science and art, and all that.","zh":"按照这本书的观点，人类文明都是我们亲手打造的，包括科学和艺术，以及其他种种。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you see?”","zh":"你明白吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was something pathetic in his concentration, as if his complacency, more acute than of old, was not enough to him any more. When, almost immediately, the telephone rang inside and the butler left the porch Daisy seized upon the momentary interruption and leaned towards me.","sentences":[{"en":"There was something pathetic in his concentration, as if his complacency, more acute than of old, was not enough to him any more.","zh":"他这种忘乎所以的劲头让我觉得有点可怜，仿佛他虽然比以前更加自命不凡，但觉得还不够踌躇满志似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When, almost immediately, the telephone rang inside and the butler left the porch Daisy seized upon the momentary interruption and leaned towards me.","zh":"此时屋里的电话铃响起来，管家离开了门廊，黛熙立刻抓住这个良机，凑到我面前来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll tell you a family secret,” she whispered enthusiastically. “It’s about the butler’s nose. Do you want to hear about the butler’s nose?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll tell you a family secret,” she whispered enthusiastically.","zh":"“我要告诉你我们家的一个秘密，”她兴致勃勃地低声说，“有关管家的鼻子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s about the butler’s nose.","zh":"“我要告诉你我们家的一个秘密，”她兴致勃勃地低声说，“有关管家的鼻子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Do you want to hear about the butler’s nose?”","zh":"你想听听管家的鼻子有什么秘密吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s why I came over tonight.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s why I came over tonight.”","zh":"你想听听管家的鼻子有什么秘密吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, he wasn’t always a butler; he used to be the silver polisher for some people in New York that had a silver service for two hundred people. He had to polish it from morning till night, until finally it began to affect his nose—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, he wasn’t always a butler; he used to be the silver polisher for some people in New York that had a silver service for two hundred people.","zh":"“这正是我今晚前来拜访的原因呀。”“好啊，他以前不是管家。他以前在纽约替某个富翁擦银器，那人的银器足以供两百人使用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had to polish it from morning till night, until finally it began to affect his nose—”","zh":"他必须从早到晚擦个不停，后来他的鼻子终于受到影响…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Things went from bad to worse,” suggested Miss Baker.","sentences":[{"en":"“Things went from bad to worse,” suggested Miss Baker.","zh":"“变得越来越糟糕，”贝克小姐帮腔说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes. Things went from bad to worse, until finally he had to give up his position.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.","zh":"“是啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Things went from bad to worse, until finally he had to give up his position.”","zh":"变得越来越糟糕，最后他只好辞职不干了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For a moment the last sunshine fell with romantic affection upon her glowing face; her voice compelled me forward breathlessly as I listened—then the glow faded, each light deserting her with lingering regret, like children leaving a pleasant street at dusk.","sentences":[{"en":"For a moment the last sunshine fell with romantic affection upon her glowing face; her voice compelled me forward breathlessly as I listened—then the glow faded, each light deserting her with lingering regret, like children leaving a pleasant street at dusk.","zh":"最后的余晖带着罗曼蒂克的色彩，将她的面容照得神采奕奕，而她美妙的声线吸引我屏住呼吸凑上前去倾听。片刻之后，那神采消失了，每道光线恋恋不舍地离她而去，就像儿童在黄昏时离开充满乐趣的街道那样。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The butler came back and murmured something close to Tom’s ear, whereupon Tom frowned, pushed back his chair, and without a word went inside. As if his absence quickened something within her, Daisy leaned forward again, her voice glowing and singing.","sentences":[{"en":"The butler came back and murmured something close to Tom’s ear, whereupon Tom frowned, pushed back his chair, and without a word went inside.","zh":"管家走了回来，在汤姆耳边密语了几句，汤姆听完皱起眉头，向后推开他的椅子，什么话也没说就走进屋里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As if his absence quickened something within her, Daisy leaned forward again, her voice glowing and singing.","zh":"他的离场似乎让黛熙活跃起来，她又侧过身来，声音像歌曲般欢快而动听。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I love to see you at my table, Nick. You remind me of a—of a rose, an absolute rose. Doesn’t he?” She turned to Miss Baker for confirmation: “An absolute rose?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I love to see you at my table, Nick.","zh":"“我很高兴请你来吃饭呀，尼克。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You remind me of a—of a rose, an absolute rose.","zh":"你让我想起了一朵玫瑰，一朵绝美的玫瑰，对吧？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Doesn’t he?”","zh":"她转头寻求贝克小姐的认可，“他像一朵绝美的玫瑰吧？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She turned to Miss Baker for confirmation: “An absolute rose?”","zh":"她转头寻求贝克小姐的认可，“他像一朵绝美的玫瑰吧？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"This was untrue. I am not even faintly like a rose. She was only extemporizing, but a stirring warmth flowed from her, as if her heart was trying to come out to you concealed in one of those breathless, thrilling words. Then suddenly she threw her napkin on the table and excused herself and went into the house.","sentences":[{"en":"This was untrue.","zh":"这很荒唐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am not even faintly like a rose.","zh":"我浑身没有半点像玫瑰的地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was only extemporizing, but a stirring warmth flowed from her, as if her heart was trying to come out to you concealed in one of those breathless, thrilling words.","zh":"她只是在信口开河，但我觉得她心里似乎有股怒气，这些足以令人屏住呼吸和激动不已的话语里隐藏着她的心事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then suddenly she threw her napkin on the table and excused herself and went into the house.","zh":"然后她突然将餐巾丢在桌子上，说了一声对不起，就走进屋子去了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Miss Baker and I exchanged a short glance consciously devoid of meaning. I was about to speak when she sat up alertly and said “Sh!” in a warning voice. A subdued impassioned murmur was audible in the room beyond, and Miss Baker leaned forward unashamed, trying to hear. The murmur trembled on the verge of coherence, sank down, mounted excitedly, and then ceased altogether.","sentences":[{"en":"Miss Baker and I exchanged a short glance consciously devoid of meaning.","zh":"贝克小姐和我故意不动声色地互使了眼色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was about to speak when she sat up alertly and said “Sh!” in a warning voice.","zh":"我正准备说话，她机警地坐直了，嘴里“嘘”了一下，示意我别做声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A subdued impassioned murmur was audible in the room beyond, and Miss Baker leaned forward unashamed, trying to hear.","zh":"屋里依稀传来一阵激烈的低声争吵，贝克小姐毫不顾忌地侧过身去，想要仔细听清楚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The murmur trembled on the verge of coherence, sank down, mounted excitedly, and then ceased altogether.","zh":"里面的低语渐渐响亮到差不多听得清，忽而低沉下去，忽而又升高，然后彻底平息了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This Mr. Gatsby you spoke of is my neighbour—” I began.","sentences":[{"en":"“This Mr. Gatsby you spoke of is my neighbour—” I began.","zh":"“你刚才提到的盖茨比先生是我的邻居…”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t talk. I want to hear what happens.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t talk.","zh":"“别说话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I want to hear what happens.”","zh":"我想听听怎么回事。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is something happening?” I inquired innocently.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is something happening?”","zh":"“发生什么事啦？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired innocently.","zh":"不知内情的我问道。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You mean to say you don’t know?” said Miss Baker, honestly surprised. “I thought everybody knew.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You mean to say you don’t know?” said Miss Baker, honestly surprised.","zh":"“你居然不知道啊？”贝克小姐感到很意外地说，“我以为大家都知道。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I thought everybody knew.”","zh":"“你居然不知道啊？”贝克小姐感到很意外地说，“我以为大家都知道。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t.”","zh":"“我不知道呀。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why—” she said hesitantly. “Tom’s got some woman in New York.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why—” she said hesitantly.","zh":"“好吧，”她吞吞吐吐地说，“汤姆在纽约有个相好。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Tom’s got some woman in New York.”","zh":"“好吧，”她吞吞吐吐地说，“汤姆在纽约有个相好。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Got some woman?” I repeated blankly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Got some woman?”","zh":"“有个相好？”我茫然地重复她的话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I repeated blankly.","zh":"“有个相好？”我茫然地重复她的话。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Miss Baker nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"Miss Baker nodded.","zh":"贝克小姐点点头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She might have the decency not to telephone him at dinner time. Don’t you think?”","sentences":[{"en":"“She might have the decency not to telephone him at dinner time.","zh":"“她应该识趣点，别在晚餐时间打电话给他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Don’t you think?”","zh":"你觉得呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Almost before I had grasped her meaning there was the flutter of a dress and the crunch of leather boots, and Tom and Daisy were back at the table.","sentences":[{"en":"Almost before I had grasped her meaning there was the flutter of a dress and the crunch of leather boots, and Tom and Daisy were back at the table.","zh":"我还没弄懂她这句话的意思，就听到裙子的沙沙响和皮靴的踏地声，汤姆和黛熙回到了餐桌。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It couldn’t be helped!” cried Daisy with tense gaiety.","sentences":[{"en":"“It couldn’t be helped!” cried Daisy with tense gaiety.","zh":"“刚才失态啦！”黛熙强颜欢笑地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She sat down, glanced searchingly at Miss Baker and then at me, and continued: “I looked outdoors for a minute, and it’s very romantic outdoors. There’s a bird on the lawn that I think must be a nightingale come over on the Cunard or White Star Line. He’s singing away—” Her voice sang: “It’s romantic, isn’t it, Tom?”","sentences":[{"en":"She sat down, glanced searchingly at Miss Baker and then at me, and continued: “I looked outdoors for a minute, and it’s very romantic outdoors.","zh":"她坐下来，目光闪烁地看看贝克小姐，又看看我，接着说：“我看了外面的景色，外面真是好浪漫呀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There’s a bird on the lawn that I think must be a nightingale come over on the Cunard or White Star Line.","zh":"有只小鸟落在草坪上，我觉得肯定是夜莺，从英国搭乘冠达或者白星邮轮过来的。它正在唱歌…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He’s singing away—” Her voice sang: “It’s romantic, isn’t it, Tom?”","zh":"”她的声音也像是在唱歌，“真是浪漫呀，汤姆，你说呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Very romantic,” he said, and then miserably to me: “If it’s light enough after dinner, I want to take you down to the stables.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very romantic,” he said, and then miserably to me: “If it’s light enough after dinner, I want to take you down to the stables.”","zh":"“非常浪漫，”他敷衍了一句，然后愁容满面地对我说，“如果吃完饭天还够亮，我带你去马房看看。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The telephone rang inside, startlingly, and as Daisy shook her head decisively at Tom the subject of the stables, in fact all subjects, vanished into air. Among the broken fragments of the last five minutes at table I remember the candles being lit again, pointlessly, and I was conscious of wanting to look squarely at everyone, and yet to avoid all eyes. I couldn’t guess what Daisy and Tom were thinking, but I doubt if even Miss Baker, who seemed to have mastered a certain hardy scepticism, was able utterly to put this fifth guest’s shrill metallic urgency out of mind. To a certain temperament the situation might have seemed intriguing—my own instinct was to telephone immediately for the police.","sentences":[{"en":"The telephone rang inside, startlingly, and as Daisy shook her head decisively at Tom the subject of the stables, in fact all subjects, vanished into air.","zh":"屋里电话突然又响了，怪吓人的，黛熙看着汤姆，坚决地摇摇头，于是所有话题，包括马房，都烟消云散了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Among the broken fragments of the last five minutes at table I remember the candles being lit again, pointlessly, and I was conscious of wanting to look squarely at everyone, and yet to avoid all eyes.","zh":"在餐桌上的最后五分钟，大家都很尴尬，我记得蜡烛毫无意义地又被点燃了，当时我想要直视每个人，却又避开大家的眼光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I couldn’t guess what Daisy and Tom were thinking, but I doubt if even Miss Baker, who seemed to have mastered a certain hardy scepticism, was able utterly to put this fifth guest’s shrill metallic urgency out of mind.","zh":"我猜不出黛熙和汤姆心里在想什么，但我敢说哪怕是显得如此玩世不恭的贝克小姐，也难以完全不去想这第三位客人刺耳而急促的电话铃声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To a certain temperament the situation might have seemed intriguing—my own instinct was to telephone immediately for the police.","zh":"也许在置身事外的人看来，这局面倒也挺有意思的——但我自己的本能反应是赶紧打电话报警。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The horses, needless to say, were not mentioned again. Tom and Miss Baker, with several feet of twilight between them, strolled back into the library, as if to a vigil beside a perfectly tangible body, while, trying to look pleasantly interested and a little deaf, I followed Daisy around a chain of connecting verandas to the porch in front. In its deep gloom we sat down side by side on a wicker settee.","sentences":[{"en":"The horses, needless to say, were not mentioned again.","zh":"不用说，马房的事再也没人提起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom and Miss Baker, with several feet of twilight between them, strolled back into the library, as if to a vigil beside a perfectly tangible body, while, trying to look pleasantly interested and a little deaf, I followed Daisy around a chain of connecting verandas to the porch in front.","zh":"汤姆和贝克小姐隔着几英尺的暮色，一前一后悠悠地走进了书房，那神情活像是要去给死人守灵；而我则装出高高兴兴、若无其事的样子，随着黛熙穿过几个相连的通道，来到屋子前面的门廊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In its deep gloom we sat down side by side on a wicker settee.","zh":"光线全然暗了下来，我们并排在一张柳条长椅上坐下。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy took her face in her hands as if feeling its lovely shape, and her eyes moved gradually out into the velvet dusk. I saw that turbulent emotions possessed her, so I asked what I thought would be some sedative questions about her little girl.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy took her face in her hands as if feeling its lovely shape, and her eyes moved gradually out into the velvet dusk.","zh":"黛熙双手捂着脸庞，仿佛是在感受它可爱的形状，她的明眸缓缓地望向天鹅绒般漆黑的夜色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw that turbulent emotions possessed her, so I asked what I thought would be some sedative questions about her little girl.","zh":"我看得出她思绪翻涌，于是问起她的女儿，想让她平静下来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We don’t know each other very well, Nick,” she said suddenly. “Even if we are cousins. You didn’t come to my wedding.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We don’t know each other very well, Nick,” she said suddenly.","zh":"“我们相互不是很了解，尼克，”她突然说，“尽管我们是表亲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Even if we are cousins.","zh":"“我们相互不是很了解，尼克，”她突然说，“尽管我们是表亲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"You didn’t come to my wedding.”","zh":"我结婚时你都没来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I wasn’t back from the war.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wasn’t back from the war.”","zh":"“当时我还在打仗呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s true.” She hesitated. “Well, I’ve had a very bad time, Nick, and I’m pretty cynical about everything.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s true.”","zh":"“那倒是，”她迟疑地说，“好吧，我有过一段伤心事，尼克，现在我真是看破红尘啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She hesitated.","zh":"“那倒是，”她迟疑地说，“好吧，我有过一段伤心事，尼克，现在我真是看破红尘啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Well, I’ve had a very bad time, Nick, and I’m pretty cynical about everything.”","zh":"“那倒是，”她迟疑地说，“好吧，我有过一段伤心事，尼克，现在我真是看破红尘啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Evidently she had reason to be. I waited but she didn’t say any more, and after a moment I returned rather feebly to the subject of her daughter.","sentences":[{"en":"Evidently she had reason to be.","zh":"这显然有隐情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I waited but she didn’t say any more, and after a moment I returned rather feebly to the subject of her daughter.","zh":"我等她透露，但她没有说下去。过了片刻，我无奈之下又把话题转回到她女儿身上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I suppose she talks, and—eats, and everything.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I suppose she talks, and—eats, and everything.”","zh":"“她现在什么都会说，什么都能吃了吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, yes.” She looked at me absently. “Listen, Nick; let me tell you what I said when she was born. Would you like to hear?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, yes.”","zh":"“是啊，”她心不在焉地说，“听着，尼克，我要跟你说说她出生时发生的事情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She looked at me absently.","zh":"“是啊，”她心不在焉地说，“听着，尼克，我要跟你说说她出生时发生的事情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Listen, Nick; let me tell you what I said when she was born.","zh":"“是啊，”她心不在焉地说，“听着，尼克，我要跟你说说她出生时发生的事情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Would you like to hear?”","zh":"你愿意听吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Very much.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very much.”","zh":"“非常愿意。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’ll show you how I’ve gotten to feel about—things. Well, she was less than an hour old and Tom was God knows where. I woke up out of the ether with an utterly abandoned feeling, and asked the nurse right away if it was a boy or a girl. She told me it was a girl, and so I turned my head away and wept. ‘All right,’ I said, ‘I’m glad it’s a girl. And I hope she’ll be a fool—that’s the best thing a girl can be in this world, a beautiful little fool.’","sentences":[{"en":"“It’ll show you how I’ve gotten to feel about—things.","zh":"“你听了就知道我为什么会感到…心灰意冷。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, she was less than an hour old and Tom was God knows where.","zh":"嗯，她出生不到一个小时，汤姆就不知道跑哪里去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I woke up out of the ether with an utterly abandoned feeling, and asked the nurse right away if it was a boy or a girl.","zh":"我从麻醉状态中醒来，感到非常凄凉，立刻问护士是男是女。她说是个女孩，所以我扭头就哭了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She told me it was a girl, and so I turned my head away and wept. ‘All right,’ I said, ‘I’m glad it’s a girl.","zh":"‘好吧，’我说，‘我很高兴是个女孩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And I hope she’ll be a fool—that’s the best thing a girl can be in this world, a beautiful little fool.’","zh":"我希望她将来是个傻瓜——在这个世界上，女孩最好当傻瓜，当一个美丽的小傻瓜。’","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You see I think everything’s terrible anyhow,” she went on in a convinced way. “Everybody thinks so—the most advanced people. And I know. I’ve been everywhere and seen everything and done everything.” Her eyes flashed around her in a defiant way, rather like Tom’s, and she laughed with thrilling scorn. “Sophisticated—God, I’m sophisticated!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You see I think everything’s terrible anyhow,” she went on in a convinced way.","zh":"“你知道吗，我觉得总之一切都特别没意思，”她继续用很诚恳的语气说，“每个人都这么想——那些最高级的人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Everybody thinks so—the most advanced people.","zh":"“你知道吗，我觉得总之一切都特别没意思，”她继续用很诚恳的语气说，“每个人都这么想——那些最高级的人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And I know.","zh":"我就知道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve been everywhere and seen everything and done everything.”","zh":"我什么地方都去过了，什么景色都看过了，什么事情都做过了。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her eyes flashed around her in a defiant way, rather like Tom’s, and she laughed with thrilling scorn.","zh":"她像汤姆那样顾盼自雄地东张西望，发出一阵动听的冷笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Sophisticated—God, I’m sophisticated!”","zh":"“这就是饱经沧桑啊——天哪，我已经饱经沧桑啦！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The instant her voice broke off, ceasing to compel my attention, my belief, I felt the basic insincerity of what she had said. It made me uneasy, as though the whole evening had been a trick of some sort to exact a contributory emotion from me. I waited, and sure enough, in a moment she looked at me with an absolute smirk on her lovely face, as if she had asserted her membership in a rather distinguished secret society to which she and Tom belonged.","sentences":[{"en":"The instant her voice broke off, ceasing to compel my attention, my belief, I felt the basic insincerity of what she had said.","zh":"她一收起那迫使我不得不专心聆听和由衷相信的声音，我立刻就察觉到她刚才说的都不是真心话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It made me uneasy, as though the whole evening had been a trick of some sort to exact a contributory emotion from me.","zh":"这让我很不爽，似乎晚上发生的一切都是圈套，用来诱骗我付出她想要的情感。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I waited, and sure enough, in a moment she looked at me with an absolute smirk on her lovely face, as if she had asserted her membership in a rather distinguished secret society to which she and Tom belonged.","zh":"我沉默不语，过了片刻，她看着我时，那张可爱的脸上果然露出了讥笑，仿佛她已经获得了某个由杰出人士组成的秘密社团的入会资格，她和汤姆都已经成为会员。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"Inside, the crimson room bloomed with light. Tom and Miss Baker sat at either end of the long couch and she read aloud to him from the Saturday Evening Post—the words, murmurous and uninflected, running together in a soothing tune. The lamplight, bright on his boots and dull on the autumn-leaf yellow of her hair, glinted along the paper as she turned a page with a flutter of slender muscles in her arms.","sentences":[{"en":"Inside, the crimson room bloomed with light.","zh":"屋内，粉红色的客厅灯火通明。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom and Miss Baker sat at either end of the long couch and she read aloud to him from the Saturday Evening Post—the words, murmurous and uninflected, running together in a soothing tune.","zh":"汤姆和贝克小姐分坐长沙发的两端，她正在念《星期六晚报》给汤姆听。她轻轻地念，不分发音的轻重，但听起来既流畅又悦耳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The lamplight, bright on his boots and dull on the autumn-leaf yellow of her hair, glinted along the paper as she turned a page with a flutter of slender muscles in her arms.","zh":"灯光照得汤姆的靴子闪闪发亮，照得贝克小姐秋叶黄的头发黯无光泽，又照得杂志的纸张白花花的很耀眼，每当翻过一页，她手臂上苗条的肌肉就会随之一动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When we came in she held us silent for a moment with a lifted hand.","sentences":[{"en":"When we came in she held us silent for a moment with a lifted hand.","zh":"我们走了进去，她抬起手，要我们保持安静。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“To be continued,” she said, tossing the magazine on the table, “in our very next issue.”","sentences":[{"en":"“To be continued,” she said, tossing the magazine on the table, “in our very next issue.”","zh":"“未完待续，”她说着把杂志往桌上一丢，“请见下期。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her body asserted itself with a restless movement of her knee, and she stood up.","sentences":[{"en":"Her body asserted itself with a restless movement of her knee, and she stood up.","zh":"她双脚着地，抖了抖两边的膝盖，然后站起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Ten o’clock,” she remarked, apparently finding the time on the ceiling. “Time for this good girl to go to bed.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ten o’clock,” she remarked, apparently finding the time on the ceiling.","zh":"“十点了，”她说，眼睛看着天花板，好像那里有个时钟，“我这个乖乖女要睡觉啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Time for this good girl to go to bed.”","zh":"“十点了，”她说，眼睛看着天花板，好像那里有个时钟，“我这个乖乖女要睡觉啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Jordan’s going to play in the tournament tomorrow,” explained Daisy, “over at Westchester.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Jordan’s going to play in the tournament tomorrow,” explained Daisy, “over at Westchester.”","zh":"“乔丹明天要参加比赛，”黛熙解释说，“在威切斯特那边。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh—you’re Jordan Baker.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh—you’re Jordan Baker.”","zh":"“啊…原来你就是乔丹·贝克。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I knew now why her face was familiar—its pleasing contemptuous expression had looked out at me from many rotogravure pictures of the sporting life at Asheville and Hot Springs and Palm Beach. I had heard some story of her too, a critical, unpleasant story, but what it was I had forgotten long ago.","sentences":[{"en":"I knew now why her face was familiar—its pleasing contemptuous expression had looked out at me from many rotogravure pictures of the sporting life at Asheville and Hot Springs and Palm Beach.","zh":"现在我知道为什么会觉得她很面熟了——我曾多次在报刊的体育版上看到这张美丽而高傲的脸庞，那些媒体会报道她在阿什维尔、温泉公园或者棕榈海滩的比赛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had heard some story of her too, a critical, unpleasant story, but what it was I had forgotten long ago.","zh":"我也听说过有关她的闲话，很难听的那种，但到底说了什么我早已忘记。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Good night,” she said softly. “Wake me at eight, won’t you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good night,” she said softly.","zh":"“晚安，”她轻轻地说，“八点叫醒我，拜托啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Wake me at eight, won’t you.”","zh":"“晚安，”她轻轻地说，“八点叫醒我，拜托啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“If you’ll get up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If you’ll get up.”","zh":"“到时你别起不来呀。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I will. Good night, Mr. Carraway. See you anon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I will.","zh":"“我会起来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good night, Mr. Carraway.","zh":"晚安，卡拉威先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"See you anon.”","zh":"希望还有机会见面。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course you will,” confirmed Daisy. “In fact I think I’ll arrange a marriage. Come over often, Nick, and I’ll sort of—oh—fling you together. You know—lock you up accidentally in linen closets and push you out to sea in a boat, and all that sort of thing—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course you will,” confirmed Daisy.","zh":"“当然有啊，”黛熙肯定地说，“其实我想当你们的媒人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“In fact I think I’ll arrange a marriage.","zh":"“当然有啊，”黛熙肯定地说，“其实我想当你们的媒人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Come over often, Nick, and I’ll sort of—oh—fling you together.","zh":"常常来玩，尼克，我会——我会撮合你们的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You know—lock you up accidentally in linen closets and push you out to sea in a boat, and all that sort of thing—”","zh":"比如说，把你们单独关进某个小房间，或者让你们坐船出海，诸如此类…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Good night,” called Miss Baker from the stairs. “I haven’t heard a word.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good night,” called Miss Baker from the stairs.","zh":"“晚安，”贝克小姐在楼梯上大声说，“我可什么都没听到。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I haven’t heard a word.”","zh":"“晚安，”贝克小姐在楼梯上大声说，“我可什么都没听到。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s a nice girl,” said Tom after a moment. “They oughtn’t to let her run around the country this way.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s a nice girl,” said Tom after a moment.","zh":"隔了片刻，汤姆说：“她是个好女孩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“They oughtn’t to let her run around the country this way.”","zh":"他们不应该让她全国到处跑的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who oughtn’t to?” inquired Daisy coldly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Who oughtn’t to?” inquired Daisy coldly.","zh":"“谁们？”黛熙冷冰冰地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Her family.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Her family.”","zh":"“她家里人啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Her family is one aunt about a thousand years old. Besides, Nick’s going to look after her, aren’t you, Nick? She’s going to spend lots of weekends out here this summer. I think the home influence will be very good for her.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Her family is one aunt about a thousand years old.","zh":"“她家里只有一个老糊涂的姑妈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, Nick’s going to look after her, aren’t you, Nick?","zh":"再说了，以后尼克会照顾她的，对吧，尼克？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She’s going to spend lots of weekends out here this summer.","zh":"今年夏天她常常到这里来过周末。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think the home influence will be very good for her.”","zh":"我觉得家庭的氛围对她非常有好处。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy and Tom looked at each other for a moment in silence.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy and Tom looked at each other for a moment in silence.","zh":"黛熙和汤姆默默无言地对视了片刻。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is she from New York?” I asked quickly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is she from New York?”","zh":"“她是纽约人吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I asked quickly.","zh":"我赶紧问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“From Louisville. Our white girlhood was passed together there. Our beautiful white—”","sentences":[{"en":"“From Louisville.","zh":"“是路易斯维尔的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Our white girlhood was passed together there.","zh":"我们在那里共同度过了纯真的少女年代。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Our beautiful white—”","zh":"我们那美丽而纯真的…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you give Nick a little heart to heart talk on the veranda?” demanded Tom suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you give Nick a little heart to heart talk on the veranda?” demanded Tom suddenly.","zh":"“刚才在门廊你是不是把心事都告诉尼克了？”汤姆突然逼问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did I?” She looked at me. “I can’t seem to remember, but I think we talked about the Nordic race. Yes, I’m sure we did. It sort of crept up on us and first thing you know—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Did I?”","zh":"“有吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked at me.","zh":"她望着我，“我不记得啦，我们好像在聊北欧民族。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I can’t seem to remember, but I think we talked about the Nordic race.","zh":"她望着我，“我不记得啦，我们好像在聊北欧民族。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Yes, I’m sure we did.","zh":"是的，我们聊的是这个。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It sort of crept up on us and first thing you know—”","zh":"我们不知道怎么就聊起来…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t believe everything you hear, Nick,” he advised me.","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t believe everything you hear, Nick,” he advised me.","zh":"“别相信你听到的每句话，尼克，”他正告我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I said lightly that I had heard nothing at all, and a few minutes later I got up to go home. They came to the door with me and stood side by side in a cheerful square of light. As I started my motor Daisy peremptorily called: “Wait!","sentences":[{"en":"I said lightly that I had heard nothing at all, and a few minutes later I got up to go home.","zh":"我轻松地说我什么也没听见，隔了几分钟，我站起来告辞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They came to the door with me and stood side by side in a cheerful square of light.","zh":"他们把我送到门口，并排站在一片明亮的灯光中。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As I started my motor Daisy peremptorily called: “Wait!","zh":"我启动引擎，这时黛熙发号施令似的大声说：“且慢！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I forgot to ask you something, and it’s important. We heard you were engaged to a girl out West.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I forgot to ask you something, and it’s important.","zh":"“有个问题忘了问你，是个很重要的问题。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We heard you were engaged to a girl out West.”","zh":"我们听说你在西部和某个姑娘定亲了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s right,” corroborated Tom kindly. “We heard that you were engaged.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s right,” corroborated Tom kindly.","zh":"“是啊，”汤姆友善地起哄说，“我们听说你订婚了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“We heard that you were engaged.”","zh":"“是啊，”汤姆友善地起哄说，“我们听说你订婚了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s a libel. I’m too poor.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s a libel.","zh":"“这是谣言。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m too poor.”","zh":"我哪有钱啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But we heard it,” insisted Daisy, surprising me by opening up again in a flower-like way. “We heard it from three people, so it must be true.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But we heard it,” insisted Daisy, surprising me by opening up again in a flower-like way.","zh":"“可是我们听说了，”黛熙坚定地说，让我奇怪的是，她现在又绽开花儿般的笑脸，“我们听三个人说的，所以肯定是真的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“We heard it from three people, so it must be true.”","zh":"“可是我们听说了，”黛熙坚定地说，让我奇怪的是，她现在又绽开花儿般的笑脸，“我们听三个人说的，所以肯定是真的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Of course I knew what they were referring to, but I wasn’t even vaguely engaged. The fact that gossip had published the banns was one of the reasons I had come East. You can’t stop going with an old friend on account of rumours, and on the other hand I had no intention of being rumoured into marriage.","sentences":[{"en":"Of course I knew what they were referring to, but I wasn’t even vaguely engaged.","zh":"我当然知道他们说的是哪回事，但我根本就没有订婚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The fact that gossip had published the banns was one of the reasons I had come East.","zh":"其实这谣传我已订婚的流言蜚语也是促使我到东部来的原因之一。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You can’t stop going with an old friend on account of rumours, and on the other hand I had no intention of being rumoured into marriage.","zh":"你不能因为不想听到谣言就跟老朋友断绝来往，可是我也不想因为谣言而去结婚。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Their interest rather touched me and made them less remotely rich—nevertheless, I was confused and a little disgusted as I drove away. It seemed to me that the thing for Daisy to do was to rush out of the house, child in arms—but apparently there were no such intentions in her head. As for Tom, the fact that he “had some woman in New York” was really less surprising than that he had been depressed by a book. Something was making him nibble at the edge of stale ideas as if his sturdy physical egotism no longer nourished his peremptory heart.","sentences":[{"en":"Their interest rather touched me and made them less remotely rich—nevertheless, I was confused and a little disgusted as I drove away.","zh":"他们的关心让我很是感动，让我觉得他们不像有些富人那样人情淡薄——尽管如此，开车离开途中，我还是很困惑，也有点厌恶。我认为黛熙应该做的是抱着孩子逃离这座别墅，但她显然没有这种念头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It seemed to me that the thing for Daisy to do was to rush out of the house, child in arms—but apparently there were no such intentions in her head.","zh":"他们的关心让我很是感动，让我觉得他们不像有些富人那样人情淡薄——尽管如此，开车离开途中，我还是很困惑，也有点厌恶。我认为黛熙应该做的是抱着孩子逃离这座别墅，但她显然没有这种念头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"As for Tom, the fact that he “had some woman in New York” was really less surprising than that he had been depressed by a book.","zh":"至于汤姆，我觉得他在纽约“有个相好”其实不足为奇，怪的是他竟然会因为读了某本书而意志消沉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something was making him nibble at the edge of stale ideas as if his sturdy physical egotism no longer nourished his peremptory heart.","zh":"不知道他怎么会去啃那种腐朽落后的书，大概是因为强壮的体魄再也滋养不了他那颗高傲的心吧。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Already it was deep summer on roadhouse roofs and in front of wayside garages, where new red petrol-pumps sat out in pools of light, and when I reached my estate at West Egg I ran the car under its shed and sat for a while on an abandoned grass roller in the yard. The wind had blown off, leaving a loud, bright night, with wings beating in the trees and a persistent organ sound as the full bellows of the earth blew the frogs full of life. The silhouette of a moving cat wavered across the moonlight, and, turning my head to watch it, I saw that I was not alone—fifty feet away a figure had emerged from the shadow of my neighbour’s mansion and was standing with his hands in his pockets regarding the silver pepper of the stars. Something in his leisurely movements and the secure position of his feet upon the lawn suggested that it was Mr. Gatsby himself, come out to determine what share was his of our local heavens.","sentences":[{"en":"Already it was deep summer on roadhouse roofs and in front of wayside garages, where new red petrol-pumps sat out in pools of light, and when I reached my estate at West Egg I ran the car under its shed and sat for a while on an abandoned grass roller in the yard.","zh":"沿途所见尽是夏日的热闹景象，各处酒馆和路边加油站门庭若市，许多崭新的红色加油机坐在电灯的光圈里。回到西卵的房子后，我把车开进停车棚，在院子里废弃的压草机上坐了片刻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The wind had blown off, leaving a loud, bright night, with wings beating in the trees and a persistent organ sound as the full bellows of the earth blew the frogs full of life.","zh":"风儿已经远走，留下热闹而明亮的夜晚，归巢的倦鸟扑打翅膀的响声，以及被万物欣荣的大地唤醒的青蛙持续不断地发出的鼓噪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The silhouette of a moving cat wavered across the moonlight, and, turning my head to watch it, I saw that I was not alone—fifty feet away a figure had emerged from the shadow of my neighbour’s mansion and was standing with his hands in his pockets regarding the silver pepper of the stars.","zh":"有只猫的身影在月光下蜿蜒移动，我转过头去望着它，这时才发现我并不是一个人——五十英尺开外，有个人从邻居那座公馆的暗影中走出来。他手插口袋，悄然伫立，凝望着漫天银色的星光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something in his leisurely movements and the secure position of his feet upon the lawn suggested that it was Mr. Gatsby himself, come out to determine what share was his of our local heavens.","zh":"他的动作不徐不疾，站在草坪上泰然自若，看来正是盖茨比先生本人，可能是出来确定我们本地的天空哪部分归他所有吧。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I decided to call to him. Miss Baker had mentioned him at dinner, and that would do for an introduction. But I didn’t call to him, for he gave a sudden intimation that he was content to be alone—he stretched out his arms toward the dark water in a curious way, and, far as I was from him, I could have sworn he was trembling. Involuntarily I glanced seaward—and distinguished nothing except a single green light, minute and far away, that might have been the end of a dock. When I looked once more for Gatsby he had vanished, and I was alone again in the unquiet darkness.","sentences":[{"en":"I decided to call to him.","zh":"我准备跟他打招呼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Miss Baker had mentioned him at dinner, and that would do for an introduction.","zh":"晚餐时贝克小姐提起过他，我可以借此和他搭讪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I didn’t call to him, for he gave a sudden intimation that he was content to be alone—he stretched out his arms toward the dark water in a curious way, and, far as I was from him, I could have sworn he was trembling.","zh":"但我并没有开口，因为他突然做出的举动表示他不愿受到打扰——他对着黑黝黝的海面，奇怪地伸出双手，而且尽管离他很远，我能看出来他正在发抖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Involuntarily I glanced seaward—and distinguished nothing except a single green light, minute and far away, that might have been the end of a dock.","zh":"我不由向海那边望去，但什么也没看到，只见远处有一点微茫的绿光，兴许是谁家码头上的电灯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When I looked once more for Gatsby he had vanished, and I was alone again in the unquiet darkness.","zh":"当我回头去看盖茨比时，他已经消失了，再次留下我一个人，在这不平静的黑暗中。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-2","n":2,"title":"Chapter II","titleZh":"第二章","paragraphs":[{"en":"About halfway between West Egg and New York the motor road hastily joins the railroad and runs beside it for a quarter of a mile, so as to shrink away from a certain desolate area of land. This is a valley of ashes—a fantastic farm where ashes grow like wheat into ridges and hills and grotesque gardens; where ashes take the forms of houses and chimneys and rising smoke and, finally, with a transcendent effort, of ash-grey men, who move dimly and already crumbling through the powdery air. Occasionally a line of grey cars crawls along an invisible track, gives out a ghastly creak, and comes to rest, and immediately the ash-grey men swarm up with leaden spades and stir up an impenetrable cloud, which screens their obscure operations from your sight.","sentences":[{"en":"About halfway between West Egg and New York the motor road hastily joins the railroad and runs beside it for a quarter of a mile, so as to shrink away from a certain desolate area of land.","zh":"差不多在西卵去往纽约的半途，汽车公路匆匆地和铁道相交，然后和它齐头并进了四分之一英里，以便避开一片荒地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This is a valley of ashes—a fantastic farm where ashes grow like wheat into ridges and hills and grotesque gardens; where ashes take the forms of houses and chimneys and rising smoke and, finally, with a transcendent effort, of ash-grey men, who move dimly and already crumbling through the powdery air.","zh":"这里其实是垃圾场——它像个神奇的庄园，垃圾如同小麦，长成高低不等的山丘和荒诞怪异的花园；有些垃圾则堆成房子的形状，附带着烟囱和袅袅升起的炊烟；此外还能看到许多满身灰尘的人，缓缓地移动着，他们的身影在灰蒙蒙的空气里隐约可见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Occasionally a line of grey cars crawls along an invisible track, gives out a ghastly creak, and comes to rest, and immediately the ash-grey men swarm up with leaden spades and stir up an impenetrable cloud, which screens their obscure operations from your sight.","zh":"偶尔会有几辆灰色的汽车列队沿着时隐时现的道路开进去，发出可怕的刹车声，然后停下来。那些满身灰尘的人立刻带着铁锹一拥而上，激起一阵乌黑的云雾，将他们本来就模糊不清的行动彻底地挡在你的视线之外。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But above the grey land and the spasms of bleak dust which drift endlessly over it, you perceive, after a moment, the eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg. The eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg are blue and gigantic—their retinas are one yard high. They look out of no face, but, instead, from a pair of enormous yellow spectacles which pass over a nonexistent nose. Evidently some wild wag of an oculist set them there to fatten his practice in the borough of Queens, and then sank down himself into eternal blindness, or forgot them and moved away. But his eyes, dimmed a little by many paintless days, under sun and rain, brood on over the solemn dumping ground.","sentences":[{"en":"But above the grey land and the spasms of bleak dust which drift endlessly over it, you perceive, after a moment, the eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg.","zh":"但是再过片刻，在这永远弥漫着阵阵尘雾的垃圾场之上，你会看到艾克堡医生的眼睛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg are blue and gigantic—their retinas are one yard high.","zh":"艾克堡医生的眼睛又蓝又大——光是瞳孔就有一码高。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They look out of no face, but, instead, from a pair of enormous yellow spectacles which pass over a nonexistent nose.","zh":"它们并不是从面孔上，而是从一副悬空虚架的巨大黄色眼镜后面向前看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Evidently some wild wag of an oculist set them there to fatten his practice in the borough of Queens, and then sank down himself into eternal blindness, or forgot them and moved away.","zh":"这显然是某个眼科医生异想天开竖起来的广告，以便为他在皇后区的诊所招徕顾客，后来他大概是永远地闭上了眼睛，或者忘记这回事搬到了别处。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But his eyes, dimmed a little by many paintless days, under sun and rain, brood on over the solemn dumping ground.","zh":"由于年久失修，而且日晒雨淋，那双眼睛已经有点暗淡，但依然忧郁地凝视着这片肃穆的垃圾场。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The valley of ashes is bounded on one side by a small foul river, and, when the drawbridge is up to let barges through, the passengers on waiting trains can stare at the dismal scene for as long as half an hour. There is always a halt there of at least a minute, and it was because of this that I first met Tom Buchanan’s mistress.","sentences":[{"en":"The valley of ashes is bounded on one side by a small foul river, and, when the drawbridge is up to let barges through, the passengers on waiting trains can stare at the dismal scene for as long as half an hour.","zh":"垃圾场边上有条污浊恶臭的小河，每逢吊桥升起，让货船通过，途经此地的列车得等上半个小时之久，乘客只能无可奈何地欣赏这片丑陋的景色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There is always a halt there of at least a minute, and it was because of this that I first met Tom Buchanan’s mistress.","zh":"平时火车开到这个站，至少会停车一分钟，也正是因为如此，我才得以初次见识汤姆·布坎南的情妇。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The fact that he had one was insisted upon wherever he was known. His acquaintances resented the fact that he turned up in popular cafés with her and, leaving her at a table, sauntered about, chatting with whomsoever he knew. Though I was curious to see her, I had no desire to meet her—but I did. I went up to New York with Tom on the train one afternoon, and when we stopped by the ash-heaps he jumped to his feet and, taking hold of my elbow, literally forced me from the car.","sentences":[{"en":"The fact that he had one was insisted upon wherever he was known.","zh":"他有情妇这回事，每个认识他的人都言之凿凿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His acquaintances resented the fact that he turned up in popular cafés with her and, leaving her at a table, sauntered about, chatting with whomsoever he knew.","zh":"他经常带着情妇出入热闹的餐厅，让她坐在餐桌边，而自己则神色如常地到处找熟人攀谈，这种做法让他的熟人很讨厌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Though I was curious to see her, I had no desire to meet her—but I did.","zh":"我挺好奇她究竟是个什么样的人，然而并没有见她的欲望——可是我却见到了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I went up to New York with Tom on the train one afternoon, and when we stopped by the ash-heaps he jumped to his feet and, taking hold of my elbow, literally forced me from the car.","zh":"那天下午，我和汤姆坐火车到纽约去，火车在垃圾场附近靠站时，他站起来，抓住我的上臂，不由分说地拖我下车。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’re getting off,” he insisted. “I want you to meet my girl.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We’re getting off,” he insisted.","zh":"“我们在这下车吧，”他坚定地说，“我带你去见我女朋友。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I want you to meet my girl.”","zh":"“我们在这下车吧，”他坚定地说，“我带你去见我女朋友。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I think he’d tanked up a good deal at luncheon, and his determination to have my company bordered on violence. The supercilious assumption was that on Sunday afternoon I had nothing better to do.","sentences":[{"en":"I think he’d tanked up a good deal at luncheon, and his determination to have my company bordered on violence.","zh":"我想他大概是午餐时喝多了酒，像这样强要我陪他去，简直是硬来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The supercilious assumption was that on Sunday afternoon I had nothing better to do.","zh":"瞧不起人如他，大概以为我在星期天下午不会有别的要紧事吧。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I followed him over a low whitewashed railroad fence, and we walked back a hundred yards along the road under Doctor Eckleburg’s persistent stare. The only building in sight was a small block of yellow brick sitting on the edge of the waste land, a sort of compact Main Street ministering to it, and contiguous to absolutely nothing. One of the three shops it contained was for rent and another was an all-night restaurant, approached by a trail of ashes; the third was a garage—Repairs. George B. Wilson. Cars bought and sold.—and I followed Tom inside.","sentences":[{"en":"I followed him over a low whitewashed railroad fence, and we walked back a hundred yards along the road under Doctor Eckleburg’s persistent stare.","zh":"我跟着他跨过铁道边一排低矮的、刷着白漆的篱笆，在艾克堡医生永恒的注视之下，沿着公路往回走了百来码。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The only building in sight was a small block of yellow brick sitting on the edge of the waste land, a sort of compact Main Street ministering to it, and contiguous to absolutely nothing.","zh":"视线里仅有的建筑物是一排黄砖砌成的矮小房子，坐落在荒地边缘，大概算是本地主要的商业街吧，四周则是空荡荡的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One of the three shops it contained was for rent and another was an all-night restaurant, approached by a trail of ashes; the third was a garage—Repairs.","zh":"这条街上有三家店铺，一家正在招租，一家是通宵营业的饭店，门前散落着许多垃圾。第三家则是汽修厂，招牌上写着“乔治·威尔逊汽修厂，兼营旧车买卖”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"George B. Wilson.","zh":"这条街上有三家店铺，一家正在招租，一家是通宵营业的饭店，门前散落着许多垃圾。第三家则是汽修厂，招牌上写着“乔治·威尔逊汽修厂，兼营旧车买卖”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Cars bought and sold.—and I followed Tom inside.","zh":"我随汤姆走了进去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The interior was unprosperous and bare; the only car visible was the dust-covered wreck of a Ford which crouched in a dim corner. It had occurred to me that this shadow of a garage must be a blind, and that sumptuous and romantic apartments were concealed overhead, when the proprietor himself appeared in the door of an office, wiping his hands on a piece of waste. He was a blond, spiritless man, anaemic, and faintly handsome. When he saw us a damp gleam of hope sprang into his light blue eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"The interior was unprosperous and bare; the only car visible was the dust-covered wreck of a Ford which crouched in a dim corner.","zh":"汽修厂里徒有四壁，一派萧条的景象，唯一能看到的是一辆破旧蒙尘的福特，蜷缩在阴暗的角落里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It had occurred to me that this shadow of a garage must be a blind, and that sumptuous and romantic apartments were concealed overhead, when the proprietor himself appeared in the door of an office, wiping his hands on a piece of waste.","zh":"我心里想，这昏暗的汽修厂肯定是为了遮人耳目，楼上也许是豪华而浪漫的藏娇金屋。就在这时，老板本人从账房走出来，边走边用破布擦手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was a blond, spiritless man, anaemic, and faintly handsome.","zh":"他满头金发，精神萎靡，脸无血色，稍微有点英俊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he saw us a damp gleam of hope sprang into his light blue eyes.","zh":"看到我们，他那双淡蓝色的眼睛闪过一道希望的光芒。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hello, Wilson, old man,” said Tom, slapping him jovially on the shoulder. “How’s business?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hello, Wilson, old man,” said Tom, slapping him jovially on the shoulder.","zh":"“你好啊，威尔逊老兄，”汤姆欢快地拍拍他的肩膀说，“生意怎么样？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“How’s business?”","zh":"“你好啊，威尔逊老兄，”汤姆欢快地拍拍他的肩膀说，“生意怎么样？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I can’t complain,” answered Wilson unconvincingly. “When are you going to sell me that car?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I can’t complain,” answered Wilson unconvincingly.","zh":"“马马虎虎吧，”威尔逊不太自信地说，“你什么时候把那辆车卖给我？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“When are you going to sell me that car?”","zh":"“马马虎虎吧，”威尔逊不太自信地说，“你什么时候把那辆车卖给我？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Next week; I’ve got my man working on it now.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Next week; I’ve got my man working on it now.”","zh":"“下星期，我已经派人去处理它了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Works pretty slow, don’t he?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Works pretty slow, don’t he?”","zh":"“那人手脚未免也太慢了，对吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, he doesn’t,” said Tom coldly. “And if you feel that way about it, maybe I’d better sell it somewhere else after all.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, he doesn’t,” said Tom coldly.","zh":"“不对，他不慢，”汤姆冷冷地说，“如果你嫌慢，那我把它卖给别人算了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And if you feel that way about it, maybe I’d better sell it somewhere else after all.”","zh":"“不对，他不慢，”汤姆冷冷地说，“如果你嫌慢，那我把它卖给别人算了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t mean that,” explained Wilson quickly. “I just meant—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t mean that,” explained Wilson quickly.","zh":"“我不是那个意思，”威尔逊赶紧解释说，“我只是…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I just meant—”","zh":"“我不是那个意思，”威尔逊赶紧解释说，“我只是…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His voice faded off and Tom glanced impatiently around the garage. Then I heard footsteps on a stairs, and in a moment the thickish figure of a woman blocked out the light from the office door. She was in the middle thirties, and faintly stout, but she carried her flesh sensuously as some women can. Her face, above a spotted dress of dark blue crêpe-de-chine, contained no facet or gleam of beauty, but there was an immediately perceptible vitality about her as if the nerves of her body were continually smouldering. She smiled slowly and, walking through her husband as if he were a ghost, shook hands with Tom, looking him flush in the eye. Then she wet her lips, and without turning around spoke to her husband in a soft, coarse voice:","sentences":[{"en":"His voice faded off and Tom glanced impatiently around the garage.","zh":"他的话音戛然而止，汤姆不耐烦地乱瞟着汽修厂的四处。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then I heard footsteps on a stairs, and in a moment the thickish figure of a woman blocked out the light from the office door.","zh":"这时我听到一阵脚踩楼梯的声音，片刻之后，有个粗壮的女人站在账房门口，挡住了透进来的光线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was in the middle thirties, and faintly stout, but she carried her flesh sensuously as some women can.","zh":"她三十来岁，有点发胖，但她像有些胖女人那样，仪表姿态看上去很舒服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her face, above a spotted dress of dark blue crêpe-de-chine, contained no facet or gleam of beauty, but there was an immediately perceptible vitality about her as if the nerves of her body were continually smouldering.","zh":"她穿着沾了油渍的深蓝色绉纱连衣裙，脸庞长得并不美，但是一眼就能看得出来她很有活力，就好像她体内的细胞不停地燃烧似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She smiled slowly and, walking through her husband as if he were a ghost, shook hands with Tom, looking him flush in the eye.","zh":"她微微笑起来，视若无睹地从她丈夫身边走过，上前握住汤姆的手，两眼放光地看着他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she wet her lips, and without turning around spoke to her husband in a soft, coarse voice:","zh":"然后她舔了舔嘴唇，头也不回，轻声但没好气地吩咐她丈夫：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Get some chairs, why don’t you, so somebody can sit down.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Get some chairs, why don’t you, so somebody can sit down.”","zh":"“你怎么不去搬两张椅子来呢，让客人坐下呀。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, sure,” agreed Wilson hurriedly, and went toward the little office, mingling immediately with the cement colour of the walls. A white ashen dust veiled his dark suit and his pale hair as it veiled everything in the vicinity—except his wife, who moved close to Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, sure,” agreed Wilson hurriedly, and went toward the little office, mingling immediately with the cement colour of the walls.","zh":"“哦，好的，”威尔逊匆忙答应，向那间狭小的账房走去，身影立刻跟水泥颜色的墙壁混成一片。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A white ashen dust veiled his dark suit and his pale hair as it veiled everything in the vicinity—except his wife, who moved close to Tom.","zh":"灰白的尘埃覆盖着他黑色的西装和淡黄的头发，也覆盖着车房里的一切——除了他妻子。她朝汤姆贴了过去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want to see you,” said Tom intently. “Get on the next train.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want to see you,” said Tom intently.","zh":"“我想见你，”汤姆热切地说，“去搭下班车。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Get on the next train.”","zh":"“我想见你，”汤姆热切地说，“去搭下班车。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right.”","zh":"“没问题。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll meet you by the newsstand on the lower level.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll meet you by the newsstand on the lower level.”","zh":"“我在车站地下一层的报刊亭等你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She nodded and moved away from him just as George Wilson emerged with two chairs from his office door.","sentences":[{"en":"She nodded and moved away from him just as George Wilson emerged with two chairs from his office door.","zh":"她点点头，从汤姆身边走开，这时威尔逊正好搬着两把椅子走出账房。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We waited for her down the road and out of sight. It was a few days before the Fourth of July, and a grey, scrawny Italian child was setting torpedoes in a row along the railroad track.","sentences":[{"en":"We waited for her down the road and out of sight.","zh":"我们在路边没有人看见的地方等她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a few days before the Fourth of July, and a grey, scrawny Italian child was setting torpedoes in a row along the railroad track.","zh":"再过几天就是七月四日了，有个脏兮兮的瘦小意大利男孩正在将炮仗沿着铁轨一字排开。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Terrible place, isn’t it,” said Tom, exchanging a frown with Doctor Eckleburg.","sentences":[{"en":"“Terrible place, isn’t it,” said Tom, exchanging a frown with Doctor Eckleburg.","zh":"“这地方很糟糕，对吧，”汤姆说，他朝艾克堡医生皱了皱眉。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Awful.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Awful.”","zh":"“糟透了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It does her good to get away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It does her good to get away.”","zh":"“出去透透气对她有好处。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Doesn’t her husband object?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Doesn’t her husband object?”","zh":"“她丈夫不反对吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wilson? He thinks she goes to see her sister in New York. He’s so dumb he doesn’t know he’s alive.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wilson?","zh":"“威尔逊啊？他以为她是去纽约探望她妹妹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He thinks she goes to see her sister in New York.","zh":"“威尔逊啊？他以为她是去纽约探望她妹妹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He’s so dumb he doesn’t know he’s alive.”","zh":"他很蠢的，连他自己是死是活都不知道。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"So Tom Buchanan and his girl and I went up together to New York—or not quite together, for Mrs. Wilson sat discreetly in another car. Tom deferred that much to the sensibilities of those East Eggers who might be on the train.","sentences":[{"en":"So Tom Buchanan and his girl and I went up together to New York—or not quite together, for Mrs. Wilson sat discreetly in another car.","zh":"于是汤姆·布坎南、他女朋友和我一起奔赴纽约——其实也不能说是一起，因为威尔逊太太很谨慎地坐到其他车厢去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom deferred that much to the sensibilities of those East Eggers who might be on the train.","zh":"汤姆之所以忍得住，主要是担心被同车的东卵居民撞见不好意思。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She had changed her dress to a brown figured muslin, which stretched tight over her rather wide hips as Tom helped her to the platform in New York. At the newsstand she bought a copy of Town Tattle and a moving-picture magazine, and in the station drugstore some cold cream and a small flask of perfume. Upstairs, in the solemn echoing drive she let four taxicabs drive away before she selected a new one, lavender-coloured with grey upholstery, and in this we slid out from the mass of the station into the glowing sunshine. But immediately she turned sharply from the window and, leaning forward, tapped on the front glass.","sentences":[{"en":"She had changed her dress to a brown figured muslin, which stretched tight over her rather wide hips as Tom helped her to the platform in New York.","zh":"她先前已换上了棕色的贴身棉裙，汤姆在纽约扶她下车时，她那宽大的臀部将裙子绷得紧紧的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the newsstand she bought a copy of Town Tattle and a moving-picture magazine, and in the station drugstore some cold cream and a small flask of perfume.","zh":"她在报刊亭买了一本《城市杂谈》和一本电影杂志，又到车站药店买了雪花膏和一小瓶香水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Upstairs, in the solemn echoing drive she let four taxicabs drive away before she selected a new one, lavender-coloured with grey upholstery, and in this we slid out from the mass of the station into the glowing sunshine.","zh":"上楼之后，我们走到阴暗而有回音的出租车上客点，她任由四辆空车驶过，才选中一辆新车，车身是薰衣草的紫色，坐垫是灰色的。我们乘着这辆车滑出巨大的车站，驶进耀眼的阳光里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But immediately she turned sharply from the window and, leaning forward, tapped on the front glass.","zh":"但她立刻从窗边扭过头，身体向前靠，敲了敲前面的玻璃。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want to get one of those dogs,” she said earnestly. “I want to get one for the apartment. They’re nice to have—a dog.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want to get one of those dogs,” she said earnestly.","zh":"“我要买只小狗，”她兴高采烈地说，“我要买只小狗养在公寓里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I want to get one for the apartment.","zh":"“我要买只小狗，”她兴高采烈地说，“我要买只小狗养在公寓里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They’re nice to have—a dog.”","zh":"那里养只狗多好呀。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We backed up to a grey old man who bore an absurd resemblance to John D. Rockefeller. In a basket swung from his neck cowered a dozen very recent puppies of an indeterminate breed.","sentences":[{"en":"We backed up to a grey old man who bore an absurd resemblance to John D. Rockefeller.","zh":"我们的车后退到一个白发老头身边，他长得很奇怪，居然特别像约翰·洛克菲勒，让人感觉很滑稽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In a basket swung from his neck cowered a dozen very recent puppies of an indeterminate breed.","zh":"挂在他胸前的篮子里拥挤着十来只刚出世的小狗，看不出来是什么品种。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What kind are they?” asked Mrs. Wilson eagerly, as he came to the taxi-window.","sentences":[{"en":"“What kind are they?” asked Mrs. Wilson eagerly, as he came to the taxi-window.","zh":"看到那老头走近车窗，威尔逊太太急切地问：“这些是什么品种啊？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All kinds. What kind do you want, lady?”","sentences":[{"en":"“All kinds.","zh":"“什么品种都有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What kind do you want, lady?”","zh":"这位太太，你想要哪一种呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’d like to get one of those police dogs; I don’t suppose you got that kind?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’d like to get one of those police dogs; I don’t suppose you got that kind?”","zh":"“我想要只警犬，你大概没有吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The man peered doubtfully into the basket, plunged in his hand and drew one up, wriggling, by the back of the neck.","sentences":[{"en":"The man peered doubtfully into the basket, plunged in his hand and drew one up, wriggling, by the back of the neck.","zh":"老头目光闪烁地朝篮子里看，把手插进去，抓住其中一只的后颈，将浑身扭动的小狗提出来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s no police dog,” said Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s no police dog,” said Tom.","zh":"“这又不是警犬，”汤姆说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, it’s not exactly a police dog,” said the man with disappointment in his voice. “It’s more of an Airedale.” He passed his hand over the brown washrag of a back. “Look at that coat. Some coat. That’s a dog that’ll never bother you with catching cold.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, it’s not exactly a police dog,” said the man with disappointment in his voice.","zh":"“是的，它确实不是警犬，”老头掩不住失望说，“它很可能是英国的河畔犬。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s more of an Airedale.”","zh":"“是的，它确实不是警犬，”老头掩不住失望说，“它很可能是英国的河畔犬。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He passed his hand over the brown washrag of a back.","zh":"他摸了摸那狗后背的棕色毛发。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Look at that coat.","zh":"“你看看它的皮毛，多茂密呀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Some coat.","zh":"“你看看它的皮毛，多茂密呀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"That’s a dog that’ll never bother you with catching cold.”","zh":"这狗永远不会因为着凉而给你带来麻烦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I think it’s cute,” said Mrs. Wilson enthusiastically. “How much is it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I think it’s cute,” said Mrs. Wilson enthusiastically.","zh":"“我觉得它很可爱耶，”威尔逊太太兴奋地说，“要多少钱？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“How much is it?”","zh":"“我觉得它很可爱耶，”威尔逊太太兴奋地说，“要多少钱？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That dog?” He looked at it admiringly. “That dog will cost you ten dollars.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That dog?”","zh":"“这只吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked at it admiringly.","zh":"老头爱慕地看着它，“这只要十块钱。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“That dog will cost you ten dollars.”","zh":"老头爱慕地看着它，“这只要十块钱。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The Airedale—undoubtedly there was an Airedale concerned in it somewhere, though its feet were startlingly white—changed hands and settled down into Mrs. Wilson’s lap, where she fondled the weatherproof coat with rapture.","sentences":[{"en":"The Airedale—undoubtedly there was an Airedale concerned in it somewhere, though its feet were startlingly white—changed hands and settled down into Mrs. Wilson’s lap, where she fondled the weatherproof coat with rapture.","zh":"那只河畔犬——它无疑有点像河畔犬，不过它的爪子白得吓人——成交了，乖乖地坐在威尔逊太太的膝盖上，她欣喜若狂地玩弄着那油光发亮的皮毛。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is it a boy or a girl?” she asked delicately.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is it a boy or a girl?” she asked delicately.","zh":"“它是女孩还是男孩呀？”她轻声细语地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That dog? That dog’s a boy.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That dog?","zh":"“这只吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That dog’s a boy.”","zh":"这只是男孩。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s a bitch,” said Tom decisively. “Here’s your money. Go and buy ten more dogs with it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s a bitch,” said Tom decisively.","zh":"“它是个婊子，”汤姆斩钉截铁地说，“这是你的钱。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Here’s your money.","zh":"“它是个婊子，”汤姆斩钉截铁地说，“这是你的钱。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Go and buy ten more dogs with it.”","zh":"拿这笔钱再去买十只吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We drove over to Fifth Avenue, warm and soft, almost pastoral, on the summer Sunday afternoon. I wouldn’t have been surprised to see a great flock of white sheep turn the corner.","sentences":[{"en":"We drove over to Fifth Avenue, warm and soft, almost pastoral, on the summer Sunday afternoon.","zh":"我们驶过第五大道，在这个夏日的星期天下午，这里的空气非常温暖和煦，甚至有点田园的气息。哪怕一拐弯看到许多白色的绵羊，我也不会吃惊。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I wouldn’t have been surprised to see a great flock of white sheep turn the corner.","zh":"我们驶过第五大道，在这个夏日的星期天下午，这里的空气非常温暖和煦，甚至有点田园的气息。哪怕一拐弯看到许多白色的绵羊，我也不会吃惊。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hold on,” I said, “I have to leave you here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hold on,” I said, “I have to leave you here.”","zh":"“停车，”我说，“我在这里下车啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No you don’t,” interposed Tom quickly. “Myrtle’ll be hurt if you don’t come up to the apartment. Won’t you, Myrtle?”","sentences":[{"en":"“No you don’t,” interposed Tom quickly.","zh":"“别下，”汤姆赶紧接口说，“你要是不到我们的公寓去，梅朵会伤心的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Myrtle’ll be hurt if you don’t come up to the apartment.","zh":"“别下，”汤姆赶紧接口说，“你要是不到我们的公寓去，梅朵会伤心的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Won’t you, Myrtle?”","zh":"对吧，梅朵？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come on,” she urged. “I’ll telephone my sister Catherine. She’s said to be very beautiful by people who ought to know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come on,” she urged.","zh":"“去嘛，”她敦促我说，“我会打电话叫我妹妹凯瑟琳来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll telephone my sister Catherine.","zh":"“去嘛，”她敦促我说，“我会打电话叫我妹妹凯瑟琳来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She’s said to be very beautiful by people who ought to know.”","zh":"大家都说她非常漂亮，你应该认识认识的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I’d like to, but—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I’d like to, but—”","zh":"“嗯，我是想认识，但…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We went on, cutting back again over the Park toward the West Hundreds. At 158th Street the cab stopped at one slice in a long white cake of apartment-houses. Throwing a regal homecoming glance around the neighbourhood, Mrs. Wilson gathered up her dog and her other purchases, and went haughtily in.","sentences":[{"en":"We went on, cutting back again over the Park toward the West Hundreds.","zh":"我们继续往前走，然后掉头穿过中央公园，直奔城西第一百多号街那边而去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At 158th Street the cab stopped at one slice in a long white cake of apartment-houses.","zh":"到了第一百五十八号街，出租车停在一座白蛋糕似的公寓楼前面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Throwing a regal homecoming glance around the neighbourhood, Mrs. Wilson gathered up her dog and her other purchases, and went haughtily in.","zh":"威尔逊太太像皇后回宫般环顾四周，收好她的小狗和其他买到的东西，趾高气扬地走了进去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m going to have the McKees come up,” she announced as we rose in the elevator. “And, of course, I got to call up my sister, too.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m going to have the McKees come up,” she announced as we rose in the elevator.","zh":"“我打算请麦基夫妇到楼上去，”我们坐电梯上楼时，她说，“当然，我也会打电话叫我妹妹来。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And, of course, I got to call up my sister, too.”","zh":"“我打算请麦基夫妇到楼上去，”我们坐电梯上楼时，她说，“当然，我也会打电话叫我妹妹来。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The apartment was on the top floor—a small living-room, a small dining-room, a small bedroom, and a bath. The living-room was crowded to the doors with a set of tapestried furniture entirely too large for it, so that to move about was to stumble continually over scenes of ladies swinging in the gardens of Versailles. The only picture was an over-enlarged photograph, apparently a hen sitting on a blurred rock. Looked at from a distance, however, the hen resolved itself into a bonnet, and the countenance of a stout old lady beamed down into the room. Several old copies of Town Tattle lay on the table together with a copy of Simon Called Peter, and some of the small scandal magazines of Broadway. Mrs. Wilson was first concerned with the dog. A reluctant elevator boy went for a box full of straw and some milk, to which he added on his own initiative a tin of large, hard dog biscuits—one of which decomposed apathetically in the saucer of milk all afternoon. Meanwhile Tom brought out a bottle of whisky from a locked bureau door.","sentences":[{"en":"The apartment was on the top floor—a small living-room, a small dining-room, a small bedroom, and a bath.","zh":"他们的公寓在顶层，有一个小小的客厅，一个小小的餐厅，一个小小的卧室，此外还有浴室。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The living-room was crowded to the doors with a set of tapestried furniture entirely too large for it, so that to move about was to stumble continually over scenes of ladies swinging in the gardens of Versailles.","zh":"客厅显得很拥挤，因为那套豪华家具实在是太大了，所以走动时很容易跌进几幅贵妇人在凡尔赛宫花园荡秋千的画面里。客厅里仅有的画是一幅尺寸过大的摄影作品，乍看是一只母鸡坐在一块模糊不清的石头上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The only picture was an over-enlarged photograph, apparently a hen sitting on a blurred rock.","zh":"客厅显得很拥挤，因为那套豪华家具实在是太大了，所以走动时很容易跌进几幅贵妇人在凡尔赛宫花园荡秋千的画面里。客厅里仅有的画是一幅尺寸过大的摄影作品，乍看是一只母鸡坐在一块模糊不清的石头上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Looked at from a distance, however, the hen resolved itself into a bonnet, and the countenance of a stout old lady beamed down into the room.","zh":"可是站到远处看，那只母鸡化为一顶女帽，而石头原来是个矮胖的老太太，笑眯眯地俯视着客厅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Several old copies of Town Tattle lay on the table together with a copy of Simon Called Peter, and some of the small scandal magazines of Broadway.","zh":"桌子上摆着几本往期的《城市杂谈》，一册《名叫彼得的西蒙》，以及几本有关百老汇的八卦杂志。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mrs. Wilson was first concerned with the dog.","zh":"威尔逊太太最先关心的是那只小狗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A reluctant elevator boy went for a box full of straw and some milk, to which he added on his own initiative a tin of large, hard dog biscuits—one of which decomposed apathetically in the saucer of milk all afternoon.","zh":"有个负责开电梯的男孩听从威尔逊太太的使唤，心不甘情不愿地去买了装满稻草的盒子和牛奶，并擅自买了一大盒狗粮——其中一块整个下午都在盛牛奶的碟子里散发出恶臭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Meanwhile Tom brought out a bottle of whisky from a locked bureau door.","zh":"在这期间，汤姆从上了锁的壁橱里取出一瓶威士忌。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I have been drunk just twice in my life, and the second time was that afternoon; so everything that happened has a dim, hazy cast over it, although until after eight o’clock the apartment was full of cheerful sun. Sitting on Tom’s lap Mrs. Wilson called up several people on the telephone; then there were no cigarettes, and I went out to buy some at the drugstore on the corner. When I came back they had both disappeared, so I sat down discreetly in the living-room and read a chapter of Simon Called Peter—either it was terrible stuff or the whisky distorted things, because it didn’t make any sense to me.","sentences":[{"en":"I have been drunk just twice in my life, and the second time was that afternoon; so everything that happened has a dim, hazy cast over it, although until after eight o’clock the apartment was full of cheerful sun.","zh":"有生以来我只喝醉过两次，第二次就在那个下午，所以后来发生的事情我都已忘却，倒是记得那天晚上八点过后，公寓里依然洒满了欢乐的阳光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sitting on Tom’s lap Mrs. Wilson called up several people on the telephone; then there were no cigarettes, and I went out to buy some at the drugstore on the corner.","zh":"威尔逊太太坐在汤姆的大腿上，打了电话给几个人，然后香烟抽光了，我下楼到路口的药店去买。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When I came back they had both disappeared, so I sat down discreetly in the living-room and read a chapter of Simon Called Peter—either it was terrible stuff or the whisky distorted things, because it didn’t make any sense to me.","zh":"回到公寓时，他们俩消失了，于是我很识趣地在客厅坐下来，翻阅那本《名叫彼得的西蒙》——要么是这本书太过糟糕，要么是威士忌太过厉害，因为我根本就看不进去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Just as Tom and Myrtle (after the first drink Mrs. Wilson and I called each other by our first names) reappeared, company commenced to arrive at the apartment door.","sentences":[{"en":"Just as Tom and Myrtle (after the first drink Mrs. Wilson and I called each other by our first names) reappeared, company commenced to arrive at the apartment door.","zh":"就在汤姆和梅朵（喝过第一杯酒之后，威尔逊太太和我就以名字相称了）重新出现时，客人陆续来到公寓门口。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The sister, Catherine, was a slender, worldly girl of about thirty, with a solid, sticky bob of red hair, and a complexion powdered milky white. Her eyebrows had been plucked and then drawn on again at a more rakish angle, but the efforts of nature toward the restoration of the old alignment gave a blurred air to her face. When she moved about there was an incessant clicking as innumerable pottery bracelets jingled up and down upon her arms. She came in with such a proprietary haste, and looked around so possessively at the furniture that I wondered if she lived here. But when I asked her she laughed immoderately, repeated my question aloud, and told me she lived with a girl friend at a hotel.","sentences":[{"en":"The sister, Catherine, was a slender, worldly girl of about thirty, with a solid, sticky bob of red hair, and a complexion powdered milky white.","zh":"梅朵的妹妹凯瑟琳身材苗条，模样俗气，大约三十岁，红色的短发又硬又油，脸上的粉搽得像牛奶那样白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her eyebrows had been plucked and then drawn on again at a more rakish angle, but the efforts of nature toward the restoration of the old alignment gave a blurred air to her face.","zh":"她的眉毛是拔掉之后重新画上的，画得更加弯了，可是她自身的眉毛又沿着原来的路线长出来，这让她的脸显得一塌糊涂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When she moved about there was an incessant clicking as innumerable pottery bracelets jingled up and down upon her arms.","zh":"她走路会不停地发出叮叮当当的声音，因为有无数条陶瓷手链在她手腕上晃动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She came in with such a proprietary haste, and looked around so possessively at the furniture that I wondered if she lived here.","zh":"她匆匆走进来，像是回到自己家，又审视了客厅里的家具，仿佛这些都是她的。我不由怀疑她就住在这里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when I asked her she laughed immoderately, repeated my question aloud, and told me she lived with a girl friend at a hotel.","zh":"可是当我问起来，她又放声高笑，大声地重复了我的问题，然后告诉我她和某个女性朋友住在酒店里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Mr. McKee was a pale, feminine man from the flat below. He had just shaved, for there was a white spot of lather on his cheekbone, and he was most respectful in his greeting to everyone in the room. He informed me that he was in the “artistic game,” and I gathered later that he was a photographer and had made the dim enlargement of Mrs. Wilson’s mother which hovered like an ectoplasm on the wall. His wife was shrill, languid, handsome, and horrible. She told me with pride that her husband had photographed her a hundred and twenty-seven times since they had been married.","sentences":[{"en":"Mr. McKee was a pale, feminine man from the flat below.","zh":"麦基先生面容苍白，有点娘娘腔，就住在楼下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had just shaved, for there was a white spot of lather on his cheekbone, and he was most respectful in his greeting to everyone in the room.","zh":"他显然刚刮了胡子，因为脸颊上有点白色的肥皂泡沫；他毕恭毕敬地和客厅里每个人打招呼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He informed me that he was in the “artistic game,” and I gathered later that he was a photographer and had made the dim enlargement of Mrs. Wilson’s mother which hovered like an ectoplasm on the wall.","zh":"他跟我说他是“吃艺术饭的”，后来我得知他是摄影师，挂在墙上那幅模糊的放大照片就是他的作品，那阴气沉沉的老太婆原来是威尔逊太太的母亲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His wife was shrill, languid, handsome, and horrible.","zh":"他的妻子声音很尖，无精打采，相貌倒挺美，但很讨厌。她自豪地告诉我，她的丈夫在婚后给她拍摄了一百二十七次照片。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She told me with pride that her husband had photographed her a hundred and twenty-seven times since they had been married.","zh":"他的妻子声音很尖，无精打采，相貌倒挺美，但很讨厌。她自豪地告诉我，她的丈夫在婚后给她拍摄了一百二十七次照片。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Mrs. Wilson had changed her costume some time before, and was now attired in an elaborate afternoon dress of cream-coloured chiffon, which gave out a continual rustle as she swept about the room. With the influence of the dress her personality had also undergone a change. The intense vitality that had been so remarkable in the garage was converted into impressive hauteur. Her laughter, her gestures, her assertions became more violently affected moment by moment, and as she expanded the room grew smaller around her, until she seemed to be revolving on a noisy, creaking pivot through the smoky air.","sentences":[{"en":"Mrs. Wilson had changed her costume some time before, and was now attired in an elaborate afternoon dress of cream-coloured chiffon, which gave out a continual rustle as she swept about the room.","zh":"威尔逊太太不知什么时候又换了衣服，现在穿着样式复杂的白色雪纺裙，上层社会的女性在午后正式会客时穿的那种，长长的裙脚拖在地上。每当她像扫帚般在客厅里走动时，裙子就会不停地沙沙响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With the influence of the dress her personality had also undergone a change.","zh":"在这套裙子的影响之下，她的气质也发生了变化。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The intense vitality that had been so remarkable in the garage was converted into impressive hauteur.","zh":"原先在汽修厂里她显得很有活力，现在活生生一副法国贵妇人的神气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her laughter, her gestures, her assertions became more violently affected moment by moment, and as she expanded the room grew smaller around her, until she seemed to be revolving on a noisy, creaking pivot through the smoky air.","zh":"她的笑声、姿势和言语渐渐地矫揉造作起来；随着她越来越膨胀，客厅显得越来越小，在醉眼朦胧的我看来，她似乎附在一根吱嘎作响的木轴上，吵闹地转个不停。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“My dear,” she told her sister in a high, mincing shout, “most of these fellas will cheat you every time. All they think of is money. I had a woman up here last week to look at my feet, and when she gave me the bill you’d of thought she had my appendicitis out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My dear,” she told her sister in a high, mincing shout, “most of these fellas will cheat you every time.","zh":"“亲爱的，”她声嘶力竭地告诉她妹妹，“现在很多人都是骗子。他们只惦记着钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All they think of is money.","zh":"上星期我请一个女人来看我的脚，你要是看到她开的账单，肯定会以为她是帮我做阑尾切割手术了。”“那女人叫什么名字？”麦基太太问。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I had a woman up here last week to look at my feet, and when she gave me the bill you’d of thought she had my appendicitis out.”","zh":"上星期我请一个女人来看我的脚，你要是看到她开的账单，肯定会以为她是帮我做阑尾切割手术了。”“那女人叫什么名字？”麦基太太问。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What was the name of the woman?” asked Mrs. McKee.","sentences":[{"en":"“What was the name of the woman?” asked Mrs. McKee.","zh":"“她姓艾伯哈特。她是上门替人家看脚的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Mrs. Eberhardt. She goes around looking at people’s feet in their own homes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Mrs. Eberhardt.","zh":"“我喜欢你的裙子，”麦基太太说，“我觉得它很漂亮。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She goes around looking at people’s feet in their own homes.”","zh":"“我喜欢你的裙子，”麦基太太说，“我觉得它很漂亮。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I like your dress,” remarked Mrs. McKee, “I think it’s adorable.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I like your dress,” remarked Mrs. McKee, “I think it’s adorable.”","zh":"威尔逊太太拒绝了这次恭维，她不以为然地扬了扬眉毛。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Mrs. Wilson rejected the compliment by raising her eyebrow in disdain.","sentences":[{"en":"Mrs. Wilson rejected the compliment by raising her eyebrow in disdain.","zh":"威尔逊太太拒绝了这次恭维，她不以为然地扬了扬眉毛。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s just a crazy old thing,” she said. “I just slip it on sometimes when I don’t care what I look like.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s just a crazy old thing,” she said.","zh":"“这只是一件过时货啦，”她说，“我是随便穿穿的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I just slip it on sometimes when I don’t care what I look like.”","zh":"“这只是一件过时货啦，”她说，“我是随便穿穿的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But it looks wonderful on you, if you know what I mean,” pursued Mrs. McKee. “If Chester could only get you in that pose I think he could make something of it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But it looks wonderful on you, if you know what I mean,” pursued Mrs. McKee.","zh":"“可是它在你身上显得很漂亮，你懂我的意思吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“If Chester could only get you in that pose I think he could make something of it.”","zh":"麦基太太固执己见地说，“如果你肯摆那个姿势，我想切斯特能够拍出一张好照片。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We all looked in silence at Mrs. Wilson, who removed a strand of hair from over her eyes and looked back at us with a brilliant smile. Mr. McKee regarded her intently with his head on one side, and then moved his hand back and forth slowly in front of his face.","sentences":[{"en":"We all looked in silence at Mrs. Wilson, who removed a strand of hair from over her eyes and looked back at us with a brilliant smile.","zh":"我们大家默默地看着威尔逊太太，她伸手掠开眼前一绺头发，笑逐颜开地看看我们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mr. McKee regarded her intently with his head on one side, and then moved his hand back and forth slowly in front of his face.","zh":"麦基先生歪过头，专注地盯着她，然后把手伸到脸前，慢慢地来回比划。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I should change the light,” he said after a moment. “I’d like to bring out the modelling of the features. And I’d try to get hold of all the back hair.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I should change the light,” he said after a moment.","zh":"“我应该改变光线，”他沉吟片刻之后说，“我想突出五官的轮廓。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’d like to bring out the modelling of the features.","zh":"“我应该改变光线，”他沉吟片刻之后说，“我想突出五官的轮廓。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And I’d try to get hold of all the back hair.”","zh":"我会尝试把背后的头发都拍进去。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I wouldn’t think of changing the light,” cried Mrs. McKee. “I think it’s—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wouldn’t think of changing the light,” cried Mrs. McKee.","zh":"“我觉得光线正正好，”麦基太太大声说，“我认为…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I think it’s—”","zh":"“我觉得光线正正好，”麦基太太大声说，“我认为…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her husband said “Sh!” and we all looked at the subject again, whereupon Tom Buchanan yawned audibly and got to his feet.","sentences":[{"en":"Her husband said “Sh!” and we all looked at the subject again, whereupon Tom Buchanan yawned audibly and got to his feet.","zh":"她的丈夫“嘘”了一声，于是我们又朝被拍摄者望去。这时布坎南大声地打了个哈欠，站起身来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You McKees have something to drink,” he said. “Get some more ice and mineral water, Myrtle, before everybody goes to sleep.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You McKees have something to drink,” he said.","zh":"“麦基，你们俩喝点什么？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Get some more ice and mineral water, Myrtle, before everybody goes to sleep.”","zh":"他说，“梅朵，再去弄点冰块和矿泉水来，否则大家都要睡着啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I told that boy about the ice.” Myrtle raised her eyebrows in despair at the shiftlessness of the lower orders. “These people! You have to keep after them all the time.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I told that boy about the ice.”","zh":"“我跟那开电梯的小子说过要冰块的，”梅朵扬起眉毛，对下等阶级的靠不住表示很绝望，“这些人啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Myrtle raised her eyebrows in despair at the shiftlessness of the lower orders.","zh":"“我跟那开电梯的小子说过要冰块的，”梅朵扬起眉毛，对下等阶级的靠不住表示很绝望，“这些人啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“These people!","zh":"“我跟那开电梯的小子说过要冰块的，”梅朵扬起眉毛，对下等阶级的靠不住表示很绝望，“这些人啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"You have to keep after them all the time.”","zh":"你不老盯着他们还不行。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She looked at me and laughed pointlessly. Then she flounced over to the dog, kissed it with ecstasy, and swept into the kitchen, implying that a dozen chefs awaited her orders there.","sentences":[{"en":"She looked at me and laughed pointlessly.","zh":"她看了看我，莫名其妙地笑起来，突然又蹦蹦跳跳地走到小狗跟前，兴高采烈地亲了亲它，然后摇摇摆摆地走进厨房，仿佛那里有十几个大厨正在等她发号施令。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she flounced over to the dog, kissed it with ecstasy, and swept into the kitchen, implying that a dozen chefs awaited her orders there.","zh":"她看了看我，莫名其妙地笑起来，突然又蹦蹦跳跳地走到小狗跟前，兴高采烈地亲了亲它，然后摇摇摆摆地走进厨房，仿佛那里有十几个大厨正在等她发号施令。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve done some nice things out on Long Island,” asserted Mr. McKee.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve done some nice things out on Long Island,” asserted Mr. McKee.","zh":"“我在长岛拍过几张好的，”麦基先生言之凿凿地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom looked at him blankly.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom looked at him blankly.","zh":"汤姆茫然地看着他。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Two of them we have framed downstairs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Two of them we have framed downstairs.”","zh":"“有两张就挂在楼下我家里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Two what?” demanded Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“Two what?” demanded Tom.","zh":"“两张什么？”汤姆问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Two studies. One of them I call Montauk Point—The Gulls, and the other I call Montauk Point—The Sea.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Two studies.","zh":"“两张作品啊。其中一张叫‘蒙塔克海角之群鸥’，另一张叫‘蒙塔克海角之汪洋’。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"One of them I call Montauk Point—The Gulls, and the other I call Montauk Point—The Sea.”","zh":"“两张作品啊。其中一张叫‘蒙塔克海角之群鸥’，另一张叫‘蒙塔克海角之汪洋’。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The sister Catherine sat down beside me on the couch.","sentences":[{"en":"The sister Catherine sat down beside me on the couch.","zh":"凯瑟琳挨着我坐到沙发上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do you live down on Long Island, too?” she inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you live down on Long Island, too?” she inquired.","zh":"“你也住在长岛吗？”她问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I live at West Egg.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I live at West Egg.”","zh":"“我住在西卵。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Really? I was down there at a party about a month ago. At a man named Gatsby’s. Do you know him?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Really?","zh":"“真的啊？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was down there at a party about a month ago.","zh":"个把月前，我去那边参加了宴会。在一个叫盖茨比的人家里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At a man named Gatsby’s.","zh":"个把月前，我去那边参加了宴会。在一个叫盖茨比的人家里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Do you know him?”","zh":"你认识他吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I live next door to him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I live next door to him.”","zh":"“我就住他隔壁。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, they say he’s a nephew or a cousin of Kaiser Wilhelm’s. That’s where all his money comes from.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, they say he’s a nephew or a cousin of Kaiser Wilhelm’s.","zh":"“嗯，大家说他是德国威廉皇帝的侄儿或者表弟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That’s where all his money comes from.”","zh":"所以他才那么有钱。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Really?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Really?”","zh":"所以他才那么有钱。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"She nodded.","zh":"“真的吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m scared of him. I’d hate to have him get anything on me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m scared of him.","zh":"她点点头。“我挺怕他的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’d hate to have him get anything on me.”","zh":"我可不想被他抓住什么把柄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"This absorbing information about my neighbour was interrupted by Mrs. McKee’s pointing suddenly at Catherine:","sentences":[{"en":"This absorbing information about my neighbour was interrupted by Mrs. McKee’s pointing suddenly at Catherine:","zh":"这份有关我邻居的新奇情报被麦基太太打断了，她突然指着凯瑟琳。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Chester, I think you could do something with her,” she broke out, but Mr. McKee only nodded in a bored way, and turned his attention to Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“Chester, I think you could do something with her,” she broke out, but Mr. McKee only nodded in a bored way, and turned his attention to Tom.","zh":"“切斯特，我觉得你可以替她拍些照片耶，”她脱口而出，但麦基先生只是爱答不理地点点头，然后扭头看着汤姆。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’d like to do more work on Long Island, if I could get the entry. All I ask is that they should give me a start.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’d like to do more work on Long Island, if I could get the entry.","zh":"“我希望在长岛揽更多的活，可惜不得其门而入。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All I ask is that they should give me a start.”","zh":"要是有人帮忙介绍就好啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Ask Myrtle,” said Tom, breaking into a short shout of laughter as Mrs. Wilson entered with a tray. “She’ll give you a letter of introduction, won’t you, Myrtle?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ask Myrtle,” said Tom, breaking into a short shout of laughter as Mrs. Wilson entered with a tray.","zh":"“找梅朵啊，”汤姆失笑说，这时威尔逊太太正端着托盘走进客厅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“She’ll give you a letter of introduction, won’t you, Myrtle?”","zh":"“她可以给你写封介绍信，对吧，梅朵？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do what?” she asked, startled.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do what?” she asked, startled.","zh":"“干什么呀？”她意外地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’ll give McKee a letter of introduction to your husband, so he can do some studies of him.” His lips moved silently for a moment as he invented, “ ‘George B. Wilson at the Gasoline Pump,’ or something like that.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’ll give McKee a letter of introduction to your husband, so he can do some studies of him.”","zh":"“请你写信介绍麦基给你丈夫啊，这样麦基就能给他拍照啦。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His lips moved silently for a moment as he invented, “ ‘George B. Wilson at the Gasoline Pump,’ or something like that.”","zh":"他略作沉吟，跟着说，“‘加油站之乔治·威尔逊’，诸如此类的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Catherine leaned close to me and whispered in my ear:","sentences":[{"en":"Catherine leaned close to me and whispered in my ear:","zh":"凯瑟琳凑到我耳边，轻轻地说：“他们俩都受不了自己的配偶。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Neither of them can stand the person they’re married to.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Neither of them can stand the person they’re married to.”","zh":"凯瑟琳凑到我耳边，轻轻地说：“他们俩都受不了自己的配偶。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Can’t they?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Can’t they?”","zh":"“不会吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Can’t stand them.” She looked at Myrtle and then at Tom. “What I say is, why go on living with them if they can’t stand them? If I was them I’d get a divorce and get married to each other right away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Can’t stand them.”","zh":"“真受不了他们，”她看看梅朵和汤姆说，“我是说，他们既然受不了，为什么还要勉强过下去呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"She looked at Myrtle and then at Tom.","zh":"“真受不了他们，”她看看梅朵和汤姆说，“我是说，他们既然受不了，为什么还要勉强过下去呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What I say is, why go on living with them if they can’t stand them?","zh":"“真受不了他们，”她看看梅朵和汤姆说，“我是说，他们既然受不了，为什么还要勉强过下去呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"If I was them I’d get a divorce and get married to each other right away.”","zh":"照我说，他们应该离婚，再彼此结为夫妻。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Doesn’t she like Wilson either?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Doesn’t she like Wilson either?”","zh":"“她也不喜欢威尔逊吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The answer to this was unexpected. It came from Myrtle, who had overheard the question, and it was violent and obscene.","sentences":[{"en":"The answer to this was unexpected.","zh":"这个问题的答案出乎我的意料。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It came from Myrtle, who had overheard the question, and it was violent and obscene.","zh":"答案来自梅朵，她偷听到了问题，满嘴脏话地给出了回答。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You see,” cried Catherine triumphantly. She lowered her voice again. “It’s really his wife that’s keeping them apart. She’s a Catholic, and they don’t believe in divorce.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You see,” cried Catherine triumphantly.","zh":"“你明白了吧，”凯瑟琳得意洋洋地大声说。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She lowered her voice again.","zh":"“你明白了吧，”凯瑟琳得意洋洋地大声说。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s really his wife that’s keeping them apart.","zh":"接着她又压低声音，“其实从中作梗的是他老婆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She’s a Catholic, and they don’t believe in divorce.”","zh":"他老婆是天主教徒，他们认为人是不能离婚的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy was not a Catholic, and I was a little shocked at the elaborateness of the lie.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy was not a Catholic, and I was a little shocked at the elaborateness of the lie.","zh":"黛熙并非天主教徒，这个精心设计的谎言让我有点震惊。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“When they do get married,” continued Catherine, “they’re going West to live for a while until it blows over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“When they do get married,” continued Catherine, “they’re going West to live for a while until it blows over.”","zh":"“等到他们真的结婚，”凯瑟琳继续说，“他们会先到西部避避风头，等事情平息了再回来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’d be more discreet to go to Europe.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’d be more discreet to go to Europe.”","zh":"“去欧洲更保险吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, do you like Europe?” she exclaimed surprisingly. “I just got back from Monte Carlo.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, do you like Europe?” she exclaimed surprisingly.","zh":"“你喜欢欧洲啊？”她惊奇地大叫，“我刚从蒙特卡罗回来呢。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I just got back from Monte Carlo.”","zh":"“你喜欢欧洲啊？”她惊奇地大叫，“我刚从蒙特卡罗回来呢。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Really.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Really.”","zh":"“真的啊？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Just last year. I went over there with another girl.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Just last year.","zh":"“就是去年的事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I went over there with another girl.”","zh":"我和另外一个女孩去的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Stay long?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Stay long?”","zh":"“待了很久吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, we just went to Monte Carlo and back. We went by way of Marseilles. We had over twelve hundred dollars when we started, but we got gyped out of it all in two days in the private rooms. We had an awful time getting back, I can tell you. God, how I hated that town!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, we just went to Monte Carlo and back.","zh":"“没有啦，我们只是去了蒙特卡罗就回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We went by way of Marseilles.","zh":"我们取道马赛去的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We had over twelve hundred dollars when we started, but we got gyped out of it all in two days in the private rooms.","zh":"出发时我们带了一千两百块钱，可是不到两天就在赌场的包房被骗光了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We had an awful time getting back, I can tell you.","zh":"实话对你说，我们回来路上吃了很多苦头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"God, how I hated that town!”","zh":"天哪，我特别讨厌那个城市！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The late afternoon sky bloomed in the window for a moment like the blue honey of the Mediterranean—then the shrill voice of Mrs. McKee called me back into the room.","sentences":[{"en":"The late afternoon sky bloomed in the window for a moment like the blue honey of the Mediterranean—then the shrill voice of Mrs. McKee called me back into the room.","zh":"我朝窗外望去，但见黄昏的天空蔚蓝得恍如地中海——然后麦基太太刺耳的声音又让我回到客厅。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I almost made a mistake, too,” she declared vigorously. “I almost married a little kike who’d been after me for years. I knew he was below me. Everybody kept saying to me: ‘Lucille, that man’s way below you!’ But if I hadn’t met Chester, he’d of got me sure.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I almost made a mistake, too,” she declared vigorously.","zh":"“我也曾差点犯了错误，”她兴奋地说，“当年我差点嫁给一个矮个子犹太佬，他追了我好多年。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I almost married a little kike who’d been after me for years.","zh":"“我也曾差点犯了错误，”她兴奋地说，“当年我差点嫁给一个矮个子犹太佬，他追了我好多年。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I knew he was below me.","zh":"我知道他配不上我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everybody kept saying to me: ‘Lucille, that man’s way below you!’","zh":"大家不停地对我说：‘露西尔，那人比你差远啦。’","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But if I hadn’t met Chester, he’d of got me sure.”","zh":"但假如我没遇到切斯特，那他肯定会得逞。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes, but listen,” said Myrtle Wilson, nodding her head up and down, “at least you didn’t marry him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, but listen,” said Myrtle Wilson, nodding her head up and down, “at least you didn’t marry him.”","zh":"“是的，但是你算走运的了，”梅朵·威尔逊不停地点着头说，“至少你没有嫁给他。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I know I didn’t.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know I didn’t.”","zh":"“我知道。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I married him,” said Myrtle, ambiguously. “And that’s the difference between your case and mine.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I married him,” said Myrtle, ambiguously.","zh":"“可是我嫁给他了，”梅朵含混地说，“这就是你和我的区别。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And that’s the difference between your case and mine.”","zh":"“可是我嫁给他了，”梅朵含混地说，“这就是你和我的区别。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why did you, Myrtle?” demanded Catherine. “Nobody forced you to.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why did you, Myrtle?” demanded Catherine.","zh":"“你干吗嫁给他呢，梅朵？”凯瑟琳责备地说，“没有人强迫你啊。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Nobody forced you to.”","zh":"“你干吗嫁给他呢，梅朵？”凯瑟琳责备地说，“没有人强迫你啊。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Myrtle considered.","sentences":[{"en":"Myrtle considered.","zh":"梅朵陷入了深思。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I married him because I thought he was a gentleman,” she said finally. “I thought he knew something about breeding, but he wasn’t fit to lick my shoe.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I married him because I thought he was a gentleman,” she said finally.","zh":"“我嫁给他，是因为我原本觉得他是个绅士，”隔了良久，她终于说，“我以为他是个很有教养的人，但他其实连替我舔鞋子都不配。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I thought he knew something about breeding, but he wasn’t fit to lick my shoe.”","zh":"“我嫁给他，是因为我原本觉得他是个绅士，”隔了良久，她终于说，“我以为他是个很有教养的人，但他其实连替我舔鞋子都不配。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You were crazy about him for a while,” said Catherine.","sentences":[{"en":"“You were crazy about him for a while,” said Catherine.","zh":"“你当时爱他爱得发疯，”凯瑟琳说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Crazy about him!” cried Myrtle incredulously. “Who said I was crazy about him? I never was any more crazy about him than I was about that man there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Crazy about him!” cried Myrtle incredulously.","zh":"“胡说八道！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Who said I was crazy about him?","zh":"梅朵仿佛遭了冤屈，大声辩白说，“谁说我爱他爱得发疯？说我爱过他，还不如说我爱过这个人呢。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I never was any more crazy about him than I was about that man there.”","zh":"梅朵仿佛遭了冤屈，大声辩白说，“谁说我爱他爱得发疯？说我爱过他，还不如说我爱过这个人呢。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She pointed suddenly at me, and everyone looked at me accusingly. I tried to show by my expression that I expected no affection.","sentences":[{"en":"She pointed suddenly at me, and everyone looked at me accusingly.","zh":"她突然朝我指来，于是每个人都用谴责的目光看着我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I tried to show by my expression that I expected no affection.","zh":"我只好努力装出一副从未指望有人爱我的表情。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The only crazy I was was when I married him. I knew right away I made a mistake. He borrowed somebody’s best suit to get married in, and never even told me about it, and the man came after it one day when he was out: ‘Oh, is that your suit?’ I said. ‘This is the first I ever heard about it.’ But I gave it to him and then I lay down and cried to beat the band all afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The only crazy I was was when I married him.","zh":"“我唯一发疯的事是嫁给他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I knew right away I made a mistake.","zh":"我立刻知道我犯错了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He borrowed somebody’s best suit to get married in, and never even told me about it, and the man came after it one day when he was out: ‘Oh, is that your suit?’","zh":"他结婚的礼服都是跟别人借的，而且从来没跟我提起。后来有一天他不在家，那个人来要回去。‘哦，这礼服是你的啊？’","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I said. ‘This is the first I ever heard about it.’","zh":"我说，‘我以前倒是没听说过嘛。’","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I gave it to him and then I lay down and cried to beat the band all afternoon.”","zh":"但我把礼服给他了，过后我躺在床上，伤心欲绝地哭了整整一个下午。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She really ought to get away from him,” resumed Catherine to me. “They’ve been living over that garage for eleven years. And Tom’s the first sweetie she ever had.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She really ought to get away from him,” resumed Catherine to me.","zh":"“她真的应该离开他，”凯瑟琳又跟我说起话来，“他们在汽修厂楼上生活了十一年。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“They’ve been living over that garage for eleven years.","zh":"“她真的应该离开他，”凯瑟琳又跟我说起话来，“他们在汽修厂楼上生活了十一年。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And Tom’s the first sweetie she ever had.”","zh":"汤姆是她第一个情人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The bottle of whisky—a second one—was now in constant demand by all present, excepting Catherine, who “felt just as good on nothing at all.” Tom rang for the janitor and sent him for some celebrated sandwiches, which were a complete supper in themselves. I wanted to get out and walk eastward toward the park through the soft twilight, but each time I tried to go I became entangled in some wild, strident argument which pulled me back, as if with ropes, into my chair. Yet high over the city our line of yellow windows must have contributed their share of human secrecy to the casual watcher in the darkening streets, and I saw him too, looking up and wondering. I was within and without, simultaneously enchanted and repelled by the inexhaustible variety of life.","sentences":[{"en":"The bottle of whisky—a second one—was now in constant demand by all present, excepting Catherine, who “felt just as good on nothing at all.”","zh":"大家纷纷拿起那瓶威士忌——第二瓶——往杯子里倒，只有凯瑟琳除外，她“觉得不喝酒也很高兴”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom rang for the janitor and sent him for some celebrated sandwiches, which were a complete supper in themselves.","zh":"汤姆按铃把门房喊来，派他去买些驰名的三明治回来当晚饭吃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wanted to get out and walk eastward toward the park through the soft twilight, but each time I tried to go I became entangled in some wild, strident argument which pulled me back, as if with ropes, into my chair.","zh":"我很想出去，在柔和的暮色中朝东向中央公园走去；可是每当想要告辞，我就会被七嘴八舌的挽留缠住，这片刺耳的声音像绳子般把我拉回座位。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet high over the city our line of yellow windows must have contributed their share of human secrecy to the casual watcher in the darkening streets, and I saw him too, looking up and wondering.","zh":"然而我们这排位于城市高空的黄色窗户，在昏暗街道的偶然过客看来，不知道隐藏着多少人生的秘密；我也看见他了，他抬头仰望，若有所思。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was within and without, simultaneously enchanted and repelled by the inexhaustible variety of life.","zh":"我既在里面又在外面，对这变幻无常的人生，我同时感到心醉神迷和恶心不已。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Myrtle pulled her chair close to mine, and suddenly her warm breath poured over me the story of her first meeting with Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"Myrtle pulled her chair close to mine, and suddenly her warm breath poured over me the story of her first meeting with Tom.","zh":"梅朵把她的椅子拉到我跟前，突然间她暖烘烘的鼻息扑面而来，对我说起来她和汤姆初次相遇的故事。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was on the two little seats facing each other that are always the last ones left on the train. I was going up to New York to see my sister and spend the night. He had on a dress suit and patent leather shoes, and I couldn’t keep my eyes off him, but every time he looked at me I had to pretend to be looking at the advertisement over his head. When we came into the station he was next to me, and his white shirtfront pressed against my arm, and so I told him I’d have to call a policeman, but he knew I lied. I was so excited that when I got into a taxi with him I didn’t hardly know I wasn’t getting into a subway train. All I kept thinking about, over and over, was ‘You can’t live forever; you can’t live forever.’ ”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was on the two little seats facing each other that are always the last ones left on the train.","zh":"“火车上有两个面对面的小位子，总是没人愿意坐，我们就是在那里相遇的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was going up to New York to see my sister and spend the night.","zh":"那天我来纽约探望我妹妹，准备在这里过夜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had on a dress suit and patent leather shoes, and I couldn’t keep my eyes off him, but every time he looked at me I had to pretend to be looking at the advertisement over his head.","zh":"他西装革履的，我忍不住老看着他，但每次他看我时，我就假装欣赏他头顶上方的广告。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When we came into the station he was next to me, and his white shirtfront pressed against my arm, and so I told him I’d have to call a policeman, but he knew I lied.","zh":"下车时他紧挨着我走，穿着雪白衬衣的前胸贴着我的手臂，所以我说我要喊警察来，但他知道我是在说谎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was so excited that when I got into a taxi with him I didn’t hardly know I wasn’t getting into a subway train.","zh":"我神魂颠倒地跟他上了出租车，甚至不知道我坐的并不是地铁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All I kept thinking about, over and over, was ‘You can’t live forever; you can’t live forever.’ ”","zh":"我心里反反复复、颠来倒去地想：‘人生苦短，人生苦短。’”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She turned to Mrs. McKee and the room rang full of her artificial laughter.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned to Mrs. McKee and the room rang full of her artificial laughter.","zh":"她扭头看着麦基太太，客厅里响起了她虚伪的笑声。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“My dear,” she cried, “I’m going to give you this dress as soon as I’m through with it. I’ve got to get another one tomorrow. I’m going to make a list of all the things I’ve got to get. A massage and a wave, and a collar for the dog, and one of those cute little ashtrays where you touch a spring, and a wreath with a black silk bow for mother’s grave that’ll last all summer. I got to write down a list so I won’t forget all the things I got to do.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My dear,” she cried, “I’m going to give you this dress as soon as I’m through with it.","zh":"“亲爱的，”她大声说，“这条裙子我等会就脱下来送给你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve got to get another one tomorrow.","zh":"我打算明天再去买一条。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m going to make a list of all the things I’ve got to get.","zh":"我准备把要做的事都记下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A massage and a wave, and a collar for the dog, and one of those cute little ashtrays where you touch a spring, and a wreath with a black silk bow for mother’s grave that’ll last all summer.","zh":"要按摩，做头发，给小狗买个颈圈，买个那种带弹簧的、小巧玲珑的烟灰缸，还要给我妈妈的坟墓买个有黑丝带的假花圈，可以摆整个夏天的那种。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I got to write down a list so I won’t forget all the things I got to do.”","zh":"我得把这些事统统记下来，免得全都忘了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was nine o’clock—almost immediately afterward I looked at my watch and found it was ten. Mr. McKee was asleep on a chair with his fists clenched in his lap, like a photograph of a man of action. Taking out my handkerchief I wiped from his cheek the spot of dried lather that had worried me all the afternoon.","sentences":[{"en":"It was nine o’clock—almost immediately afterward I looked at my watch and found it was ten.","zh":"这时已经九点了——过了片刻我再看表，转眼间已是十点。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mr. McKee was asleep on a chair with his fists clenched in his lap, like a photograph of a man of action.","zh":"麦基先生坐在椅子上打盹，双手握拳放在膝盖上，活像一幅黑社会打手的照片。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Taking out my handkerchief I wiped from his cheek the spot of dried lather that had worried me all the afternoon.","zh":"我取出手帕，擦掉他脸上那点让我难受了整个下午的、已经干掉的肥皂泡。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The little dog was sitting on the table looking with blind eyes through the smoke, and from time to time groaning faintly. People disappeared, reappeared, made plans to go somewhere, and then lost each other, searched for each other, found each other a few feet away. Some time toward midnight Tom Buchanan and Mrs. Wilson stood face to face discussing, in impassioned voices, whether Mrs. Wilson had any right to mention Daisy’s name.","sentences":[{"en":"The little dog was sitting on the table looking with blind eyes through the smoke, and from time to time groaning faintly.","zh":"小狗坐在餐桌上，在烟雾迷蒙的空气中茫然四顾，时不时发出微弱的吠声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People disappeared, reappeared, made plans to go somewhere, and then lost each other, searched for each other, found each other a few feet away.","zh":"大家消失了又出现，合计着要去哪里，然后又找不到对方，于是到处找，却发现对方原来近在眼前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some time toward midnight Tom Buchanan and Mrs. Wilson stood face to face discussing, in impassioned voices, whether Mrs. Wilson had any right to mention Daisy’s name.","zh":"快到午夜时分，汤姆·布坎南和威尔逊太太面对面地站着，激烈地争吵威尔逊太太是否有权利喊黛熙的名字。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Daisy! Daisy! Daisy!” shouted Mrs. Wilson. “I’ll say it whenever I want to! Daisy! Dai—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Daisy!","zh":"“黛熙！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy!","zh":"黛熙！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy!” shouted Mrs. Wilson.","zh":"黛熙！”威尔逊太太歇斯底里地大喊，“我想喊就喊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll say it whenever I want to!","zh":"黛熙！”威尔逊太太歇斯底里地大喊，“我想喊就喊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Daisy!","zh":"黛熙！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Dai—”","zh":"黛…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Making a short deft movement, Tom Buchanan broke her nose with his open hand.","sentences":[{"en":"Making a short deft movement, Tom Buchanan broke her nose with his open hand.","zh":"汤姆·布坎南非常迅捷地甩了她一个耳光，打得她鼻血直流。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Then there were bloody towels upon the bathroom floor, and women’s voices scolding, and high over the confusion a long broken wail of pain. Mr. McKee awoke from his doze and started in a daze toward the door. When he had gone halfway he turned around and stared at the scene—his wife and Catherine scolding and consoling as they stumbled here and there among the crowded furniture with articles of aid, and the despairing figure on the couch, bleeding fluently, and trying to spread a copy of Town Tattle over the tapestry scenes of Versailles. Then Mr. McKee turned and continued on out the door. Taking my hat from the chandelier, I followed.","sentences":[{"en":"Then there were bloody towels upon the bathroom floor, and women’s voices scolding, and high over the confusion a long broken wail of pain.","zh":"然后许多血红的毛巾出现在浴室的地板上，阵阵女人的指责声在房间里回荡，而盖过这片混乱的，是一长串时断时续的、痛苦的哀嚎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mr. McKee awoke from his doze and started in a daze toward the door.","zh":"麦基先生被惊醒了，开始迷迷糊糊地向门口走去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he had gone halfway he turned around and stared at the scene—his wife and Catherine scolding and consoling as they stumbled here and there among the crowded furniture with articles of aid, and the despairing figure on the couch, bleeding fluently, and trying to spread a copy of Town Tattle over the tapestry scenes of Versailles.","zh":"走到半路，他转过身来，望着眼前的景象：他的妻子和凯瑟琳又是痛骂又是安慰，跌跌撞撞地在拥挤的家具中来回寻找药品，有个伤心欲绝的人躺在沙发上，血流如注，却还试图铺开一份《城市杂谈》，遮住沙发套上的凡尔赛风景画。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Mr. McKee turned and continued on out the door.","zh":"然后麦基先生转头继续向门外走去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Taking my hat from the chandelier, I followed.","zh":"我从衣架上拿起帽子，跟在他后面。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come to lunch some day,” he suggested, as we groaned down in the elevator.","sentences":[{"en":"“Come to lunch some day,” he suggested, as we groaned down in the elevator.","zh":"“改天一起吃午饭吧，”电梯吱吱嘎嘎地往下降时，他对我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where?”","zh":"“到哪吃？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Anywhere.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Anywhere.”","zh":"“到哪吃？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Keep your hands off the lever,” snapped the elevator boy.","sentences":[{"en":"“Keep your hands off the lever,” snapped the elevator boy.","zh":"“哪都可以。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I beg your pardon,” said Mr. McKee with dignity, “I didn’t know I was touching it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I beg your pardon,” said Mr. McKee with dignity, “I didn’t know I was touching it.”","zh":"“手别碰升降杆，”那管电梯的男孩不客气地说。“你别乱说，”麦基先生神气十足地说，“我哪里碰到了？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right,” I agreed, “I’ll be glad to.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right,” I agreed, “I’ll be glad to.”","zh":"“手别碰升降杆，”那管电梯的男孩不客气地说。“你别乱说，”麦基先生神气十足地说，“我哪里碰到了？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"… I was standing beside his bed and he was sitting up between the sheets, clad in his underwear, with a great portfolio in his hands.","sentences":[{"en":"…","zh":"“好啊，”我说，“我很愿意的。”我站在他的床边，而他坐在被窝里，穿着内衣，手里捧着一本大相册。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I was standing beside his bed and he was sitting up between the sheets, clad in his underwear, with a great portfolio in his hands.","zh":"“好啊，”我说，“我很愿意的。”我站在他的床边，而他坐在被窝里，穿着内衣，手里捧着一本大相册。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Beauty and the Beast… Loneliness… Old Grocery Horse… Brook’n Bridge…”","sentences":[{"en":"“Beauty and the Beast…","zh":"“美女与野兽…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Loneliness…","zh":"寂寞…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Old Grocery Horse…","zh":"拉货的老马…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Brook’n Bridge…”","zh":"布鲁克林大桥…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Then I was lying half asleep in the cold lower level of the Pennsylvania Station, staring at the morning Tribune, and waiting for the four o’clock train.","sentences":[{"en":"Then I was lying half asleep in the cold lower level of the Pennsylvania Station, staring at the morning Tribune, and waiting for the four o’clock train.","zh":"然后我半睡半醒地躺在宾夕法尼亚火车站寒冷的地下候车室里，直盯着早晨刚出版的《纽约论坛报》出神，呆呆地等待那班四点的火车。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-3","n":3,"title":"Chapter III","titleZh":"第三章","paragraphs":[{"en":"There was music from my neighbour’s house through the summer nights. In his blue gardens men and girls came and went like moths among the whisperings and the champagne and the stars. At high tide in the afternoon I watched his guests diving from the tower of his raft, or taking the sun on the hot sand of his beach while his two motorboats slit the waters of the Sound, drawing aquaplanes over cataracts of foam. On weekends his Rolls-Royce became an omnibus, bearing parties to and from the city between nine in the morning and long past midnight, while his station wagon scampered like a brisk yellow bug to meet all trains. And on Mondays eight servants, including an extra gardener, toiled all day with mops and scrubbing-brushes and hammers and garden-shears, repairing the ravages of the night before.","sentences":[{"en":"There was music from my neighbour’s house through the summer nights.","zh":"那年夏天，我邻居的房子常常在夜里传来音乐声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In his blue gardens men and girls came and went like moths among the whisperings and the champagne and the stars.","zh":"那蓝色的花园里，许多男男女女飞蛾似的在呢喃、香槟和星辰之间走来走去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At high tide in the afternoon I watched his guests diving from the tower of his raft, or taking the sun on the hot sand of his beach while his two motorboats slit the waters of the Sound, drawing aquaplanes over cataracts of foam.","zh":"午后涨潮时分，我看见那些客人有的纷纷从水上的木架跳进水里，有的在炙热的沙滩上晒太阳，两艘汽艇拖着滑水板在港湾里逡巡，激起两道白浪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On weekends his Rolls-Royce became an omnibus, bearing parties to and from the city between nine in the morning and long past midnight, while his station wagon scampered like a brisk yellow bug to meet all trains.","zh":"每逢周末，他的劳斯莱斯变成穿梭巴士，从早晨九点到三更半夜，不停地往来市区接送客人，而他的旅行轿车则像敏捷的黄色甲虫般，蹦蹦跳跳地去接所有到站的火车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And on Mondays eight servants, including an extra gardener, toiled all day with mops and scrubbing-brushes and hammers and garden-shears, repairing the ravages of the night before.","zh":"到了星期一，八个佣人，包括一个临时请来帮忙的园丁，会用抹布、板刷、铁锤和园艺剪来收拾前一晚的残局。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Every Friday five crates of oranges and lemons arrived from a fruiterer in New York—every Monday these same oranges and lemons left his back door in a pyramid of pulpless halves. There was a machine in the kitchen which could extract the juice of two hundred oranges in half an hour if a little button was pressed two hundred times by a butler’s thumb.","sentences":[{"en":"Every Friday five crates of oranges and lemons arrived from a fruiterer in New York—every Monday these same oranges and lemons left his back door in a pyramid of pulpless halves.","zh":"每到星期五，纽约某家水果店会送来五筐橙子和柠檬；这些柠檬会被切成两半，取出果肉，剩下的果皮在每个星期一早上成堆地从他家后门离开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a machine in the kitchen which could extract the juice of two hundred oranges in half an hour if a little button was pressed two hundred times by a butler’s thumb.","zh":"盖茨比家厨房有台机器，管家只要用拇指把一个小小的按钮揿两百下，就能在半个小时内榨出两百杯果汁。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At least once a fortnight a corps of caterers came down with several hundred feet of canvas and enough coloured lights to make a Christmas tree of Gatsby’s enormous garden. On buffet tables, garnished with glistening hors-d’oeuvre, spiced baked hams crowded against salads of harlequin designs and pastry pigs and turkeys bewitched to a dark gold. In the main hall a bar with a real brass rail was set up, and stocked with gins and liquors and with cordials so long forgotten that most of his female guests were too young to know one from another.","sentences":[{"en":"At least once a fortnight a corps of caterers came down with several hundred feet of canvas and enough coloured lights to make a Christmas tree of Gatsby’s enormous garden.","zh":"每两周至少一次，会有大批包办宴席的人从城里赶过来；他们带着几百英尺的帆布和足够多的彩色灯泡，把盖茨比家巨大的花园打扮得像圣诞树那样灯火辉煌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On buffet tables, garnished with glistening hors-d’oeuvre, spiced baked hams crowded against salads of harlequin designs and pastry pigs and turkeys bewitched to a dark gold.","zh":"花园里有许多自助餐桌，摆满各种餐前小菜，五香火腿紧挨着奇形怪状的色拉，更有金黄色的烤乳猪和烤火鸡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the main hall a bar with a real brass rail was set up, and stocked with gins and liquors and with cordials so long forgotten that most of his female guests were too young to know one from another.","zh":"大厅里搭起了真正的吧台，有架脚的铜杆那种。吧台备有各种金酒和烈酒，还有许多种早已绝迹的果酒，而来的女客大多数太过年轻，都分不清哪种是哪种。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"By seven o’clock the orchestra has arrived, no thin five-piece affair, but a whole pitful of oboes and trombones and saxophones and viols and cornets and piccolos, and low and high drums. The last swimmers have come in from the beach now and are dressing upstairs; the cars from New York are parked five deep in the drive, and already the halls and salons and verandas are gaudy with primary colours, and hair bobbed in strange new ways, and shawls beyond the dreams of Castile. The bar is in full swing, and floating rounds of cocktails permeate the garden outside, until the air is alive with chatter and laughter, and casual innuendo and introductions forgotten on the spot, and enthusiastic meetings between women who never knew each other’s names.","sentences":[{"en":"By seven o’clock the orchestra has arrived, no thin five-piece affair, but a whole pitful of oboes and trombones and saxophones and viols and cornets and piccolos, and low and high drums.","zh":"到了晚上七点，管弦乐团已经抵达，不是那种五人小乐队，而是正式的乐团，双簧管、长号、萨克斯管、小提琴、短号、短笛、低音鼓和高音鼓，样样齐备。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The last swimmers have come in from the beach now and are dressing upstairs; the cars from New York are parked five deep in the drive, and already the halls and salons and verandas are gaudy with primary colours, and hair bobbed in strange new ways, and shawls beyond the dreams of Castile.","zh":"在海里游泳的宾客都已从沙滩进来，正在楼上换衣服；纽约来的轿车停了整整五排，而各处走廊、客厅和阳台站满了明艳的女宾，她们穿着五颜六色的衣服，顶着稀奇古怪的发型，披着卡斯蒂利亚人做梦也想不到的纱巾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The bar is in full swing, and floating rounds of cocktails permeate the garden outside, until the air is alive with chatter and laughter, and casual innuendo and introductions forgotten on the spot, and enthusiastic meetings between women who never knew each other’s names.","zh":"吧台忙个不停，诸多盛放着鸡尾酒的托盘飞也似的飘到外面的花园。花园里充满了笑语和欢声、毫不经意的寒暄和转身即忘的介绍，还有彼此不知姓名的女人之间热烈的攀谈。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The lights grow brighter as the earth lurches away from the sun, and now the orchestra is playing yellow cocktail music, and the opera of voices pitches a key higher. Laughter is easier minute by minute, spilled with prodigality, tipped out at a cheerful word. The groups change more swiftly, swell with new arrivals, dissolve and form in the same breath; already there are wanderers, confident girls who weave here and there among the stouter and more stable, become for a sharp, joyous moment the centre of a group, and then, excited with triumph, glide on through the sea-change of faces and voices and colour under the constantly changing light.","sentences":[{"en":"The lights grow brighter as the earth lurches away from the sun, and now the orchestra is playing yellow cocktail music, and the opera of voices pitches a key higher.","zh":"大地蹒跚地远离太阳，于是电灯变得更加明亮，现在管弦乐团演奏着黄色的鸡尾酒曲目，众声交汇的歌剧提高了一个音调。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Laughter is easier minute by minute, spilled with prodigality, tipped out at a cheerful word.","zh":"随着时间的流逝，笑声越来越容易响起，大量地流溢着，一句欢乐的话就能让它倾泻而出。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The groups change more swiftly, swell with new arrivals, dissolve and form in the same breath; already there are wanderers, confident girls who weave here and there among the stouter and more stable, become for a sharp, joyous moment the centre of a group, and then, excited with triumph, glide on through the sea-change of faces and voices and colour under the constantly changing light.","zh":"各组人群的变化也更快了，忽而由于有新的人加入而膨胀，忽而又散开并随即重新组合。有些自信的女孩左右逢源地在几堆较为固定的人群中穿来插去，在不停变幻的灯光下，她们忽而成为某组谈笑风生的人群的中心，忽而又意气风发地移步到激烈变化的面孔、声音和颜色之间。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Suddenly one of these gypsies, in trembling opal, seizes a cocktail out of the air, dumps it down for courage and, moving her hands like Frisco, dances out alone on the canvas platform. A momentary hush; the orchestra leader varies his rhythm obligingly for her, and there is a burst of chatter as the erroneous news goes around that she is Gilda Gray’s understudy from the Follies. The party has begun.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly one of these gypsies, in trembling opal, seizes a cocktail out of the air, dumps it down for courage and, moving her hands like Frisco, dances out alone on the canvas platform.","zh":"忽然间，这些交际花中有个珠光宝气的少女，不知道从哪里抓过一杯鸡尾酒，一口喝下去壮胆，双手像弗里斯科那样乱摆，独自在帆布铺就的舞池里起舞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A momentary hush; the orchestra leader varies his rhythm obligingly for her, and there is a burst of chatter as the erroneous news goes around that she is Gilda Gray’s understudy from the Follies.","zh":"花园里霎时安静下来，乐团指挥殷勤地为她改变了节奏，众人纷纷交头接耳地传递着谣言，把她当成吉尔达·格雷在《愚人列传》中的替角。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The party has begun.","zh":"宴会开始了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I believe that on the first night I went to Gatsby’s house I was one of the few guests who had actually been invited. People were not invited—they went there. They got into automobiles which bore them out to Long Island, and somehow they ended up at Gatsby’s door. Once there they were introduced by somebody who knew Gatsby, and after that they conducted themselves according to the rules of behaviour associated with an amusement park. Sometimes they came and went without having met Gatsby at all, came for the party with a simplicity of heart that was its own ticket of admission.","sentences":[{"en":"I believe that on the first night I went to Gatsby’s house I was one of the few guests who had actually been invited.","zh":"那是我第一次去盖茨比家。我相信那天晚上真正受邀请的人不多，而我是其中之一。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People were not invited—they went there.","zh":"很多人没有接到邀请——但不请自来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They got into automobiles which bore them out to Long Island, and somehow they ended up at Gatsby’s door.","zh":"他们坐上从城里开往长岛的汽车，也不知道怎么就来到盖茨比门口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once there they were introduced by somebody who knew Gatsby, and after that they conducted themselves according to the rules of behaviour associated with an amusement park.","zh":"到了这里，总有认识盖茨比的人给他们引见。介绍过后他们就可以随意走动了，像是走进了游乐园似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes they came and went without having met Gatsby at all, came for the party with a simplicity of heart that was its own ticket of admission.","zh":"有时候他们从来到走都没有见过盖茨比，似乎是认为一颗渴望参加宴会的心就足以充当门票了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I had been actually invited. A chauffeur in a uniform of robin’s-egg blue crossed my lawn early that Saturday morning with a surprisingly formal note from his employer: the honour would be entirely Gatsby’s, it said, if I would attend his “little party” that night. He had seen me several times, and had intended to call on me long before, but a peculiar combination of circumstances had prevented it—signed Jay Gatsby, in a majestic hand.","sentences":[{"en":"I had been actually invited.","zh":"我是真正受到邀请的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A chauffeur in a uniform of robin’s-egg blue crossed my lawn early that Saturday morning with a surprisingly formal note from his employer: the honour would be entirely Gatsby’s, it said, if I would attend his “little party” that night.","zh":"那个星期六早晨，有个穿着罗宾蛋蓝色制服的司机踏过我的草坪，送来他主人写的一张让我大感意外的纸条。纸条上大概写着，如果我晚上愿意参加他的“寒酸宴会”，盖茨比家将会蓬荜生辉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had seen me several times, and had intended to call on me long before, but a peculiar combination of circumstances had prevented it—signed Jay Gatsby, in a majestic hand.","zh":"又说他见过我几次，早就想来拜访，但时机总是不凑巧——落款是“杰伊·盖茨比”，笔迹很漂亮。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Dressed up in white flannels I went over to his lawn a little after seven, and wandered around rather ill at ease among swirls and eddies of people I didn’t know—though here and there was a face I had noticed on the commuting train. I was immediately struck by the number of young Englishmen dotted about; all well dressed, all looking a little hungry, and all talking in low, earnest voices to solid and prosperous Americans. I was sure that they were selling something: bonds or insurance or automobiles. They were at least agonizingly aware of the easy money in the vicinity and convinced that it was theirs for a few words in the right key.","sentences":[{"en":"Dressed up in white flannels I went over to his lawn a little after seven, and wandered around rather ill at ease among swirls and eddies of people I didn’t know—though here and there was a face I had noticed on the commuting train.","zh":"晚上七点过后，我穿上白色的法兰绒便装，相当不舒服地在忽聚忽散的陌生人流中晃来晃去——不过我时不时能看到几张曾在来往纽约的火车上见过的脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was immediately struck by the number of young Englishmen dotted about; all well dressed, all looking a little hungry, and all talking in low, earnest voices to solid and prosperous Americans.","zh":"我很快发现，人群中散落着许多年轻的英国人，他们全都穿得很整齐，全都带着渴望的表情，全都在用轻微而热切的声音和殷实富裕的美国人交谈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was sure that they were selling something: bonds or insurance or automobiles.","zh":"我敢说他们是在推销什么东西，不是债券就是保险，要么是汽车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were at least agonizingly aware of the easy money in the vicinity and convinced that it was theirs for a few words in the right key.","zh":"反正他们苦恼地认识到，眼前就有轻松赚钱的机会，只要几句话说得投机，大把的钱就会落进他们的口袋。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As soon as I arrived I made an attempt to find my host, but the two or three people of whom I asked his whereabouts stared at me in such an amazed way, and denied so vehemently any knowledge of his movements, that I slunk off in the direction of the cocktail table—the only place in the garden where a single man could linger without looking purposeless and alone.","sentences":[{"en":"As soon as I arrived I made an attempt to find my host, but the two or three people of whom I asked his whereabouts stared at me in such an amazed way, and denied so vehemently any knowledge of his movements, that I slunk off in the direction of the cocktail table—the only place in the garden where a single man could linger without looking purposeless and alone.","zh":"到了之后，我立刻想要找到主人；我向两三个人问他在哪里，但他们用很惊奇的眼神看着我，忙不迭地说根本不知道他的行踪，所以我偷偷地朝鸡尾酒桌走去——单身的男人唯有在这个地方才不会显得无聊和孤独。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was on my way to get roaring drunk from sheer embarrassment when Jordan Baker came out of the house and stood at the head of the marble steps, leaning a little backward and looking with contemptuous interest down into the garden.","sentences":[{"en":"I was on my way to get roaring drunk from sheer embarrassment when Jordan Baker came out of the house and stood at the head of the marble steps, leaning a little backward and looking with contemptuous interest down into the garden.","zh":"穷极无聊的我正准备喝个酩酊大醉，这时乔丹·贝克从屋子里走出来，站在大理石台阶的上端，头部微微后仰，轻蔑而好奇地俯视着花园。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Welcome or not, I found it necessary to attach myself to someone before I should begin to address cordial remarks to the passersby.","sentences":[{"en":"Welcome or not, I found it necessary to attach myself to someone before I should begin to address cordial remarks to the passersby.","zh":"不管是否受欢迎，我觉得有必要找个人来攀谈，否则我恐怕就要跟从身边走过的陌生人搭讪了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hello!” I roared, advancing toward her. My voice seemed unnaturally loud across the garden.","sentences":[{"en":"“Hello!”","zh":"“你好啊！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I roared, advancing toward her.","zh":"我大声地说，朝她走过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My voice seemed unnaturally loud across the garden.","zh":"我的声音似乎非同凡响地穿过了花园。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I thought you might be here,” she responded absently as I came up. “I remembered you lived next door to—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought you might be here,” she responded absently as I came up.","zh":"“我刚才想你或许会来，”看到我走上前，她心不在焉地说，“我记得你住在隔壁…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I remembered you lived next door to—”","zh":"“我刚才想你或许会来，”看到我走上前，她心不在焉地说，“我记得你住在隔壁…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She held my hand impersonally, as a promise that she’d take care of me in a minute, and gave ear to two girls in twin yellow dresses, who stopped at the foot of the steps.","sentences":[{"en":"She held my hand impersonally, as a promise that she’d take care of me in a minute, and gave ear to two girls in twin yellow dresses, who stopped at the foot of the steps.","zh":"她不动声色地握住我的手，表示她过会儿再搭理我，然后扭头去看两个穿着相同黄色裙子的女孩，她们在台阶下面站住了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hello!” they cried together. “Sorry you didn’t win.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hello!” they cried together.","zh":"“你好，”她们齐声说，“可惜你没赢呀。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Sorry you didn’t win.”","zh":"“你好，”她们齐声说，“可惜你没赢呀。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That was for the golf tournament. She had lost in the finals the week before.","sentences":[{"en":"That was for the golf tournament.","zh":"她们指的是高尔夫球大奖赛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had lost in the finals the week before.","zh":"她在上个星期的决赛中输掉了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You don’t know who we are,” said one of the girls in yellow, “but we met you here about a month ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You don’t know who we are,” said one of the girls in yellow, “but we met you here about a month ago.”","zh":"“你不认识我们，”其中一个黄裙女孩说，“但我们上个月在这里见过你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’ve dyed your hair since then,” remarked Jordan, and I started, but the girls had moved casually on and her remark was addressed to the premature moon, produced like the supper, no doubt, out of a caterer’s basket. With Jordan’s slender golden arm resting in mine, we descended the steps and sauntered about the garden. A tray of cocktails floated at us through the twilight, and we sat down at a table with the two girls in yellow and three men, each one introduced to us as Mr. Mumble.","sentences":[{"en":"“You’ve dyed your hair since then,” remarked Jordan, and I started, but the girls had moved casually on and her remark was addressed to the premature moon, produced like the supper, no doubt, out of a caterer’s basket.","zh":"“你后来染头发了吧，”乔丹说，我把手抽出来，但那两个女孩已经漫不经心地走开，于是她这句话显得像是对早升的月亮说的——这月亮无疑跟晚餐一样，也是由包办宴席的人制造的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With Jordan’s slender golden arm resting in mine, we descended the steps and sauntered about the garden.","zh":"乔丹金黄色的长臂挽着我的手，我们走下台阶，在花园里漫步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A tray of cocktails floated at us through the twilight, and we sat down at a table with the two girls in yellow and three men, each one introduced to us as Mr. Mumble.","zh":"一盘鸡尾酒穿过夜色向我们飘来，我们找了张桌子坐下，同桌的是那两个黄裙女孩和三个男人，听介绍，他们的姓名都是“叽里咕噜先生”。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do you come to these parties often?” inquired Jordan of the girl beside her.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you come to these parties often?” inquired Jordan of the girl beside her.","zh":"“你常来这里参加宴会吗？”乔丹问她身边的女孩。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The last one was the one I met you at,” answered the girl, in an alert confident voice. She turned to her companion: “Wasn’t it for you, Lucille?”","sentences":[{"en":"“The last one was the one I met you at,” answered the girl, in an alert confident voice.","zh":"“上次我来就是遇到你那次呀，”那女孩回答说，听起来显得机灵又自信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She turned to her companion: “Wasn’t it for you, Lucille?”","zh":"她扭头问她的同伴：“你不也是吗，露西尔？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was for Lucille, too.","sentences":[{"en":"It was for Lucille, too.","zh":"露西尔也是。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I like to come,” Lucille said. “I never care what I do, so I always have a good time. When I was here last I tore my gown on a chair, and he asked me my name and address—inside of a week I got a package from Croirier’s with a new evening gown in it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I like to come,” Lucille said.","zh":"“我喜欢来这里，”露西尔说，“我这人要求不高，所以每次来都玩得很开心。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I never care what I do, so I always have a good time.","zh":"“我喜欢来这里，”露西尔说，“我这人要求不高，所以每次来都玩得很开心。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When I was here last I tore my gown on a chair, and he asked me my name and address—inside of a week I got a package from Croirier’s with a new evening gown in it.”","zh":"上次我的晚礼服被椅子钩破了，他问了我的名字和地址——不到一个星期，我就收到科洛耶成衣店寄来的包裹，里面是一件新的晚礼服。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you keep it?” asked Jordan.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you keep it?” asked Jordan.","zh":"“那你收下了吗？”乔丹问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Sure I did. I was going to wear it tonight, but it was too big in the bust and had to be altered. It was gas blue with lavender beads. Two hundred and sixty-five dollars.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sure I did.","zh":"“当然啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was going to wear it tonight, but it was too big in the bust and had to be altered.","zh":"今晚我本来想穿它的，可是它的胸口太大，得改改才能穿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was gas blue with lavender beads.","zh":"它是浅蓝色的，缀着紫色的珠子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Two hundred and sixty-five dollars.”","zh":"要卖两百六十五美元呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There’s something funny about a fellow that’ll do a thing like that,” said the other girl eagerly. “He doesn’t want any trouble with anybody.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There’s something funny about a fellow that’ll do a thing like that,” said the other girl eagerly.","zh":"“这家伙真有意思，居然会做这样的事情，”另外那女孩感慨说，“他什么人都不想得罪。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He doesn’t want any trouble with anybody.”","zh":"“这家伙真有意思，居然会做这样的事情，”另外那女孩感慨说，“他什么人都不想得罪。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who doesn’t?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Who doesn’t?”","zh":"“他是谁？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Gatsby. Somebody told me—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Gatsby.","zh":"“盖茨比呀。有人跟我说…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Somebody told me—”","zh":"“盖茨比呀。有人跟我说…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The two girls and Jordan leaned together confidentially.","sentences":[{"en":"The two girls and Jordan leaned together confidentially.","zh":"那两个女孩和乔丹凑到一起窃窃私语。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Somebody told me they thought he killed a man once.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Somebody told me they thought he killed a man once.”","zh":"“有人跟我说，他们认为他曾经杀过人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A thrill passed over all of us. The three Mr. Mumbles bent forward and listened eagerly.","sentences":[{"en":"A thrill passed over all of us.","zh":"我们大家都感到不寒而栗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The three Mr. Mumbles bent forward and listened eagerly.","zh":"三位“叽里咕噜先生”身体向前靠，热切地想听个究竟。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t think it’s so much that,” argued Lucille sceptically; “It’s more that he was a German spy during the war.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t think it’s so much that,” argued Lucille sceptically; “It’s more that he was a German spy during the war.”","zh":"“我倒认为不是这么回事，”露西尔将信将疑地说，“他更可能是战争期间的德国间谍。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"One of the men nodded in confirmation.","sentences":[{"en":"One of the men nodded in confirmation.","zh":"有个男的点头表示赞同。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I heard that from a man who knew all about him, grew up with him in Germany,” he assured us positively.","sentences":[{"en":"“I heard that from a man who knew all about him, grew up with him in Germany,” he assured us positively.","zh":"“这我听人说过，那人对他很了解，是跟他在德国一起长大的，”他言之凿凿地向我们保证。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, no,” said the first girl, “it couldn’t be that, because he was in the American army during the war.” As our credulity switched back to her she leaned forward with enthusiasm. “You look at him sometimes when he thinks nobody’s looking at him. I’ll bet he killed a man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no,” said the first girl, “it couldn’t be that, because he was in the American army during the war.”","zh":"“哎呀，不是啦，”第一个女孩说，“不可能是这样的，因为战争期间，他是在美国陆军服役的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As our credulity switched back to her she leaned forward with enthusiasm.","zh":"看到我们又倾向于相信她，她兴致勃勃地凑向前说：“有时候你看他不经意流露的神态。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You look at him sometimes when he thinks nobody’s looking at him.","zh":"看到我们又倾向于相信她，她兴致勃勃地凑向前说：“有时候你看他不经意流露的神态。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll bet he killed a man.”","zh":"我敢打赌他肯定杀过人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She narrowed her eyes and shivered. Lucille shivered. We all turned and looked around for Gatsby. It was testimony to the romantic speculation he inspired that there were whispers about him from those who had found little that it was necessary to whisper about in this world.","sentences":[{"en":"She narrowed her eyes and shivered.","zh":"她眯起眼睛，打了个寒颤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lucille shivered.","zh":"露西尔也浑身激灵。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We all turned and looked around for Gatsby.","zh":"我们大家都扭过头，想看看盖茨比在哪里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was testimony to the romantic speculation he inspired that there were whispers about him from those who had found little that it was necessary to whisper about in this world.","zh":"连这些平时说话谈天百无禁忌的人在提到他时都需要交头接耳，可见笼罩在他身上的神秘色彩有多么罗曼蒂克了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The first supper—there would be another one after midnight—was now being served, and Jordan invited me to join her own party, who were spread around a table on the other side of the garden. There were three married couples and Jordan’s escort, a persistent undergraduate given to violent innuendo, and obviously under the impression that sooner or later Jordan was going to yield him up her person to a greater or lesser degree. Instead of rambling, this party had preserved a dignified homogeneity, and assumed to itself the function of representing the staid nobility of the countryside—East Egg condescending to West Egg and carefully on guard against its spectroscopic gaiety.","sentences":[{"en":"The first supper—there would be another one after midnight—was now being served, and Jordan invited me to join her own party, who were spread around a table on the other side of the garden.","zh":"第一次晚餐——午夜过后会有第二次——已经开动，乔丹邀请我和她坐到一块，那桌子在花园的另外一边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were three married couples and Jordan’s escort, a persistent undergraduate given to violent innuendo, and obviously under the impression that sooner or later Jordan was going to yield him up her person to a greater or lesser degree.","zh":"同桌的是三对夫妻和陪乔丹前来的男伴，这人是个言语无味的大学生，说起话来总是拐弯抹角、含沙射影，一副自以为乔丹迟早会委身于他的神气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of rambling, this party had preserved a dignified homogeneity, and assumed to itself the function of representing the staid nobility of the countryside—East Egg condescending to West Egg and carefully on guard against its spectroscopic gaiety.","zh":"这些人倒也不随意走动，不约而同地保持了矜持的姿态，并自认为他们代表着老成持重的乡绅贵族——从东卵屈尊光临西卵，谨慎地抵制这里光怪陆离的娱乐。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Let’s get out,” whispered Jordan, after a somehow wasteful and inappropriate half-hour; “this is much too polite for me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let’s get out,” whispered Jordan, after a somehow wasteful and inappropriate half-hour; “this is much too polite for me.”","zh":"无谓地浪费了格格不入的半小时之后，乔丹低声说：“我们走吧，我觉得这里太客套了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We got up, and she explained that we were going to find the host: I had never met him, she said, and it was making me uneasy. The undergraduate nodded in a cynical, melancholy way.","sentences":[{"en":"We got up, and she explained that we were going to find the host: I had never met him, she said, and it was making me uneasy.","zh":"于是我们站起来，她解释说，我们要去找主人：我从来没见过他，她说，这让我很不好意思。大学生点点头，表情像是无所谓，又有点郁闷。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The undergraduate nodded in a cynical, melancholy way.","zh":"于是我们站起来，她解释说，我们要去找主人：我从来没见过他，她说，这让我很不好意思。大学生点点头，表情像是无所谓，又有点郁闷。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The bar, where we glanced first, was crowded, but Gatsby was not there. She couldn’t find him from the top of the steps, and he wasn’t on the veranda. On a chance we tried an important-looking door, and walked into a high Gothic library, panelled with carved English oak, and probably transported complete from some ruin overseas.","sentences":[{"en":"The bar, where we glanced first, was crowded, but Gatsby was not there.","zh":"我们先到吧台去，那里人满为患，但见不到盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She couldn’t find him from the top of the steps, and he wasn’t on the veranda.","zh":"乔丹站在台阶上面没看见他，他也不在阳台上。我们试探着推开一扇看上去很重要的门，走进去才发现原来是个哥特式的书房，里面的摆设都是精雕细琢的英格兰橡木家具，很可能是从国外某个古堡整套运过来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"On a chance we tried an important-looking door, and walked into a high Gothic library, panelled with carved English oak, and probably transported complete from some ruin overseas.","zh":"乔丹站在台阶上面没看见他，他也不在阳台上。我们试探着推开一扇看上去很重要的门，走进去才发现原来是个哥特式的书房，里面的摆设都是精雕细琢的英格兰橡木家具，很可能是从国外某个古堡整套运过来的。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A stout, middle-aged man, with enormous owl-eyed spectacles, was sitting somewhat drunk on the edge of a great table, staring with unsteady concentration at the shelves of books. As we entered he wheeled excitedly around and examined Jordan from head to foot.","sentences":[{"en":"A stout, middle-aged man, with enormous owl-eyed spectacles, was sitting somewhat drunk on the edge of a great table, staring with unsteady concentration at the shelves of books.","zh":"有个矮胖的中年男子戴着巨大的猫头鹰式眼镜，醉态可掬地坐在一张大书桌边缘，眼光闪烁地盯着几个书架。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As we entered he wheeled excitedly around and examined Jordan from head to foot.","zh":"听到我们走进去，他兴奋地转过身来，从头到脚地打量着乔丹。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What do you think?” he demanded impetuously.","sentences":[{"en":"“What do you think?” he demanded impetuously.","zh":"“你觉得怎么样？”他唐突地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“About what?”","sentences":[{"en":"“About what?”","zh":"“什么怎么样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He waved his hand toward the bookshelves.","sentences":[{"en":"He waved his hand toward the bookshelves.","zh":"他的手朝那些书架一摆。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“About that. As a matter of fact you needn’t bother to ascertain. I ascertained. They’re real.”","sentences":[{"en":"“About that.","zh":"“这些啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As a matter of fact you needn’t bother to ascertain.","zh":"其实你不必细看了，我已经仔细查看过，都是真的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I ascertained.","zh":"其实你不必细看了，我已经仔细查看过，都是真的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"They’re real.”","zh":"其实你不必细看了，我已经仔细查看过，都是真的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The books?”","sentences":[{"en":"“The books?”","zh":"“这些书吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"He nodded.","zh":"他点点头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Absolutely real—have pages and everything. I thought they’d be a nice durable cardboard. Matter of fact, they’re absolutely real. Pages and—Here! Lemme show you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Absolutely real—have pages and everything.","zh":"“绝对是真的——里面有纸有字的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought they’d be a nice durable cardboard.","zh":"我原本以为它们是漂亮的假书。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Matter of fact, they’re absolutely real.","zh":"可实际上，它们绝对是真的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Pages and—Here!","zh":"有纸有…这里！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lemme show you.”","zh":"我翻给你们看。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Taking our scepticism for granted, he rushed to the bookcases and returned with Volume One of the Stoddard Lectures.","sentences":[{"en":"Taking our scepticism for granted, he rushed to the bookcases and returned with Volume One of the Stoddard Lectures.","zh":"他想当然地以为我们也不相信，冲到书架旁边，走回来时手里拿着《斯托达德讲演集·第一卷》。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“See!” he cried triumphantly. “It’s a bona-fide piece of printed matter. It fooled me. This fella’s a regular Belasco. It’s a triumph. What thoroughness! What realism! Knew when to stop, too—didn’t cut the pages. But what do you want? What do you expect?”","sentences":[{"en":"“See!” he cried triumphantly.","zh":"“看！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It’s a bona-fide piece of printed matter.","zh":"他得意地大喊，“这是如假包换的印刷品啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It fooled me.","zh":"它把我唬住了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This fella’s a regular Belasco.","zh":"这家伙简直是毕拉斯科。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s a triumph.","zh":"太成功了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What thoroughness!","zh":"太仔细了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What realism!","zh":"多么逼真啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Knew when to stop, too—didn’t cut the pages.","zh":"而且也没有装得太过分——这些书页还没有裁开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But what do you want?","zh":"但你想怎么样？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What do you expect?”","zh":"你还有什么好说的呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He snatched the book from me and replaced it hastily on its shelf, muttering that if one brick was removed the whole library was liable to collapse.","sentences":[{"en":"He snatched the book from me and replaced it hastily on its shelf, muttering that if one brick was removed the whole library was liable to collapse.","zh":"他把书从我手里抢回去，匆忙把它放回书架上，嘴里叽里咕噜地说，假如挪走一块砖头，整个书房就会倒塌。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who brought you?” he demanded. “Or did you just come? I was brought. Most people were brought.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who brought you?” he demanded.","zh":"“谁带你们来的？”他质问说，“或者你们是不请自来的？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Or did you just come?","zh":"“谁带你们来的？”他质问说，“或者你们是不请自来的？","scope":"group"},{"en":"I was brought.","zh":"我是有人带的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Most people were brought.”","zh":"大多数人都有人带。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Jordan looked at him alertly, cheerfully, without answering.","sentences":[{"en":"Jordan looked at him alertly, cheerfully, without answering.","zh":"乔丹清醒而欢乐地看着他，没有搭话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I was brought by a woman named Roosevelt,” he continued. “Mrs. Claud Roosevelt. Do you know her? I met her somewhere last night. I’ve been drunk for about a week now, and I thought it might sober me up to sit in a library.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was brought by a woman named Roosevelt,” he continued.","zh":"“带我来的那个女人姓罗斯福，”他继续说，“克劳德·罗斯福太太。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Mrs. Claud Roosevelt.","zh":"“带我来的那个女人姓罗斯福，”他继续说，“克劳德·罗斯福太太。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Do you know her?","zh":"你们认识她吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I met her somewhere last night.","zh":"昨晚我不知道在哪里遇见她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve been drunk for about a week now, and I thought it might sober me up to sit in a library.”","zh":"我醉了个把星期啦，我想坐在书房里也许能让我清醒一点。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Has it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Has it?”","zh":"“那你清醒了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“A little bit, I think. I can’t tell yet. I’ve only been here an hour. Did I tell you about the books? They’re real. They’re—”","sentences":[{"en":"“A little bit, I think.","zh":"“有一点吧，我觉得。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I can’t tell yet.","zh":"我说不出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve only been here an hour.","zh":"我到这里才一个小时。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did I tell you about the books?","zh":"我跟你们说过这些书吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They’re real.","zh":"它们是真的。它们…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They’re—”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You told us.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You told us.”","zh":"“你跟我们说过了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We shook hands with him gravely and went back outdoors.","sentences":[{"en":"We shook hands with him gravely and went back outdoors.","zh":"我们一本正经地和他握手，然后回到外边。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was dancing now on the canvas in the garden; old men pushing young girls backward in eternal graceless circles, superior couples holding each other tortuously, fashionably, and keeping in the corners—and a great number of single girls dancing individually or relieving the orchestra for a moment of the burden of the banjo or the traps. By midnight the hilarity had increased. A celebrated tenor had sung in Italian, and a notorious contralto had sung in jazz, and between the numbers people were doing “stunts” all over the garden, while happy, vacuous bursts of laughter rose toward the summer sky. A pair of stage twins, who turned out to be the girls in yellow, did a baby act in costume, and champagne was served in glasses bigger than finger-bowls. The moon had risen higher, and floating in the Sound was a triangle of silver scales, trembling a little to the stiff, tinny drip of the banjoes on the lawn.","sentences":[{"en":"There was dancing now on the canvas in the garden; old men pushing young girls backward in eternal graceless circles, superior couples holding each other tortuously, fashionably, and keeping in the corners—and a great number of single girls dancing individually or relieving the orchestra for a moment of the burden of the banjo or the traps.","zh":"花园里帆布铺成的舞池上已经有人在跳舞。有些糟老头子推着妙龄少女往后退，永无休止地绕着难看的圈圈；有些神气的男女紧紧相拥，躲在角落里踏着时髦的舞步——还有许多单身女郎，有的独自翩跹起舞，有的则在乐团挑起弹奏五弦琴或敲击鼓钹的重任。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By midnight the hilarity had increased.","zh":"到了午夜时分，大家的兴致更加高涨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A celebrated tenor had sung in Italian, and a notorious contralto had sung in jazz, and between the numbers people were doing “stunts” all over the garden, while happy, vacuous bursts of laughter rose toward the summer sky.","zh":"有位著名的男高音先演唱了意大利歌曲，然后有个声名狼藉的女低音唱了爵士乐；而在两个节目之间，花园里到处都有人在表演“绝技”，阵阵欢乐而空洞的笑声响彻夏夜的天空。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A pair of stage twins, who turned out to be the girls in yellow, did a baby act in costume, and champagne was served in glasses bigger than finger-bowls.","zh":"另外有两个少女——原来就是那两个黄裙女孩——穿着戏服，表演了一出简单的剧目。香槟装在玻璃杯里被端出来，那些杯子比洗手指的碗还要大。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The moon had risen higher, and floating in the Sound was a triangle of silver scales, trembling a little to the stiff, tinny drip of the banjoes on the lawn.","zh":"月亮升得更高了，海湾里漂浮着天秤座三颗银色的星星，随着草坪上五弦琴清脆细密的琴音轻轻地颤动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was still with Jordan Baker. We were sitting at a table with a man of about my age and a rowdy little girl, who gave way upon the slightest provocation to uncontrollable laughter. I was enjoying myself now. I had taken two finger-bowls of champagne, and the scene had changed before my eyes into something significant, elemental, and profound.","sentences":[{"en":"I was still with Jordan Baker.","zh":"我仍在乔丹·贝克身边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We were sitting at a table with a man of about my age and a rowdy little girl, who gave way upon the slightest provocation to uncontrollable laughter.","zh":"我们那张桌子还坐着一个年纪和我相若的男子，一个举止粗鲁的少女，她动不动就笑得前俯后仰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was enjoying myself now.","zh":"现在我也玩得挺开心了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had taken two finger-bowls of champagne, and the scene had changed before my eyes into something significant, elemental, and profound.","zh":"我已经喝下两大杯香槟，眼前的景象早已变成一幅颇具哲学意味的复杂图画。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At a lull in the entertainment the man looked at me and smiled.","sentences":[{"en":"At a lull in the entertainment the man looked at me and smiled.","zh":"娱乐节目暂时停止了，那人看着我，露出了微笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Your face is familiar,” he said politely. “Weren’t you in the First Division during the war?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Your face is familiar,” he said politely.","zh":"“你看起来很面善，”他礼貌地说，“打仗时你是在第一师吧？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Weren’t you in the First Division during the war?”","zh":"“你看起来很面善，”他礼貌地说，“打仗时你是在第一师吧？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why yes. I was in the Twenty-eighth Infantry.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why yes.","zh":"“是啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was in the Twenty-eighth Infantry.”","zh":"当时我在第二十八步兵团。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I was in the Sixteenth until June nineteen-eighteen. I knew I’d seen you somewhere before.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was in the Sixteenth until June nineteen-eighteen.","zh":"“我在第十六步兵团待到1918年。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I knew I’d seen you somewhere before.”","zh":"我就知道我以前肯定在什么地方见过你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We talked for a moment about some wet, grey little villages in France. Evidently he lived in this vicinity, for he told me that he had just bought a hydroplane, and was going to try it out in the morning.","sentences":[{"en":"We talked for a moment about some wet, grey little villages in France.","zh":"我们倾谈了片刻，聊起法国那些灰暗多雨的小村庄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Evidently he lived in this vicinity, for he told me that he had just bought a hydroplane, and was going to try it out in the morning.","zh":"他显然住在附近，因为他跟我说他刚买了一架水上飞机，准备明天早上去试开。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Want to go with me, old sport? Just near the shore along the Sound.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Want to go with me, old sport?","zh":"“老兄，你想跟我去吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just near the shore along the Sound.”","zh":"就在海湾沿岸转转。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What time?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What time?”","zh":"“什么时候？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Any time that suits you best.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Any time that suits you best.”","zh":"“看你方便咯。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was on the tip of my tongue to ask his name when Jordan looked around and smiled.","sentences":[{"en":"It was on the tip of my tongue to ask his name when Jordan looked around and smiled.","zh":"我正准备问他尊姓大名，这时乔丹转过头来，微微一笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Having a gay time now?” she inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Having a gay time now?” she inquired.","zh":"“现在你高兴了吧？”她问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Much better.” I turned again to my new acquaintance. “This is an unusual party for me. I haven’t even seen the host. I live over there—” I waved my hand at the invisible hedge in the distance, “and this man Gatsby sent over his chauffeur with an invitation.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Much better.”","zh":"“好多啦。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I turned again to my new acquaintance.","zh":"我扭头看着我的新交。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“This is an unusual party for me.","zh":"“对我来说，这宴会有点特别。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I haven’t even seen the host.","zh":"我到现在还没见过主人呢，我住在那边…”我伸手指着远处那消失在夜色里的篱笆，“这个姓盖茨比的早上派他的司机过去邀请我。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I live over there—” I waved my hand at the invisible hedge in the distance, “and this man Gatsby sent over his chauffeur with an invitation.”","zh":"我到现在还没见过主人呢，我住在那边…”我伸手指着远处那消失在夜色里的篱笆，“这个姓盖茨比的早上派他的司机过去邀请我。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For a moment he looked at me as if he failed to understand.","sentences":[{"en":"For a moment he looked at me as if he failed to understand.","zh":"他朝我看了一会，脸上满是不解的神色。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m Gatsby,” he said suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m Gatsby,” he said suddenly.","zh":"“我就是盖茨比，”他突然说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What!” I exclaimed. “Oh, I beg your pardon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!”","zh":"“什么！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I exclaimed.","zh":"我惊叫起来，“对不起啊。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Oh, I beg your pardon.”","zh":"我惊叫起来，“对不起啊。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I thought you knew, old sport. I’m afraid I’m not a very good host.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought you knew, old sport.","zh":"“老兄，我还以为你认识我呢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m afraid I’m not a very good host.”","zh":"看来我这个主人做得不够好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He smiled understandingly—much more than understandingly. It was one of those rare smiles with a quality of eternal reassurance in it, that you may come across four or five times in life. It faced—or seemed to face—the whole eternal world for an instant, and then concentrated on you with an irresistible prejudice in your favour. It understood you just so far as you wanted to be understood, believed in you as you would like to believe in yourself, and assured you that it had precisely the impression of you that, at your best, you hoped to convey. Precisely at that point it vanished—and I was looking at an elegant young roughneck, a year or two over thirty, whose elaborate formality of speech just missed being absurd. Some time before he introduced himself I’d got a strong impression that he was picking his words with care.","sentences":[{"en":"He smiled understandingly—much more than understandingly.","zh":"他善解人意地笑了——不仅是善解人意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was one of those rare smiles with a quality of eternal reassurance in it, that you may come across four or five times in life.","zh":"它是那种很罕见、让你心里非常舒坦的笑容，你一辈子或许只能遇到四五次。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It faced—or seemed to face—the whole eternal world for an instant, and then concentrated on you with an irresistible prejudice in your favour.","zh":"它是专门为你准备的，好像芸芸众生之中，只有你让他感到不由自主地喜欢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It understood you just so far as you wanted to be understood, believed in you as you would like to believe in yourself, and assured you that it had precisely the impression of you that, at your best, you hoped to convey.","zh":"这笑容表示他完全理解你，绝对相信你，他对你的印象恰恰是你最乐意给人留下的。就在此时，它消失了——于是我看到的不过是一个表现得很有风度的粗俗汉子，三十一二岁的样子，谈吐客套得简直有点可笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Precisely at that point it vanished—and I was looking at an elegant young roughneck, a year or two over thirty, whose elaborate formality of speech just missed being absurd.","zh":"这笑容表示他完全理解你，绝对相信你，他对你的印象恰恰是你最乐意给人留下的。就在此时，它消失了——于是我看到的不过是一个表现得很有风度的粗俗汉子，三十一二岁的样子，谈吐客套得简直有点可笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Some time before he introduced himself I’d got a strong impression that he was picking his words with care.","zh":"在他自我介绍之前，我已经强烈地感觉到他说话时选词用字特别谨慎。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Almost at the moment when Mr. Gatsby identified himself a butler hurried toward him with the information that Chicago was calling him on the wire. He excused himself with a small bow that included each of us in turn.","sentences":[{"en":"Almost at the moment when Mr. Gatsby identified himself a butler hurried toward him with the information that Chicago was calling him on the wire.","zh":"盖茨比先生刚刚揭示了自己的身份，他的管家就匆匆走过来，说芝加哥有人打电话来找他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He excused himself with a small bow that included each of us in turn.","zh":"他站起来告辞，朝我们三个微微欠身。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“If you want anything just ask for it, old sport,” he urged me. “Excuse me. I will rejoin you later.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If you want anything just ask for it, old sport,” he urged me.","zh":"“你想要什么尽管开口，老兄，”他殷勤地说，“对不起啦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Excuse me.","zh":"“你想要什么尽管开口，老兄，”他殷勤地说，“对不起啦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I will rejoin you later.”","zh":"我等会再来找你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When he was gone I turned immediately to Jordan—constrained to assure her of my surprise. I had expected that Mr. Gatsby would be a florid and corpulent person in his middle years.","sentences":[{"en":"When he was gone I turned immediately to Jordan—constrained to assure her of my surprise.","zh":"他走了之后，我立刻转身看着乔丹——我迫不及待地要向她表达我的惊讶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had expected that Mr. Gatsby would be a florid and corpulent person in his middle years.","zh":"我原本以为盖茨比先生是个油光满面、猪头猪脑的中年人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who is he?” I demanded. “Do you know?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who is he?”","zh":"“他是什么人？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I demanded.","zh":"我急切地问，“你知道吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Do you know?”","zh":"我急切地问，“你知道吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He’s just a man named Gatsby.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He’s just a man named Gatsby.”","zh":"“他不就是盖茨比嘛。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where is he from, I mean? And what does he do?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where is he from, I mean?","zh":"“我想问的是，他从哪里来？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And what does he do?”","zh":"他是干什么的？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Now you’re started on the subject,” she answered with a wan smile. “Well, he told me once he was an Oxford man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now you’re started on the subject,” she answered with a wan smile.","zh":"“你怎么也八卦起这个来了，”她娇慵地笑着说，“他曾经跟我说他念过牛津大学。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Well, he told me once he was an Oxford man.”","zh":"“你怎么也八卦起这个来了，”她娇慵地笑着说，“他曾经跟我说他念过牛津大学。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A dim background started to take shape behind him, but at her next remark it faded away.","sentences":[{"en":"A dim background started to take shape behind him, but at her next remark it faded away.","zh":"我开始对他的出身有了模糊的了解，但她随后那句话又打消了我的猜测。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“However, I don’t believe it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“However, I don’t believe it.”","zh":"“可是我不信他的话。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why not?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why not?”","zh":"“为什么呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t know,” she insisted, “I just don’t think he went there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t know,” she insisted, “I just don’t think he went there.”","zh":"“不知道呀，”她固执地说，“我就是觉得他没去过那里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Something in her tone reminded me of the other girl’s “I think he killed a man,” and had the effect of stimulating my curiosity. I would have accepted without question the information that Gatsby sprang from the swamps of Louisiana or from the lower East Side of New York. That was comprehensible. But young men didn’t—at least in my provincial inexperience I believed they didn’t—drift coolly out of nowhere and buy a palace on Long Island Sound.","sentences":[{"en":"Something in her tone reminded me of the other girl’s “I think he killed a man,” and had the effect of stimulating my curiosity.","zh":"她的口气有点像刚才说“我认为他杀过人”的那女孩，这也激起了我的好奇心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I would have accepted without question the information that Gatsby sprang from the swamps of Louisiana or from the lower East Side of New York.","zh":"你说盖茨比来自路易斯安那的沼泽地区也好，哪怕说他来自纽约的下东区也好，我是绝对相信的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That was comprehensible.","zh":"那是情理之所有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But young men didn’t—at least in my provincial inexperience I believed they didn’t—drift coolly out of nowhere and buy a palace on Long Island Sound.","zh":"但要是说一个年轻人在长岛海湾买下宫殿般的豪宅，却没有人知道他的来历，那至少在我这个见识浅陋的乡下人看来，绝对是情理之所无。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Anyhow, he gives large parties,” said Jordan, changing the subject with an urban distaste for the concrete. “And I like large parties. They’re so intimate. At small parties there isn’t any privacy.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Anyhow, he gives large parties,” said Jordan, changing the subject with an urban distaste for the concrete.","zh":"“反正他喜欢举办大型的宴会，”乔丹转移了话题，她是城里人，讨厌谈论具体问题，“而我又喜欢大型的宴会，多么自在呀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And I like large parties.","zh":"“反正他喜欢举办大型的宴会，”乔丹转移了话题，她是城里人，讨厌谈论具体问题，“而我又喜欢大型的宴会，多么自在呀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They’re so intimate.","zh":"“反正他喜欢举办大型的宴会，”乔丹转移了话题，她是城里人，讨厌谈论具体问题，“而我又喜欢大型的宴会，多么自在呀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At small parties there isn’t any privacy.”","zh":"小型的聚会片刻不得清净。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was the boom of a bass drum, and the voice of the orchestra leader rang out suddenly above the echolalia of the garden.","sentences":[{"en":"There was the boom of a bass drum, and the voice of the orchestra leader rang out suddenly above the echolalia of the garden.","zh":"鼓声响起，乐团指挥的声音突然盖过了花园里的嘈杂。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Ladies and gentlemen,” he cried. “At the request of Mr. Gatsby we are going to play for you Mr. Vladmir Tostoff’s latest work, which attracted so much attention at Carnegie Hall last May. If you read the papers you know there was a big sensation.” He smiled with jovial condescension, and added: “Some sensation!” Whereupon everybody laughed.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ladies and gentlemen,” he cried.","zh":"“各位来宾，”他大声说，“应盖茨比先生之请，我们将为各位演奏弗拉基米尔·陀斯托夫的最新作品，五月份在卡内基音乐厅引起许多关注那首。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“At the request of Mr. Gatsby we are going to play for you Mr. Vladmir Tostoff’s latest work, which attracted so much attention at Carnegie Hall last May.","zh":"“各位来宾，”他大声说，“应盖茨比先生之请，我们将为各位演奏弗拉基米尔·陀斯托夫的最新作品，五月份在卡内基音乐厅引起许多关注那首。","scope":"group"},{"en":"If you read the papers you know there was a big sensation.”","zh":"如果看过报纸，你们会知道它确实很轰动。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He smiled with jovial condescension, and added: “Some sensation!”","zh":"他高兴地笑着，带着倨傲的神气，补充说道：“真的是轰动一时呀！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Whereupon everybody laughed.","zh":"话音一落，大家都哈哈大笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The piece is known,” he concluded lustily, “as ‘Vladmir Tostoff’s Jazz History of the World!’ ”","sentences":[{"en":"“The piece is known,” he concluded lustily, “as ‘Vladmir Tostoff’s Jazz History of the World!’ ”","zh":"“这首曲子很著名，”他中气十足地说，“名字叫做《弗拉基米尔·陀斯托夫的爵士世界史》。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The nature of Mr. Tostoff’s composition eluded me, because just as it began my eyes fell on Gatsby, standing alone on the marble steps and looking from one group to another with approving eyes. His tanned skin was drawn attractively tight on his face and his short hair looked as though it were trimmed every day. I could see nothing sinister about him. I wondered if the fact that he was not drinking helped to set him off from his guests, for it seemed to me that he grew more correct as the fraternal hilarity increased. When the “Jazz History of the World” was over, girls were putting their heads on men’s shoulders in a puppyish, convivial way, girls were swooning backward playfully into men’s arms, even into groups, knowing that someone would arrest their falls—but no one swooned backward on Gatsby, and no French bob touched Gatsby’s shoulder, and no singing quartets were formed with Gatsby’s head for one link.","sentences":[{"en":"The nature of Mr. Tostoff’s composition eluded me, because just as it began my eyes fell on Gatsby, standing alone on the marble steps and looking from one group to another with approving eyes.","zh":"我无心欣赏陀斯托夫先生的杰作，因为就在它响起的刹那间，我看见了盖茨比，他独自站在大理石台阶之上，用赞许的眼光扫视花园里的人群。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His tanned skin was drawn attractively tight on his face and his short hair looked as though it were trimmed every day.","zh":"他那晒得泛黄的皮肤在英俊的脸上绷得很紧，头发短得像是每天都有修剪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I could see nothing sinister about him.","zh":"我看不出他有任何邪气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wondered if the fact that he was not drinking helped to set him off from his guests, for it seemed to me that he grew more correct as the fraternal hilarity increased.","zh":"我不知道是不是因为他滴酒不沾的缘故，反正他跟他的客人截然不同；我觉得大家玩得越是疯癫，他就显得越是庄重。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When the “Jazz History of the World” was over, girls were putting their heads on men’s shoulders in a puppyish, convivial way, girls were swooning backward playfully into men’s arms, even into groups, knowing that someone would arrest their falls—but no one swooned backward on Gatsby, and no French bob touched Gatsby’s shoulder, and no singing quartets were formed with Gatsby’s head for one link.","zh":"等到《爵士世界史》一曲终了，有些女孩像哈巴狗似的，甜蜜地把头依偎在男人的肩膀上，有些女孩则高高兴兴地认准某些男人的怀抱倒下去，或者干脆倒进人群里，反正肯定会有人把她们扶住——但没有人倒在盖茨比怀里，没有法式波波头靠住盖茨比的肩膀，也没有人来拉盖茨比去跟他们载歌载舞。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I beg your pardon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I beg your pardon.”","zh":"“打扰了。”盖茨比的管家突然站在我们旁边。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby’s butler was suddenly standing beside us.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby’s butler was suddenly standing beside us.","zh":"“打扰了。”盖茨比的管家突然站在我们旁边。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Miss Baker?” he inquired. “I beg your pardon, but Mr. Gatsby would like to speak to you alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Miss Baker?” he inquired.","zh":"“是贝克小姐吧？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I beg your pardon, but Mr. Gatsby would like to speak to you alone.”","zh":"他问，“打扰您了，盖茨比先生想单独跟您谈谈。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“With me?” she exclaimed in surprise.","sentences":[{"en":"“With me?” she exclaimed in surprise.","zh":"“跟我？”她惊奇地叫了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes, madame.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, madame.”","zh":"“是的，小姐。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She got up slowly, raising her eyebrows at me in astonishment, and followed the butler toward the house. I noticed that she wore her evening-dress, all her dresses, like sports clothes—there was a jauntiness about her movements as if she had first learned to walk upon golf courses on clean, crisp mornings.","sentences":[{"en":"She got up slowly, raising her eyebrows at me in astonishment, and followed the butler toward the house.","zh":"她慢慢站起身，朝我扬扬眉头，表示很吃惊，然后随着管家走进屋里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I noticed that she wore her evening-dress, all her dresses, like sports clothes—there was a jauntiness about her movements as if she had first learned to walk upon golf courses on clean, crisp mornings.","zh":"我发现她穿晚礼服，无论什么衣服，都像穿运动服——她的动作很敏捷，好像她从小就是每天早晨在空气清新的高尔夫球场上学走路似的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was alone and it was almost two. For some time confused and intriguing sounds had issued from a long, many-windowed room which overhung the terrace. Eluding Jordan’s undergraduate, who was now engaged in an obstetrical conversation with two chorus girls, and who implored me to join him, I went inside.","sentences":[{"en":"I was alone and it was almost two.","zh":"我又变得孤家寡人，而且将近两点了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For some time confused and intriguing sounds had issued from a long, many-windowed room which overhung the terrace.","zh":"露台上方那间有着一长排窗户的房间传出阵阵乱七八糟而又引人遐想的声音。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Eluding Jordan’s undergraduate, who was now engaged in an obstetrical conversation with two chorus girls, and who implored me to join him, I went inside.","zh":"陪乔丹来的那大学生正在跟两个合唱团的女孩大谈生孩子的事情，他央求我指点一二，我避之唯恐不及，赶紧走进屋内。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The large room was full of people. One of the girls in yellow was playing the piano, and beside her stood a tall, red-haired young lady from a famous chorus, engaged in song. She had drunk a quantity of champagne, and during the course of her song she had decided, ineptly, that everything was very, very sad—she was not only singing, she was weeping too. Whenever there was a pause in the song she filled it with gasping, broken sobs, and then took up the lyric again in a quavering soprano. The tears coursed down her cheeks—not freely, however, for when they came into contact with her heavily beaded eyelashes they assumed an inky colour, and pursued the rest of their way in slow black rivulets. A humorous suggestion was made that she sing the notes on her face, whereupon she threw up her hands, sank into a chair, and went off into a deep vinous sleep.","sentences":[{"en":"The large room was full of people.","zh":"大客厅里全是人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One of the girls in yellow was playing the piano, and beside her stood a tall, red-haired young lady from a famous chorus, engaged in song.","zh":"两个黄裙女孩中的一个正在弹奏钢琴，在她身边站着的是一位高个子红发少妇，来自某个著名的合唱团，正在放声歌唱。她已经豪饮很多香槟，唱着唱着忽然伤心欲绝——她不仅是在唱歌，她还在哭泣。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She had drunk a quantity of champagne, and during the course of her song she had decided, ineptly, that everything was very, very sad—she was not only singing, she was weeping too.","zh":"两个黄裙女孩中的一个正在弹奏钢琴，在她身边站着的是一位高个子红发少妇，来自某个著名的合唱团，正在放声歌唱。她已经豪饮很多香槟，唱着唱着忽然伤心欲绝——她不仅是在唱歌，她还在哭泣。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Whenever there was a pause in the song she filled it with gasping, broken sobs, and then took up the lyric again in a quavering soprano.","zh":"唱到停顿之处，她失声痛哭，然后再次用颤巍巍的女高音接上歌词。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The tears coursed down her cheeks—not freely, however, for when they came into contact with her heavily beaded eyelashes they assumed an inky colour, and pursued the rest of their way in slow black rivulets.","zh":"泪水沿着她的脸颊滚滚而下——然而并非畅通无阻，因为泪水碰到画得很浓的睫毛之后就变成了墨水，宛如两道黑色的小溪，慢慢地往下流完剩余的旅程。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A humorous suggestion was made that she sing the notes on her face, whereupon she threw up her hands, sank into a chair, and went off into a deep vinous sleep.","zh":"有人开玩笑地建议她唱脸上的音符，她听见之后双手往上一摆，瘫坐在椅子里，醉醺醺地睡着了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She had a fight with a man who says he’s her husband,” explained a girl at my elbow.","sentences":[{"en":"“She had a fight with a man who says he’s her husband,” explained a girl at my elbow.","zh":"“她刚才和一个自称是她丈夫的人吵架了，”我身边有个女孩解释说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I looked around. Most of the remaining women were now having fights with men said to be their husbands. Even Jordan’s party, the quartet from East Egg, were rent asunder by dissension. One of the men was talking with curious intensity to a young actress, and his wife, after attempting to laugh at the situation in a dignified and indifferent way, broke down entirely and resorted to flank attacks—at intervals she appeared suddenly at his side like an angry diamond, and hissed: “You promised!” into his ear.","sentences":[{"en":"I looked around.","zh":"我看看四周。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Most of the remaining women were now having fights with men said to be their husbands.","zh":"大多数尚未告辞的妇女正在跟她们所谓的丈夫吵架。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Even Jordan’s party, the quartet from East Egg, were rent asunder by dissension.","zh":"甚至连乔丹那伙人，那两对从东卵来的夫妇，也产生了分歧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One of the men was talking with curious intensity to a young actress, and his wife, after attempting to laugh at the situation in a dignified and indifferent way, broke down entirely and resorted to flank attacks—at intervals she appeared suddenly at his side like an angry diamond, and hissed: “You promised!” into his ear.","zh":"其中有个男的色迷迷地和一个年轻的女演员聊天，他老婆开始还顾着脸面，装出满不在乎的样子，后来实在受不了，于是开始旁敲侧击——时不时突然贴到她丈夫身旁，像愤怒的毒蛇般，在他耳边嘶嘶地说：“你答应过我的！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The reluctance to go home was not confined to wayward men. The hall was at present occupied by two deplorably sober men and their highly indignant wives. The wives were sympathizing with each other in slightly raised voices.","sentences":[{"en":"The reluctance to go home was not confined to wayward men.","zh":"迟迟不愿归去的不只是心怀不轨的男宾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The hall was at present occupied by two deplorably sober men and their highly indignant wives.","zh":"这时门厅里站着两个清醒的可怜男人，以及他们极其愤慨的妻子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The wives were sympathizing with each other in slightly raised voices.","zh":"两位太太正在彼此表示同情，她们的声音稍微有点高。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Whenever he sees I’m having a good time he wants to go home.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Whenever he sees I’m having a good time he wants to go home.”","zh":"“每当我玩得很高兴，他就闹着要回家。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Never heard anything so selfish in my life.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Never heard anything so selfish in my life.”","zh":"“我这辈子从来没听说过这么自私的事情。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’re always the first ones to leave.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We’re always the first ones to leave.”","zh":"“我们总是最早离开的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“So are we.”","sentences":[{"en":"“So are we.”","zh":"“我们也是啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, we’re almost the last tonight,” said one of the men sheepishly. “The orchestra left half an hour ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, we’re almost the last tonight,” said one of the men sheepishly.","zh":"“好啦，今晚我们几乎是最晚离开的了，”有个男人说，口气温驯得像绵羊，“乐团半个小时前就离开啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“The orchestra left half an hour ago.”","zh":"“好啦，今晚我们几乎是最晚离开的了，”有个男人说，口气温驯得像绵羊，“乐团半个小时前就离开啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"In spite of the wives’ agreement that such malevolence was beyond credibility, the dispute ended in a short struggle, and both wives were lifted, kicking, into the night.","sentences":[{"en":"In spite of the wives’ agreement that such malevolence was beyond credibility, the dispute ended in a short struggle, and both wives were lifted, kicking, into the night.","zh":"尽管太太们认为现在就走简直是胡作非为，这场纠纷终于在短暂的缠斗中结束了，两位双脚乱踢的太太被抱进了黑夜。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As I waited for my hat in the hall the door of the library opened and Jordan Baker and Gatsby came out together. He was saying some last word to her, but the eagerness in his manner tightened abruptly into formality as several people approached him to say goodbye.","sentences":[{"en":"As I waited for my hat in the hall the door of the library opened and Jordan Baker and Gatsby came out together.","zh":"我在门厅等佣人把我的帽子拿来，这时书房的门打开，乔丹·贝克和盖茨比一起走了出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was saying some last word to her, but the eagerness in his manner tightened abruptly into formality as several people approached him to say goodbye.","zh":"他还在跟乔丹说话，但他恳切的神情随即变得很客套，因为有几个人走过去跟他道别。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Jordan’s party were calling impatiently to her from the porch, but she lingered for a moment to shake hands.","sentences":[{"en":"Jordan’s party were calling impatiently to her from the porch, but she lingered for a moment to shake hands.","zh":"那几个东卵来的人在门廊不耐烦地招呼乔丹，但她留下来跟我握手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve just heard the most amazing thing,” she whispered. “How long were we in there?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve just heard the most amazing thing,” she whispered.","zh":"“我刚刚听说了最离奇的事情，”她低声说，“我们在那边待了多久？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“How long were we in there?”","zh":"“我刚刚听说了最离奇的事情，”她低声说，“我们在那边待了多久？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why, about an hour.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, about an hour.”","zh":"“大概一个小时吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was… simply amazing,” she repeated abstractedly. “But I swore I wouldn’t tell it and here I am tantalizing you.” She yawned gracefully in my face. “Please come and see me… Phone book… Under the name of Mrs. Sigourney Howard… My aunt…” She was hurrying off as she talked—her brown hand waved a jaunty salute as she melted into her party at the door.","sentences":[{"en":"“It was… simply amazing,” she repeated abstractedly.","zh":"“实在是太…太离奇了，”她魂不守舍地重复说，“我刚才发誓不说出来的，但现在我又在逗你。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“But I swore I wouldn’t tell it and here I am tantalizing you.”","zh":"“实在是太…太离奇了，”她魂不守舍地重复说，“我刚才发誓不说出来的，但现在我又在逗你。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She yawned gracefully in my face.","zh":"她优雅地在我面前打了个哈欠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Please come and see me…","zh":"“有空来看看我呀…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Phone book…","zh":"电话黄页…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Under the name of Mrs. Sigourney Howard…","zh":"西格尔尼·霍华德太太的名字下面…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My aunt…”","zh":"是我姑妈…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was hurrying off as she talked—her brown hand waved a jaunty salute as she melted into her party at the door.","zh":"”她边说边匆忙走开——她那棕色的手干净利落地挥了一下跟我告别，然后在门口跟那几个人会合了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Rather ashamed that on my first appearance I had stayed so late, I joined the last of Gatsby’s guests, who were clustered around him. I wanted to explain that I’d hunted for him early in the evening and to apologize for not having known him in the garden.","sentences":[{"en":"Rather ashamed that on my first appearance I had stayed so late, I joined the last of Gatsby’s guests, who were clustered around him.","zh":"第一次来做客就待到这么晚，我觉得怪不好意思的，所以效仿最后那批客人，走到盖茨比身边去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wanted to explain that I’d hunted for him early in the evening and to apologize for not having known him in the garden.","zh":"我解释说当晚早些时候我找过他，并为在花园里没认出他而道歉。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t mention it,” he enjoined me eagerly. “Don’t give it another thought, old sport.” The familiar expression held no more familiarity than the hand which reassuringly brushed my shoulder. “And don’t forget we’re going up in the hydroplane tomorrow morning, at nine o’clock.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t mention it,” he enjoined me eagerly.","zh":"“别提啦，”他诚恳地吩咐我，“别放在心上，老兄。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Don’t give it another thought, old sport.”","zh":"“别提啦，”他诚恳地吩咐我，“别放在心上，老兄。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"The familiar expression held no more familiarity than the hand which reassuringly brushed my shoulder.","zh":"除了嘴上套近乎，他的手也很亲热地拍拍我的肩膀，要我放心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“And don’t forget we’re going up in the hydroplane tomorrow morning, at nine o’clock.”","zh":"“别忘了我们明天早上要去试乘水上飞机，就在九点。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Then the butler, behind his shoulder:","sentences":[{"en":"Then the butler, behind his shoulder:","zh":"接着管家出现在他身后。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Philadelphia wants you on the phone, sir.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Philadelphia wants you on the phone, sir.”","zh":"“老爷，费城有电话找你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right, in a minute. Tell them I’ll be right there… Good night.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right, in a minute.","zh":"“好的，马上就来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell them I’ll be right there…","zh":"告诉他们我马上就来…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good night.”","zh":"晚安。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Good night.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good night.”","zh":"“晚安。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Good night.” He smiled—and suddenly there seemed to be a pleasant significance in having been among the last to go, as if he had desired it all the time. “Good night, old sport… Good night.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good night.”","zh":"“晚安，”他笑着说——突然间我觉得他很高兴看到我这么晚才走，似乎这正是他一直所希望看到的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He smiled—and suddenly there seemed to be a pleasant significance in having been among the last to go, as if he had desired it all the time.","zh":"“晚安，”他笑着说——突然间我觉得他很高兴看到我这么晚才走，似乎这正是他一直所希望看到的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Good night, old sport…","zh":"“晚安，老兄…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good night.”","zh":"晚安。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But as I walked down the steps I saw that the evening was not quite over. Fifty feet from the door a dozen headlights illuminated a bizarre and tumultuous scene. In the ditch beside the road, right side up, but violently shorn of one wheel, rested a new coupé which had left Gatsby’s drive not two minutes before. The sharp jut of a wall accounted for the detachment of the wheel, which was now getting considerable attention from half a dozen curious chauffeurs. However, as they had left their cars blocking the road, a harsh, discordant din from those in the rear had been audible for some time, and added to the already violent confusion of the scene.","sentences":[{"en":"But as I walked down the steps I saw that the evening was not quite over.","zh":"但走下台阶时，我发现今晚曲虽已终，人却未散。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Fifty feet from the door a dozen headlights illuminated a bizarre and tumultuous scene.","zh":"大门口五十英尺开外，十几个车头灯照亮了一个古怪而混乱的场面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the ditch beside the road, right side up, but violently shorn of one wheel, rested a new coupé which had left Gatsby’s drive not two minutes before.","zh":"路边的水沟里，有辆两分钟前才从盖茨比家驶出的新车左边陷了下去，轮胎也掉了一个。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sharp jut of a wall accounted for the detachment of the wheel, which was now getting considerable attention from half a dozen curious chauffeurs.","zh":"导致轮胎脱落的罪魁祸首是围墙突出的一块石头，这时有五六个好奇的司机在现场指指点点。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, as they had left their cars blocking the road, a harsh, discordant din from those in the rear had been audible for some time, and added to the already violent confusion of the scene.","zh":"可是他们留下的车把路堵住了，那些被挡在后面的车辆响起了此起彼伏的喇叭声，让整个场面变得更加混乱。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A man in a long duster had dismounted from the wreck and now stood in the middle of the road, looking from the car to the tyre and from the tyre to the observers in a pleasant, puzzled way.","sentences":[{"en":"A man in a long duster had dismounted from the wreck and now stood in the middle of the road, looking from the car to the tyre and from the tyre to the observers in a pleasant, puzzled way.","zh":"有个穿着长风衣的人从事故车辆下来，站在马路中央，从轿车看到轮胎，从轮胎看到旁观者，一副既觉得好玩又大惑不解的表情。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“See!” he explained. “It went in the ditch.”","sentences":[{"en":"“See!” he explained.","zh":"“看！”他解释说，“我刚才掉进水沟了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It went in the ditch.”","zh":"“看！”他解释说，“我刚才掉进水沟了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The fact was infinitely astonishing to him, and I recognized first the unusual quality of wonder, and then the man—it was the late patron of Gatsby’s library.","sentences":[{"en":"The fact was infinitely astonishing to him, and I recognized first the unusual quality of wonder, and then the man—it was the late patron of Gatsby’s library.","zh":"看来这件事让他感到无限的惊奇，我先是认出了这大惊小怪的口气，然后认出了这个人——原来就是刚才在盖茨比书房遇到的那位仁兄。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How’d it happen?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How’d it happen?”","zh":"“怎么会这样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He shrugged his shoulders.","sentences":[{"en":"He shrugged his shoulders.","zh":"他耸了耸肩膀。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I know nothing whatever about mechanics,” he said decisively.","sentences":[{"en":"“I know nothing whatever about mechanics,” he said decisively.","zh":"“机械方面我真是一窍不通，”他斩钉截铁地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But how did it happen? Did you run into the wall?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But how did it happen?","zh":"“但是怎么出事的呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did you run into the wall?”","zh":"你撞上围墙了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t ask me,” said Owl Eyes, washing his hands of the whole matter. “I know very little about driving—next to nothing. It happened, and that’s all I know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t ask me,” said Owl Eyes, washing his hands of the whole matter.","zh":"“别问我，”猫头鹰眼镜先生说，把责任推得干干净净，“我不懂开车——完全不懂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I know very little about driving—next to nothing.","zh":"“别问我，”猫头鹰眼镜先生说，把责任推得干干净净，“我不懂开车——完全不懂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It happened, and that’s all I know.”","zh":"反正发生事故了，我只知道这么多。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, if you’re a poor driver you oughtn’t to try driving at night.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, if you’re a poor driver you oughtn’t to try driving at night.”","zh":"“既然你技术不行，就不应该在夜里学开车。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But I wasn’t even trying,” he explained indignantly, “I wasn’t even trying.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But I wasn’t even trying,” he explained indignantly, “I wasn’t even trying.”","zh":"“但我没有学过，”他愤愤不平地解释说，“我根本没有学过。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"An awed hush fell upon the bystanders.","sentences":[{"en":"An awed hush fell upon the bystanders.","zh":"旁观者震惊得安静了下来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do you want to commit suicide?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you want to commit suicide?”","zh":"“你想找死吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re lucky it was just a wheel! A bad driver and not even trying!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re lucky it was just a wheel!","zh":"“幸好只是掉了个车轮！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A bad driver and not even trying!”","zh":"开得这么烂，还不去学！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You don’t understand,” explained the criminal. “I wasn’t driving. There’s another man in the car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You don’t understand,” explained the criminal.","zh":"“你们不知道的啦，”这罪人说，“开车的人不是我。车里还有个人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I wasn’t driving.","zh":"“你们不知道的啦，”这罪人说，“开车的人不是我。车里还有个人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"There’s another man in the car.”","zh":"“你们不知道的啦，”这罪人说，“开车的人不是我。车里还有个人。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The shock that followed this declaration found voice in a sustained “Ah-h-h!” as the door of the coupé swung slowly open. The crowd—it was now a crowd—stepped back involuntarily, and when the door had opened wide there was a ghostly pause. Then, very gradually, part by part, a pale, dangling individual stepped out of the wreck, pawing tentatively at the ground with a large uncertain dancing shoe.","sentences":[{"en":"The shock that followed this declaration found voice in a sustained “Ah-h-h!” as the door of the coupé swung slowly open.","zh":"听了这句话，大家感到更为震惊，纷纷地发出“啊！”的声音。这时那辆车的车门慢慢地打开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The crowd—it was now a crowd—stepped back involuntarily, and when the door had opened wide there was a ghostly pause.","zh":"围观的人群——这时围过来的人已经很多——情不自禁地后退了几步，车门打开后静悄悄的毫无动静。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, very gradually, part by part, a pale, dangling individual stepped out of the wreck, pawing tentatively at the ground with a large uncertain dancing shoe.","zh":"然后非常缓慢地，一点一点地，有个脸色苍白、摇摇晃晃的人从出事的车里伸出脚来，犹疑不定地用那只巨大的舞鞋试探地踩了几下地面。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Blinded by the glare of the headlights and confused by the incessant groaning of the horns, the apparition stood swaying for a moment before he perceived the man in the duster.","sentences":[{"en":"Blinded by the glare of the headlights and confused by the incessant groaning of the horns, the apparition stood swaying for a moment before he perceived the man in the duster.","zh":"这个幽灵被明亮的车灯照得睁不开眼，又被持续不断的喇叭声吵得稀里糊涂，他颤巍巍地站了片刻，方始认出那个穿长风衣的人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wha’s matter?” he inquired calmly. “Did we run outa gas?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wha’s matter?” he inquired calmly.","zh":"“怎么回事？”他镇定地问，“我们没油了吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Did we run outa gas?”","zh":"“怎么回事？”他镇定地问，“我们没油了吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look!”","zh":"“看！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Half a dozen fingers pointed at the amputated wheel—he stared at it for a moment, and then looked upward as though he suspected that it had dropped from the sky.","sentences":[{"en":"Half a dozen fingers pointed at the amputated wheel—he stared at it for a moment, and then looked upward as though he suspected that it had dropped from the sky.","zh":"五六根手指指着那脱落的车轮——他盯着车轮看了一会，然后抬头向上看，似乎在怀疑车轮是从天上掉下来的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It came off,” someone explained.","sentences":[{"en":"“It came off,” someone explained.","zh":"“车轮掉了，”有人解释说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"He nodded.","zh":"他点点头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“At first I din’ notice we’d stopped.”","sentences":[{"en":"“At first I din’ notice we’d stopped.”","zh":"“刚开始我还没发现车停了呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A pause. Then, taking a long breath and straightening his shoulders, he remarked in a determined voice:","sentences":[{"en":"A pause.","zh":"隔了片刻，他深深地吸一口气，挺起胸膛，终于做出决定似的说：“请问哪里有加油站？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, taking a long breath and straightening his shoulders, he remarked in a determined voice:","zh":"隔了片刻，他深深地吸一口气，挺起胸膛，终于做出决定似的说：“请问哪里有加油站？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wonder’ff tell me where there’s a gas’line station?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wonder’ff tell me where there’s a gas’line station?”","zh":"隔了片刻，他深深地吸一口气，挺起胸膛，终于做出决定似的说：“请问哪里有加油站？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At least a dozen men, some of them a little better off than he was, explained to him that wheel and car were no longer joined by any physical bond.","sentences":[{"en":"At least a dozen men, some of them a little better off than he was, explained to him that wheel and car were no longer joined by any physical bond.","zh":"至少有十来个人——有几个比他清醒不了多少——争先恐后地对他说，车轮和车身已经没有任何实质性的联系了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Back out,” he suggested after a moment. “Put her in reverse.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Back out,” he suggested after a moment.","zh":"“倒车，”他沉默一会之后提议，“挂倒车挡。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Put her in reverse.”","zh":"“倒车，”他沉默一会之后提议，“挂倒车挡。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But the wheel’s off!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But the wheel’s off!”","zh":"“但车轮掉了！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He hesitated.","sentences":[{"en":"He hesitated.","zh":"他迟疑着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No harm in trying,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“No harm in trying,” he said.","zh":"“试试也无妨嘛，”他说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The caterwauling horns had reached a crescendo and I turned away and cut across the lawn toward home. I glanced back once. A wafer of a moon was shining over Gatsby’s house, making the night fine as before, and surviving the laughter and the sound of his still glowing garden. A sudden emptiness seemed to flow now from the windows and the great doors, endowing with complete isolation the figure of the host, who stood on the porch, his hand up in a formal gesture of farewell.","sentences":[{"en":"The caterwauling horns had reached a crescendo and I turned away and cut across the lawn toward home.","zh":"刺耳的喇叭声越来越响，我转过身，穿过草坪走回家。我回头望了一眼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I glanced back once.","zh":"圆圆的月亮照耀着盖茨比的豪宅，使夜色美好得如同往常。他的花园里仍是灯火辉煌，但欢声笑语已消逝，唯有明月依旧在。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A wafer of a moon was shining over Gatsby’s house, making the night fine as before, and surviving the laughter and the sound of his still glowing garden.","zh":"圆圆的月亮照耀着盖茨比的豪宅，使夜色美好得如同往常。他的花园里仍是灯火辉煌，但欢声笑语已消逝，唯有明月依旧在。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A sudden emptiness seemed to flow now from the windows and the great doors, endowing with complete isolation the figure of the host, who stood on the porch, his hand up in a formal gesture of farewell.","zh":"一阵突如其来的空虚仿佛正从那些窗户和房门流溢而出，让主人的身影益发显得孤独：此际他独自站在门廊上，举手摆出依依惜别的姿势。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"Reading over what I have written so far, I see I have given the impression that the events of three nights several weeks apart were all that absorbed me. On the contrary, they were merely casual events in a crowded summer, and, until much later, they absorbed me infinitely less than my personal affairs.","sentences":[{"en":"Reading over what I have written so far, I see I have given the impression that the events of three nights several weeks apart were all that absorbed me.","zh":"翻读前面写下的文字，我发现我给人一种印象，好像除了在三个相隔数周的夜晚参加这些活动，我整天无所事事似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the contrary, they were merely casual events in a crowded summer, and, until much later, they absorbed me infinitely less than my personal affairs.","zh":"事实恰好相反，那年夏天我很忙，这些只是无关紧要的活动，而且随后很长一段时间里，我耗在私事上的时间，远远比参加这些活动要多。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Most of the time I worked. In the early morning the sun threw my shadow westward as I hurried down the white chasms of lower New York to the Probity Trust. I knew the other clerks and young bond-salesmen by their first names, and lunched with them in dark, crowded restaurants on little pig sausages and mashed potatoes and coffee. I even had a short affair with a girl who lived in Jersey City and worked in the accounting department, but her brother began throwing mean looks in my direction, so when she went on her vacation in July I let it blow quietly away.","sentences":[{"en":"Most of the time I worked.","zh":"大多数时间我在工作。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the early morning the sun threw my shadow westward as I hurried down the white chasms of lower New York to the Probity Trust.","zh":"每日清晨，我背对太阳，踏着自己的影子，在纽约下城诸多摩天大楼之间匆匆走向正诚信托。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I knew the other clerks and young bond-salesmen by their first names, and lunched with them in dark, crowded restaurants on little pig sausages and mashed potatoes and coffee.","zh":"我和公司里其他文员及年轻的债券销售员混得很熟，到了中午，我跟他们去那些阴暗拥挤的小饭店，买点猪肉肠、土豆泥和咖啡当午饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I even had a short affair with a girl who lived in Jersey City and worked in the accounting department, but her brother began throwing mean looks in my direction, so when she went on her vacation in July I let it blow quietly away.","zh":"我甚至和某个姑娘有过短暂的交往，她住在泽西城，是会计部的职员。但她哥哥后来总是给我脸色看，所以七月份她去度假时，我就趁机结束了这段关系。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I took dinner usually at the Yale Club—for some reason it was the gloomiest event of my day—and then I went upstairs to the library and studied investments and securities for a conscientious hour. There were generally a few rioters around, but they never came into the library, so it was a good place to work. After that, if the night was mellow, I strolled down Madison Avenue past the old Murray Hill Hotel, and over 33rd Street to the Pennsylvania Station.","sentences":[{"en":"I took dinner usually at the Yale Club—for some reason it was the gloomiest event of my day—and then I went upstairs to the library and studied investments and securities for a conscientious hour.","zh":"晚饭我通常是在耶鲁俱乐部吃的——不知道怎么回事，我觉得这是每天最凄凉的活动。饭后我会去楼上的资料室，聚精会神地研究一小时的投资和证券。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were generally a few rioters around, but they never came into the library, so it was a good place to work.","zh":"俱乐部里往往会有几个吵闹的人，但他们从不进资料室，所以那里是学习的好地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After that, if the night was mellow, I strolled down Madison Avenue past the old Murray Hill Hotel, and over 33rd Street to the Pennsylvania Station.","zh":"自修后，如果夜色美好，我会沿着麦迪逊大道散步，经过古老的穆雷山酒店，再沿着第三十三街走到宾夕法尼亚火车站。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I began to like New York, the racy, adventurous feel of it at night, and the satisfaction that the constant flicker of men and women and machines gives to the restless eye. I liked to walk up Fifth Avenue and pick out romantic women from the crowd and imagine that in a few minutes I was going to enter into their lives, and no one would ever know or disapprove. Sometimes, in my mind, I followed them to their apartments on the corners of hidden streets, and they turned and smiled back at me before they faded through a door into warm darkness. At the enchanted metropolitan twilight I felt a haunting loneliness sometimes, and felt it in others—poor young clerks who loitered in front of windows waiting until it was time for a solitary restaurant dinner—young clerks in the dusk, wasting the most poignant moments of night and life.","sentences":[{"en":"I began to like New York, the racy, adventurous feel of it at night, and the satisfaction that the constant flicker of men and women and machines gives to the restless eye.","zh":"我渐渐喜欢上纽约，这里的夜晚别有活力十足而引人入胜的情调，摩肩接踵的红男绿女和川流不息的往来车辆让人感到目不暇给和心满意足。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I liked to walk up Fifth Avenue and pick out romantic women from the crowd and imagine that in a few minutes I was going to enter into their lives, and no one would ever know or disapprove.","zh":"我喜欢沿着第五大道朝北走，从人潮中挑选出罗曼蒂克的女人，幻想再过几分钟我就要进入她们的生活，没有人会知道或指责我想入非非。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes, in my mind, I followed them to their apartments on the corners of hidden streets, and they turned and smiled back at me before they faded through a door into warm darkness.","zh":"有时候，我在脑海里尾随着她们，跟到她们位于某个阴暗街角的公寓，她们转过头来，朝我嫣然一笑，然后走进门，消失在温暖的黑暗里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the enchanted metropolitan twilight I felt a haunting loneliness sometimes, and felt it in others—poor young clerks who loitered in front of windows waiting until it was time for a solitary restaurant dinner—young clerks in the dusk, wasting the most poignant moments of night and life.","zh":"这大都会的黄昏很迷人，可我偶尔会有挥之不去的孤寂，每当看见那些囊中羞涩的年轻职员在商店橱窗之前倘佯，捱到晚饭时间形影相吊地去餐厅填肚子，我知道他们也深有同感——我们这些薄暮中的年轻职员啊，正在虚度一生中最灿烂的年华、一夜中最美好的时辰。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Again at eight o’clock, when the dark lanes of the Forties were lined five deep with throbbing taxicabs, bound for the theatre district, I felt a sinking in my heart. Forms leaned together in the taxis as they waited, and voices sang, and there was laughter from unheard jokes, and lighted cigarettes made unintelligible circles inside. Imagining that I, too, was hurrying towards gaiety and sharing their intimate excitement, I wished them well.","sentences":[{"en":"Again at eight o’clock, when the dark lanes of the Forties were lined five deep with throbbing taxicabs, bound for the theatre district, I felt a sinking in my heart.","zh":"到了晚上八点，第四十几街那边灯光昏黄，开向戏院区的出租车突突地响着，把五车道的马路挤得水泄不通，这时我的心会再次感到怅惘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Forms leaned together in the taxis as they waited, and voices sang, and there was laughter from unheard jokes, and lighted cigarettes made unintelligible circles inside.","zh":"出租车停下时，车窗里人影依偎，歌声飘荡，听不见的谑词引起了笑声，被点燃的香烟划出细小的圆圈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Imagining that I, too, was hurrying towards gaiety and sharing their intimate excitement, I wished them well.","zh":"我幻想我也匆匆赶去寻欢作乐，分享这种恋人密友间的兴奋。我暗暗地为他们祝福。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For a while I lost sight of Jordan Baker, and then in midsummer I found her again. At first I was flattered to go places with her, because she was a golf champion, and everyone knew her name. Then it was something more. I wasn’t actually in love, but I felt a sort of tender curiosity. The bored haughty face that she turned to the world concealed something—most affectations conceal something eventually, even though they don’t in the beginning—and one day I found what it was. When we were on a house-party together up in Warwick, she left a borrowed car out in the rain with the top down, and then lied about it—and suddenly I remembered the story about her that had eluded me that night at Daisy’s. At her first big golf tournament there was a row that nearly reached the newspapers—a suggestion that she had moved her ball from a bad lie in the semifinal round. The thing approached the proportions of a scandal—then died away. A caddy retracted his statement, and the only other witness admitted that he might have been mistaken. The incident and the name had remained together in my mind.","sentences":[{"en":"For a while I lost sight of Jordan Baker, and then in midsummer I found her again.","zh":"我很久没有见到乔丹·贝克，然后到了盛夏我又与她相遇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At first I was flattered to go places with her, because she was a golf champion, and everyone knew her name.","zh":"起初我为有幸和她出双入对而感到飘飘然，因为她拿过高尔夫球赛冠军，每个人都知道她的大名。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then it was something more.","zh":"后来我的感情发生了变化。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wasn’t actually in love, but I felt a sort of tender curiosity.","zh":"其实我没有爱上她，但对她有种温柔的好奇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The bored haughty face that she turned to the world concealed something—most affectations conceal something eventually, even though they don’t in the beginning—and one day I found what it was.","zh":"她摆给世人看的那张厌世而骄傲的面孔隐藏着某种东西——大多数装腔作势最终都隐藏着什么，哪怕它们起初并不如此——后来我发现那种东西是什么了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When we were on a house-party together up in Warwick, she left a borrowed car out in the rain with the top down, and then lied about it—and suddenly I remembered the story about her that had eluded me that night at Daisy’s.","zh":"那天我们北上瓦维克，去参加某个家庭宴会，她借了一辆敞篷车，停车时没将车篷升起，车被雨淋湿了，但后来她说了谎话——于是我突然忆起那夜我在黛熙家想不起来的故事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At her first big golf tournament there was a row that nearly reached the newspapers—a suggestion that she had moved her ball from a bad lie in the semifinal round.","zh":"她第一次参加高尔夫球大奖赛就发生了一件差点闹上报纸的纠纷——有人说她在半决赛时做了手脚，偷偷把球挪到好位置上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The thing approached the proportions of a scandal—then died away.","zh":"这引起了轩然大波——后来却平息了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A caddy retracted his statement, and the only other witness admitted that he might have been mistaken.","zh":"有个球童收回了他的话，仅有的目击者也承认他有可能看错。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The incident and the name had remained together in my mind.","zh":"但这件事，连同她的名字，都留在我脑海里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Jordan Baker instinctively avoided clever, shrewd men, and now I saw that this was because she felt safer on a plane where any divergence from a code would be thought impossible. She was incurably dishonest. She wasn’t able to endure being at a disadvantage and, given this unwillingness, I suppose she had begun dealing in subterfuges when she was very young in order to keep that cool, insolent smile turned to the world and yet satisfy the demands of her hard, jaunty body.","sentences":[{"en":"Jordan Baker instinctively avoided clever, shrewd men, and now I saw that this was because she felt safer on a plane where any divergence from a code would be thought impossible.","zh":"乔丹·贝克本能地避开那些聪明而狡猾的男人，现在我才明白，这是因为她觉得跟那些从不离经叛道的老实人来往比较保险。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was incurably dishonest.","zh":"她不诚实得无可救药。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wasn’t able to endure being at a disadvantage and, given this unwillingness, I suppose she had begun dealing in subterfuges when she was very young in order to keep that cool, insolent smile turned to the world and yet satisfy the demands of her hard, jaunty body.","zh":"她无法忍受落人下风，我想正是由于这种争强好胜的性格，导致她从小就学会了各种骗人的花招，这样她才能对世人摆出冷漠而倨傲的笑脸，却还能满足她那漂亮结实的身体的各种需求。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It made no difference to me. Dishonesty in a woman is a thing you never blame deeply—I was casually sorry, and then I forgot. It was on that same house-party that we had a curious conversation about driving a car. It started because she passed so close to some workmen that our fender flicked a button on one man’s coat.","sentences":[{"en":"It made no difference to me.","zh":"我觉得这没什么。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Dishonesty in a woman is a thing you never blame deeply—I was casually sorry, and then I forgot.","zh":"女人爱说谎倒也算不上特别严重的缺点——我当时觉得很可惜，后来就忘记了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was on that same house-party that we had a curious conversation about driving a car.","zh":"也是去参加家庭宴会那天，我们就开车的问题有过一段奇怪的对话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It started because she passed so close to some workmen that our fender flicked a button on one man’s coat.","zh":"我们谈起这个话题，是因为她开车从几个工人身边经过时挨得太近，以至于轮胎上的挡泥板擦到了一个工人外套上的纽扣。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re a rotten driver,” I protested. “Either you ought to be more careful, or you oughtn’t to drive at all.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re a rotten driver,” I protested.","zh":"“你的驾驶技术真烂，”我抗议说，“你要么小心点，要么干脆别开车。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Either you ought to be more careful, or you oughtn’t to drive at all.”","zh":"“你的驾驶技术真烂，”我抗议说，“你要么小心点，要么干脆别开车。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I am careful.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I am careful.”","zh":"“我很小心的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, you’re not.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, you’re not.”","zh":"“你很小心才怪。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, other people are,” she said lightly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, other people are,” she said lightly.","zh":"“好吧，别人会小心的，”她若无其事地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s that got to do with it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s that got to do with it?”","zh":"“这跟你开车有什么关系？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They’ll keep out of my way,” she insisted. “It takes two to make an accident.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They’ll keep out of my way,” she insisted.","zh":"“他们会避开我啊，”她固执地说，“要双方都不小心才会出车祸。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It takes two to make an accident.”","zh":"“他们会避开我啊，”她固执地说，“要双方都不小心才会出车祸。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Suppose you met somebody just as careless as yourself.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Suppose you met somebody just as careless as yourself.”","zh":"“假如你遇到某个像你这样不小心的人呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I hope I never will,” she answered. “I hate careless people. That’s why I like you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I hope I never will,” she answered.","zh":"“我希望我永远不要遇到，”她回答说，“我讨厌不小心的人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I hate careless people.","zh":"“我希望我永远不要遇到，”她回答说，“我讨厌不小心的人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"That’s why I like you.”","zh":"所以我喜欢你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her grey, sun-strained eyes stared straight ahead, but she had deliberately shifted our relations, and for a moment I thought I loved her. But I am slow-thinking and full of interior rules that act as brakes on my desires, and I knew that first I had to get myself definitely out of that tangle back home. I’d been writing letters once a week and signing them: “Love, Nick,” and all I could think of was how, when that certain girl played tennis, a faint moustache of perspiration appeared on her upper lip. Nevertheless there was a vague understanding that had to be tactfully broken off before I was free.","sentences":[{"en":"Her grey, sun-strained eyes stared straight ahead, but she had deliberately shifted our relations, and for a moment I thought I loved her.","zh":"她那双被太阳照得眯起来的灰色眼睛专注地望着前方，但她这句话改变了我们的关系，刹那间，我想我爱上她了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I am slow-thinking and full of interior rules that act as brakes on my desires, and I knew that first I had to get myself definitely out of that tangle back home.","zh":"但我是个愚钝的人，内心有许多做人的准则，它们刹住了我的欲望。我知道我首先应该彻底从家乡那段感情纠葛中脱身。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’d been writing letters once a week and signing them: “Love, Nick,” and all I could think of was how, when that certain girl played tennis, a faint moustache of perspiration appeared on her upper lip.","zh":"我每周寄回几封信，落款写着“爱你的尼克”。关于那个女孩，我没有太多的印象，只记得她每次打完网球，嘴唇上的汗珠看上去很像汗毛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nevertheless there was a vague understanding that had to be tactfully broken off before I was free.","zh":"不管怎么说，我们确实有着未经挑明的恋爱关系，我得想办法把它解除了，才可以爱别人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Everyone suspects himself of at least one of the cardinal virtues, and this is mine: I am one of the few honest people that I have ever known.","sentences":[{"en":"Everyone suspects himself of at least one of the cardinal virtues, and this is mine: I am one of the few honest people that I have ever known.","zh":"每个人都怀疑自己身上至少有一种美德，我是这么想的：据我所知，世界上诚实的人不多，而我是其中一个。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-4","n":4,"title":"Chapter IV","titleZh":"第四章","paragraphs":[{"en":"On Sunday morning while church bells rang in the villages alongshore, the world and its mistress returned to Gatsby’s house and twinkled hilariously on his lawn.","sentences":[{"en":"On Sunday morning while church bells rang in the villages alongshore, the world and its mistress returned to Gatsby’s house and twinkled hilariously on his lawn.","zh":"礼拜天早晨，当钟声从沿岸各处村庄的教堂响起，许多名流贤达带着情妇重返盖茨比的别墅，在他的草坪上尽情挥洒着欢乐。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He’s a bootlegger,” said the young ladies, moving somewhere between his cocktails and his flowers. “One time he killed a man who had found out that he was nephew to Von Hindenburg and second cousin to the devil. Reach me a rose, honey, and pour me a last drop into that there crystal glass.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He’s a bootlegger,” said the young ladies, moving somewhere between his cocktails and his flowers.","zh":"那些年轻的女人喝着他的酒，赏着他的花，同时说：“他是个走私烈酒的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“One time he killed a man who had found out that he was nephew to Von Hindenburg and second cousin to the devil.","zh":"曾经有人打探出他是兴登堡的侄儿，是那个杀人魔王的近亲。他把那人杀了灭口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Reach me a rose, honey, and pour me a last drop into that there crystal glass.”","zh":"摘朵玫瑰给我呀，亲爱的，再替我倒点酒，我的水晶杯在那边。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Once I wrote down on the empty spaces of a timetable the names of those who came to Gatsby’s house that summer. It is an old timetable now, disintegrating at its folds, and headed “This schedule in effect July 5th, 1922.” But I can still read the grey names, and they will give you a better impression than my generalities of those who accepted Gatsby’s hospitality and paid him the subtle tribute of knowing nothing whatever about him.","sentences":[{"en":"Once I wrote down on the empty spaces of a timetable the names of those who came to Gatsby’s house that summer.","zh":"我曾在一张火车时刻表的空白处写下那年夏天去盖茨比家做客的那些人的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is an old timetable now, disintegrating at its folds, and headed “This schedule in effect July 5th, 1922.”","zh":"这张时刻表现在很破旧了，折叠处就要裂开，上面印着“此表1922年7月5日起生效”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I can still read the grey names, and they will give you a better impression than my generalities of those who accepted Gatsby’s hospitality and paid him the subtle tribute of knowing nothing whatever about him.","zh":"但我依然能看清那些暗淡的名字。和我笼统的介绍相比，这张时刻表能让你更清楚哪些人接受过盖茨比的热情招待，而回赠给他的，却是对他的一无所知。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"From East Egg, then, came the Chester Beckers and the Leeches, and a man named Bunsen, whom I knew at Yale, and Doctor Webster Civet, who was drowned last summer up in Maine. And the Hornbeams and the Willie Voltaires, and a whole clan named Blackbuck, who always gathered in a corner and flipped up their noses like goats at whosoever came near. And the Ismays and the Chrysties (or rather Hubert Auerbach and Mr. Chrystie’s wife), and Edgar Beaver, whose hair, they say, turned cotton-white one winter afternoon for no good reason at all.","sentences":[{"en":"From East Egg, then, came the Chester Beckers and the Leeches, and a man named Bunsen, whom I knew at Yale, and Doctor Webster Civet, who was drowned last summer up in Maine.","zh":"来自东卵的有切斯特·贝克尔夫妇、里奇夫妇，我在耶鲁就认识的一位姓邦森的男子、韦伯斯特·西维特医生，就是去年夏天在缅因州淹死的那位。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the Hornbeams and the Willie Voltaires, and a whole clan named Blackbuck, who always gathered in a corner and flipped up their noses like goats at whosoever came near.","zh":"还有霍恩毕姆夫妇、维利·伏尔泰夫妇，以及布莱巴克全家，这家人总是聚集在角落里，看到外人走近，他们就会像山羊生气那样鼻孔朝天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the Ismays and the Chrysties (or rather Hubert Auerbach and Mr. Chrystie’s wife), and Edgar Beaver, whose hair, they say, turned cotton-white one winter afternoon for no good reason at all.","zh":"此外还有伊斯梅夫妇和克里斯蒂夫妇（其实是哈贝特·奥尔巴赫和克里斯蒂先生的太太），以及埃德加·毕弗，后来有人说，他的头发在某个冬日下午毫无原因地变得像棉花那样白。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Clarence Endive was from East Egg, as I remember. He came only once, in white knickerbockers, and had a fight with a bum named Etty in the garden. From farther out on the Island came the Cheadles and the O. R. P. Schraeders, and the Stonewall Jackson Abrams of Georgia, and the Fishguards and the Ripley Snells. Snell was there three days before he went to the penitentiary, so drunk out on the gravel drive that Mrs. Ulysses Swett’s automobile ran over his right hand. The Dancies came, too, and S. B. Whitebait, who was well over sixty, and Maurice A. Flink, and the Hammerheads, and Beluga the tobacco importer, and Beluga’s girls.","sentences":[{"en":"Clarence Endive was from East Egg, as I remember.","zh":"我记得克拉伦斯·恩迪维也是从东卵来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He came only once, in white knickerbockers, and had a fight with a bum named Etty in the garden.","zh":"他只来过一次，穿着白色的灯笼裤，在花园里和某个姓艾迪的混混打了一架。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From farther out on the Island came the Cheadles and the O. R. P. Schraeders, and the Stonewall Jackson Abrams of Georgia, and the Fishguards and the Ripley Snells.","zh":"从长岛更远地方来的有夏德尔夫妇和施雷德夫妇、原籍乔治亚州的斯通瓦尔·杰克逊·亚勃拉姆斯夫妇、费斯贾德夫妇和瑞普利·斯奈尔夫妇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Snell was there three days before he went to the penitentiary, so drunk out on the gravel drive that Mrs. Ulysses Swett’s automobile ran over his right hand.","zh":"斯奈尔锒铛入狱前三天还在这里，那天他喝得酩酊大醉，倒在碎石车道上，右手被尤利西斯·斯威特太太开的轿车给碾了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The Dancies came, too, and S. B. Whitebait, who was well over sixty, and Maurice A. Flink, and the Hammerheads, and Beluga the tobacco importer, and Beluga’s girls.","zh":"但希夫妇也来了，此外还有年近七十的怀特贝特、莫里斯·弗林克、哈默赫德夫妇、烟草进口商贝鲁加，以及贝鲁加的几个女孩。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"From West Egg came the Poles and the Mulreadys and Cecil Roebuck and Cecil Schoen and Gulick the State senator and Newton Orchid, who controlled Films Par Excellence, and Eckhaust and Clyde Cohen and Don S. Schwartz (the son) and Arthur McCarty, all connected with the movies in one way or another. And the Catlips and the Bembergs and G. Earl Muldoon, brother to that Muldoon who afterward strangled his wife. Da Fontano the promoter came there, and Ed Legros and James B. (“Rot-Gut”) Ferret and the De Jongs and Ernest Lilly—they came to gamble, and when Ferret wandered into the garden it meant he was cleaned out and Associated Traction would have to fluctuate profitably next day.","sentences":[{"en":"From West Egg came the Poles and the Mulreadys and Cecil Roebuck and Cecil Schoen and Gulick the State senator and Newton Orchid, who controlled Films Par Excellence, and Eckhaust and Clyde Cohen and Don S. Schwartz (the son) and Arthur McCarty, all connected with the movies in one way or another.","zh":"来自西卵的有珀尔夫妇、穆拉迪夫妇、西希尔·罗巴克、西希尔·肖恩、纽约州参议员顾里克、卓越电影公司的幕后老板牛顿·奥启德、埃克豪斯·科恩和他太太克莱德、唐·施瓦茨二世和亚瑟·麦卡蒂，后面这几个多多少少都算是电影圈的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the Catlips and the Bembergs and G. Earl Muldoon, brother to that Muldoon who afterward strangled his wife.","zh":"还有卡特利普夫妇、本伯格夫妇和艾尔·穆尔东——那个后来杀死自己妻子的穆尔东就是他的亲兄弟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Da Fontano the promoter came there, and Ed Legros and James B. (“Rot-Gut”) Ferret and the De Jongs and Ernest Lilly—they came to gamble, and when Ferret wandered into the garden it meant he was cleaned out and Associated Traction would have to fluctuate profitably next day.","zh":"此外还有投资者达方塔诺、埃德·勒格洛斯、“酒鬼”詹姆斯·费雷特、德琼斯夫妇和恩尼斯特·莱利——这些人是来赌钱的，费雷特要是走进花园，那就意味着他输得干干净净，而且第二天联合拖拉机公司的股票将会大起大落，这样他才能把老本捞回来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A man named Klipspringer was there so often that he became known as “the boarder”—I doubt if he had any other home. Of theatrical people there were Gus Waize and Horace O’Donavan and Lester Myer and George Duckweed and Francis Bull. Also from New York were the Chromes and the Backhyssons and the Dennickers and Russel Betty and the Corrigans and the Kellehers and the Dewars and the Scullys and S. W. Belcher and the Smirkes and the young Quinns, divorced now, and Henry L. Palmetto, who killed himself by jumping in front of a subway train in Times Square.","sentences":[{"en":"A man named Klipspringer was there so often that he became known as “the boarder”—I doubt if he had any other home.","zh":"有个姓克里普斯普林格的因为去得很频繁，大家都说他是“房客”——我猜他可能真的是无家可归。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Of theatrical people there were Gus Waize and Horace O’Donavan and Lester Myer and George Duckweed and Francis Bull.","zh":"戏剧界的来宾有古斯·魏兹、贺拉斯·奥多纳万、莱斯特·梅耶、乔治·达克维德和弗朗西斯·布尔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Also from New York were the Chromes and the Backhyssons and the Dennickers and Russel Betty and the Corrigans and the Kellehers and the Dewars and the Scullys and S. W. Belcher and the Smirkes and the young Quinns, divorced now, and Henry L. Palmetto, who killed himself by jumping in front of a subway train in Times Square.","zh":"也有从纽约来的客人，比如说克罗姆夫妇、巴克海森夫妇、邓尼克夫妇、拉塞尔·贝迪、柯立甘夫妇、凯勒赫尔夫妇、德瓦兹夫妇、斯卡里夫妇、S.W.贝尔克、斯默克夫妇和年轻的奎因夫妇，他们现在已经离婚，还有亨利·帕尔默托，他后来在时报广场地铁站自寻短见，跳到行驶的火车前面被撞死了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Benny McClenahan arrived always with four girls. They were never quite the same ones in physical person, but they were so identical one with another that it inevitably seemed they had been there before. I have forgotten their names—Jaqueline, I think, or else Consuela, or Gloria or Judy or June, and their last names were either the melodious names of flowers and months or the sterner ones of the great American capitalists whose cousins, if pressed, they would confess themselves to be.","sentences":[{"en":"Benny McClenahan arrived always with four girls.","zh":"本尼·麦克伦纳汉每次来都带着四个女孩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were never quite the same ones in physical person, but they were so identical one with another that it inevitably seemed they had been there before.","zh":"虽然每次来的人不尽相同，但这些女孩的打扮大同小异，所以一眼看上去你会觉得她们以前都来过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I have forgotten their names—Jaqueline, I think, or else Consuela, or Gloria or Judy or June, and their last names were either the melodious names of flowers and months or the sterner ones of the great American capitalists whose cousins, if pressed, they would confess themselves to be.","zh":"我记不清她们的芳名了——好像有杰奎琳，或许还有康修拉、格罗迪雅、茱迪、茱恩什么的。她们的姓氏不是悦耳动听的花草名字，就是令人肃然起敬的美国大资本家的尊姓。如果你追着问，她们会承认是某个大人物的亲戚。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"In addition to all these I can remember that Faustina O’Brien came there at least once and the Baedeker girls and young Brewer, who had his nose shot off in the war, and Mr. Albrucksburger and Miss Haag, his fiancée, and Ardita Fitz-Peters and Mr. P. Jewett, once head of the American Legion, and Miss Claudia Hip, with a man reputed to be her chauffeur, and a prince of something, whom we called Duke, and whose name, if I ever knew it, I have forgotten.","sentences":[{"en":"In addition to all these I can remember that Faustina O’Brien came there at least once and the Baedeker girls and young Brewer, who had his nose shot off in the war, and Mr. Albrucksburger and Miss Haag, his fiancée, and Ardita Fitz-Peters and Mr. P. Jewett, once head of the American Legion, and Miss Claudia Hip, with a man reputed to be her chauffeur, and a prince of something, whom we called Duke, and whose name, if I ever knew it, I have forgotten.","zh":"除了上面这些人，我还记得福斯蒂娜·奥布莱恩至少来过一次。此外还有贝迪科尔家的几位姑娘、年轻的布勒伊尔（他的鼻子在战争中被子弹打飞了）、奥布鲁克伯格先生和他的未婚妻哈格小姐、阿迪塔·菲兹彼得、曾担任美国退伍军人联合会主席的朱维特先生、克劳迪娅·希普小姐和一个据说是她司机的男子，以及一位皇亲国戚，我们都管他叫公爵，我不知道他的名字，或者原先知道，但现在忘记了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"All these people came to Gatsby’s house in the summer.","sentences":[{"en":"All these people came to Gatsby’s house in the summer.","zh":"那年夏天，这些人都去盖茨比的别墅做客。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"At nine o’clock, one morning late in July, Gatsby’s gorgeous car lurched up the rocky drive to my door and gave out a burst of melody from its three-noted horn.","sentences":[{"en":"At nine o’clock, one morning late in July, Gatsby’s gorgeous car lurched up the rocky drive to my door and gave out a burst of melody from its three-noted horn.","zh":"七月底某天早晨九点，盖茨比的豪华车沿着崎岖的车道驶到我家门口，有三个音调的喇叭发出一阵动听的乐曲。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was the first time he had called on me, though I had gone to two of his parties, mounted in his hydroplane, and, at his urgent invitation, made frequent use of his beach.","sentences":[{"en":"It was the first time he had called on me, though I had gone to two of his parties, mounted in his hydroplane, and, at his urgent invitation, made frequent use of his beach.","zh":"这是他第一次光临寒舍，但我已经两次参加过他的宴会，坐过他的水上飞机，而且还应他恳切的邀请，多次使用他的沙滩。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Good morning, old sport. You’re having lunch with me today and I thought we’d ride up together.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good morning, old sport.","zh":"“早上好，老兄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You’re having lunch with me today and I thought we’d ride up together.”","zh":"既然我们说好一起吃午饭，我想我们不如同车进城吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was balancing himself on the dashboard of his car with that resourcefulness of movement that is so peculiarly American—that comes, I suppose, with the absence of lifting work in youth and, even more, with the formless grace of our nervous, sporadic games. This quality was continually breaking through his punctilious manner in the shape of restlessness. He was never quite still; there was always a tapping foot somewhere or the impatient opening and closing of a hand.","sentences":[{"en":"He was balancing himself on the dashboard of his car with that resourcefulness of movement that is so peculiarly American—that comes, I suppose, with the absence of lifting work in youth and, even more, with the formless grace of our nervous, sporadic games.","zh":"他在挡泥板上稳稳地站着，那姿势显得很轻松，带着美国人特有的潇洒——我觉得可能是因为从小不干重活，也可能是因为热衷于参加各种紧张激烈的体育比赛，美国人的行为举止中自有一种自然大方的风度。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This quality was continually breaking through his punctilious manner in the shape of restlessness.","zh":"但盖茨比身上的潇洒风采常常被局促不安的表现打断。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was never quite still; there was always a tapping foot somewhere or the impatient opening and closing of a hand.","zh":"他没有完全静止的时候，要么是脚不停地拍打着地面，要么是手焦躁地张开又合上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He saw me looking with admiration at his car.","sentences":[{"en":"He saw me looking with admiration at his car.","zh":"他发现我羡慕地看着他的车。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s pretty, isn’t it, old sport?” He jumped off to give me a better view. “Haven’t you ever seen it before?”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s pretty, isn’t it, old sport?”","zh":"“很漂亮，对吧，老兄？”他从挡泥板上跳下来，以便让我看得更清楚。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He jumped off to give me a better view.","zh":"“很漂亮，对吧，老兄？”他从挡泥板上跳下来，以便让我看得更清楚。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Haven’t you ever seen it before?”","zh":"“你以前没见过这辆车吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I’d seen it. Everybody had seen it. It was a rich cream colour, bright with nickel, swollen here and there in its monstrous length with triumphant hatboxes and supper-boxes and toolboxes, and terraced with a labyrinth of windshields that mirrored a dozen suns. Sitting down behind many layers of glass in a sort of green leather conservatory, we started to town.","sentences":[{"en":"I’d seen it.","zh":"其实我见过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everybody had seen it.","zh":"每个人都见过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a rich cream colour, bright with nickel, swollen here and there in its monstrous length with triumphant hatboxes and supper-boxes and toolboxes, and terraced with a labyrinth of windshields that mirrored a dozen suns.","zh":"这辆车是奶黄色的，镀镍的地方闪闪发亮，极长的车身线条非常优美，车里有衣帽箱、食物箱和工具箱，层层叠叠的挡风玻璃反射出十几个太阳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sitting down behind many layers of glass in a sort of green leather conservatory, we started to town.","zh":"我们坐在绿皮座位上，车厢被几层玻璃隔起来，感觉像坐在温室里，就此启程前往城区。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I had talked with him perhaps half a dozen times in the past month and found, to my disappointment, that he had little to say. So my first impression, that he was a person of some undefined consequence, had gradually faded and he had become simply the proprietor of an elaborate roadhouse next door.","sentences":[{"en":"I had talked with him perhaps half a dozen times in the past month and found, to my disappointment, that he had little to say.","zh":"过去一个月来，我已经跟他聊过大概五六次，让我失望的是，他这人口风很紧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So my first impression, that he was a person of some undefined consequence, had gradually faded and he had become simply the proprietor of an elaborate roadhouse next door.","zh":"我原本以为他是个神秘的大人物，但这个印象渐渐消退了，现在我觉得他只是某个开在我家隔壁的豪华饭店的大老板。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And then came that disconcerting ride. We hadn’t reached West Egg village before Gatsby began leaving his elegant sentences unfinished and slapping himself indecisively on the knee of his caramel-coloured suit.","sentences":[{"en":"And then came that disconcerting ride.","zh":"可是这次同车却让我感到很窘迫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We hadn’t reached West Egg village before Gatsby began leaving his elegant sentences unfinished and slapping himself indecisively on the knee of his caramel-coloured suit.","zh":"我们的车还没开到西卵村，盖茨比就已经是欲言又止的样子，他的手也犹疑不决地拍打穿着褐色西装裤的膝盖。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look here, old sport,” he broke out surprisingly, “what’s your opinion of me, anyhow?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look here, old sport,” he broke out surprisingly, “what’s your opinion of me, anyhow?”","zh":"“喂，老兄，”他突然打破了沉默，“你到底觉得我这个人怎么样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A little overwhelmed, I began the generalized evasions which that question deserves.","sentences":[{"en":"A little overwhelmed, I began the generalized evasions which that question deserves.","zh":"我有点始料未及，于是含糊其辞地搪塞了几句。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I’m going to tell you something about my life,” he interrupted. “I don’t want you to get a wrong idea of me from all these stories you hear.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I’m going to tell you something about my life,” he interrupted.","zh":"“好吧，我准备跟你说说我的人生，”他打断我的话头说，“我不希望你听了那些闲话之后对我有误解。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I don’t want you to get a wrong idea of me from all these stories you hear.”","zh":"“好吧，我准备跟你说说我的人生，”他打断我的话头说，“我不希望你听了那些闲话之后对我有误解。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"So he was aware of the bizarre accusations that flavoured conversation in his halls.","sentences":[{"en":"So he was aware of the bizarre accusations that flavoured conversation in his halls.","zh":"原来他也知道那些别人在他家里引为谈资的流言蜚语。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll tell you God’s truth.” His right hand suddenly ordered divine retribution to stand by. “I am the son of some wealthy people in the Middle West—all dead now. I was brought up in America but educated at Oxford, because all my ancestors have been educated there for many years. It is a family tradition.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll tell you God’s truth.”","zh":"“上帝作证，我要对你说真话，”他突然赌咒似的举起了右手，“我是中西部一户有钱人家的儿子，家里人现在都过世了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His right hand suddenly ordered divine retribution to stand by.","zh":"“上帝作证，我要对你说真话，”他突然赌咒似的举起了右手，“我是中西部一户有钱人家的儿子，家里人现在都过世了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I am the son of some wealthy people in the Middle West—all dead now.","zh":"“上帝作证，我要对你说真话，”他突然赌咒似的举起了右手，“我是中西部一户有钱人家的儿子，家里人现在都过世了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I was brought up in America but educated at Oxford, because all my ancestors have been educated there for many years.","zh":"我长大是在美国，但上学是在牛津，因为许多年来，我的先辈都是在那里受教育的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is a family tradition.”","zh":"这是我们家族的传统。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He looked at me sideways—and I knew why Jordan Baker had believed he was lying. He hurried the phrase “educated at Oxford,” or swallowed it, or choked on it, as though it had bothered him before. And with this doubt, his whole statement fell to pieces, and I wondered if there wasn’t something a little sinister about him, after all.","sentences":[{"en":"He looked at me sideways—and I knew why Jordan Baker had believed he was lying.","zh":"他说话时瞟了我好几次——于是我明白乔丹·贝克为何会认为他是在说谎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He hurried the phrase “educated at Oxford,” or swallowed it, or choked on it, as though it had bothered him before.","zh":"说到“上学是在牛津”时，他含糊其辞地支吾过去，好像是觉得有点说不出口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And with this doubt, his whole statement fell to pieces, and I wondered if there wasn’t something a little sinister about him, after all.","zh":"由于这点让我起疑，他说的话我都不信了，我甚至于怀疑他这人到底是有点邪门的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What part of the Middle West?” I inquired casually.","sentences":[{"en":"“What part of the Middle West?”","zh":"“中西部什么地方啊？”我漫不经心地问。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I inquired casually.","zh":"“中西部什么地方啊？”我漫不经心地问。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“San Francisco.”","sentences":[{"en":"“San Francisco.”","zh":"“旧金山。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I see.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I see.”","zh":"“原来是这样。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“My family all died and I came into a good deal of money.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My family all died and I came into a good deal of money.”","zh":"“我的家人都死了，我继承了大笔财富。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His voice was solemn, as if the memory of that sudden extinction of a clan still haunted him. For a moment I suspected that he was pulling my leg, but a glance at him convinced me otherwise.","sentences":[{"en":"His voice was solemn, as if the memory of that sudden extinction of a clan still haunted him.","zh":"他的语气很沉重，仿佛整个家族的突然消失迄今仍让他心痛不已。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a moment I suspected that he was pulling my leg, but a glance at him convinced me otherwise.","zh":"刹那间我怀疑他是不是在跟我开玩笑，但看了他一眼之后，我又觉得不像。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“After that I lived like a young rajah in all the capitals of Europe—Paris, Venice, Rome—collecting jewels, chiefly rubies, hunting big game, painting a little, things for myself only, and trying to forget something very sad that had happened to me long ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“After that I lived like a young rajah in all the capitals of Europe—Paris, Venice, Rome—collecting jewels, chiefly rubies, hunting big game, painting a little, things for myself only, and trying to forget something very sad that had happened to me long ago.”","zh":"“起初我像年轻的印度王子般生活在欧洲各国的首都，就像巴黎、威尼斯、维也纳啦，成天就是收集珠宝，主要是红宝石，猎杀凶猛的动物，自娱自乐地绘几幅小画，试图借此来忘记一件不久之前发生在我身上的伤心事。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"With an effort I managed to restrain my incredulous laughter. The very phrases were worn so threadbare that they evoked no image except that of a turbaned “character” leaking sawdust at every pore as he pursued a tiger through the Bois de Boulogne.","sentences":[{"en":"With an effort I managed to restrain my incredulous laughter.","zh":"我费了好大力气，强行抑制住笑声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The very phrases were worn so threadbare that they evoked no image except that of a turbaned “character” leaking sawdust at every pore as he pursued a tiger through the Bois de Boulogne.","zh":"他说的谎话未免也太老套了，让我忍不住想起一幅滑稽的画面：有个戴着白头巾的印度“阿三”，像木偶戏里的小丑，在布洛涅森林追逐着老虎。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Then came the war, old sport. It was a great relief, and I tried very hard to die, but I seemed to bear an enchanted life. I accepted a commission as first lieutenant when it began. In the Argonne Forest I took the remains of my machine-gun battalion so far forward that there was a half mile gap on either side of us where the infantry couldn’t advance. We stayed there two days and two nights, a hundred and thirty men with sixteen Lewis guns, and when the infantry came up at last they found the insignia of three German divisions among the piles of dead. I was promoted to be a major, and every Allied government gave me a decoration—even Montenegro, little Montenegro down on the Adriatic Sea!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Then came the war, old sport.","zh":"“然后就是打仗了，老兄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a great relief, and I tried very hard to die, but I seemed to bear an enchanted life.","zh":"这对我来说是很大的解脱，我费尽心机想干脆死了算了，但我这条小命似乎有神仙保佑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I accepted a commission as first lieutenant when it began.","zh":"战争开始时，我接受了中尉的任命。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the Argonne Forest I took the remains of my machine-gun battalion so far forward that there was a half mile gap on either side of us where the infantry couldn’t advance.","zh":"在阿贡森林战役中，我率领机枪连的残部，勇猛地向前突击，距离敌人只有半英里之遥，而我方的步兵在我们身后半英里便寸步难行。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We stayed there two days and two nights, a hundred and thirty men with sixteen Lewis guns, and when the infantry came up at last they found the insignia of three German divisions among the piles of dead.","zh":"我们在那里激战了两天两夜，一百三十个人，十六架刘易斯机枪，战斗结束后，我方的步兵终于能跟过来了，他们在堆积如山的德军尸体中发现了三个师的旗帜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was promoted to be a major, and every Allied government gave me a decoration—even Montenegro, little Montenegro down on the Adriatic Sea!”","zh":"我的军衔升为少校，每个同盟军政府都给我颁发了军功章——甚至包括黑山，就是亚德里亚海边上那个小小的黑山！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Little Montenegro! He lifted up the words and nodded at them—with his smile. The smile comprehended Montenegro’s troubled history and sympathized with the brave struggles of the Montenegrin people. It appreciated fully the chain of national circumstances which had elicited this tribute from Montenegro’s warm little heart. My incredulity was submerged in fascination now; it was like skimming hastily through a dozen magazines.","sentences":[{"en":"Little Montenegro!","zh":"小小的黑山！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He lifted up the words and nodded at them—with his smile.","zh":"说到这几个字时，他提高了音量，还点点头——带着微笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The smile comprehended Montenegro’s troubled history and sympathized with the brave struggles of the Montenegrin people.","zh":"这笑容似乎表示他理解黑山多灾多难的历史，同情黑山人民英勇不屈的奋斗，也十分感激这个蕞尔小国热情地给他嘉奖。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It appreciated fully the chain of national circumstances which had elicited this tribute from Montenegro’s warm little heart.","zh":"这笑容似乎表示他理解黑山多灾多难的历史，同情黑山人民英勇不屈的奋斗，也十分感激这个蕞尔小国热情地给他嘉奖。","scope":"group"},{"en":"My incredulity was submerged in fascination now; it was like skimming hastily through a dozen magazines.","zh":"这时我的疑心已经被惊奇取代，感觉就像正在匆匆翻阅十几本杂志一样。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He reached in his pocket, and a piece of metal, slung on a ribbon, fell into my palm.","sentences":[{"en":"He reached in his pocket, and a piece of metal, slung on a ribbon, fell into my palm.","zh":"他把手伸进口袋，掏出一块系着绳子的金属牌，把它放到我手里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s the one from Montenegro.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s the one from Montenegro.”","zh":"“这就是黑山给我发的那块。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"To my astonishment, the thing had an authentic look. “Orderi di Danilo,” ran the circular legend, “Montenegro, Nicolas Rex.”","sentences":[{"en":"To my astonishment, the thing had an authentic look.","zh":"我吃惊地发现这东西看上去竟然像真的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Orderi di Danilo,” ran the circular legend, “Montenegro, Nicolas Rex.”","zh":"这圆牌上用斯拉夫文写着：“丹尼罗勋章，黑山国王尼古拉斯。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Turn it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Turn it.”","zh":"“翻过来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Major Jay Gatsby,” I read, “For Valour Extraordinary.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Major Jay Gatsby,” I read, “For Valour Extraordinary.”","zh":"“献给英勇非凡的，”我念出上面的文字，“杰伊·盖茨比少校。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Here’s another thing I always carry. A souvenir of Oxford days. It was taken in Trinity Quad—the man on my left is now the Earl of Doncaster.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Here’s another thing I always carry.","zh":"“还有件玩意也是我随身带着的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A souvenir of Oxford days.","zh":"我在牛津上学时的纪念品。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was taken in Trinity Quad—the man on my left is now the Earl of Doncaster.”","zh":"是在三一学院拍的——我左边那个人现在是唐卡斯特伯爵。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was a photograph of half a dozen young men in blazers loafing in an archway through which were visible a host of spires. There was Gatsby, looking a little, not much, younger—with a cricket bat in his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a photograph of half a dozen young men in blazers loafing in an archway through which were visible a host of spires.","zh":"那张照片上有五六个年轻人，穿着光鲜的校服，站在拱廊下面，拱廊之后可以见到许多哥特式建筑的塔尖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was Gatsby, looking a little, not much, younger—with a cricket bat in his hand.","zh":"里面有个人就是盖茨比，看上去比现在稍微年轻一点点——手里拿着一只板球拍。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Then it was all true. I saw the skins of tigers flaming in his palace on the Grand Canal; I saw him opening a chest of rubies to ease, with their crimson-lighted depths, the gnawings of his broken heart.","sentences":[{"en":"Then it was all true.","zh":"原来这都是真的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw the skins of tigers flaming in his palace on the Grand Canal; I saw him opening a chest of rubies to ease, with their crimson-lighted depths, the gnawings of his broken heart.","zh":"我看见他在威尼斯大运河畔有座宫殿，里面挂着许多五彩斑斓的老虎皮；我看见他打开满满的珠宝箱，用明艳夺目的红宝石来抚慰他那颗破碎痛苦的心。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m going to make a big request of you today,” he said, pocketing his souvenirs with satisfaction, “so I thought you ought to know something about me. I didn’t want you to think I was just some nobody. You see, I usually find myself among strangers because I drift here and there trying to forget the sad things that happened to me.” He hesitated. “You’ll hear about it this afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m going to make a big request of you today,” he said, pocketing his souvenirs with satisfaction, “so I thought you ought to know something about me.","zh":"“今天我要请你帮个大忙，”他说着心满意足地把两件纪念品装回口袋，“所以我觉得你应该对我有所了解。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I didn’t want you to think I was just some nobody.","zh":"我不希望你认为我只是个无名小卒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You see, I usually find myself among strangers because I drift here and there trying to forget the sad things that happened to me.”","zh":"你知道吗，我喜欢招待陌生人，是因为我想要在迎来送往中忘记我的伤心事。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He hesitated.","zh":"他犹疑了片刻，“今天下午你会听说这件事的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’ll hear about it this afternoon.”","zh":"他犹疑了片刻，“今天下午你会听说这件事的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“At lunch?”","sentences":[{"en":"“At lunch?”","zh":"“吃午饭的时候吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, this afternoon. I happened to find out that you’re taking Miss Baker to tea.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, this afternoon.","zh":"“不，要到下午。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I happened to find out that you’re taking Miss Baker to tea.”","zh":"我碰巧知道你下午要跟贝克小姐去喝茶。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do you mean you’re in love with Miss Baker?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you mean you’re in love with Miss Baker?”","zh":"“你是说你爱上贝克小姐了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, old sport, I’m not. But Miss Baker has kindly consented to speak to you about this matter.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, old sport, I’m not.","zh":"“没有啦，老兄，我没有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Miss Baker has kindly consented to speak to you about this matter.”","zh":"但贝克小姐人很好，愿意跟你谈谈这件事。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I hadn’t the faintest idea what “this matter” was, but I was more annoyed than interested. I hadn’t asked Jordan to tea in order to discuss Mr. Jay Gatsby. I was sure the request would be something utterly fantastic, and for a moment I was sorry I’d ever set foot upon his overpopulated lawn.","sentences":[{"en":"I hadn’t the faintest idea what “this matter” was, but I was more annoyed than interested.","zh":"我完全不知道“这件事”会是什么，但我没有兴趣，而是感到很恼火。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I hadn’t asked Jordan to tea in order to discuss Mr. Jay Gatsby.","zh":"我请乔丹喝茶，可不是为了讨论杰伊·盖茨比先生的事情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was sure the request would be something utterly fantastic, and for a moment I was sorry I’d ever set foot upon his overpopulated lawn.","zh":"我敢肯定他要请我做的是非常离谱的事情，刹那间，我真后悔当初踏足过他那人满为患的草坪。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He wouldn’t say another word. His correctness grew on him as we neared the city. We passed Port Roosevelt, where there was a glimpse of red-belted oceangoing ships, and sped along a cobbled slum lined with the dark, undeserted saloons of the faded-gilt nineteen-hundreds. Then the valley of ashes opened out on both sides of us, and I had a glimpse of Mrs. Wilson straining at the garage pump with panting vitality as we went by.","sentences":[{"en":"He wouldn’t say another word.","zh":"他再也没有说话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His correctness grew on him as we neared the city.","zh":"离城区越近，他就显得越是矜持。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We passed Port Roosevelt, where there was a glimpse of red-belted oceangoing ships, and sped along a cobbled slum lined with the dark, undeserted saloons of the faded-gilt nineteen-hundreds.","zh":"我们驶过罗斯福港，在那里瞥见许多涂着红腰线的远洋巨轮；又穿过一处贫民窟，碎石路两边是许多二十世纪初就有的酒馆，虽然仍有客人，但镀金年代的繁华已经褪尽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the valley of ashes opened out on both sides of us, and I had a glimpse of Mrs. Wilson straining at the garage pump with panting vitality as we went by.","zh":"接着垃圾场在马路两边展开，路过威尔逊先生的汽修厂时，我瞥见他太太气喘吁吁，卖力地抽动着加油泵。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"With fenders spread like wings we scattered light through half Astoria—only half, for as we twisted among the pillars of the elevated I heard the familiar “jug-jug-spat!” of a motorcycle, and a frantic policeman rode alongside.","sentences":[{"en":"With fenders spread like wings we scattered light through half Astoria—only half, for as we twisted among the pillars of the elevated I heard the familiar “jug-jug-spat!” of a motorcycle, and a frantic policeman rode alongside.","zh":"轿车两边的挡泥板就像张开的翅膀，而我们就像撒播光明的天使，飞也似的开过半个阿斯陀利亚——只是半个而已，因为正当我们在高架铁路的支柱间前行，我听到一阵“突、突、突”的熟悉声响，有个气急败坏的警察骑着摩托车驶到我们旁边。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right, old sport,” called Gatsby. We slowed down. Taking a white card from his wallet, he waved it before the man’s eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"“All right, old sport,” called Gatsby.","zh":"“没问题，老兄，”盖茨比大声说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We slowed down.","zh":"我们把车停下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Taking a white card from his wallet, he waved it before the man’s eyes.","zh":"他从钱包里取出一张白色的卡片，在警察眼前晃了晃。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Right you are,” agreed the policeman, tipping his cap. “Know you next time, Mr. Gatsby. Excuse me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Right you are,” agreed the policeman, tipping his cap.","zh":"“原来是您，”警察摘下帽子敬了个礼，毕恭毕敬地说，“下回认得您啦，盖茨比先生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Know you next time, Mr. Gatsby.","zh":"“原来是您，”警察摘下帽子敬了个礼，毕恭毕敬地说，“下回认得您啦，盖茨比先生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Excuse me!”","zh":"这次真对不起！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What was that?” I inquired. “The picture of Oxford?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What was that?”","zh":"“你给他看什么？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"我问，“那张牛津的照片吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“The picture of Oxford?”","zh":"我问，“那张牛津的照片吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I was able to do the commissioner a favour once, and he sends me a Christmas card every year.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was able to do the commissioner a favour once, and he sends me a Christmas card every year.”","zh":"“我曾经帮过警察局长的忙，他每年都给我寄圣诞贺卡。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Over the great bridge, with the sunlight through the girders making a constant flicker upon the moving cars, with the city rising up across the river in white heaps and sugar lumps all built with a wish out of nonolfactory money. The city seen from the Queensboro Bridge is always the city seen for the first time, in its first wild promise of all the mystery and the beauty in the world.","sentences":[{"en":"Over the great bridge, with the sunlight through the girders making a constant flicker upon the moving cars, with the city rising up across the river in white heaps and sugar lumps all built with a wish out of nonolfactory money.","zh":"我们驶上大桥，但见阳光穿过钢架，在川流不息的车辆上照耀出一道闪烁的光线，而纽约在对岸高高耸立，那座座白色的大厦和糖块般低矮的楼房，尽是人们用没有铜臭的钱发愿盖起来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The city seen from the Queensboro Bridge is always the city seen for the first time, in its first wild promise of all the mystery and the beauty in the world.","zh":"从皇后区大桥望去，这座城市总是那么新奇，依然如初见那样，充满了人世间所有的神秘和美丽。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A dead man passed us in a hearse heaped with blooms, followed by two carriages with drawn blinds, and by more cheerful carriages for friends. The friends looked out at us with the tragic eyes and short upper lips of southeastern Europe, and I was glad that the sight of Gatsby’s splendid car was included in their sombre holiday. As we crossed Blackwell’s Island a limousine passed us, driven by a white chauffeur, in which sat three modish negroes, two bucks and a girl. I laughed aloud as the yolks of their eyeballs rolled toward us in haughty rivalry.","sentences":[{"en":"A dead man passed us in a hearse heaped with blooms, followed by two carriages with drawn blinds, and by more cheerful carriages for friends.","zh":"有个死人躺在堆满鲜花的灵车中超过我们，后面跟着两辆拉起了窗帘的轿车，再后面那几辆车看上去没那么肃穆，载着的应该是死者的朋友。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The friends looked out at us with the tragic eyes and short upper lips of southeastern Europe, and I was glad that the sight of Gatsby’s splendid car was included in their sombre holiday.","zh":"那些朋友看着我们，眼里充满了悲伤，他们的上唇很短，看上去像东南欧人。他们在出殡的日子居然有幸目睹盖茨比这辆豪华的轿车，我真替他们高兴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As we crossed Blackwell’s Island a limousine passed us, driven by a white chauffeur, in which sat three modish negroes, two bucks and a girl.","zh":"我们驶过黑井岛时，有辆轿车超过了我们，开车的司机是白人，车里坐着三个打扮时髦的黑人，两男一女。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I laughed aloud as the yolks of their eyeballs rolled toward us in haughty rivalry.","zh":"看到那些家伙不以为然地朝我们翻白眼，我不由哈哈大笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Anything can happen now that we’ve slid over this bridge,” I thought; “anything at all…”","sentences":[{"en":"“Anything can happen now that we’ve slid over this bridge,” I thought; “anything at all…”","zh":"“过了这座桥，那边什么事情都有可能发生，”我心里想，“无论什么事情…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Even Gatsby could happen, without any particular wonder.","sentences":[{"en":"Even Gatsby could happen, without any particular wonder.","zh":"连盖茨比这种人物都有，别的更不需要大惊小怪了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"Roaring noon. In a well-fanned Forty-second Street cellar I met Gatsby for lunch. Blinking away the brightness of the street outside, my eyes picked him out obscurely in the anteroom, talking to another man.","sentences":[{"en":"Roaring noon.","zh":"酷热的正午。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In a well-fanned Forty-second Street cellar I met Gatsby for lunch.","zh":"我走进第四十二街一家风扇开得很猛的地下餐厅，去找盖茨比吃午饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Blinking away the brightness of the street outside, my eyes picked him out obscurely in the anteroom, talking to another man.","zh":"眨眼把外面街道的明亮挤掉之后，我的眼睛模模糊糊地看见他在候座区，跟另一个人在说话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Mr. Carraway, this is my friend Mr. Wolfshiem.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Mr. Carraway, this is my friend Mr. Wolfshiem.”","zh":"“卡拉威先生，这是我的朋友沃夫希姆。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A small, flat-nosed Jew raised his large head and regarded me with two fine growths of hair which luxuriated in either nostril. After a moment I discovered his tiny eyes in the half-darkness.","sentences":[{"en":"A small, flat-nosed Jew raised his large head and regarded me with two fine growths of hair which luxuriated in either nostril.","zh":"一个矮小的塌鼻子犹太人抬起他的大头，用两撮长得极其茂盛的鼻毛来问候我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After a moment I discovered his tiny eyes in the half-darkness.","zh":"隔了片刻，我才在阴暗中找到他那双小眼睛。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“—So I took one look at him,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, shaking my hand earnestly, “and what do you think I did?”","sentences":[{"en":"“—So I took one look at him,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, shaking my hand earnestly, “and what do you think I did?”","zh":"“…于是我又看着他，”沃夫希姆先生热切地握着我的手说，“你猜我做了什么事？”“你做了什么事呢？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What?” I inquired politely.","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“…于是我又看着他，”沃夫希姆先生热切地握着我的手说，“你猜我做了什么事？”“你做了什么事呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I inquired politely.","zh":"我礼貌地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But evidently he was not addressing me, for he dropped my hand and covered Gatsby with his expressive nose.","sentences":[{"en":"But evidently he was not addressing me, for he dropped my hand and covered Gatsby with his expressive nose.","zh":"但他这句话显然不是对我说的，因为他随即松开我的手，用他那很具表现力的鼻子对准了盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I handed the money to Katspaugh and I said: ‘All right, Katspaugh, don’t pay him a penny till he shuts his mouth.’ He shut it then and there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I handed the money to Katspaugh and I said: ‘All right, Katspaugh, don’t pay him a penny till he shuts his mouth.’","zh":"“我把钱交给凯兹堡，然后说：‘没问题，凯兹堡，假如他不闭嘴，半分钱也别给他。’自那以后，他就闭上了他的臭嘴。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He shut it then and there.”","zh":"“我把钱交给凯兹堡，然后说：‘没问题，凯兹堡，假如他不闭嘴，半分钱也别给他。’自那以后，他就闭上了他的臭嘴。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby took an arm of each of us and moved forward into the restaurant, whereupon Mr. Wolfshiem swallowed a new sentence he was starting and lapsed into a somnambulatory abstraction.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby took an arm of each of us and moved forward into the restaurant, whereupon Mr. Wolfshiem swallowed a new sentence he was starting and lapsed into a somnambulatory abstraction.","zh":"盖茨比拉着我们两个的手臂走进餐厅，沃夫希姆先生似乎还想开口，但话到嘴边又咽了下去，梦游似的跟着往前走。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Highballs?” asked the head waiter.","sentences":[{"en":"“Highballs?” asked the head waiter.","zh":"“要喝点酒吗？”领班服务员问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This is a nice restaurant here,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, looking at the presbyterian nymphs on the ceiling. “But I like across the street better!”","sentences":[{"en":"“This is a nice restaurant here,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, looking at the presbyterian nymphs on the ceiling.","zh":"“这家餐厅不错，”沃夫希姆先生看着天花板上几个长老会神话传说中的仙女说，“但我更喜欢马路对面那家！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“But I like across the street better!”","zh":"“这家餐厅不错，”沃夫希姆先生看着天花板上几个长老会神话传说中的仙女说，“但我更喜欢马路对面那家！”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes, highballs,” agreed Gatsby, and then to Mr. Wolfshiem: “It’s too hot over there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, highballs,” agreed Gatsby, and then to Mr. Wolfshiem: “It’s too hot over there.”","zh":"“好的，来几杯酒，”盖茨比同意了，然后他对沃夫希姆说，“那边太热了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hot and small—yes,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, “but full of memories.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hot and small—yes,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, “but full of memories.”","zh":"“是啊，很热，地方又小，”沃夫希姆先生说，“但充满了记忆。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What place is that?” I asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“What place is that?”","zh":"“那家餐厅叫什么？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I asked.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The old Metropole.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The old Metropole.”","zh":"“旧京。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The old Metropole,” brooded Mr. Wolfshiem gloomily. “Filled with faces dead and gone. Filled with friends gone now forever. I can’t forget so long as I live the night they shot Rosy Rosenthal there. It was six of us at the table, and Rosy had eat and drunk a lot all evening. When it was almost morning the waiter came up to him with a funny look and says somebody wants to speak to him outside. ‘All right,’ says Rosy, and begins to get up, and I pulled him down in his chair.","sentences":[{"en":"“The old Metropole,” brooded Mr. Wolfshiem gloomily.","zh":"“旧京，”沃夫希姆先生悲伤地回忆道，“那里有过许多死去的面容。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Filled with faces dead and gone.","zh":"“旧京，”沃夫希姆先生悲伤地回忆道，“那里有过许多死去的面容。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Filled with friends gone now forever.","zh":"那里有过许多逝去的朋友。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I can’t forget so long as I live the night they shot Rosy Rosenthal there.","zh":"只要活着，我就不会忘记他们开枪打死罗西·罗森泰尔的那个晚上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was six of us at the table, and Rosy had eat and drunk a lot all evening.","zh":"当时我们六个人同桌吃饭，罗西整个晚上都在吃吃喝喝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When it was almost morning the waiter came up to him with a funny look and says somebody wants to speak to him outside. ‘All right,’ says Rosy, and begins to get up, and I pulled him down in his chair.","zh":"天快亮时，那服务员走过来，很古怪地看了他一眼，然后说有人想请他到外面谈谈。‘没问题，’罗西说着就要站起来，我一把拉住他，让他坐回椅子里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“ ‘Let the bastards come in here if they want you, Rosy, but don’t you, so help me, move outside this room.’","sentences":[{"en":"“ ‘Let the bastards come in here if they want you, Rosy, but don’t you, so help me, move outside this room.’","zh":"“‘那帮混蛋要想跟你谈就到里面来，罗西，但你千万要听我的，别走出这个房间。’”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was four o’clock in the morning then, and if we’d of raised the blinds we’d of seen daylight.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was four o’clock in the morning then, and if we’d of raised the blinds we’d of seen daylight.”","zh":"“那时是凌晨四点，如果我们走过去拉开窗帘，应该能看到天光。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did he go?” I asked innocently.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did he go?”","zh":"“他出去了吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I asked innocently.","zh":"我天真地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Sure he went.” Mr. Wolfshiem’s nose flashed at me indignantly. “He turned around in the door and says: ‘Don’t let that waiter take away my coffee!’ Then he went out on the sidewalk, and they shot him three times in his full belly and drove away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sure he went.”","zh":"“他当然出去了，”沃夫希姆先生愤慨地看着我，鼻子涨得通红，“他走到门口，转过身说：‘别让服务员端走我的咖啡！’","scope":"group"},{"en":"Mr. Wolfshiem’s nose flashed at me indignantly.","zh":"“他当然出去了，”沃夫希姆先生愤慨地看着我，鼻子涨得通红，“他走到门口，转过身说：‘别让服务员端走我的咖啡！’","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He turned around in the door and says: ‘Don’t let that waiter take away my coffee!’","zh":"“他当然出去了，”沃夫希姆先生愤慨地看着我，鼻子涨得通红，“他走到门口，转过身说：‘别让服务员端走我的咖啡！’","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he went out on the sidewalk, and they shot him three times in his full belly and drove away.”","zh":"然后他走到外面的人行道上，他们朝他吃得饱饱的肚子开了三枪，开车跑掉了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Four of them were electrocuted,” I said, remembering.","sentences":[{"en":"“Four of them were electrocuted,” I said, remembering.","zh":"我终于想起这件事来了，于是说：“其中有四个人后来被电刑处死。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Five, with Becker.” His nostrils turned to me in an interested way. “I understand you’re looking for a business gonnegtion.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Five, with Becker.”","zh":"“五个，还有贝克尔。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His nostrils turned to me in an interested way.","zh":"他的鼻孔好奇地向我转过来，“听说你想找‘光系’做点生意？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I understand you’re looking for a business gonnegtion.”","zh":"他的鼻孔好奇地向我转过来，“听说你想找‘光系’做点生意？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The juxtaposition of these two remarks was startling. Gatsby answered for me:","sentences":[{"en":"The juxtaposition of these two remarks was startling.","zh":"他这句话让我感到莫名其妙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby answered for me:","zh":"盖茨比开口替我回答。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, no,” he exclaimed, “this isn’t the man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no,” he exclaimed, “this isn’t the man.”","zh":"“不是啦，”他说，“他不是那个人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No?” Mr. Wolfshiem seemed disappointed.","sentences":[{"en":"“No?”","zh":"“不是啊？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mr. Wolfshiem seemed disappointed.","zh":"沃夫希姆先生似乎很失望。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This is just a friend. I told you we’d talk about that some other time.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This is just a friend.","zh":"“这位只是我的朋友。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I told you we’d talk about that some other time.”","zh":"那件事我们下回再谈。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I beg your pardon,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, “I had a wrong man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I beg your pardon,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, “I had a wrong man.”","zh":"“真对不起，”沃夫希姆先生说，“我刚才认错人了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A succulent hash arrived, and Mr. Wolfshiem, forgetting the more sentimental atmosphere of the old Metropole, began to eat with ferocious delicacy. His eyes, meanwhile, roved very slowly all around the room—he completed the arc by turning to inspect the people directly behind. I think that, except for my presence, he would have taken one short glance beneath our own table.","sentences":[{"en":"A succulent hash arrived, and Mr. Wolfshiem, forgetting the more sentimental atmosphere of the old Metropole, began to eat with ferocious delicacy.","zh":"一道美味的菜被端上来，沃夫希姆先生也就忘记旧京饭店那些伤感的往事，开始狼吞虎咽地吃起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His eyes, meanwhile, roved very slowly all around the room—he completed the arc by turning to inspect the people directly behind.","zh":"与此同时，他的眼睛非常缓慢地扫过整个餐厅——还不忘转过头去看坐在他正后面的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think that, except for my presence, he would have taken one short glance beneath our own table.","zh":"我想要不是我在场，他可能连我们的桌子底下也要瞄两眼。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look here, old sport,” said Gatsby, leaning toward me, “I’m afraid I made you a little angry this morning in the car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look here, old sport,” said Gatsby, leaning toward me, “I’m afraid I made you a little angry this morning in the car.”","zh":"“喂，老兄，”盖茨比凑过来对我说，“我今天早上在车里让你有点生气吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was the smile again, but this time I held out against it.","sentences":[{"en":"There was the smile again, but this time I held out against it.","zh":"他又是满脸堆欢，但这次我可不买他的账。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t like mysteries,” I answered, “and I don’t understand why you won’t come out frankly and tell me what you want. Why has it all got to come through Miss Baker?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t like mysteries,” I answered, “and I don’t understand why you won’t come out frankly and tell me what you want.","zh":"“我不喜欢搞得很神秘的样子，”我回答说，“我不明白你为什么不直截了当跟我说你想要什么。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why has it all got to come through Miss Baker?”","zh":"为什么非得通过贝克小姐不可呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, it’s nothing underhand,” he assured me. “Miss Baker’s a great sportswoman, you know, and she’d never do anything that wasn’t all right.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it’s nothing underhand,” he assured me.","zh":"“哎呀，不是什么见不得人的事情啦，”他宽慰我说，“贝克小姐是个伟大的运动员，这你也知道的，她不会做歪门邪道的事。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Miss Baker’s a great sportswoman, you know, and she’d never do anything that wasn’t all right.”","zh":"“哎呀，不是什么见不得人的事情啦，”他宽慰我说，“贝克小姐是个伟大的运动员，这你也知道的，她不会做歪门邪道的事。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Suddenly he looked at his watch, jumped up, and hurried from the room, leaving me with Mr. Wolfshiem at the table.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly he looked at his watch, jumped up, and hurried from the room, leaving me with Mr. Wolfshiem at the table.","zh":"他突然看看手表，猛地站起来，匆匆走出餐厅，留下我和沃夫希姆先生。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He has to telephone,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, following him with his eyes. “Fine fellow, isn’t he? Handsome to look at and a perfect gentleman.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He has to telephone,” said Mr. Wolfshiem, following him with his eyes.","zh":"“他得去打电话，”沃夫希姆目送他出去，同时说，“他是个好家伙，对吧？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Fine fellow, isn’t he?","zh":"“他得去打电话，”沃夫希姆目送他出去，同时说，“他是个好家伙，对吧？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Handsome to look at and a perfect gentleman.”","zh":"长得那么帅，真是个完美的绅士。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“是啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He’s an Oggsford man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He’s an Oggsford man.”","zh":"“他是‘牛精’人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh!”","zh":"“哦！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He went to Oggsford College in England. You know Oggsford College?”","sentences":[{"en":"“He went to Oggsford College in England.","zh":"“他念过英国的‘牛精’大学。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You know Oggsford College?”","zh":"你知道‘牛精’大学吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve heard of it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve heard of it.”","zh":"“略有耳闻。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s one of the most famous colleges in the world.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s one of the most famous colleges in the world.”","zh":"“那是世界上最著名的大学。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Have you known Gatsby for a long time?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you known Gatsby for a long time?”","zh":"“你认识盖茨比很久了吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Several years,” he answered in a gratified way. “I made the pleasure of his acquaintance just after the war. But I knew I had discovered a man of fine breeding after I talked with him an hour. I said to myself: ‘There’s the kind of man you’d like to take home and introduce to your mother and sister.’ ” He paused. “I see you’re looking at my cuff buttons.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Several years,” he answered in a gratified way.","zh":"“有几年了，”他颇感荣幸地说，“直到战争结束后不久，我才有幸结识他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I made the pleasure of his acquaintance just after the war.","zh":"“有几年了，”他颇感荣幸地说，“直到战争结束后不久，我才有幸结识他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But I knew I had discovered a man of fine breeding after I talked with him an hour.","zh":"但跟他聊了一个小时之后，我就知道这人的家世肯定很显赫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I said to myself: ‘There’s the kind of man you’d like to take home and introduce to your mother and sister.’ ” He paused.","zh":"我心里想：‘原来真有这种你愿意带回家介绍给你母亲和姐妹认识的人啊。’”他停顿片刻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I see you’re looking at my cuff buttons.”","zh":"“我发现你在看着我的袖扣。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I hadn’t been looking at them, but I did now. They were composed of oddly familiar pieces of ivory.","sentences":[{"en":"I hadn’t been looking at them, but I did now.","zh":"我本来没有看，但现在看了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were composed of oddly familiar pieces of ivory.","zh":"它们的形状很奇怪，似乎是象牙做的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Finest specimens of human molars,” he informed me.","sentences":[{"en":"“Finest specimens of human molars,” he informed me.","zh":"“这是最好的人类臼齿的标本。”他告诉我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well!” I inspected them. “That’s a very interesting idea.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well!”","zh":"“哇！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inspected them.","zh":"我仔细地看着它们，“这是个非常有趣的创意。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“That’s a very interesting idea.”","zh":"我仔细地看着它们，“这是个非常有趣的创意。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yeah.” He flipped his sleeves up under his coat. “Yeah, Gatsby’s very careful about women. He would never so much as look at a friend’s wife.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yeah.”","zh":"“是啊，”他把衬衣的袖口缩回到外套之下，“是啊，盖茨比对女人非常规矩。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He flipped his sleeves up under his coat.","zh":"“是啊，”他把衬衣的袖口缩回到外套之下，“是啊，盖茨比对女人非常规矩。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Yeah, Gatsby’s very careful about women.","zh":"“是啊，”他把衬衣的袖口缩回到外套之下，“是啊，盖茨比对女人非常规矩。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He would never so much as look at a friend’s wife.”","zh":"他从来不正眼看朋友的太太。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When the subject of this instinctive trust returned to the table and sat down Mr. Wolfshiem drank his coffee with a jerk and got to his feet.","sentences":[{"en":"When the subject of this instinctive trust returned to the table and sat down Mr. Wolfshiem drank his coffee with a jerk and got to his feet.","zh":"此时这种信赖所托付的对象回到餐桌坐下，沃夫希姆先生猛然喝掉他的咖啡，然后站起身来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I have enjoyed my lunch,” he said, “and I’m going to run off from you two young men before I outstay my welcome.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I have enjoyed my lunch,” he said, “and I’m going to run off from you two young men before I outstay my welcome.”","zh":"“我很喜欢今天的午餐，”他说，“我离开你们两位年轻人啦，免得你们嫌我待得太久。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t hurry Meyer,” said Gatsby, without enthusiasm. Mr. Wolfshiem raised his hand in a sort of benediction.","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t hurry Meyer,” said Gatsby, without enthusiasm.","zh":"“别着急，梅耶，”盖茨比言不由衷地说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mr. Wolfshiem raised his hand in a sort of benediction.","zh":"沃夫希姆先生抬起手，像是替我们赐福。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re very polite, but I belong to another generation,” he announced solemnly. “You sit here and discuss your sports and your young ladies and your—” He supplied an imaginary noun with another wave of his hand. “As for me, I am fifty years old, and I won’t impose myself on you any longer.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re very polite, but I belong to another generation,” he announced solemnly.","zh":"“你们非常有礼貌，但我是老人家啦，”他表情沉重地宣布，“你们就坐在这里吧，可以谈谈体育，谈谈年轻的女人和…”他又挥了挥手，用以代替我们的第三个话题。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You sit here and discuss your sports and your young ladies and your—” He supplied an imaginary noun with another wave of his hand.","zh":"“你们非常有礼貌，但我是老人家啦，”他表情沉重地宣布，“你们就坐在这里吧，可以谈谈体育，谈谈年轻的女人和…”他又挥了挥手，用以代替我们的第三个话题。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“As for me, I am fifty years old, and I won’t impose myself on you any longer.”","zh":"“至于我，我已经五十岁，不会再打扰你们啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As he shook hands and turned away his tragic nose was trembling. I wondered if I had said anything to offend him.","sentences":[{"en":"As he shook hands and turned away his tragic nose was trembling.","zh":"跟我们握手道别、转身离去期间，他那悲剧的鼻子不停地抽动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wondered if I had said anything to offend him.","zh":"我在想我是不是哪句话得罪他了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He becomes very sentimental sometimes,” explained Gatsby. “This is one of his sentimental days. He’s quite a character around New York—a denizen of Broadway.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He becomes very sentimental sometimes,” explained Gatsby.","zh":"“他有时候会变得非常忧郁，”盖茨比解释说，“今天他又多愁善感了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“This is one of his sentimental days.","zh":"“他有时候会变得非常忧郁，”盖茨比解释说，“今天他又多愁善感了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He’s quite a character around New York—a denizen of Broadway.”","zh":"在纽约他也算是个人物了——百老汇的地头蛇。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who is he, anyhow, an actor?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who is he, anyhow, an actor?”","zh":"“他到底是什么人？演员吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No.”","zh":"“不是。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“A dentist?”","sentences":[{"en":"“A dentist?”","zh":"“牙医？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Meyer Wolfshiem? No, he’s a gambler.” Gatsby hesitated, then added, coolly: “He’s the man who fixed the World’s Series back in 1919.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Meyer Wolfshiem?","zh":"“梅耶·沃夫希姆？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No, he’s a gambler.”","zh":"不是啦，他是开赌场的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby hesitated, then added, coolly: “He’s the man who fixed the World’s Series back in 1919.”","zh":"盖茨比欲言又止，然后淡淡地补充说，“他就是1919年世界棒球大赛舞弊案的幕后黑手。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Fixed the World’s Series?” I repeated.","sentences":[{"en":"“Fixed the World’s Series?”","zh":"盖茨比欲言又止，然后淡淡地补充说，“他就是1919年世界棒球大赛舞弊案的幕后黑手。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I repeated.","zh":"盖茨比欲言又止，然后淡淡地补充说，“他就是1919年世界棒球大赛舞弊案的幕后黑手。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The idea staggered me. I remembered, of course, that the World’s Series had been fixed in 1919, but if I had thought of it at all I would have thought of it as a thing that merely happened, the end of some inevitable chain. It never occurred to me that one man could start to play with the faith of fifty million people—with the single-mindedness of a burglar blowing a safe.","sentences":[{"en":"The idea staggered me.","zh":"“世界棒球大赛舞弊案？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I remembered, of course, that the World’s Series had been fixed in 1919, but if I had thought of it at all I would have thought of it as a thing that merely happened, the end of some inevitable chain.","zh":"我喃喃地说。这简直让我瞠目结舌。我当然记得1919年的世界棒球大赛舞弊案，但我总以为那桩丑闻是自动发生的，是许多因素发生连锁反应导致的不可避免的结果。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It never occurred to me that one man could start to play with the faith of fifty million people—with the single-mindedness of a burglar blowing a safe.","zh":"我从来没想到居然有人能够单枪匹马地愚弄五千万球迷——而且就像小偷专注地撬开保险箱那么简单。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How did he happen to do that?” I asked after a minute.","sentences":[{"en":"“How did he happen to do that?”","zh":"“他怎么会做那样的事呢？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I asked after a minute.","zh":"我沉默半晌问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He just saw the opportunity.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He just saw the opportunity.”","zh":"“他只是发现有机可乘而已。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why isn’t he in jail?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why isn’t he in jail?”","zh":"“他怎么没坐牢呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They can’t get him, old sport. He’s a smart man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They can’t get him, old sport.","zh":"“他们抓不到他的把柄啊，老兄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He’s a smart man.”","zh":"他是个聪明人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I insisted on paying the check. As the waiter brought my change I caught sight of Tom Buchanan across the crowded room.","sentences":[{"en":"I insisted on paying the check.","zh":"我执意付了账单。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As the waiter brought my change I caught sight of Tom Buchanan across the crowded room.","zh":"服务员把零钱拿给我时，我看见布坎南隔着许多人，坐在餐厅的另一边。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come along with me for a minute,” I said; “I’ve got to say hello to someone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come along with me for a minute,” I said; “I’ve got to say hello to someone.”","zh":"“请稍等我片刻，”我说，“我得去跟人打个招呼。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When he saw us Tom jumped up and took half a dozen steps in our direction.","sentences":[{"en":"When he saw us Tom jumped up and took half a dozen steps in our direction.","zh":"汤姆看到我们立刻跳了起来，三步并作两步走到我们面前。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where’ve you been?” he demanded eagerly. “Daisy’s furious because you haven’t called up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where’ve you been?” he demanded eagerly.","zh":"“你到哪里去了？”他热情地问，“黛熙很生气，因为你没打电话给我们。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Daisy’s furious because you haven’t called up.”","zh":"“你到哪里去了？”他热情地问，“黛熙很生气，因为你没打电话给我们。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This is Mr. Gatsby, Mr. Buchanan.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This is Mr. Gatsby, Mr. Buchanan.”","zh":"“这位是盖茨比先生，布坎南先生。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They shook hands briefly, and a strained, unfamiliar look of embarrassment came over Gatsby’s face.","sentences":[{"en":"They shook hands briefly, and a strained, unfamiliar look of embarrassment came over Gatsby’s face.","zh":"他们草草地握了手，一阵紧张、不自然的尴尬神色掠过盖茨比的脸。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How’ve you been, anyhow?” demanded Tom of me. “How’d you happen to come up this far to eat?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How’ve you been, anyhow?” demanded Tom of me.","zh":"“你最近到底怎么样啊？”汤姆追问我说，“你怎么会大老远地跑来这里吃饭？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“How’d you happen to come up this far to eat?”","zh":"“你最近到底怎么样啊？”汤姆追问我说，“你怎么会大老远地跑来这里吃饭？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve been having lunch with Mr. Gatsby.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve been having lunch with Mr. Gatsby.”","zh":"“我跟盖茨比先生约好在这里吃午饭。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I turned toward Mr. Gatsby, but he was no longer there.","sentences":[{"en":"I turned toward Mr. Gatsby, but he was no longer there.","zh":"我回头去看盖茨比，但他已经不见踪影了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"One October day in nineteen-seventeen—","sentences":[{"en":"One October day in nineteen-seventeen—","zh":"一九一七年十月某天…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"(said Jordan Baker that afternoon, sitting up very straight on a straight chair in the tea-garden at the Plaza Hotel)","sentences":[{"en":"(said Jordan Baker that afternoon, sitting up very straight on a straight chair in the tea-garden at the Plaza Hotel)","zh":"（那天下午，在广场酒店茶厅里的高背椅上，乔丹·贝克正襟危坐，向我娓娓道来）","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"—I was walking along from one place to another, half on the sidewalks and half on the lawns. I was happier on the lawns because I had on shoes from England with rubber knobs on the soles that bit into the soft ground. I had on a new plaid skirt also that blew a little in the wind, and whenever this happened the red, white, and blue banners in front of all the houses stretched out stiff and said tut-tut-tut-tut, in a disapproving way.","sentences":[{"en":"—I was walking along from one place to another, half on the sidewalks and half on the lawns.","zh":"我要去某个地方，于是便出了门，有时在人行道上走，有时在草地上走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was happier on the lawns because I had on shoes from England with rubber knobs on the soles that bit into the soft ground.","zh":"我更喜欢走在草地上，因为我穿的鞋是英国来的，圆圆的橡胶鞋跟踩在软软的草地上很舒服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had on a new plaid skirt also that blew a little in the wind, and whenever this happened the red, white, and blue banners in front of all the houses stretched out stiff and said tut-tut-tut-tut, in a disapproving way.","zh":"当时我还穿着一条新的格子裙，每当我的裙子随风飘扬，路边所有人家门前红白蓝三色国旗就会挺得笔直，发出“啧…啧…啧”的声音，好像很不以为然。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The largest of the banners and the largest of the lawns belonged to Daisy Fay’s house. She was just eighteen, two years older than me, and by far the most popular of all the young girls in Louisville. She dressed in white, and had a little white roadster, and all day long the telephone rang in her house and excited young officers from Camp Taylor demanded the privilege of monopolizing her that night. “Anyways, for an hour!”","sentences":[{"en":"The largest of the banners and the largest of the lawns belonged to Daisy Fay’s house.","zh":"最大的国旗和最大的草坪属于黛熙·费伊家。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was just eighteen, two years older than me, and by far the most popular of all the young girls in Louisville.","zh":"她那年只有十八岁，比我大两岁，是路易斯维尔最最受欢迎的少女。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She dressed in white, and had a little white roadster, and all day long the telephone rang in her house and excited young officers from Camp Taylor demanded the privilege of monopolizing her that night.","zh":"她喜欢穿白色的衣服，开的跑车也是白色的，家里的电话整天响个不停，泰勒军营那些兴奋的年轻军官纷纷打电话给她，想要得到独占她整个夜晚的特权。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Anyways, for an hour!”","zh":"“哪怕一个小时也行啊！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When I came opposite her house that morning her white roadster was beside the kerb, and she was sitting in it with a lieutenant I had never seen before. They were so engrossed in each other that she didn’t see me until I was five feet away.","sentences":[{"en":"When I came opposite her house that morning her white roadster was beside the kerb, and she was sitting in it with a lieutenant I had never seen before.","zh":"那天早晨我走到她家门口时，她的白色跑车就停在路边，她坐在车里，同车是一个我以前从未见过的中尉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were so engrossed in each other that she didn’t see me until I was five feet away.","zh":"他们含情脉脉地看着对方，等我走到五英尺之内她才看见我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hello, Jordan,” she called unexpectedly. “Please come here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hello, Jordan,” she called unexpectedly.","zh":"“你好啊，乔丹，”她突然喊了起来，“麻烦你过来一下。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Please come here.”","zh":"“你好啊，乔丹，”她突然喊了起来，“麻烦你过来一下。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was flattered that she wanted to speak to me, because of all the older girls I admired her most. She asked me if I was going to the Red Cross to make bandages. I was. Well, then, would I tell them that she couldn’t come that day? The officer looked at Daisy while she was speaking, in a way that every young girl wants to be looked at sometime, and because it seemed romantic to me I have remembered the incident ever since. His name was Jay Gatsby, and I didn’t lay eyes on him again for over four years—even after I’d met him on Long Island I didn’t realize it was the same man.","sentences":[{"en":"I was flattered that she wanted to speak to me, because of all the older girls I admired her most.","zh":"她居然想跟我说话，这让我受宠若惊，因为在所有比我大的女孩当中，我最崇拜的就是她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She asked me if I was going to the Red Cross to make bandages.","zh":"她问我是否要到红十字会去做绷带。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was.","zh":"我说是的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, then, would I tell them that she couldn’t come that day?","zh":"那好啊，能否请我告诉他们，她今天不来了？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The officer looked at Daisy while she was speaking, in a way that every young girl wants to be looked at sometime, and because it seemed romantic to me I have remembered the incident ever since.","zh":"黛熙说话时，那军官如痴如醉地看着她，每个女孩都希望有人这样仰慕自己。在我看来，这是非常罗曼蒂克的，所以后来我一直记得这件事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His name was Jay Gatsby, and I didn’t lay eyes on him again for over four years—even after I’d met him on Long Island I didn’t realize it was the same man.","zh":"他的名字叫杰伊·盖茨比，随后四年多的时间里，我再也没有见过他——甚至直到我在长岛遇见他之后，我都没有意识到他就是那个人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That was nineteen-seventeen. By the next year I had a few beaux myself, and I began to play in tournaments, so I didn’t see Daisy very often. She went with a slightly older crowd—when she went with anyone at all. Wild rumours were circulating about her—how her mother had found her packing her bag one winter night to go to New York and say goodbye to a soldier who was going overseas. She was effectually prevented, but she wasn’t on speaking terms with her family for several weeks. After that she didn’t play around with the soldiers any more, but only with a few flat-footed, shortsighted young men in town, who couldn’t get into the army at all.","sentences":[{"en":"That was nineteen-seventeen.","zh":"那是一九一七年。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By the next year I had a few beaux myself, and I began to play in tournaments, so I didn’t see Daisy very often.","zh":"第二年我自己也交了几个男朋友，并开始参加高尔夫球赛，所以并不经常见到黛熙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went with a slightly older crowd—when she went with anyone at all.","zh":"她交往的人年纪都比我稍微大几岁，不过她已经很少跟人走动了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wild rumours were circulating about her—how her mother had found her packing her bag one winter night to go to New York and say goodbye to a soldier who was going overseas.","zh":"有关她的谣言传得很厉害——人们说在某个冬天的夜晚，她母亲发现她正在收拾行李，准备去纽约跟一个即将远赴海外的士兵道别。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was effectually prevented, but she wasn’t on speaking terms with her family for several weeks.","zh":"她父母成功地把她拦下了，但她接连几个星期不跟家里人说话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After that she didn’t play around with the soldiers any more, but only with a few flat-footed, shortsighted young men in town, who couldn’t get into the army at all.","zh":"自那以后，她再也不跟部队的人交朋友了，只跟本地几个扁平足或者近视、根本就当不了兵的年轻人来往。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"By the next autumn she was gay again, gay as ever. She had a début after the armistice, and in February she was presumably engaged to a man from New Orleans. In June she married Tom Buchanan of Chicago, with more pomp and circumstance than Louisville ever knew before. He came down with a hundred people in four private cars, and hired a whole floor of the Muhlbach Hotel, and the day before the wedding he gave her a string of pearls valued at three hundred and fifty thousand dollars.","sentences":[{"en":"By the next autumn she was gay again, gay as ever.","zh":"等到秋天来临，她又活泼起来了，像从前那样活泼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had a début after the armistice, and in February she was presumably engaged to a man from New Orleans.","zh":"停战之后，她父母为她举办了盛大的成年礼，据说她在二月订婚，对方来自新奥尔良。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In June she married Tom Buchanan of Chicago, with more pomp and circumstance than Louisville ever knew before.","zh":"六月她嫁给了芝加哥的汤姆·布坎南，他们结婚时的盛况是路易斯维尔人前所未见的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He came down with a hundred people in four private cars, and hired a whole floor of the Muhlbach Hotel, and the day before the wedding he gave her a string of pearls valued at three hundred and fifty thousand dollars.","zh":"他带着上百个人，租了四节车厢，浩浩荡荡地南下，在穆尔巴赫酒店租了整整一层楼。结婚前那天，他送给黛熙一串珍珠项链，价值三十五万美元。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was a bridesmaid. I came into her room half an hour before the bridal dinner, and found her lying on her bed as lovely as the June night in her flowered dress—and as drunk as a monkey. She had a bottle of Sauterne in one hand and a letter in the other.","sentences":[{"en":"I was a bridesmaid.","zh":"我是伴娘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I came into her room half an hour before the bridal dinner, and found her lying on her bed as lovely as the June night in her flowered dress—and as drunk as a monkey.","zh":"婚礼前夕，新娘出阁晚会开始前半小时，我走进她的房间，发现她躺在床上，美得像那个六月的夜晚，穿着绣花的裙子——醉得像只猴子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had a bottle of Sauterne in one hand and a letter in the other.","zh":"她一手拿着一瓶苏玳白葡萄酒，一手拿着一封信。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“ ’Gratulate me,” she muttered. “Never had a drink before, but oh how I do enjoy it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“ ’Gratulate me,” she muttered.","zh":"“恭喜我呀，”她喃喃地说，“我以前没喝过酒，但我今天喝得很高兴。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Never had a drink before, but oh how I do enjoy it.”","zh":"“恭喜我呀，”她喃喃地说，“我以前没喝过酒，但我今天喝得很高兴。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s the matter, Daisy?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the matter, Daisy?”","zh":"“黛熙，你怎么了？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was scared, I can tell you; I’d never seen a girl like that before.","sentences":[{"en":"I was scared, I can tell you; I’d never seen a girl like that before.","zh":"当时我吓坏了，我告诉你。我从来没有见过醉成那样的女孩。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Here, dearies.” She groped around in a wastebasket she had with her on the bed and pulled out the string of pearls. “Take ’em downstairs and give ’em back to whoever they belong to. Tell ’em all Daisy’s change’ her mine. Say: ‘Daisy’s change’ her mine!’ ”","sentences":[{"en":"“Here, dearies.”","zh":"“这里，亲爱的。”她在早前搬到床上的废纸篓里面乱摸，掏出那串珍珠项链。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She groped around in a wastebasket she had with her on the bed and pulled out the string of pearls.","zh":"“这里，亲爱的。”她在早前搬到床上的废纸篓里面乱摸，掏出那串珍珠项链。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Take ’em downstairs and give ’em back to whoever they belong to.","zh":"“把它拿到楼下去，是谁的就还给谁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell ’em all Daisy’s change’ her mine.","zh":"你告诉他们，黛熙改变主意了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Say: ‘Daisy’s change’ her mine!’ ”","zh":"就这么说：‘黛熙改变主意了！’”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She began to cry—she cried and cried. I rushed out and found her mother’s maid, and we locked the door and got her into a cold bath. She wouldn’t let go of the letter. She took it into the tub with her and squeezed it up in a wet ball, and only let me leave it in the soap-dish when she saw that it was coming to pieces like snow.","sentences":[{"en":"She began to cry—she cried and cried.","zh":"她哭了起来——哭了又哭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I rushed out and found her mother’s maid, and we locked the door and got her into a cold bath.","zh":"我赶紧跑出去，找到她母亲的女佣，我们把她的房门关起来，让她洗了冷水澡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wouldn’t let go of the letter.","zh":"她不肯松开那封信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She took it into the tub with her and squeezed it up in a wet ball, and only let me leave it in the soap-dish when she saw that it was coming to pieces like snow.","zh":"她把信带进浴缸，浸湿了之后紧紧地揉成一团，后来看见它变成雪花般的碎片，才让我拿起来放在香皂碟里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But she didn’t say another word. We gave her spirits of ammonia and put ice on her forehead and hooked her back into her dress, and half an hour later, when we walked out of the room, the pearls were around her neck and the incident was over. Next day at five o’clock she married Tom Buchanan without so much as a shiver, and started off on a three months’ trip to the South Seas.","sentences":[{"en":"But she didn’t say another word.","zh":"但她再也没有说话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We gave her spirits of ammonia and put ice on her forehead and hooked her back into her dress, and half an hour later, when we walked out of the room, the pearls were around her neck and the incident was over.","zh":"我们拿来醒酒的精油让她闻，在她额头上放了冰块，哄她穿上裙子。半个小时后，当我们走出房间，珍珠项链挂在她的脖子上，这事就算过去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Next day at five o’clock she married Tom Buchanan without so much as a shiver, and started off on a three months’ trip to the South Seas.","zh":"第二天下午五点，她若无其事地嫁给了汤姆·布坎南，然后启程去南太平洋旅游三个月。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I saw them in Santa Barbara when they came back, and I thought I’d never seen a girl so mad about her husband. If he left the room for a minute she’d look around uneasily, and say: “Where’s Tom gone?” and wear the most abstracted expression until she saw him coming in the door. She used to sit on the sand with his head in her lap by the hour, rubbing her fingers over his eyes and looking at him with unfathomable delight. It was touching to see them together—it made you laugh in a hushed, fascinated way. That was in August. A week after I left Santa Barbara Tom ran into a wagon on the Ventura road one night, and ripped a front wheel off his car. The girl who was with him got into the papers, too, because her arm was broken—she was one of the chambermaids in the Santa Barbara Hotel.","sentences":[{"en":"I saw them in Santa Barbara when they came back, and I thought I’d never seen a girl so mad about her husband.","zh":"他们回来后，我曾在圣塔芭芭拉遇见过他们，我认识的女孩中，没有人像她那么在乎她的丈夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If he left the room for a minute she’d look around uneasily, and say: “Where’s Tom gone?” and wear the most abstracted expression until she saw him coming in the door.","zh":"如果他有片刻不在房间里，黛熙就会心绪不宁地到处找，并说：“汤姆去哪里了啊？”而且会满脸失魂落魄的神色，直到看见他从门口走进来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She used to sit on the sand with his head in her lap by the hour, rubbing her fingers over his eyes and looking at him with unfathomable delight.","zh":"黛熙常常在沙滩上一坐个把小时，让他把头枕在大腿上，用手轻抚他的眼睛，无限欣喜地看着他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was touching to see them together—it made you laugh in a hushed, fascinated way.","zh":"这种恩爱的景象真叫人感动——它会让你悄悄地、向往地笑起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That was in August.","zh":"当时是八月。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A week after I left Santa Barbara Tom ran into a wagon on the Ventura road one night, and ripped a front wheel off his car.","zh":"我离开圣塔芭芭拉之后一个星期，汤姆有天晚上在文图拉公路撞上一辆货车，轿车的一个前轮撞得飞掉了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The girl who was with him got into the papers, too, because her arm was broken—she was one of the chambermaids in the Santa Barbara Hotel.","zh":"和他同车的女孩也登上了报纸，因为她撞断了手——她是圣塔芭芭拉酒店的服务员。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The next April Daisy had her little girl, and they went to France for a year. I saw them one spring in Cannes, and later in Deauville, and then they came back to Chicago to settle down. Daisy was popular in Chicago, as you know. They moved with a fast crowd, all of them young and rich and wild, but she came out with an absolutely perfect reputation. Perhaps because she doesn’t drink. It’s a great advantage not to drink among hard-drinking people. You can hold your tongue and, moreover, you can time any little irregularity of your own so that everybody else is so blind that they don’t see or care. Perhaps Daisy never went in for amour at all—and yet there’s something in that voice of hers…","sentences":[{"en":"The next April Daisy had her little girl, and they went to France for a year.","zh":"隔年四月，黛熙生下女儿，他们搬到法国住了一年。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw them one spring in Cannes, and later in Deauville, and then they came back to Chicago to settle down.","zh":"有一年春天，我在戛纳遇到他们，后来在多维尔又碰了面，然后他们就到芝加哥定居了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy was popular in Chicago, as you know.","zh":"黛熙在芝加哥很受欢迎，这你也知道的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They moved with a fast crowd, all of them young and rich and wild, but she came out with an absolutely perfect reputation.","zh":"他们跟一帮花天酒地的人交朋友，都是些年少多金的浪荡子，但她的名誉始终是绝对的完美无瑕。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps because she doesn’t drink.","zh":"也许是因为她不喝酒吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s a great advantage not to drink among hard-drinking people.","zh":"在酗酒的人群中，滴酒不沾可以占很大的便宜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You can hold your tongue and, moreover, you can time any little irregularity of your own so that everybody else is so blind that they don’t see or care.","zh":"不喝酒你就不会乱说话，而且就算你想做点离经叛道的事，也可以等到其他每个人都喝得烂醉时再做，这样他们就不会看到，看到了也不关心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps Daisy never went in for amour at all—and yet there’s something in that voice of hers…","zh":"也许黛熙从来没想过要勾引别人吧——可是她的声音又总是让人觉得她…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Well, about six weeks ago, she heard the name Gatsby for the first time in years. It was when I asked you—do you remember?—if you knew Gatsby in West Egg. After you had gone home she came into my room and woke me up, and said: “What Gatsby?” and when I described him—I was half asleep—she said in the strangest voice that it must be the man she used to know. It wasn’t until then that I connected this Gatsby with the officer in her white car.","sentences":[{"en":"Well, about six weeks ago, she heard the name Gatsby for the first time in years.","zh":"好啦，大概六个星期之前，她时隔多年，再次听到盖茨比的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was when I asked you—do you remember?—if you knew Gatsby in West Egg.","zh":"就是那天晚上，我问你——你还记得吗——认不认识西卵的盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After you had gone home she came into my room and woke me up, and said: “What Gatsby?” and when I described him—I was half asleep—she said in the strangest voice that it must be the man she used to know.","zh":"你回家后，她走进我的房间，把我摇醒，然后说：“哪个盖茨比？”听我迷迷糊糊地描述了他的模样——当时我还没全醒，她用最奇怪的声音说，这肯定就是她以前认识的那个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It wasn’t until then that I connected this Gatsby with the officer in her white car.","zh":"直到那时，我才把这位盖茨比和她白色跑车里那位军官联系起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"When Jordan Baker had finished telling all this we had left the Plaza for half an hour and were driving in a victoria through Central Park. The sun had gone down behind the tall apartments of the movie stars in the West Fifties, and the clear voices of children, already gathered like crickets on the grass, rose through the hot twilight:","sentences":[{"en":"When Jordan Baker had finished telling all this we had left the Plaza for half an hour and were driving in a victoria through Central Park.","zh":"等到乔丹·贝克讲完这个故事，我们离开广场酒店已经半个小时，坐着维多利亚马车在中央公园里穿行。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sun had gone down behind the tall apartments of the movie stars in the West Fifties, and the clear voices of children, already gathered like crickets on the grass, rose through the hot twilight:","zh":"这时太阳已经落在西城第五十几街那些电影明星居住的公寓楼后面，许多儿童已经像蟋蟀般聚集到草坪上，他们清脆的歌声在温热的暮色里响起：我是阿拉伯的大酋长。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m the Sheik of Araby. Your love belongs to me. At night when you’re asleep Into your tent I’ll creep—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m the Sheik of Araby.","zh":"你的心呀系在我身上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Your love belongs to me.","zh":"今夜里等你睡得正香，","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At night when you’re asleep Into your tent I’ll creep—”","zh":"我要偷偷爬进你闺帐。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was a strange coincidence,” I said.","sentences":[{"en":"“It was a strange coincidence,” I said.","zh":"“真是巧合得有点古怪，”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But it wasn’t a coincidence at all.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But it wasn’t a coincidence at all.”","zh":"“其实根本不是巧合。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why not?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why not?”","zh":"“为什么呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Gatsby bought that house so that Daisy would be just across the bay.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Gatsby bought that house so that Daisy would be just across the bay.”","zh":"“盖茨比买下那座房子，是因为黛熙就住在海湾正对面。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Then it had not been merely the stars to which he had aspired on that June night. He came alive to me, delivered suddenly from the womb of his purposeless splendour.","sentences":[{"en":"Then it had not been merely the stars to which he had aspired on that June night.","zh":"原来他在那个六月的夜晚仰望的不仅仅是天边的星星。在我心里，他的形象突然丰满起来了，不再是一个漫无目的地挥霍着财富的暴发户。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He came alive to me, delivered suddenly from the womb of his purposeless splendour.","zh":"原来他在那个六月的夜晚仰望的不仅仅是天边的星星。在我心里，他的形象突然丰满起来了，不再是一个漫无目的地挥霍着财富的暴发户。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He wants to know,” continued Jordan, “if you’ll invite Daisy to your house some afternoon and then let him come over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He wants to know,” continued Jordan, “if you’ll invite Daisy to your house some afternoon and then let him come over.”","zh":"“他想知道，”乔丹接着说，“你能不能找个下午去请黛熙到你家做客，然后让他过去坐坐。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The modesty of the demand shook me. He had waited five years and bought a mansion where he dispensed starlight to casual moths—so that he could “come over” some afternoon to a stranger’s garden.","sentences":[{"en":"The modesty of the demand shook me.","zh":"他的要求居然这么简单，这让我很吃惊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had waited five years and bought a mansion where he dispensed starlight to casual moths—so that he could “come over” some afternoon to a stranger’s garden.","zh":"他等了整整五年，买下那座华厦，把星光施舍给那些想来就来、想去就去的飞蛾——他费了这么多心血，只是为了能够在某天下午，到一个陌生人家里“坐坐”。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did I have to know all this before he could ask such a little thing?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Did I have to know all this before he could ask such a little thing?”","zh":"“不就是托我帮个小忙嘛，有必要原原本本地让我知道吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He’s afraid, he’s waited so long. He thought you might be offended. You see, he’s regular tough underneath it all.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He’s afraid, he’s waited so long.","zh":"“他很害怕，他等了这么久。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thought you might be offended.","zh":"他怕会得罪你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You see, he’s regular tough underneath it all.”","zh":"你看，他为人其实挺细心周到的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Something worried me.","sentences":[{"en":"Something worried me.","zh":"我还是觉得有点蹊跷。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why didn’t he ask you to arrange a meeting?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why didn’t he ask you to arrange a meeting?”","zh":"“他为什么不请你安排他们相见呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He wants her to see his house,” she explained. “And your house is right next door.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He wants her to see his house,” she explained.","zh":"“他想让黛熙看看他的房子，”她解释说，“而你的房子又正好在隔壁。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And your house is right next door.”","zh":"“他想让黛熙看看他的房子，”她解释说，“而你的房子又正好在隔壁。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh!”","zh":"“哦！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I think he half expected her to wander into one of his parties, some night,” went on Jordan, “but she never did. Then he began asking people casually if they knew her, and I was the first one he found. It was that night he sent for me at his dance, and you should have heard the elaborate way he worked up to it. Of course, I immediately suggested a luncheon in New York—and I thought he’d go mad:","sentences":[{"en":"“I think he half expected her to wander into one of his parties, some night,” went on Jordan, “but she never did.","zh":"“我估计他原本也有点期望黛熙会在某个晚上参加他的宴会，”乔丹继续说，“但她从来不去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he began asking people casually if they knew her, and I was the first one he found.","zh":"然后他开始假装不经意地问别人是否认识她，我是他问的人中第一个认识她的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was that night he sent for me at his dance, and you should have heard the elaborate way he worked up to it.","zh":"那晚舞会上他派人来找我，就是为了这事。可惜你没听到他开始是怎么拐弯抹角、大做铺垫，然后才提起来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Of course, I immediately suggested a luncheon in New York—and I thought he’d go mad:","zh":"当然，我立刻建议他们到纽约吃午饭——他一听急死了：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“ ‘I don’t want to do anything out of the way!’ he kept saying. ‘I want to see her right next door.’","sentences":[{"en":"“ ‘I don’t want to do anything out of the way!’ he kept saying. ‘I want to see her right next door.’","zh":"“‘我不想做得那么过分！’他不停地说，‘我只想在隔壁看看她。’","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“When I said you were a particular friend of Tom’s, he started to abandon the whole idea. He doesn’t know very much about Tom, though he says he’s read a Chicago paper for years just on the chance of catching a glimpse of Daisy’s name.”","sentences":[{"en":"“When I said you were a particular friend of Tom’s, he started to abandon the whole idea.","zh":"“后来我说你是汤姆的好朋友，他开始放弃这整个计划。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He doesn’t know very much about Tom, though he says he’s read a Chicago paper for years just on the chance of catching a glimpse of Daisy’s name.”","zh":"他对汤姆不是很了解，不过他说他订了一份芝加哥报纸好几年，只是为了偶尔能够看见黛熙的名字。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was dark now, and as we dipped under a little bridge I put my arm around Jordan’s golden shoulder and drew her toward me and asked her to dinner. Suddenly I wasn’t thinking of Daisy and Gatsby any more, but of this clean, hard, limited person, who dealt in universal scepticism, and who leaned back jauntily just within the circle of my arm. A phrase began to beat in my ears with a sort of heady excitement: “There are only the pursued, the pursuing, the busy, and the tired.”","sentences":[{"en":"It was dark now, and as we dipped under a little bridge I put my arm around Jordan’s golden shoulder and drew her toward me and asked her to dinner.","zh":"这时天全黑了，马车从一座小桥下面穿过，我伸手搂住了乔丹金黄色的肩膀，把她揽到我身边，请她和我共进晚餐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suddenly I wasn’t thinking of Daisy and Gatsby any more, but of this clean, hard, limited person, who dealt in universal scepticism, and who leaned back jauntily just within the circle of my arm.","zh":"突然间，我心里想着的不再是黛熙和盖茨比，而是这个干净而结实、脑筋有点笨的女孩，这个对一切都抱着怀疑的心态、轻轻地靠在我臂弯里的女孩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A phrase began to beat in my ears with a sort of heady excitement: “There are only the pursued, the pursuing, the busy, and the tired.”","zh":"有句话开始令人激动地在我耳边响起：“世上只有两类人，追求者和被追求者，忙碌者和厌倦者。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And Daisy ought to have something in her life,” murmured Jordan to me.","sentences":[{"en":"“And Daisy ought to have something in her life,” murmured Jordan to me.","zh":"“黛熙的生活也应该有点安慰，”乔丹喃喃地对我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Does she want to see Gatsby?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Does she want to see Gatsby?”","zh":"“她想见盖茨比吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s not to know about it. Gatsby doesn’t want her to know. You’re just supposed to invite her to tea.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s not to know about it.","zh":"“别让她知道怎么回事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby doesn’t want her to know.","zh":"盖茨比不想让她知道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You’re just supposed to invite her to tea.”","zh":"你只要假装请她过来喝茶就好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We passed a barrier of dark trees, and then the façade of Fifty-Ninth Street, a block of delicate pale light, beamed down into the park. Unlike Gatsby and Tom Buchanan, I had no girl whose disembodied face floated along the dark cornices and blinding signs, and so I drew up the girl beside me, tightening my arms. Her wan, scornful mouth smiled, and so I drew her up again closer, this time to my face.","sentences":[{"en":"We passed a barrier of dark trees, and then the façade of Fifty-Ninth Street, a block of delicate pale light, beamed down into the park.","zh":"我们穿过一排黝黑的树，第五十九街的高楼出现在眼前，昏黄的灯光从漂亮的楼面照进了公园。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Unlike Gatsby and Tom Buchanan, I had no girl whose disembodied face floated along the dark cornices and blinding signs, and so I drew up the girl beside me, tightening my arms.","zh":"我不像盖茨比，也不像汤姆·布坎南，我没有魂牵梦萦的情人，不会在那些阴暗的屋檐和刺眼的招牌中看到她忽隐忽现的面容，所以我手臂用力，搂紧了身边这位女孩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her wan, scornful mouth smiled, and so I drew her up again closer, this time to my face.","zh":"她那苍白而高傲的双唇微微笑起来，于是我把她搂得更紧，凑过去亲吻她。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-5","n":5,"title":"Chapter V","titleZh":"第五章","paragraphs":[{"en":"When I came home to West Egg that night I was afraid for a moment that my house was on fire. Two o’clock and the whole corner of the peninsula was blazing with light, which fell unreal on the shrubbery and made thin elongating glints upon the roadside wires. Turning a corner, I saw that it was Gatsby’s house, lit from tower to cellar.","sentences":[{"en":"When I came home to West Egg that night I was afraid for a moment that my house was on fire.","zh":"那天晚上回到西卵时，我差点以为我的房子着火了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Two o’clock and the whole corner of the peninsula was blazing with light, which fell unreal on the shrubbery and made thin elongating glints upon the roadside wires.","zh":"当时已是凌晨两点，半岛末端散发出通红的光芒，似真似幻地照耀着灌木丛，路边的电线也被照成几道细长的射线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Turning a corner, I saw that it was Gatsby’s house, lit from tower to cellar.","zh":"拐弯之后我才发现，原来是盖茨比的房子，从塔楼到地窖灯火通明。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At first I thought it was another party, a wild rout that had resolved itself into “hide-and-go-seek” or “sardines-in-the-box” with all the house thrown open to the game. But there wasn’t a sound. Only wind in the trees, which blew the wires and made the lights go off and on again as if the house had winked into the darkness. As my taxi groaned away I saw Gatsby walking toward me across his lawn.","sentences":[{"en":"At first I thought it was another party, a wild rout that had resolved itself into “hide-and-go-seek” or “sardines-in-the-box” with all the house thrown open to the game.","zh":"起初我以为他又在大摆宴席，大家余兴未尽，干脆把整座房子的灯光都打开，玩起了“捉迷藏”或者“活捉沙丁鱼”的游戏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But there wasn’t a sound.","zh":"但四下里悄无声息。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Only wind in the trees, which blew the wires and made the lights go off and on again as if the house had winked into the darkness.","zh":"只有风儿吹动树木，而树木则拉动电线，使得许多电灯忽明忽暗，仿佛这座房子正在黑暗中眨眼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As my taxi groaned away I saw Gatsby walking toward me across his lawn.","zh":"出租车“突突”开走时，我看见盖茨比从他的草坪向我走过来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Your place looks like the World’s Fair,” I said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Your place looks like the World’s Fair,” I said.","zh":"“你家好像在开世博会嘛，”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Does it?” He turned his eyes toward it absently. “I have been glancing into some of the rooms. Let’s go to Coney Island, old sport. In my car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Does it?”","zh":"“是吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He turned his eyes toward it absently.","zh":"他转过头，心不在焉地望了一眼，“我刚才在查看几个房间呢。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I have been glancing into some of the rooms.","zh":"他转过头，心不在焉地望了一眼，“我刚才在查看几个房间呢。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Let’s go to Coney Island, old sport.","zh":"我们去康尼岛走走吧，老兄，坐我的车去。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"In my car.”","zh":"我们去康尼岛走走吧，老兄，坐我的车去。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s too late.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s too late.”","zh":"“太晚了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, suppose we take a plunge in the swimming pool? I haven’t made use of it all summer.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, suppose we take a plunge in the swimming pool?","zh":"“那好吧，或许我们可以到游泳池玩水？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I haven’t made use of it all summer.”","zh":"今年夏天我还没用过它呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got to go to bed.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got to go to bed.”","zh":"“我要去睡啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right.”","zh":"“好吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He waited, looking at me with suppressed eagerness.","sentences":[{"en":"He waited, looking at me with suppressed eagerness.","zh":"他忍不住急切地望着我，等着我开口。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I talked with Miss Baker,” I said after a moment. “I’m going to call up Daisy tomorrow and invite her over here to tea.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I talked with Miss Baker,” I said after a moment.","zh":"“我跟贝克小姐聊过了，”沉默片刻之后，我说，“我准备明天就给黛熙打电话，请她来喝茶。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m going to call up Daisy tomorrow and invite her over here to tea.”","zh":"“我跟贝克小姐聊过了，”沉默片刻之后，我说，“我准备明天就给黛熙打电话，请她来喝茶。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, that’s all right,” he said carelessly. “I don’t want to put you to any trouble.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, that’s all right,” he said carelessly.","zh":"“哦，那倒不必了，”他若无其事地说，“我不希望给你带来麻烦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I don’t want to put you to any trouble.”","zh":"“哦，那倒不必了，”他若无其事地说，“我不希望给你带来麻烦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What day would suit you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What day would suit you?”","zh":"“你觉得哪天比较合适？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What day would suit you?” he corrected me quickly. “I don’t want to put you to any trouble, you see.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What day would suit you?” he corrected me quickly.","zh":"“看你哪天方便啊，”他马上纠正我说，“我不希望给你带来麻烦，你知道的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I don’t want to put you to any trouble, you see.”","zh":"“看你哪天方便啊，”他马上纠正我说，“我不希望给你带来麻烦，你知道的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How about the day after tomorrow?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How about the day after tomorrow?”","zh":"“后天怎么样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He considered for a moment. Then, with reluctance: “I want to get the grass cut,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"He considered for a moment.","zh":"他考虑了半晌，然后不太情愿地说：“我得先让人把草坪修剪整齐。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, with reluctance: “I want to get the grass cut,” he said.","zh":"他考虑了半晌，然后不太情愿地说：“我得先让人把草坪修剪整齐。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We both looked down at the grass—there was a sharp line where my ragged lawn ended and the darker, well-kept expanse of his began. I suspected that he meant my grass.","sentences":[{"en":"We both looked down at the grass—there was a sharp line where my ragged lawn ended and the darker, well-kept expanse of his began.","zh":"我们不约而同地低头看着周围的草地——有一条非常明显的分界线，我的这边零乱不堪，光线较暗处是他的草坪，修剪得整整齐齐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I suspected that he meant my grass.","zh":"我猜他要找人修剪的是我的草。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There’s another little thing,” he said uncertainly, and hesitated.","sentences":[{"en":"“There’s another little thing,” he said uncertainly, and hesitated.","zh":"“还有件小事，”他吞吞吐吐、欲言又止地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Would you rather put it off for a few days?” I asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Would you rather put it off for a few days?”","zh":"“你希望再往后推几天吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I asked.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t about that. At least—” He fumbled with a series of beginnings. “Why, I thought—why, look here, old sport, you don’t make much money, do you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t about that.","zh":"“不是啦，跟这个没关系。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At least—” He fumbled with a series of beginnings.","zh":"至少…”他结结巴巴，好像不知道该怎么说，“哎，我在想…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why, I thought—why, look here, old sport, you don’t make much money, do you?”","zh":"喂，老兄，你赚的钱不是很多，对吧？”“是不多。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Not very much.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not very much.”","zh":"这句话似乎让他信心大增，于是他较为镇定地说下去。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"This seemed to reassure him and he continued more confidently.","sentences":[{"en":"This seemed to reassure him and he continued more confidently.","zh":"这句话似乎让他信心大增，于是他较为镇定地说下去。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I thought you didn’t, if you’ll pardon my—you see, I carry on a little business on the side, a sort of side line, you understand. And I thought that if you don’t make very much—You’re selling bonds, aren’t you, old sport?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought you didn’t, if you’ll pardon my—you see, I carry on a little business on the side, a sort of side line, you understand.","zh":"“我想也是，如果你不介意我…你也知道的，我在那边有门小生意，算是某种副业吧，你能明白的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And I thought that if you don’t make very much—You’re selling bonds, aren’t you, old sport?”","zh":"我在想，既然你赚的钱不是很多…你是销售债券的，对吧，老兄？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Trying to.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Trying to.”","zh":"“我还在学。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, this would interest you. It wouldn’t take up much of your time and you might pick up a nice bit of money. It happens to be a rather confidential sort of thing.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, this would interest you.","zh":"“嗯，这件事你会有兴趣的。它不会占用你太多时间，你可以赚很大一笔钱。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It wouldn’t take up much of your time and you might pick up a nice bit of money.","zh":"“嗯，这件事你会有兴趣的。它不会占用你太多时间，你可以赚很大一笔钱。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It happens to be a rather confidential sort of thing.”","zh":"这件事说起来倒是十分机密的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I realize now that under different circumstances that conversation might have been one of the crises of my life. But, because the offer was obviously and tactlessly for a service to be rendered, I had no choice except to cut him off there.","sentences":[{"en":"I realize now that under different circumstances that conversation might have been one of the crises of my life.","zh":"现在我已经明白，要是发生在别的场合，这次对话很可能会让我的生活发生巨大的转变。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, because the offer was obviously and tactlessly for a service to be rendered, I had no choice except to cut him off there.","zh":"但他显然是因为要我帮忙而直截了当地想给我好处，所以我别无选择，只能拦住他的话头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got my hands full,” I said. “I’m much obliged but I couldn’t take on any more work.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got my hands full,” I said.","zh":"“我已经够忙的，”我说，“我非常感谢你，但不能再接更多的活了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m much obliged but I couldn’t take on any more work.”","zh":"“我已经够忙的，”我说，“我非常感谢你，但不能再接更多的活了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You wouldn’t have to do any business with Wolfshiem.” Evidently he thought that I was shying away from the “gonnegtion” mentioned at lunch, but I assured him he was wrong. He waited a moment longer, hoping I’d begin a conversation, but I was too absorbed to be responsive, so he went unwillingly home.","sentences":[{"en":"“You wouldn’t have to do any business with Wolfshiem.”","zh":"“做这门生意你不用跟沃夫希姆打交道的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Evidently he thought that I was shying away from the “gonnegtion” mentioned at lunch, but I assured him he was wrong.","zh":"他显然以为我耻于搭上午饭时提到的“光系”，但我告诉他不是这个原因。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He waited a moment longer, hoping I’d begin a conversation, but I was too absorbed to be responsive, so he went unwillingly home.","zh":"他又等了片刻，希望我会开口说话，但我已经很困，想不起来有什么好说的，于是他怏怏不乐地回家去了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The evening had made me lightheaded and happy; I think I walked into a deep sleep as I entered my front door. So I don’t know whether or not Gatsby went to Coney Island, or for how many hours he “glanced into rooms” while his house blazed gaudily on. I called up Daisy from the office next morning, and invited her to come to tea.","sentences":[{"en":"The evening had made me lightheaded and happy; I think I walked into a deep sleep as I entered my front door.","zh":"上半夜的约会让我很快乐，整个人感到轻飘飘的；我记得踏进家门之后，我很快就睡着了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So I don’t know whether or not Gatsby went to Coney Island, or for how many hours he “glanced into rooms” while his house blazed gaudily on.","zh":"所以我不知道盖茨比到底有没有去康尼岛，或者他花了多少个小时在灯火通明中“查看几个房间”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I called up Daisy from the office next morning, and invited her to come to tea.","zh":"第二天早上，我在办公室给黛熙打了电话，约她到我家喝茶。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t bring Tom,” I warned her.","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t bring Tom,” I warned her.","zh":"“别带上汤姆，”我提醒她。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“什么？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t bring Tom.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t bring Tom.”","zh":"“别带上汤姆。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who is ‘Tom’?” she asked innocently.","sentences":[{"en":"“Who is ‘Tom’?” she asked innocently.","zh":"“‘汤姆’是谁呀？”她故作天真地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The day agreed upon was pouring rain. At eleven o’clock a man in a raincoat, dragging a lawn-mower, tapped at my front door and said that Mr. Gatsby had sent him over to cut my grass. This reminded me that I had forgotten to tell my Finn to come back, so I drove into West Egg Village to search for her among soggy whitewashed alleys and to buy some cups and lemons and flowers.","sentences":[{"en":"The day agreed upon was pouring rain.","zh":"约好那天下起了倾盆大雨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At eleven o’clock a man in a raincoat, dragging a lawn-mower, tapped at my front door and said that Mr. Gatsby had sent him over to cut my grass.","zh":"到了十一点，有个人穿着雨衣，拖着割草机，跑来敲我的前门，说盖茨比先生派他来替我剪草。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This reminded me that I had forgotten to tell my Finn to come back, so I drove into West Egg Village to search for her among soggy whitewashed alleys and to buy some cups and lemons and flowers.","zh":"这倒提醒我了，我忘记让那个芬兰女佣过来，于是我驱车前往西卵村，在几条湿漉漉的灰白巷子中找到她，又买了些茶杯、柠檬和鲜花。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The flowers were unnecessary, for at two o’clock a greenhouse arrived from Gatsby’s, with innumerable receptacles to contain it. An hour later the front door opened nervously, and Gatsby in a white flannel suit, silver shirt, and gold-coloured tie, hurried in. He was pale, and there were dark signs of sleeplessness beneath his eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"The flowers were unnecessary, for at two o’clock a greenhouse arrived from Gatsby’s, with innumerable receptacles to contain it.","zh":"鲜花白买了，因为下午两点时，盖茨比家送来各种奇花异草，还有无数个花瓶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"An hour later the front door opened nervously, and Gatsby in a white flannel suit, silver shirt, and gold-coloured tie, hurried in.","zh":"又过了一个小时，前门紧张地打开，盖茨比穿着白色的法兰绒西装和银色的衬衣，系着金色的领带，匆匆走进来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was pale, and there were dark signs of sleeplessness beneath his eyes.","zh":"他脸色苍白，黑眼圈很重，显然昨晚是彻夜无眠了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is everything all right?” he asked immediately.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is everything all right?” he asked immediately.","zh":"“全都准备好了吗？”他迫不及待地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The grass looks fine, if that’s what you mean.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The grass looks fine, if that’s what you mean.”","zh":"“你说的是草坪吗？看上去很整齐。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What grass?” he inquired blankly. “Oh, the grass in the yard.” He looked out the window at it, but, judging from his expression, I don’t believe he saw a thing.","sentences":[{"en":"“What grass?” he inquired blankly.","zh":"“什么草坪？”他茫然地问，“哦，你家的草坪。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Oh, the grass in the yard.”","zh":"“什么草坪？”他茫然地问，“哦，你家的草坪。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He looked out the window at it, but, judging from his expression, I don’t believe he saw a thing.","zh":"他向窗外望去，但从他的表情判断，我相信他什么也没看到。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Looks very good,” he remarked vaguely. “One of the papers said they thought the rain would stop about four. I think it was The Journal. Have you got everything you need in the shape of—of tea?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Looks very good,” he remarked vaguely.","zh":"“看上去非常好，”他含糊其辞地说，“报纸上说这雨四点钟左右会停。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“One of the papers said they thought the rain would stop about four.","zh":"“看上去非常好，”他含糊其辞地说，“报纸上说这雨四点钟左右会停。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I think it was The Journal.","zh":"应该是《纽约晚报》上说的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Have you got everything you need in the shape of—of tea?”","zh":"喝…喝茶需要的东西你都准备好了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I took him into the pantry, where he looked a little reproachfully at the Finn. Together we scrutinized the twelve lemon cakes from the delicatessen shop.","sentences":[{"en":"I took him into the pantry, where he looked a little reproachfully at the Finn.","zh":"我把他带进厨房，他看见那个芬兰女佣，好像有点不满。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Together we scrutinized the twelve lemon cakes from the delicatessen shop.","zh":"我们一起视察了从外卖店买回来的十二个柠檬蛋糕。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Will they do?” I asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Will they do?”","zh":"“这些还可以吧？”我问。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I asked.","zh":"“这些还可以吧？”我问。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course, of course! They’re fine!” and he added hollowly, “… old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course, of course!","zh":"“当然，当然！看上去很好！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They’re fine!” and he added hollowly, “… old sport.”","zh":"他言不由衷地补上一句，“…老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The rain cooled about half-past three to a damp mist, through which occasional thin drops swam like dew. Gatsby looked with vacant eyes through a copy of Clay’s Economics, starting at the Finnish tread that shook the kitchen floor, and peering towards the bleared windows from time to time as if a series of invisible but alarming happenings were taking place outside. Finally he got up and informed me, in an uncertain voice, that he was going home.","sentences":[{"en":"The rain cooled about half-past three to a damp mist, through which occasional thin drops swam like dew.","zh":"三点半过后，大雨渐渐停了，变成潮湿的浓雾，偶尔飘洒着几滴露珠似的小雨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby looked with vacant eyes through a copy of Clay’s Economics, starting at the Finnish tread that shook the kitchen floor, and peering towards the bleared windows from time to time as if a series of invisible but alarming happenings were taking place outside.","zh":"盖茨比两眼无神地看着一本克莱写的《经济学》，每次芬兰女佣的脚步踩动厨房的地板他就一惊，时不时向雾蒙蒙的窗户望去，仿佛外面有一系列肉眼看不见但怵目惊心的事情正在发生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Finally he got up and informed me, in an uncertain voice, that he was going home.","zh":"最后他站起来，犹豫地对我说，他要回家了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why’s that?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why’s that?”","zh":"“为什么？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nobody’s coming to tea. It’s too late!” He looked at his watch as if there was some pressing demand on his time elsewhere. “I can’t wait all day.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nobody’s coming to tea.","zh":"“没有人会来喝茶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s too late!”","zh":"太晚啦！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked at his watch as if there was some pressing demand on his time elsewhere.","zh":"他看看手表，仿佛他在别的地方还有紧要事，“我不能等一整天。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I can’t wait all day.”","zh":"他看看手表，仿佛他在别的地方还有紧要事，“我不能等一整天。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t be silly; it’s just two minutes to four.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t be silly; it’s just two minutes to four.”","zh":"“别傻了，这会还有两分钟才到四点。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He sat down miserably, as if I had pushed him, and simultaneously there was the sound of a motor turning into my lane. We both jumped up, and, a little harrowed myself, I went out into the yard.","sentences":[{"en":"He sat down miserably, as if I had pushed him, and simultaneously there was the sound of a motor turning into my lane.","zh":"他哭丧着脸坐下，仿佛我强迫了他，就在这时，我家的小径上响起了汽车引擎的声音。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We both jumped up, and, a little harrowed myself, I went out into the yard.","zh":"我们俩立刻站起来，连我也有点紧张。我走到外面的院子里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Under the dripping bare lilac-trees a large open car was coming up the drive. It stopped. Daisy’s face, tipped sideways beneath a three-cornered lavender hat, looked out at me with a bright ecstatic smile.","sentences":[{"en":"Under the dripping bare lilac-trees a large open car was coming up the drive.","zh":"院子里几株没有花的丁香树正在滴水，一辆巨大的敞篷车开到树下的车道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It stopped.","zh":"它停了下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy’s face, tipped sideways beneath a three-cornered lavender hat, looked out at me with a bright ecstatic smile.","zh":"黛熙的脸庞在薰衣草色的三角帽之下斜翘着，带着明艳的微笑，欣喜地看着我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is this absolutely where you live, my dearest one?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Is this absolutely where you live, my dearest one?”","zh":"“这就是你住的地方吗，我最亲爱的表哥？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The exhilarating ripple of her voice was a wild tonic in the rain. I had to follow the sound of it for a moment, up and down, with my ear alone, before any words came through. A damp streak of hair lay like a dash of blue paint across her cheek, and her hand was wet with glistening drops as I took it to help her from the car.","sentences":[{"en":"The exhilarating ripple of her voice was a wild tonic in the rain.","zh":"她那抑扬顿挫的声音令人精神振奋，在细雨中格外动听。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had to follow the sound of it for a moment, up and down, with my ear alone, before any words came through.","zh":"我的耳朵不由自主地随着她的话音高高低低地起伏，隔了片刻才领会到她说的话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A damp streak of hair lay like a dash of blue paint across her cheek, and her hand was wet with glistening drops as I took it to help her from the car.","zh":"她的脸颊上贴着一绺被雨水打湿的秀发，像是一笔浓墨重彩似的，我伸手扶她下车时，发现她的手湿漉漉的在滴水。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Are you in love with me,” she said low in my ear, “or why did I have to come alone?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you in love with me,” she said low in my ear, “or why did I have to come alone?”","zh":"“你是爱上我了吧，”她在我耳边轻轻地说，“否则为什么让我一个人来呀？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s the secret of Castle Rackrent. Tell your chauffeur to go far away and spend an hour.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s the secret of Castle Rackrent.","zh":"“这是拉克伦特城堡的秘密。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell your chauffeur to go far away and spend an hour.”","zh":"你吩咐司机走吧，让他去消磨一个小时。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come back in an hour, Ferdie.” Then in a grave murmur: “His name is Ferdie.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come back in an hour, Ferdie.”","zh":"“费迪，你过一个小时再来。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then in a grave murmur: “His name is Ferdie.”","zh":"然后严肃地低声说，“他的名字叫费迪。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Does the gasoline affect his nose?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Does the gasoline affect his nose?”","zh":"“汽油影响到他的鼻子吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t think so,” she said innocently. “Why?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t think so,” she said innocently.","zh":"“没有吧，”她天真地问，“干吗这么问？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Why?”","zh":"“没有吧，”她天真地问，“干吗这么问？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We went in. To my overwhelming surprise the living-room was deserted.","sentences":[{"en":"We went in.","zh":"我们走进去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To my overwhelming surprise the living-room was deserted.","zh":"让我始料未及的是，客厅里居然没有人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, that’s funny,” I exclaimed.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, that’s funny,” I exclaimed.","zh":"“咦，这下好玩了，”我惊奇地说。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s funny?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s funny?”","zh":"“咦，这下好玩了，”我惊奇地说。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She turned her head as there was a light dignified knocking at the front door. I went out and opened it. Gatsby, pale as death, with his hands plunged like weights in his coat pockets, was standing in a puddle of water glaring tragically into my eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned her head as there was a light dignified knocking at the front door.","zh":"“什么好玩了？”她转过头，因为有人在轻轻地敲响了前门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I went out and opened it.","zh":"我走出去，把门打开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby, pale as death, with his hands plunged like weights in his coat pockets, was standing in a puddle of water glaring tragically into my eyes.","zh":"盖茨比脸如死灰，双手沉重地插进上衣的口袋，站在一滩水里，凄然地盯着我的双眼。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"With his hands still in his coat pockets he stalked by me into the hall, turned sharply as if he were on a wire, and disappeared into the living-room. It wasn’t a bit funny. Aware of the loud beating of my own heart I pulled the door to against the increasing rain.","sentences":[{"en":"With his hands still in his coat pockets he stalked by me into the hall, turned sharply as if he were on a wire, and disappeared into the living-room.","zh":"他双手仍然插在口袋里，三步并作两步从我旁边跨进门厅，然后踩钢丝似的突然转了个身，走进客厅消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It wasn’t a bit funny.","zh":"这一点都不好玩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Aware of the loud beating of my own heart I pulled the door to against the increasing rain.","zh":"我自己的心怦怦地猛跳着，掩起前门，把又逐渐下大的雨水挡在门外。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For half a minute there wasn’t a sound. Then from the living-room I heard a sort of choking murmur and part of a laugh, followed by Daisy’s voice on a clear artificial note:","sentences":[{"en":"For half a minute there wasn’t a sound.","zh":"大概有半分钟时间，四下里悄无声息。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then from the living-room I heard a sort of choking murmur and part of a laugh, followed by Daisy’s voice on a clear artificial note:","zh":"然后我听见客厅传来一阵哽噎的诉说和几下笑声，接着是黛熙的声音，故意很响亮地说：“再次见到你，我当然非常非常高兴啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I certainly am awfully glad to see you again.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I certainly am awfully glad to see you again.”","zh":"然后我听见客厅传来一阵哽噎的诉说和几下笑声，接着是黛熙的声音，故意很响亮地说：“再次见到你，我当然非常非常高兴啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A pause; it endured horribly. I had nothing to do in the hall, so I went into the room.","sentences":[{"en":"A pause; it endured horribly.","zh":"又是一阵寂静，持续了很长时间。我在门厅里无事可做，于是走进客厅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I had nothing to do in the hall, so I went into the room.","zh":"又是一阵寂静，持续了很长时间。我在门厅里无事可做，于是走进客厅。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby, his hands still in his pockets, was reclining against the mantelpiece in a strained counterfeit of perfect ease, even of boredom. His head leaned back so far that it rested against the face of a defunct mantelpiece clock, and from this position his distraught eyes stared down at Daisy, who was sitting, frightened but graceful, on the edge of a stiff chair.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby, his hands still in his pockets, was reclining against the mantelpiece in a strained counterfeit of perfect ease, even of boredom.","zh":"盖茨比两只手还在口袋里，背靠壁炉架站着，勉强装出一副完全放松的样子，甚至显得有点无精打采。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His head leaned back so far that it rested against the face of a defunct mantelpiece clock, and from this position his distraught eyes stared down at Daisy, who was sitting, frightened but graceful, on the edge of a stiff chair.","zh":"他的头靠得很后，都碰到壁炉架上那台失灵的时钟了。他就摆着这个姿势，眼神迷乱地俯视着黛熙，而黛熙则慌张但优雅地坐在一张硬背椅子的边缘。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ve met before,” muttered Gatsby. His eyes glanced momentarily at me, and his lips parted with an abortive attempt at a laugh. Luckily the clock took this moment to tilt dangerously at the pressure of his head, whereupon he turned and caught it with trembling fingers, and set it back in place. Then he sat down, rigidly, his elbow on the arm of the sofa and his chin in his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ve met before,” muttered Gatsby.","zh":"“我们以前认识，”盖茨比喃喃地说。他朝我瞥了一眼，嘴唇咧开，想笑但又笑不出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His eyes glanced momentarily at me, and his lips parted with an abortive attempt at a laugh.","zh":"“我们以前认识，”盖茨比喃喃地说。他朝我瞥了一眼，嘴唇咧开，想笑但又笑不出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Luckily the clock took this moment to tilt dangerously at the pressure of his head, whereupon he turned and caught it with trembling fingers, and set it back in place.","zh":"这时幸亏那台时钟被他的头压得摇摇欲坠，他赶紧转过去，用发抖的手指抓住它，把它摆回原处。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he sat down, rigidly, his elbow on the arm of the sofa and his chin in his hand.","zh":"然后他动作僵硬地坐下来，手肘撑在沙发的扶手上，手心抬着下巴。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m sorry about the clock,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m sorry about the clock,” he said.","zh":"“很抱歉碰到你的时钟，”他说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"My own face had now assumed a deep tropical burn. I couldn’t muster up a single commonplace out of the thousand in my head.","sentences":[{"en":"My own face had now assumed a deep tropical burn.","zh":"我自己的脸现在涨得通红，脑子里有上千句客气的话，但一句也说不出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I couldn’t muster up a single commonplace out of the thousand in my head.","zh":"我自己的脸现在涨得通红，脑子里有上千句客气的话，但一句也说不出来。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s an old clock,” I told them idiotically.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s an old clock,” I told them idiotically.","zh":"“这台时钟很旧了，”我白痴似的告诉他们。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I think we all believed for a moment that it had smashed in pieces on the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"I think we all believed for a moment that it had smashed in pieces on the floor.","zh":"大家都不知道该说些什么，好像那台时钟已经在地上摔得粉碎似的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We haven’t met for many years,” said Daisy, her voice as matter-of-fact as it could ever be.","sentences":[{"en":"“We haven’t met for many years,” said Daisy, her voice as matter-of-fact as it could ever be.","zh":"“我们很多年没见了，”黛熙说，她尽可能装得不动声色。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Five years next November.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Five years next November.”","zh":"“到十一月就五年整了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The automatic quality of Gatsby’s answer set us all back at least another minute. I had them both on their feet with the desperate suggestion that they help me make tea in the kitchen when the demoniac Finn brought it in on a tray.","sentences":[{"en":"The automatic quality of Gatsby’s answer set us all back at least another minute.","zh":"盖茨比这机械式的回答让我们至少又愣了一分钟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had them both on their feet with the desperate suggestion that they help me make tea in the kitchen when the demoniac Finn brought it in on a tray.","zh":"我急中生智，建议他们到厨房帮我准备下午茶，于是他们都站起来，但这时那个幽灵般的芬兰女佣端着茶盘走进来了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Amid the welcome confusion of cups and cakes a certain physical decency established itself. Gatsby got himself into a shadow and, while Daisy and I talked, looked conscientiously from one to the other of us with tense, unhappy eyes. However, as calmness wasn’t an end in itself, I made an excuse at the first possible moment, and got to my feet.","sentences":[{"en":"Amid the welcome confusion of cups and cakes a certain physical decency established itself.","zh":"手忙脚乱地倒茶切蛋糕之后，大家总算恢复了常态。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby got himself into a shadow and, while Daisy and I talked, looked conscientiously from one to the other of us with tense, unhappy eyes.","zh":"盖茨比躲到角落里听我跟黛熙聊天，他那双紧张而闷闷不乐的眼神来回地看着我们两人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, as calmness wasn’t an end in itself, I made an excuse at the first possible moment, and got to my feet.","zh":"然而平静的局面本身并不是目的，我找个机会说了声抱歉就站起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where are you going?” demanded Gatsby in immediate alarm.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where are you going?” demanded Gatsby in immediate alarm.","zh":"“你要去哪里？”盖茨比立刻警惕地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll be back.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll be back.”","zh":"“我很快就回来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got to speak to you about something before you go.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got to speak to you about something before you go.”","zh":"“先别走，我有话要跟你说。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He followed me wildly into the kitchen, closed the door, and whispered: “Oh, God!” in a miserable way.","sentences":[{"en":"He followed me wildly into the kitchen, closed the door, and whispered: “Oh, God!” in a miserable way.","zh":"他慌忙跟着我走进厨房，把门关上，低声说：“天啊！”看上去很痛苦的样子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s the matter?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the matter?”","zh":"“怎么回事？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This is a terrible mistake,” he said, shaking his head from side to side, “a terrible, terrible mistake.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This is a terrible mistake,” he said, shaking his head from side to side, “a terrible, terrible mistake.”","zh":"“这是个可怕的错误，”他不停地摇着头说，“非常可怕的错误。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re just embarrassed, that’s all,” and luckily I added: “Daisy’s embarrassed too.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re just embarrassed, that’s all,” and luckily I added: “Daisy’s embarrassed too.”","zh":"“你只是觉得不好意思，仅此而已，”我劝解他说，“黛熙也有点不好意思。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s embarrassed?” he repeated incredulously.","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s embarrassed?” he repeated incredulously.","zh":"“她有点不好意思？”他将信将疑地重复了我的话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Just as much as you are.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Just as much as you are.”","zh":"“她跟你彼此彼此啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t talk so loud.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t talk so loud.”","zh":"“别说得那么大声。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re acting like a little boy,” I broke out impatiently. “Not only that, but you’re rude. Daisy’s sitting in there all alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re acting like a little boy,” I broke out impatiently.","zh":"“你表现得像个小男孩，”我不耐烦地说，“你不仅很幼稚，还很没礼貌。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Not only that, but you’re rude.","zh":"“你表现得像个小男孩，”我不耐烦地说，“你不仅很幼稚，还很没礼貌。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Daisy’s sitting in there all alone.”","zh":"黛熙一个人坐在那里呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He raised his hand to stop my words, looked at me with unforgettable reproach, and, opening the door cautiously, went back into the other room.","sentences":[{"en":"He raised his hand to stop my words, looked at me with unforgettable reproach, and, opening the door cautiously, went back into the other room.","zh":"他抬手不让我说下去，用令人难忘的责备眼神瞪了我一眼，然后小心翼翼地把门打开，重新回到了客厅。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I walked out the back way—just as Gatsby had when he had made his nervous circuit of the house half an hour before—and ran for a huge black knotted tree, whose massed leaves made a fabric against the rain. Once more it was pouring, and my irregular lawn, well-shaved by Gatsby’s gardener, abounded in small muddy swamps and prehistoric marshes. There was nothing to look at from under the tree except Gatsby’s enormous house, so I stared at it, like Kant at his church steeple, for half an hour. A brewer had built it early in the “period” craze, a decade before, and there was a story that he’d agreed to pay five years’ taxes on all the neighbouring cottages if the owners would have their roofs thatched with straw. Perhaps their refusal took the heart out of his plan to Found a Family—he went into an immediate decline. His children sold his house with the black wreath still on the door. Americans, while willing, even eager, to be serfs, have always been obstinate about being peasantry.","sentences":[{"en":"I walked out the back way—just as Gatsby had when he had made his nervous circuit of the house half an hour before—and ran for a huge black knotted tree, whose massed leaves made a fabric against the rain.","zh":"我从后门出去——半小时前盖茨比也是从这里出去，神经兮兮地绕到前门走进来——走到一棵黑色的大树下面。这棵盘根错节的大树枝繁叶茂，替我挡住了雨水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once more it was pouring, and my irregular lawn, well-shaved by Gatsby’s gardener, abounded in small muddy swamps and prehistoric marshes.","zh":"这时雨又倾盆而下，我这不规则的草坪虽然经过盖茨比家园丁的修剪，但到处坑坑洼洼的，看上去像是洪荒年代的沼泽地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was nothing to look at from under the tree except Gatsby’s enormous house, so I stared at it, like Kant at his church steeple, for half an hour.","zh":"在这棵大树下面没什么好看的，除了盖茨比那座巨大的房子，于是我像康德凝视教堂的尖顶那样，盯着它看了足足半小时。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A brewer had built it early in the “period” craze, a decade before, and there was a story that he’d agreed to pay five years’ taxes on all the neighbouring cottages if the owners would have their roofs thatched with straw.","zh":"这座房子是一个啤酒商在十年前那股复古热潮初期建造的，据说他愿意替周边所有寒酸的房子支付五年的税金，只要这些房东肯在屋顶上铺一层稻草。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps their refusal took the heart out of his plan to Found a Family—he went into an immediate decline.","zh":"也许他们的拒绝伤了他那颗成家立业的心——他很快就一病不起了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His children sold his house with the black wreath still on the door.","zh":"哀悼的花圈还挂在门上，他的子女等不及地把房子卖掉了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Americans, while willing, even eager, to be serfs, have always been obstinate about being peasantry.","zh":"美国人虽然愿意、甚至渴望当农奴，但却永远不甘心做乡巴佬。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"After half an hour, the sun shone again, and the grocer’s automobile rounded Gatsby’s drive with the raw material for his servants’ dinner—I felt sure he wouldn’t eat a spoonful. A maid began opening the upper windows of his house, appeared momentarily in each, and, leaning from the large central bay, spat meditatively into the garden. It was time I went back. While the rain continued it had seemed like the murmur of their voices, rising and swelling a little now and then with gusts of emotion. But in the new silence I felt that silence had fallen within the house too.","sentences":[{"en":"After half an hour, the sun shone again, and the grocer’s automobile rounded Gatsby’s drive with the raw material for his servants’ dinner—I felt sure he wouldn’t eat a spoonful.","zh":"半小时过去，太阳又出来了，杂货店的汽车开上盖茨比家的车道，给他的仆人送来了晚餐所需的生鲜食材——我敢肯定他今晚一口也吃不下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A maid began opening the upper windows of his house, appeared momentarily in each, and, leaning from the large central bay, spat meditatively into the garden.","zh":"有个女仆开始打开楼上的窗户，每打开一扇就会短暂地露面，然后从宽大的中央阳台探出身子，似有深意地朝花园里吐了口痰。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was time I went back.","zh":"有个女仆开始打开楼上的窗户，每打开一扇就会短暂地露面，然后从宽大的中央阳台探出身子，似有深意地朝花园里吐了口痰。","scope":"group"},{"en":"While the rain continued it had seemed like the murmur of their voices, rising and swelling a little now and then with gusts of emotion.","zh":"我该回去了。刚才滴滴答答的雨声听起来像是他们的窃窃私语，时不时随着感情的波动而高低起伏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But in the new silence I felt that silence had fallen within the house too.","zh":"但现在外面一片寂静，我觉得屋子里应该也已平静下来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I went in—after making every possible noise in the kitchen, short of pushing over the stove—but I don’t believe they heard a sound. They were sitting at either end of the couch, looking at each other as if some question had been asked, or was in the air, and every vestige of embarrassment was gone. Daisy’s face was smeared with tears, and when I came in she jumped up and began wiping at it with her handkerchief before a mirror. But there was a change in Gatsby that was simply confounding. He literally glowed; without a word or a gesture of exultation a new well-being radiated from him and filled the little room.","sentences":[{"en":"I went in—after making every possible noise in the kitchen, short of pushing over the stove—but I don’t believe they heard a sound.","zh":"我走了进去，故意在厨房里弄出各种声响，就差把炉子打翻，但我相信他们什么也听不到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were sitting at either end of the couch, looking at each other as if some question had been asked, or was in the air, and every vestige of embarrassment was gone.","zh":"他们坐在沙发的两端，相互望着对方，似乎正在思考什么悬而未决的问题，而尴尬的气氛已经消失得干干净净。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy’s face was smeared with tears, and when I came in she jumped up and began wiping at it with her handkerchief before a mirror.","zh":"黛熙脸上还有泪痕，看到我走进来，赶紧对着镜子用手帕把它擦干。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But there was a change in Gatsby that was simply confounding.","zh":"但盖茨比身上发生了惊人的变化。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He literally glowed; without a word or a gesture of exultation a new well-being radiated from him and filled the little room.","zh":"他容光焕发，虽然没有经过言语或动作流露出来，但他浑身上下散发出幸福的光芒，充盈着我那小小的客厅。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, hello, old sport,” he said, as if he hadn’t seen me for years. I thought for a moment he was going to shake hands.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, hello, old sport,” he said, as if he hadn’t seen me for years.","zh":"“你好啊，老兄，”他热情地说，似乎和我已经多年未曾谋面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought for a moment he was going to shake hands.","zh":"刹那间，我简直以为他要来跟我握手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s stopped raining.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s stopped raining.”","zh":"“外面雨停了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Has it?” When he realized what I was talking about, that there were twinkle-bells of sunshine in the room, he smiled like a weather man, like an ecstatic patron of recurrent light, and repeated the news to Daisy. “What do you think of that? It’s stopped raining.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Has it?”","zh":"“雨停了？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he realized what I was talking about, that there were twinkle-bells of sunshine in the room, he smiled like a weather man, like an ecstatic patron of recurrent light, and repeated the news to Daisy.","zh":"刚开始他还没意识到我在说什么，后来看到客厅里阳光灿烂，这才笑了起来，好像他是气象预报员，或者是阳光守护神，并将这个新闻汇报给黛熙，“你觉得怎么样？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What do you think of that?","zh":"刚开始他还没意识到我在说什么，后来看到客厅里阳光灿烂，这才笑了起来，好像他是气象预报员，或者是阳光守护神，并将这个新闻汇报给黛熙，“你觉得怎么样？","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s stopped raining.”","zh":"雨已经停了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m glad, Jay.” Her throat, full of aching, grieving beauty, told only of her unexpected joy.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m glad, Jay.”","zh":"“我很高兴，杰伊。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her throat, full of aching, grieving beauty, told only of her unexpected joy.","zh":"她的喉咙刚才哭得有点嘶哑，但语气中透露出意想不到的欢乐。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want you and Daisy to come over to my house,” he said, “I’d like to show her around.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want you and Daisy to come over to my house,” he said, “I’d like to show her around.”","zh":"“我想请你和黛熙到我家里去，”他说，“我想带她到处看看。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re sure you want me to come?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re sure you want me to come?”","zh":"“你真的想要我去吗？”“绝对是真的啊，老兄。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Absolutely, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Absolutely, old sport.”","zh":"“你真的想要我去吗？”“绝对是真的啊，老兄。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy went upstairs to wash her face—too late I thought with humiliation of my towels—while Gatsby and I waited on the lawn.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy went upstairs to wash her face—too late I thought with humiliation of my towels—while Gatsby and I waited on the lawn.","zh":"黛熙走上楼去洗脸——这时我才想起我的毛巾很寒碜，但已经太迟了。盖茨比和我则在草坪上等她。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“My house looks well, doesn’t it?” he demanded. “See how the whole front of it catches the light.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My house looks well, doesn’t it?” he demanded.","zh":"“我的房子看上去不错吧？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“See how the whole front of it catches the light.”","zh":"他问，“你看，它的正面在阳光的照耀下多么漂亮。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I agreed that it was splendid.","sentences":[{"en":"I agreed that it was splendid.","zh":"我承认它确实富丽堂皇。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes.” His eyes went over it, every arched door and square tower. “It took me just three years to earn the money that bought it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“是啊，”他的眼睛扫视着他的房子，每个拱门和每座方塔都不放过。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His eyes went over it, every arched door and square tower.","zh":"“是啊，”他的眼睛扫视着他的房子，每个拱门和每座方塔都不放过。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It took me just three years to earn the money that bought it.”","zh":"“我只花了三年，就赚够了买下它的钱。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I thought you inherited your money.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought you inherited your money.”","zh":"“你不是说你的钱是继承来的吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I did, old sport,” he said automatically, “but I lost most of it in the big panic—the panic of the war.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I did, old sport,” he said automatically, “but I lost most of it in the big panic—the panic of the war.”","zh":"“是的，老兄，”他想也不想就回答，“但那些遗产在大恐慌时被我亏掉很多——就是战争引起的那次大恐慌。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I think he hardly knew what he was saying, for when I asked him what business he was in he answered: “That’s my affair,” before he realized that it wasn’t an appropriate reply.","sentences":[{"en":"I think he hardly knew what he was saying, for when I asked him what business he was in he answered: “That’s my affair,” before he realized that it wasn’t an appropriate reply.","zh":"我知道他是在信口开河，因为当我问他做什么生意时，他的回答是：“这不关你的事。”话说出口才想起来这个回答很不礼貌。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, I’ve been in several things,” he corrected himself. “I was in the drug business and then I was in the oil business. But I’m not in either one now.” He looked at me with more attention. “Do you mean you’ve been thinking over what I proposed the other night?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I’ve been in several things,” he corrected himself.","zh":"“哦，我做过好几样生意，”他改口说，“我先是卖药材，然后又做点石油生意。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I was in the drug business and then I was in the oil business.","zh":"“哦，我做过好几样生意，”他改口说，“我先是卖药材，然后又做点石油生意。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But I’m not in either one now.”","zh":"但现在这两行我都不做了。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked at me with more attention.","zh":"他更加专注地看着我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you mean you’ve been thinking over what I proposed the other night?”","zh":"“你是说你在考虑我前天晚上的提议吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Before I could answer, Daisy came out of the house and two rows of brass buttons on her dress gleamed in the sunlight.","sentences":[{"en":"Before I could answer, Daisy came out of the house and two rows of brass buttons on her dress gleamed in the sunlight.","zh":"我还没来得及回答，黛熙就从我家里走出来，长裙上两排铜纽扣在阳光下闪闪发亮。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That huge place there?” she cried pointing.","sentences":[{"en":"“That huge place there?” she cried pointing.","zh":"“那么大的地方啊？”她指着盖茨比的房子惊叹说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do you like it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you like it?”","zh":"“你喜欢吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I love it, but I don’t see how you live there all alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I love it, but I don’t see how you live there all alone.”","zh":"“喜欢啊，但我不明白你一个人怎能住那么大的房子。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I keep it always full of interesting people, night and day. People who do interesting things. Celebrated people.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I keep it always full of interesting people, night and day.","zh":"“我总是请很多有趣的人来，白天黑夜都有客人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People who do interesting things.","zh":"那些客人做的事情都很有趣，有些还是名人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Celebrated people.”","zh":"那些客人做的事情都很有趣，有些还是名人。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Instead of taking the shortcut along the Sound we went down to the road and entered by the big postern. With enchanting murmurs Daisy admired this aspect or that of the feudal silhouette against the sky, admired the gardens, the sparkling odour of jonquils and the frothy odour of hawthorn and plum blossoms and the pale gold odour of kiss-me-at-the-gate. It was strange to reach the marble steps and find no stir of bright dresses in and out the door, and hear no sound but bird voices in the trees.","sentences":[{"en":"Instead of taking the shortcut along the Sound we went down to the road and entered by the big postern.","zh":"我们没有抄海边的近路，而是故意沿着大路从宏伟的后门走进去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With enchanting murmurs Daisy admired this aspect or that of the feudal silhouette against the sky, admired the gardens, the sparkling odour of jonquils and the frothy odour of hawthorn and plum blossoms and the pale gold odour of kiss-me-at-the-gate.","zh":"黛熙忘我地欣赏起这座古堡，嘴里用她那迷人的声音喃喃低语，这边的墙壁真是漂亮，那边的屋顶多么好看。接着走进芳香扑鼻的花园，那些闪闪发亮的黄水仙、白泡沫般的山楂花、挂满枝头的西梅花，还有淡金色的忍冬花，也都让她赞不绝口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was strange to reach the marble steps and find no stir of bright dresses in and out the door, and hear no sound but bird voices in the trees.","zh":"登上大理石台阶时，周边的氛围有点异样，因为看不见走来走去的光鲜衣着，也听不见此起彼伏的欢声笑语，只有鸟儿在树上啁啾。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And inside, as we wandered through Marie Antoinette music-rooms and Restoration Salons, I felt that there were guests concealed behind every couch and table, under orders to be breathlessly silent until we had passed through. As Gatsby closed the door of “the Merton College Library” I could have sworn I heard the owl-eyed man break into ghostly laughter.","sentences":[{"en":"And inside, as we wandered through Marie Antoinette music-rooms and Restoration Salons, I felt that there were guests concealed behind every couch and table, under orders to be breathlessly silent until we had passed through.","zh":"进门之后，我们依次穿过几间玛丽·安托瓦内特式的音乐厅和复辟时代风格的会客室，我觉得有许多客人躲在每张沙发和桌子后面，奉命屏息不动地静待我们走过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As Gatsby closed the door of “the Merton College Library” I could have sworn I heard the owl-eyed man break into ghostly laughter.","zh":"盖茨比关上默顿学院图书馆的大门时，我简直听见那位猫头鹰眼镜先生突然发出几声鬼叫似的笑声。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We went upstairs, through period bedrooms swathed in rose and lavender silk and vivid with new flowers, through dressing-rooms and poolrooms, and bathrooms with sunken baths—intruding into one chamber where a dishevelled man in pyjamas was doing liver exercises on the floor. It was Mr. Klipspringer, the “boarder.” I had seen him wandering hungrily about the beach that morning. Finally we came to Gatsby’s own apartment, a bedroom and a bath, and an Adam’s study, where we sat down and drank a glass of some Chartreuse he took from a cupboard in the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"We went upstairs, through period bedrooms swathed in rose and lavender silk and vivid with new flowers, through dressing-rooms and poolrooms, and bathrooms with sunken baths—intruding into one chamber where a dishevelled man in pyjamas was doing liver exercises on the floor.","zh":"我们登上楼梯，楼上有几间古色古香的卧室，里面铺着玫瑰色和薰衣草色的绸缎，摆放着许多生机勃勃的鲜花，还有更衣室、撞球室和装着嵌入式浴缸的浴室——期间我们闯进一间卧房，发现有个邋遢的男子穿着睡衣，正在地板上做俯卧撑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Mr. Klipspringer, the “boarder.”","zh":"那人就是“房客”克里普斯普林格先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had seen him wandering hungrily about the beach that morning.","zh":"那天早上，我曾看见他面有饥色地在沙滩上瞎逛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Finally we came to Gatsby’s own apartment, a bedroom and a bath, and an Adam’s study, where we sat down and drank a glass of some Chartreuse he took from a cupboard in the wall.","zh":"最后我们走进了盖茨比本人的套房，里面有卧室、浴室和亚当式书房。我们在书房坐下，用玻璃杯喝起他从壁柜里拿出来的黄绿色查特酒。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He hadn’t once ceased looking at Daisy, and I think he revalued everything in his house according to the measure of response it drew from her well-loved eyes. Sometimes too, he stared around at his possessions in a dazed way, as though in her actual and astounding presence none of it was any longer real. Once he nearly toppled down a flight of stairs.","sentences":[{"en":"He hadn’t once ceased looking at Daisy, and I think he revalued everything in his house according to the measure of response it drew from her well-loved eyes.","zh":"他片刻不停地盯着黛熙看，我猜他是在根据黛熙那双明眸的反应，重新估量家里所有事物的价值。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes too, he stared around at his possessions in a dazed way, as though in her actual and astounding presence none of it was any longer real.","zh":"有时候他也失魂落魄地望望他的财物，似乎黛熙的真身神奇地出现之后，这一切都变得不再重要。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once he nearly toppled down a flight of stairs.","zh":"有一次他差点从楼梯上摔下去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His bedroom was the simplest room of all—except where the dresser was garnished with a toilet set of pure dull gold. Daisy took the brush with delight, and smoothed her hair, whereupon Gatsby sat down and shaded his eyes and began to laugh.","sentences":[{"en":"His bedroom was the simplest room of all—except where the dresser was garnished with a toilet set of pure dull gold.","zh":"他的卧室是所有房间中最简朴的——不过梳妆台上摆着一套纯金的化妆工具。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy took the brush with delight, and smoothed her hair, whereupon Gatsby sat down and shaded his eyes and began to laugh.","zh":"黛熙高兴地拿起刷子顺顺她的头发，引得盖茨比坐下来，捂着脸忍不住开怀大笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s the funniest thing, old sport,” he said hilariously. “I can’t—When I try to—”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s the funniest thing, old sport,” he said hilariously.","zh":"“我实在是太高兴了，老兄，”他笑个不停地说，“我忍不住…我想要…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I can’t—When I try to—”","zh":"“我实在是太高兴了，老兄，”他笑个不停地说，“我忍不住…我想要…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He had passed visibly through two states and was entering upon a third. After his embarrassment and his unreasoning joy he was consumed with wonder at her presence. He had been full of the idea so long, dreamed it right through to the end, waited with his teeth set, so to speak, at an inconceivable pitch of intensity. Now, in the reaction, he was running down like an over-wound clock.","sentences":[{"en":"He had passed visibly through two states and was entering upon a third.","zh":"他明显经历过两种状态，这时正在进入第三种。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After his embarrassment and his unreasoning joy he was consumed with wonder at her presence.","zh":"他先是局促不安，然后欣喜若狂，现在则是因为黛熙的出现而忘乎所以。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had been full of the idea so long, dreamed it right through to the end, waited with his teeth set, so to speak, at an inconceivable pitch of intensity.","zh":"这次相遇曾让他朝思暮想、魂牵梦萦了许多年，他咬紧牙关苦苦地等待，紧张的心理实在是难以形容。现在美梦成真，他的情绪渐渐地松弛下来，不再像发条被拧得太紧的时钟。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Now, in the reaction, he was running down like an over-wound clock.","zh":"这次相遇曾让他朝思暮想、魂牵梦萦了许多年，他咬紧牙关苦苦地等待，紧张的心理实在是难以形容。现在美梦成真，他的情绪渐渐地松弛下来，不再像发条被拧得太紧的时钟。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Recovering himself in a minute he opened for us two hulking patent cabinets which held his massed suits and dressing-gowns and ties, and his shirts, piled like bricks in stacks a dozen high.","sentences":[{"en":"Recovering himself in a minute he opened for us two hulking patent cabinets which held his massed suits and dressing-gowns and ties, and his shirts, piled like bricks in stacks a dozen high.","zh":"片刻之后，他恢复了常态，随即打开两个巨大的古董式衣橱，里面装满了西装、长袍、领带，还有一打一打像砖头那样垒着的衬衣。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got a man in England who buys me clothes. He sends over a selection of things at the beginning of each season, spring and fall.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got a man in England who buys me clothes.","zh":"“我在英国请了个人帮我买衣服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sends over a selection of things at the beginning of each season, spring and fall.”","zh":"每年春季和秋季开始时，他会选一些给我寄过来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He took out a pile of shirts and began throwing them, one by one, before us, shirts of sheer linen and thick silk and fine flannel, which lost their folds as they fell and covered the table in many-coloured disarray. While we admired he brought more and the soft rich heap mounted higher—shirts with stripes and scrolls and plaids in coral and apple-green and lavender and faint orange, with monograms of indian blue. Suddenly, with a strained sound, Daisy bent her head into the shirts and began to cry stormily.","sentences":[{"en":"He took out a pile of shirts and began throwing them, one by one, before us, shirts of sheer linen and thick silk and fine flannel, which lost their folds as they fell and covered the table in many-coloured disarray.","zh":"他抱起一叠衬衣，一件一件扔在我们面前，有亚麻布的、丝绸的、法兰绒的，本来叠得很整齐，但都被他抖开了，五颜六色地散落在桌子上。我们还在仔细欣赏，他又把更多的衬衣抱出来，于是那座柔软而昂贵的小山越堆越高——条纹的、印花的、格子的，珊瑚红的、苹果绿的、薰衣草紫的、橙子黄的，各种款式颜色应有尽有，每件都用深蓝色的丝线绣着他的名字缩写。","scope":"group"},{"en":"While we admired he brought more and the soft rich heap mounted higher—shirts with stripes and scrolls and plaids in coral and apple-green and lavender and faint orange, with monograms of indian blue.","zh":"他抱起一叠衬衣，一件一件扔在我们面前，有亚麻布的、丝绸的、法兰绒的，本来叠得很整齐，但都被他抖开了，五颜六色地散落在桌子上。我们还在仔细欣赏，他又把更多的衬衣抱出来，于是那座柔软而昂贵的小山越堆越高——条纹的、印花的、格子的，珊瑚红的、苹果绿的、薰衣草紫的、橙子黄的，各种款式颜色应有尽有，每件都用深蓝色的丝线绣着他的名字缩写。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Suddenly, with a strained sound, Daisy bent her head into the shirts and began to cry stormily.","zh":"突然间，黛熙忍不住叫了一声，把头埋进衬衣堆里，开始嚎啕大哭。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They’re such beautiful shirts,” she sobbed, her voice muffled in the thick folds. “It makes me sad because I’ve never seen such—such beautiful shirts before.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They’re such beautiful shirts,” she sobbed, her voice muffled in the thick folds.","zh":"“这些衬衣太漂亮了，”她呜呜咽咽地说，声音被厚厚的布料蒙住，听起来不是很清楚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It makes me sad because I’ve never seen such—such beautiful shirts before.”","zh":"“我觉得很伤心，因为我以前从未见过这么…这么漂亮的衬衣。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"After the house, we were to see the grounds and the swimming pool, and the hydroplane, and the midsummer flowers—but outside Gatsby’s window it began to rain again, so we stood in a row looking at the corrugated surface of the Sound.","sentences":[{"en":"After the house, we were to see the grounds and the swimming pool, and the hydroplane, and the midsummer flowers—but outside Gatsby’s window it began to rain again, so we stood in a row looking at the corrugated surface of the Sound.","zh":"看过房子后，本来准备去看草地、游泳池、水上飞机和盛夏的繁花——但盖茨比的窗外又开始下雨，于是我们站成一排，眺望着海湾波澜起伏的水面。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“If it wasn’t for the mist we could see your home across the bay,” said Gatsby. “You always have a green light that burns all night at the end of your dock.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If it wasn’t for the mist we could see your home across the bay,” said Gatsby.","zh":"“可惜有雾，不然我们可以看见对岸你家的房子，”盖茨比说，“你家码头末端总是亮着一盏彻夜不灭的绿灯。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You always have a green light that burns all night at the end of your dock.”","zh":"“可惜有雾，不然我们可以看见对岸你家的房子，”盖茨比说，“你家码头末端总是亮着一盏彻夜不灭的绿灯。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy put her arm through his abruptly, but he seemed absorbed in what he had just said. Possibly it had occurred to him that the colossal significance of that light had now vanished forever. Compared to the great distance that had separated him from Daisy it had seemed very near to her, almost touching her. It had seemed as close as a star to the moon. Now it was again a green light on a dock. His count of enchanted objects had diminished by one.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy put her arm through his abruptly, but he seemed absorbed in what he had just said.","zh":"黛熙突然伸手挽住他，但他似乎沉浸在他刚才说的话里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Possibly it had occurred to him that the colossal significance of that light had now vanished forever.","zh":"也许他已经明白，绿灯无与伦比的重要意义从现在起永远地消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Compared to the great distance that had separated him from Daisy it had seemed very near to her, almost touching her.","zh":"在从前，和他与黛熙之间遥远的距离相比，那盏绿灯似乎离她非常近，近得几乎触手可及。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It had seemed as close as a star to the moon.","zh":"它和黛熙的距离，就像星星和月亮那么近。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now it was again a green light on a dock.","zh":"现在它原形毕露，无非是码头上的一盏灯而已。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His count of enchanted objects had diminished by one.","zh":"让他心醉神迷的物品从此减少了一件。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I began to walk about the room, examining various indefinite objects in the half darkness. A large photograph of an elderly man in yachting costume attracted me, hung on the wall over his desk.","sentences":[{"en":"I began to walk about the room, examining various indefinite objects in the half darkness.","zh":"我开始在房间里随意走走，在昏暗的光线中观看各种模糊不清的摆设。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A large photograph of an elderly man in yachting costume attracted me, hung on the wall over his desk.","zh":"有幅巨大的照片引起了我的注意，画面中是一位穿着游艇服的老先生，就在书桌前面的墙上挂着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who’s this?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who’s this?”","zh":"“这人是谁？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That? That’s Mr. Dan Cody, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That?","zh":"“那个吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That’s Mr. Dan Cody, old sport.”","zh":"那是达恩·科迪先生，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The name sounded faintly familiar.","sentences":[{"en":"The name sounded faintly familiar.","zh":"我觉得这个名字有点耳熟。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He’s dead now. He used to be my best friend years ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He’s dead now.","zh":"“他已经去世了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He used to be my best friend years ago.”","zh":"许多年前，他是我最好的朋友。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was a small picture of Gatsby, also in yachting costume, on the bureau—Gatsby with his head thrown back defiantly—taken apparently when he was about eighteen.","sentences":[{"en":"There was a small picture of Gatsby, also in yachting costume, on the bureau—Gatsby with his head thrown back defiantly—taken apparently when he was about eighteen.","zh":"盖茨比也有张穿着游艇服的照片，很小，就摆在床头柜上。照片里，他桀骜不驯地仰着头，看上去像十八岁左右时拍的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I adore it,” exclaimed Daisy. “The pompadour! You never told me you had a pompadour—or a yacht.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I adore it,” exclaimed Daisy.","zh":"“我好喜欢这张照片呀，”黛熙惊喜地说，“蓬巴杜发型！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“The pompadour!","zh":"“我好喜欢这张照片呀，”黛熙惊喜地说，“蓬巴杜发型！","scope":"group"},{"en":"You never told me you had a pompadour—or a yacht.”","zh":"你以前没跟我说过你剪过蓬巴杜头——也没说过你有游艇。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look at this,” said Gatsby quickly. “Here’s a lot of clippings—about you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look at this,” said Gatsby quickly.","zh":"“快来看，”盖茨比催促说，“这里有很多剪报——都是有关你的新闻。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Here’s a lot of clippings—about you.”","zh":"“快来看，”盖茨比催促说，“这里有很多剪报——都是有关你的新闻。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They stood side by side examining it. I was going to ask to see the rubies when the phone rang, and Gatsby took up the receiver.","sentences":[{"en":"They stood side by side examining it.","zh":"他们肩并肩站着，仔细翻看那本剪报。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was going to ask to see the rubies when the phone rang, and Gatsby took up the receiver.","zh":"我正要请他把红宝石拿出来让我开开眼界，这时电话响了，盖茨比拿起了话筒。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes… Well, I can’t talk now… I can’t talk now, old sport… I said a small town… He must know what a small town is… Well, he’s no use to us if Detroit is his idea of a small town…”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes…","zh":"“是我…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, I can’t talk now…","zh":"嗯，现在我不方便跟你聊…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I can’t talk now, old sport…","zh":"现在我不方便跟你聊，老兄…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I said a small town…","zh":"我说过那是个小城市…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He must know what a small town is…","zh":"他难道连什么是小城市都不懂吗…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, he’s no use to us if Detroit is his idea of a small town…”","zh":"算了，如果他认为底特律是个小城市，那他对我们来说没有用了…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He rang off.","sentences":[{"en":"He rang off.","zh":"他挂了电话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come here quick!” cried Daisy at the window.","sentences":[{"en":"“Come here quick!” cried Daisy at the window.","zh":"“快点过来！”黛熙在窗边大喊。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The rain was still falling, but the darkness had parted in the west, and there was a pink and golden billow of foamy clouds above the sea.","sentences":[{"en":"The rain was still falling, but the darkness had parted in the west, and there was a pink and golden billow of foamy clouds above the sea.","zh":"雨仍在下，但西边的乌云已经分开，几朵粉红色和金色的灿烂晚霞像巨浪般在海面上空翻滚着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look at that,” she whispered, and then after a moment: “I’d like to just get one of those pink clouds and put you in it and push you around.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look at that,” she whispered, and then after a moment: “I’d like to just get one of those pink clouds and put you in it and push you around.”","zh":"“你看，”她喃喃地说。过了片刻，她又说，“我真想弄一片红云，把你放在上面，然后推着你到处走。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I tried to go then, but they wouldn’t hear of it; perhaps my presence made them feel more satisfactorily alone.","sentences":[{"en":"I tried to go then, but they wouldn’t hear of it; perhaps my presence made them feel more satisfactorily alone.","zh":"这时我想要告辞，但他们不许我走；可能有我在场他们才能更加心安理得地幽会吧。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I know what we’ll do,” said Gatsby, “we’ll have Klipspringer play the piano.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know what we’ll do,” said Gatsby, “we’ll have Klipspringer play the piano.”","zh":"“我知道接下来做什么了，”盖茨比说，“我们请克里普斯普林格弹钢琴。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He went out of the room calling “Ewing!” and returned in a few minutes accompanied by an embarrassed, slightly worn young man, with shell-rimmed glasses and scanty blond hair. He was now decently clothed in a “sport shirt,” open at the neck, sneakers, and duck trousers of a nebulous hue.","sentences":[{"en":"He went out of the room calling “Ewing!” and returned in a few minutes accompanied by an embarrassed, slightly worn young man, with shell-rimmed glasses and scanty blond hair.","zh":"他走出房间大喊“埃文”，几分钟后回来了，身后跟着一个表情尴尬、略显憔悴的年轻人。这人戴着玳瑁框眼镜，有一头乱糟糟的金发。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was now decently clothed in a “sport shirt,” open at the neck, sneakers, and duck trousers of a nebulous hue.","zh":"这时他的打扮比较体面，穿着敞领的“运动衫”、运动鞋和一条看不清颜色的帆布长裤。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did we interrupt your exercise?” inquired Daisy politely.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did we interrupt your exercise?” inquired Daisy politely.","zh":"“我们打扰你运动了吗？”黛熙礼貌地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I was asleep,” cried Mr. Klipspringer, in a spasm of embarrassment. “That is, I’d been asleep. Then I got up…”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was asleep,” cried Mr. Klipspringer, in a spasm of embarrassment.","zh":"“我刚才在睡觉，”克里普斯普林格先生尴尬万分地说，“我是说，我原本在睡觉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“That is, I’d been asleep.","zh":"“我刚才在睡觉，”克里普斯普林格先生尴尬万分地说，“我是说，我原本在睡觉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then I got up…”","zh":"然后我就起床…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Klipspringer plays the piano,” said Gatsby, cutting him off. “Don’t you, Ewing, old sport?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Klipspringer plays the piano,” said Gatsby, cutting him off.","zh":"“克里普斯普林格先生会弹钢琴，”盖茨比拦住他的话头说，“对吧，埃文老兄？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Don’t you, Ewing, old sport?”","zh":"“克里普斯普林格先生会弹钢琴，”盖茨比拦住他的话头说，“对吧，埃文老兄？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t play well. I don’t—hardly play at all. I’m all out of prac—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t play well.","zh":"“我弹得不好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t—hardly play at all.","zh":"我不…我根本就不会弹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m all out of prac—”","zh":"我很久没有练…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ll go downstairs,” interrupted Gatsby. He flipped a switch. The grey windows disappeared as the house glowed full of light.","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ll go downstairs,” interrupted Gatsby.","zh":"“我们到楼下去，”盖茨比插嘴说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He flipped a switch.","zh":"他按了一个开关。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The grey windows disappeared as the house glowed full of light.","zh":"房间里变得很亮，那些灰暗的窗户都消失了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"In the music-room Gatsby turned on a solitary lamp beside the piano. He lit Daisy’s cigarette from a trembling match, and sat down with her on a couch far across the room, where there was no light save what the gleaming floor bounced in from the hall.","sentences":[{"en":"In the music-room Gatsby turned on a solitary lamp beside the piano.","zh":"走进音乐厅后，盖茨比旋开钢琴旁边一盏孤独的台灯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He lit Daisy’s cigarette from a trembling match, and sat down with her on a couch far across the room, where there was no light save what the gleaming floor bounced in from the hall.","zh":"他颤抖着用火柴替黛熙点燃香烟，然后陪她在房间远端的沙发上坐下，那边光线很暗，只有地板反照出走廊漏进来的微弱灯光。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When Klipspringer had played “The Love Nest” he turned around on the bench and searched unhappily for Gatsby in the gloom.","sentences":[{"en":"When Klipspringer had played “The Love Nest” he turned around on the bench and searched unhappily for Gatsby in the gloom.","zh":"克里普斯普林格先生弹完《爱巢》之后，坐在凳子上转过身，闷闷不乐地在黑暗中寻找盖茨比的身影。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m all out of practice, you see. I told you I couldn’t play. I’m all out of prac—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m all out of practice, you see.","zh":"“我好久没练习了，这你也知道的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I told you I couldn’t play.","zh":"我跟你说过我不能弹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m all out of prac—”","zh":"我好久没练…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t talk so much, old sport,” commanded Gatsby. “Play!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t talk so much, old sport,” commanded Gatsby.","zh":"“别说这么多话，老兄，”盖茨比命令他，“弹吧！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Play!”","zh":"“别说这么多话，老兄，”盖茨比命令他，“弹吧！”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“In the morning, In the evening, Ain’t we got fun—”","sentences":[{"en":"“In the morning, In the evening, Ain’t we got fun—”","zh":"无论是早上，还是晚上，我们玩得很爽…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Outside the wind was loud and there was a faint flow of thunder along the Sound. All the lights were going on in West Egg now; the electric trains, men-carrying, were plunging home through the rain from New York. It was the hour of a profound human change, and excitement was generating on the air.","sentences":[{"en":"Outside the wind was loud and there was a faint flow of thunder along the Sound.","zh":"外面风声变大了，海湾上掠过一道微弱的闪电。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the lights were going on in West Egg now; the electric trains, men-carrying, were plunging home through the rain from New York.","zh":"此刻西卵已是万家灯火，电动火车载满乘客，冒雨从纽约归来。在这人世发生巨变的时刻，空气中弥漫着兴奋的情绪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the hour of a profound human change, and excitement was generating on the air.","zh":"毫无疑问，千真万确富人会生钱，穷人只会生…孩子","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“One thing’s sure and nothing’s surer The rich get richer and the poor get—children. In the meantime, In between time—”","sentences":[{"en":"“One thing’s sure and nothing’s surer The rich get richer and the poor get—children.","zh":"尽管如此，","scope":"group"},{"en":"In the meantime, In between time—”","zh":"尽管如此，","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As I went over to say goodbye I saw that the expression of bewilderment had come back into Gatsby’s face, as though a faint doubt had occurred to him as to the quality of his present happiness. Almost five years! There must have been moments even that afternoon when Daisy tumbled short of his dreams—not through her own fault, but because of the colossal vitality of his illusion. It had gone beyond her, beyond everything. He had thrown himself into it with a creative passion, adding to it all the time, decking it out with every bright feather that drifted his way. No amount of fire or freshness can challenge what a man can store up in his ghostly heart.","sentences":[{"en":"As I went over to say goodbye I saw that the expression of bewilderment had come back into Gatsby’s face, as though a faint doubt had occurred to him as to the quality of his present happiness.","zh":"哪怕如此…走过去道别的时候，我发现那种惶惑的表情又回到了盖茨比脸上，仿佛有点怀疑他目前这种快乐的真假。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Almost five years!","zh":"差不多五年了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There must have been moments even that afternoon when Daisy tumbled short of his dreams—not through her own fault, but because of the colossal vitality of his illusion.","zh":"那天下午，黛熙肯定有不少地方让他大失所望——倒不是说黛熙本人有什么缺点，而是因为他把黛熙幻想得太美好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It had gone beyond her, beyond everything.","zh":"这幻想超越了黛熙，超越了所有事物。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had thrown himself into it with a creative passion, adding to it all the time, decking it out with every bright feather that drifted his way.","zh":"他这几年的心血全用来创造这个幻想，不停地为它添砖加瓦，将他遇到的一切美好东西都用来修饰它。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No amount of fire or freshness can challenge what a man can store up in his ghostly heart.","zh":"再似火的热情，再漂亮的外表，也比不上为情所困的心堆积起来的幻想。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As I watched him he adjusted himself a little, visibly. His hand took hold of hers, and as she said something low in his ear he turned toward her with a rush of emotion. I think that voice held him most, with its fluctuating, feverish warmth, because it couldn’t be over-dreamed—that voice was a deathless song.","sentences":[{"en":"As I watched him he adjusted himself a little, visibly.","zh":"就在我望着他时，他明显已经有点适应现实了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His hand took hold of hers, and as she said something low in his ear he turned toward her with a rush of emotion.","zh":"他握紧黛熙的手；黛熙在他耳边轻轻说了几句话，于是他动情地转过身去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think that voice held him most, with its fluctuating, feverish warmth, because it couldn’t be over-dreamed—that voice was a deathless song.","zh":"我想最让他入迷的是那声音，那抑扬顿挫、热情奔放的声音，因为它的动听是盖茨比梦想不到的——那声音是一曲不死的歌。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They had forgotten me, but Daisy glanced up and held out her hand; Gatsby didn’t know me now at all. I looked once more at them and they looked back at me, remotely, possessed by intense life. Then I went out of the room and down the marble steps into the rain, leaving them there together.","sentences":[{"en":"They had forgotten me, but Daisy glanced up and held out her hand; Gatsby didn’t know me now at all.","zh":"他们完全忘了我，但随后黛熙眼睛朝上看了我一眼，把手伸出来跟我握别；至于盖茨比，他对我根本视若无睹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I looked once more at them and they looked back at me, remotely, possessed by intense life.","zh":"我走到门口，再次回头望望他们，他们也在看着我，远远地，仿佛处在另一个世界。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then I went out of the room and down the marble steps into the rain, leaving them there together.","zh":"然后我走出那个房间，走下大理石台阶，走进雨里，留下他们两个在一起。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-6","n":6,"title":"Chapter VI","titleZh":"第六章","paragraphs":[{"en":"About this time an ambitious young reporter from New York arrived one morning at Gatsby’s door and asked him if he had anything to say.","sentences":[{"en":"About this time an ambitious young reporter from New York arrived one morning at Gatsby’s door and asked him if he had anything to say.","zh":"大约在这段时间的某天早上，纽约有个上进的青年记者来到盖茨比家门口，问他是否有话要说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Anything to say about what?” inquired Gatsby politely.","sentences":[{"en":"“Anything to say about what?” inquired Gatsby politely.","zh":"“你要我说什么话呢？”盖茨比礼貌地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why—any statement to give out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why—any statement to give out.”","zh":"“哎呀…随便说说就可以。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It transpired after a confused five minutes that the man had heard Gatsby’s name around his office in a connection which he either wouldn’t reveal or didn’t fully understand. This was his day off and with laudable initiative he had hurried out “to see.”","sentences":[{"en":"It transpired after a confused five minutes that the man had heard Gatsby’s name around his office in a connection which he either wouldn’t reveal or didn’t fully understand.","zh":"不清不楚地纠缠了五分钟之后，终于弄明白是怎么回事了。原来那记者曾在报社听人提到盖茨比的名字，但他不肯说那人是谁，也许根本就不认识。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This was his day off and with laudable initiative he had hurried out “to see.”","zh":"这天他正好休息，于是精神可嘉地赶过来“看看”。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was a random shot, and yet the reporter’s instinct was right. Gatsby’s notoriety, spread about by the hundreds who had accepted his hospitality and so become authorities upon his past, had increased all summer until he fell just short of being news. Contemporary legends such as the “underground pipeline to Canada” attached themselves to him, and there was one persistent story that he didn’t live in a house at all, but in a boat that looked like a house and was moved secretly up and down the Long Island shore. Just why these inventions were a source of satisfaction to James Gatz of North Dakota, isn’t easy to say.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a random shot, and yet the reporter’s instinct was right.","zh":"那记者是无的放矢，但他的直觉是对的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby’s notoriety, spread about by the hundreds who had accepted his hospitality and so become authorities upon his past, had increased all summer until he fell just short of being news.","zh":"那年夏天，数百个接受过盖茨比招待的人自诩为他的知交，到处信口开河地宣扬他的经历，于是盖茨比的名头越来越响，就快成为新闻人物了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Contemporary legends such as the “underground pipeline to Canada” attached themselves to him, and there was one persistent story that he didn’t live in a house at all, but in a boat that looked like a house and was moved secretly up and down the Long Island shore.","zh":"各种轰动一时的传说，比如“用地下管道从加拿大走私烈酒”，都被说成跟他有关；还有个流传很久的谣言，说他住的地方根本不是一座房子，而是一艘外观像房子的船，偷偷地在长岛沿岸开来开去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just why these inventions were a source of satisfaction to James Gatz of North Dakota, isn’t easy to say.","zh":"至于北达科他州的詹姆斯·盖兹为何对这些流言甘之如饴，这倒是个很难回答的问题。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"James Gatz—that was really, or at least legally, his name. He had changed it at the age of seventeen and at the specific moment that witnessed the beginning of his career—when he saw Dan Cody’s yacht drop anchor over the most insidious flat on Lake Superior. It was James Gatz who had been loafing along the beach that afternoon in a torn green jersey and a pair of canvas pants, but it was already Jay Gatsby who borrowed a rowboat, pulled out to the Tuolomee, and informed Cody that a wind might catch him and break him up in half an hour.","sentences":[{"en":"James Gatz—that was really, or at least legally, his name.","zh":"詹姆斯·盖兹——这是他的真名，至少是他法律上的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had changed it at the age of seventeen and at the specific moment that witnessed the beginning of his career—when he saw Dan Cody’s yacht drop anchor over the most insidious flat on Lake Superior.","zh":"把名字改掉那年他十七岁，那是他毕生事业的开端——当时他看见达恩·科迪的游艇停泊在苏必利湖最危险的水面上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was James Gatz who had been loafing along the beach that afternoon in a torn green jersey and a pair of canvas pants, but it was already Jay Gatsby who borrowed a rowboat, pulled out to the Tuolomee, and informed Cody that a wind might catch him and break him up in half an hour.","zh":"那天下午穿着破旧的绿色球衣和帆布裤在沙滩上消磨时间的是詹姆士·盖兹，而借了小船划到“陀罗美号”通知科迪半小时内可能会有大风刮翻游艇的，却已经是杰伊·盖茨比了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I suppose he’d had the name ready for a long time, even then. His parents were shiftless and unsuccessful farm people—his imagination had never really accepted them as his parents at all. The truth was that Jay Gatsby of West Egg, Long Island, sprang from his Platonic conception of himself. He was a son of God—a phrase which, if it means anything, means just that—and he must be about His Father’s business, the service of a vast, vulgar, and meretricious beauty. So he invented just the sort of Jay Gatsby that a seventeen-year-old boy would be likely to invent, and to this conception he was faithful to the end.","sentences":[{"en":"I suppose he’d had the name ready for a long time, even then.","zh":"我猜他早就想好要换成这个名字了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His parents were shiftless and unsuccessful farm people—his imagination had never really accepted them as his parents at all.","zh":"他父母是穷困潦倒的农民——他从来就没有把他们当成亲生父母。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The truth was that Jay Gatsby of West Egg, Long Island, sprang from his Platonic conception of himself.","zh":"其实长岛西卵的杰伊·盖茨比来自他对自己的柏拉图理念。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was a son of God—a phrase which, if it means anything, means just that—and he must be about His Father’s business, the service of a vast, vulgar, and meretricious beauty.","zh":"他是上帝之子——他确实是这么自许的——他必须为他的天父效命，献身于一种庸俗而浮华的大美。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So he invented just the sort of Jay Gatsby that a seventeen-year-old boy would be likely to invent, and to this conception he was faithful to the end.","zh":"所以他创造的这个杰伊·盖茨比，正是十七岁的男孩所崇拜的英雄人物，而他也矢志不渝地忠于这个理想。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For over a year he had been beating his way along the south shore of Lake Superior as a clam-digger and a salmon-fisher or in any other capacity that brought him food and bed. His brown, hardening body lived naturally through the half-fierce, half-lazy work of the bracing days. He knew women early, and since they spoiled him he became contemptuous of them, of young virgins because they were ignorant, of the others because they were hysterical about things which in his overwhelming self-absorption he took for granted.","sentences":[{"en":"For over a year he had been beating his way along the south shore of Lake Superior as a clam-digger and a salmon-fisher or in any other capacity that brought him food and bed.","zh":"此前一年多的时间里，他在苏必利湖南岸艰难度日，每天捞蛤蜊、打鲑鱼，也做其他能带来食物和床铺的事情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His brown, hardening body lived naturally through the half-fierce, half-lazy work of the bracing days.","zh":"他那被阳光晒得发黄的结实身体时而勤劳时而懒惰，自在地度过了那些气候宜人的日子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He knew women early, and since they spoiled him he became contemptuous of them, of young virgins because they were ignorant, of the others because they were hysterical about things which in his overwhelming self-absorption he took for granted.","zh":"他早就跟不少女人发生过关系，这些女人很宠爱他，反倒惹他看不起，因为年轻的少女太无知，成熟的女人则常常因为他做了某些事情变得歇斯底里——而在只顾自己感受的他看来，他做那些事情是理所当然的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But his heart was in a constant, turbulent riot. The most grotesque and fantastic conceits haunted him in his bed at night. A universe of ineffable gaudiness spun itself out in his brain while the clock ticked on the washstand and the moon soaked with wet light his tangled clothes upon the floor. Each night he added to the pattern of his fancies until drowsiness closed down upon some vivid scene with an oblivious embrace. For a while these reveries provided an outlet for his imagination; they were a satisfactory hint of the unreality of reality, a promise that the rock of the world was founded securely on a fairy’s wing.","sentences":[{"en":"But his heart was in a constant, turbulent riot.","zh":"但他的心总是止不住地躁动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The most grotesque and fantastic conceits haunted him in his bed at night.","zh":"夜里躺在床上时，他会产生各种荒诞离奇的想法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A universe of ineffable gaudiness spun itself out in his brain while the clock ticked on the washstand and the moon soaked with wet light his tangled clothes upon the floor.","zh":"他脑海中慢慢浮现的是美好得难以言喻的浮华世界，全然忘了时钟在脸盆架上滴答响，月光如水般地浸润着地上乱糟糟的衣服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Each night he added to the pattern of his fancies until drowsiness closed down upon some vivid scene with an oblivious embrace.","zh":"每天晚上他都会为各种梦想锦上添花，直到倦意袭来，让他在栩栩如生的幻境中沉沉睡去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a while these reveries provided an outlet for his imagination; they were a satisfactory hint of the unreality of reality, a promise that the rock of the world was founded securely on a fairy’s wing.","zh":"这些胡思乱想让他的想象力有了宣泄的出口，也给了令他心满意足的暗示：现状并不是真实的，世界是可以牢牢地建立在仙女的羽翼之上的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"An instinct toward his future glory had led him, some months before, to the small Lutheran College of St. Olaf’s in southern Minnesota. He stayed there two weeks, dismayed at its ferocious indifference to the drums of his destiny, to destiny itself, and despising the janitor’s work with which he was to pay his way through. Then he drifted back to Lake Superior, and he was still searching for something to do on the day that Dan Cody’s yacht dropped anchor in the shallows alongshore.","sentences":[{"en":"An instinct toward his future glory had led him, some months before, to the small Lutheran College of St. Olaf’s in southern Minnesota.","zh":"更早之前几个月，为了寻找光明的前程，他曾到明尼苏达州南部的圣奥拉夫学院半工半读。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stayed there two weeks, dismayed at its ferocious indifference to the drums of his destiny, to destiny itself, and despising the janitor’s work with which he was to pay his way through.","zh":"他在这个路德派的小学校待了两个星期，大失所望地发现那里对他的远大抱负和命运本身漠不关心，也很憎恶那份打扫宿舍的工作。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he drifted back to Lake Superior, and he was still searching for something to do on the day that Dan Cody’s yacht dropped anchor in the shallows alongshore.","zh":"然后他四处流落，最后还是回到了苏必利湖；那天他依然为没找到正经事情做而发愁，随即看见达恩·科迪的游艇在湖边浅水区抛下锚来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Cody was fifty years old then, a product of the Nevada silver fields, of the Yukon, of every rush for metal since seventy-five. The transactions in Montana copper that made him many times a millionaire found him physically robust but on the verge of soft-mindedness, and, suspecting this, an infinite number of women tried to separate him from his money. The none too savoury ramifications by which Ella Kaye, the newspaper woman, played Madame de Maintenon to his weakness and sent him to sea in a yacht, were common property of the turgid journalism in 1902. He had been coasting along all too hospitable shores for five years when he turned up as James Gatz’s destiny in Little Girl Bay.","sentences":[{"en":"Cody was fifty years old then, a product of the Nevada silver fields, of the Yukon, of every rush for metal since seventy-five.","zh":"当时科迪已是五十几岁的老人，他曾涉足内华达州的银矿、犹空地区，以及1875年以来每个发现金属矿藏的地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The transactions in Montana copper that made him many times a millionaire found him physically robust but on the verge of soft-mindedness, and, suspecting this, an infinite number of women tried to separate him from his money.","zh":"蒙大拿铜矿的生意让他发了好几百万的横财之后，他的身体依然健壮，但头脑已经有点糊涂了。无数察觉到这种情况的女人都想来骗他的钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The none too savoury ramifications by which Ella Kaye, the newspaper woman, played Madame de Maintenon to his weakness and sent him to sea in a yacht, were common property of the turgid journalism in 1902.","zh":"其中最成功的莫过于艾拉·凯伊，这位女记者抓住他的弱点，扮演了曼特农夫人的角色，打发他乘坐游艇到海上环游，这是1902年许多报刊竞相披露的新闻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had been coasting along all too hospitable shores for five years when he turned up as James Gatz’s destiny in Little Girl Bay.","zh":"他乘游艇沿着各处海岸游玩了五年，所到之处大受欢迎，然后来到苏必利湖的少女湾，成为詹姆斯·盖兹的命中贵人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"To young Gatz, resting on his oars and looking up at the railed deck, that yacht represented all the beauty and glamour in the world. I suppose he smiled at Cody—he had probably discovered that people liked him when he smiled. At any rate Cody asked him a few questions (one of them elicited the brand new name) and found that he was quick and extravagantly ambitious. A few days later he took him to Duluth and bought him a blue coat, six pairs of white duck trousers, and a yachting cap. And when the Tuolomee left for the West Indies and the Barbary Coast, Gatsby left too.","sentences":[{"en":"To young Gatz, resting on his oars and looking up at the railed deck, that yacht represented all the beauty and glamour in the world.","zh":"当年轻的盖兹扶着双桨，仰望围着栏杆的甲板，那艘游艇在他眼里代表了人世间所有的美丽和魅力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I suppose he smiled at Cody—he had probably discovered that people liked him when he smiled.","zh":"我猜想他对科迪微笑了——他可能早已发现人们喜欢他的笑脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At any rate Cody asked him a few questions (one of them elicited the brand new name) and found that he was quick and extravagantly ambitious.","zh":"反正科迪问了他几个问题（其中之一引出了那个崭新的名字），发现他机智敏捷，而且又极有抱负。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A few days later he took him to Duluth and bought him a blue coat, six pairs of white duck trousers, and a yachting cap.","zh":"几天后，科迪把他带到德卢斯，给他买了一件蓝色的上衣、六条白色的帆布裤和一顶游艇帽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And when the Tuolomee left for the West Indies and the Barbary Coast, Gatsby left too.","zh":"当“陀罗美号”扬帆前往西印度群岛和巴贝里海岸时，盖茨比也跟着去了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was employed in a vague personal capacity—while he remained with Cody he was in turn steward, mate, skipper, secretary, and even jailor, for Dan Cody sober knew what lavish doings Dan Cody drunk might soon be about, and he provided for such contingencies by reposing more and more trust in Gatsby. The arrangement lasted five years, during which the boat went three times around the Continent. It might have lasted indefinitely except for the fact that Ella Kaye came on board one night in Boston and a week later Dan Cody inhospitably died.","sentences":[{"en":"He was employed in a vague personal capacity—while he remained with Cody he was in turn steward, mate, skipper, secretary, and even jailor, for Dan Cody sober knew what lavish doings Dan Cody drunk might soon be about, and he provided for such contingencies by reposing more and more trust in Gatsby.","zh":"他并没有特定的职务——陪在科迪身边时，他先后当过厨房总管、大副、船长和秘书，甚至当过监护人，因为清醒的达恩·科迪知道醉后的达恩·科迪会做出各种挥金如土的荒唐事，于是逐渐把各种重要的任务都托付给盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The arrangement lasted five years, during which the boat went three times around the Continent.","zh":"这种关系维持了五年，在此期间“陀罗美号”环绕美洲大陆转了三圈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It might have lasted indefinitely except for the fact that Ella Kaye came on board one night in Boston and a week later Dan Cody inhospitably died.","zh":"它本来会永久持续下去的，只是某天夜里艾拉·凯伊在波士顿登上了游艇，一个星期之后，达恩·科迪被活活气死了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I remember the portrait of him up in Gatsby’s bedroom, a grey, florid man with a hard, empty face—the pioneer debauchee, who during one phase of American life brought back to the Eastern seaboard the savage violence of the frontier brothel and saloon. It was indirectly due to Cody that Gatsby drank so little. Sometimes in the course of gay parties women used to rub champagne into his hair; for himself he formed the habit of letting liquor alone.","sentences":[{"en":"I remember the portrait of him up in Gatsby’s bedroom, a grey, florid man with a hard, empty face—the pioneer debauchee, who during one phase of American life brought back to the Eastern seaboard the savage violence of the frontier brothel and saloon.","zh":"我记得曾在盖茨比的卧室见过他的照片，这老人满头白发，面色红润，有一张冷酷无情的脸。他是那种沉湎酒色的拓荒者；这类人曾在某个时期将西部妓院酒馆的粗暴习气带到东部沿海地区的社交生活中来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was indirectly due to Cody that Gatsby drank so little.","zh":"大概是受到科迪的间接影响吧，盖茨比基本上不喝酒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes in the course of gay parties women used to rub champagne into his hair; for himself he formed the habit of letting liquor alone.","zh":"在那些欢乐的宴会上，常常有女人死皮赖脸向他劝酒，但盖茨比本人早就养成了远离酒精的习惯。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And it was from Cody that he inherited money—a legacy of twenty-five thousand dollars. He didn’t get it. He never understood the legal device that was used against him, but what remained of the millions went intact to Ella Kaye. He was left with his singularly appropriate education; the vague contour of Jay Gatsby had filled out to the substantiality of a man.","sentences":[{"en":"And it was from Cody that he inherited money—a legacy of twenty-five thousand dollars.","zh":"他继承的钱其实来自科迪，一笔两万五千美元的遗产。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He didn’t get it.","zh":"他没拿到这笔钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He never understood the legal device that was used against him, but what remained of the millions went intact to Ella Kaye.","zh":"他始终不明白别人用来对付他的法律手段，但数百万美元完完整整地都归艾拉·凯伊所有了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was left with his singularly appropriate education; the vague contour of Jay Gatsby had filled out to the substantiality of a man.","zh":"他得到的是一段特别适合他的教育；杰伊·盖茨比原本只是模糊的轮廓，这时已经变得具体而形象了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"He told me all this very much later, but I’ve put it down here with the idea of exploding those first wild rumours about his antecedents, which weren’t even faintly true. Moreover he told it to me at a time of confusion, when I had reached the point of believing everything and nothing about him. So I take advantage of this short halt, while Gatsby, so to speak, caught his breath, to clear this set of misconceptions away.","sentences":[{"en":"He told me all this very much later, but I’ve put it down here with the idea of exploding those first wild rumours about his antecedents, which weren’t even faintly true.","zh":"这个故事是他很久以后才告诉我的，我在这里写下来，是为了替他辟谣，那些有关其经历的传言，没有一丁半点是真的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover he told it to me at a time of confusion, when I had reached the point of believing everything and nothing about him.","zh":"再者，他跟我说起这些话时，我对他的看法已经很矛盾了，既相信他说的都是真话，又觉得半句都不可信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So I take advantage of this short halt, while Gatsby, so to speak, caught his breath, to clear this set of misconceptions away.","zh":"所以我趁这个短暂的停顿，趁着命途多舛的盖茨比终于能喘口气的时候，把它写出来以正视听。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was a halt, too, in my association with his affairs. For several weeks I didn’t see him or hear his voice on the phone—mostly I was in New York, trotting around with Jordan and trying to ingratiate myself with her senile aunt—but finally I went over to his house one Sunday afternoon. I hadn’t been there two minutes when somebody brought Tom Buchanan in for a drink. I was startled, naturally, but the really surprising thing was that it hadn’t happened before.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a halt, too, in my association with his affairs.","zh":"当时我和他的交往也陷入了停顿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For several weeks I didn’t see him or hear his voice on the phone—mostly I was in New York, trotting around with Jordan and trying to ingratiate myself with her senile aunt—but finally I went over to his house one Sunday afternoon.","zh":"我接连几个星期没有见到他，也没在电话里听到他的声音。大多数时间我住在纽约，和乔丹谈情说爱，试图讨好她那年迈的姑妈。但最后我又去他家了，是在某个星期天下午。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I hadn’t been there two minutes when somebody brought Tom Buchanan in for a drink.","zh":"我进去还不到两分钟，就有人带着汤姆·布坎南来讨杯酒喝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was startled, naturally, but the really surprising thing was that it hadn’t happened before.","zh":"我当然吓坏了，但其实真正值得吃惊的是，这种事情居然直到现在才发生。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They were a party of three on horseback—Tom and a man named Sloane and a pretty woman in a brown riding-habit, who had been there previously.","sentences":[{"en":"They were a party of three on horseback—Tom and a man named Sloane and a pretty woman in a brown riding-habit, who had been there previously.","zh":"他们三个人之前在外面骑马——汤姆、一个叫斯隆的男人，还有个漂亮的女人，她穿着棕色的骑马服，以前来过这里的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m delighted to see you,” said Gatsby, standing on his porch. “I’m delighted that you dropped in.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m delighted to see you,” said Gatsby, standing on his porch.","zh":"“我很高兴见到你们，”盖茨比站在门廊上说，“很欢迎你们进来坐坐。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m delighted that you dropped in.”","zh":"“我很高兴见到你们，”盖茨比站在门廊上说，“很欢迎你们进来坐坐。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As though they cared!","sentences":[{"en":"As though they cared!","zh":"其实他们才不管盖茨比是否欢迎呢！","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Sit right down. Have a cigarette or a cigar.” He walked around the room quickly, ringing bells. “I’ll have something to drink for you in just a minute.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sit right down.","zh":"“请坐，请坐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Have a cigarette or a cigar.”","zh":"来根香烟或者雪茄吧。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He walked around the room quickly, ringing bells.","zh":"他在客厅里匆匆地走来走去，不停地按铃叫佣人来。“喝的东西马上就来。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll have something to drink for you in just a minute.”","zh":"他在客厅里匆匆地走来走去，不停地按铃叫佣人来。“喝的东西马上就来。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was profoundly affected by the fact that Tom was there. But he would be uneasy anyhow until he had given them something, realizing in a vague way that that was all they came for. Mr. Sloane wanted nothing. A lemonade? No, thanks. A little champagne? Nothing at all, thanks… I’m sorry—","sentences":[{"en":"He was profoundly affected by the fact that Tom was there.","zh":"汤姆的光临让他有点措手不及。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he would be uneasy anyhow until he had given them something, realizing in a vague way that that was all they came for.","zh":"但反正每逢有客人上门，他总是很拘谨地忙着拿东西出来招待他们，因为他其实隐约知道这些人就是为了这个来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mr. Sloane wanted nothing.","zh":"斯隆先生什么都不想要。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A lemonade?","zh":"斯隆先生什么都不想要。","scope":"group"},{"en":"No, thanks.","zh":"来杯柠檬汁？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A little champagne?","zh":"不用啦，谢谢。香槟呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nothing at all, thanks…","zh":"什么都不要，谢谢…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m sorry—","zh":"真是抱歉…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you have a nice ride?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you have a nice ride?”","zh":"“你们骑马骑得好吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Very good roads around here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very good roads around here.”","zh":"“这周围的道路非常好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I suppose the automobiles—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I suppose the automobiles—”","zh":"“我想汽车不…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yeah.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yeah.”","zh":"“是啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Moved by an irresistible impulse, Gatsby turned to Tom, who had accepted the introduction as a stranger.","sentences":[{"en":"Moved by an irresistible impulse, Gatsby turned to Tom, who had accepted the introduction as a stranger.","zh":"盖茨比抑制不住心里的冲动，转头去看汤姆，刚才他是被当成陌生人介绍给盖茨比的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I believe we’ve met somewhere before, Mr. Buchanan.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I believe we’ve met somewhere before, Mr. Buchanan.”","zh":"“我们以前见过面的，布坎南先生。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, yes,” said Tom, gruffly polite, but obviously not remembering. “So we did. I remember very well.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, yes,” said Tom, gruffly polite, but obviously not remembering.","zh":"“是啊，”汤姆强装礼貌地说，但他显然没想起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“So we did.","zh":"“我们见过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I remember very well.”","zh":"我记得非常清楚。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“About two weeks ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“About two weeks ago.”","zh":"“大约两个星期前。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s right. You were with Nick here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s right.","zh":"“对，对。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You were with Nick here.”","zh":"当时你和尼克在一起。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I know your wife,” continued Gatsby, almost aggressively.","sentences":[{"en":"“I know your wife,” continued Gatsby, almost aggressively.","zh":"“我认识你太太，”盖茨比继续说，这几乎是挑衅了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That so?”","sentences":[{"en":"“That so?”","zh":"“真的吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom turned to me.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom turned to me.","zh":"汤姆扭头看着我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You live near here, Nick?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You live near here, Nick?”","zh":"“尼克，你就住在附近吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Next door.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Next door.”","zh":"“隔壁。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That so?”","sentences":[{"en":"“That so?”","zh":"“真的吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Mr. Sloane didn’t enter into the conversation, but lounged back haughtily in his chair; the woman said nothing either—until unexpectedly, after two highballs, she became cordial.","sentences":[{"en":"Mr. Sloane didn’t enter into the conversation, but lounged back haughtily in his chair; the woman said nothing either—until unexpectedly, after two highballs, she became cordial.","zh":"斯隆先生没有开口，而是大模大样地靠在椅背上；那女人也没有说话——后来两杯香槟下肚，她突然变得健谈起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ll all come over to your next party, Mr. Gatsby,” she suggested. “What do you say?”","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ll all come over to your next party, Mr. Gatsby,” she suggested.","zh":"“下次我们都来参加你的宴会吧，盖茨比先生，”她提议说，“你觉得呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What do you say?”","zh":"“下次我们都来参加你的宴会吧，盖茨比先生，”她提议说，“你觉得呢？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Certainly; I’d be delighted to have you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly; I’d be delighted to have you.”","zh":"“当然好啊，你们肯来我很高兴。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Be ver’ nice,” said Mr. Sloane, without gratitude. “Well—think ought to be starting home.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Be ver’ nice,” said Mr. Sloane, without gratitude.","zh":"“非常好，”斯隆先生毫不感激地说，“嗯——我们应该回家了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Well—think ought to be starting home.”","zh":"“非常好，”斯隆先生毫不感激地说，“嗯——我们应该回家了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Please don’t hurry,” Gatsby urged them. He had control of himself now, and he wanted to see more of Tom. “Why don’t you—why don’t you stay for supper? I wouldn’t be surprised if some other people dropped in from New York.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Please don’t hurry,” Gatsby urged them.","zh":"“不要这么着急，”盖茨比恳切地对他们说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had control of himself now, and he wanted to see more of Tom.","zh":"现在他变得镇定了，想要多了解汤姆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why don’t you—why don’t you stay for supper?","zh":"“你们何不…何不留下来吃晚饭呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wouldn’t be surprised if some other people dropped in from New York.”","zh":"说不定纽约也会有人来呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You come to supper with me,” said the lady enthusiastically. “Both of you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You come to supper with me,” said the lady enthusiastically.","zh":"“你到我家吃饭吧，”那位女士热心地说，“你们俩都来。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Both of you.”","zh":"“你到我家吃饭吧，”那位女士热心地说，“你们俩都来。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"This included me. Mr. Sloane got to his feet.","sentences":[{"en":"This included me.","zh":"她连我也请了。斯隆先生站起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Mr. Sloane got to his feet.","zh":"她连我也请了。斯隆先生站起来。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come along,” he said—but to her only.","sentences":[{"en":"“Come along,” he said—but to her only.","zh":"“走吧，”他说——但只对那位女士说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I mean it,” she insisted. “I’d love to have you. Lots of room.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I mean it,” she insisted.","zh":"“说真的，”她执意地说，“我希望你们去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’d love to have you.","zh":"“说真的，”她执意地说，“我希望你们去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Lots of room.”","zh":"我家地方很大。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby looked at me questioningly. He wanted to go and he didn’t see that Mr. Sloane had determined he shouldn’t.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby looked at me questioningly.","zh":"盖茨比犹疑地看着我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He wanted to go and he didn’t see that Mr. Sloane had determined he shouldn’t.","zh":"他想要去，但没看出来斯隆先生刚刚表示他不该去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m afraid I won’t be able to,” I said.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m afraid I won’t be able to,” I said.","zh":"“我恐怕去不了，”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, you come,” she urged, concentrating on Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you come,” she urged, concentrating on Gatsby.","zh":"“好吧，那你来，”她极力邀请盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Mr. Sloane murmured something close to her ear.","sentences":[{"en":"Mr. Sloane murmured something close to her ear.","zh":"斯隆先生在她耳边嘀咕了几句。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We won’t be late if we start now,” she insisted aloud.","sentences":[{"en":"“We won’t be late if we start now,” she insisted aloud.","zh":"“现在出发就还来得及，”她大声地固执己见。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I haven’t got a horse,” said Gatsby. “I used to ride in the army, but I’ve never bought a horse. I’ll have to follow you in my car. Excuse me for just a minute.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I haven’t got a horse,” said Gatsby.","zh":"“我没有马，”盖茨比说，“以前我在部队常常骑，但我没买过马。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I used to ride in the army, but I’ve never bought a horse.","zh":"“我没有马，”盖茨比说，“以前我在部队常常骑，但我没买过马。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll have to follow you in my car.","zh":"我只能开车跟你们去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Excuse me for just a minute.”","zh":"请稍等我一分钟。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The rest of us walked out on the porch, where Sloane and the lady began an impassioned conversation aside.","sentences":[{"en":"The rest of us walked out on the porch, where Sloane and the lady began an impassioned conversation aside.","zh":"我们四个人走到门廊，斯隆和那位女士站到旁边，激烈地争论着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“My God, I believe the man’s coming,” said Tom. “Doesn’t he know she doesn’t want him?”","sentences":[{"en":"“My God, I believe the man’s coming,” said Tom.","zh":"“天哪，他居然要去，”汤姆说，“难道他不知道她根本不想请他吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Doesn’t he know she doesn’t want him?”","zh":"“天哪，他居然要去，”汤姆说，“难道他不知道她根本不想请他吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She says she does want him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She says she does want him.”","zh":"“她说她要请的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She has a big dinner party and he won’t know a soul there.” He frowned. “I wonder where in the devil he met Daisy. By God, I may be old-fashioned in my ideas, but women run around too much these days to suit me. They meet all kinds of crazy fish.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She has a big dinner party and he won’t know a soul there.”","zh":"“她今晚有个盛大的宴会，他去了谁也不认识。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He frowned.","zh":"他皱起眉头，“我很奇怪他到底是在哪里遇到黛熙的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I wonder where in the devil he met Daisy.","zh":"他皱起眉头，“我很奇怪他到底是在哪里遇到黛熙的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"By God, I may be old-fashioned in my ideas, but women run around too much these days to suit me.","zh":"上帝作证，可能我是老思想，但现在的女人到处抛头露面，在我看来是不合适的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They meet all kinds of crazy fish.”","zh":"她们会遇到各种各样的疯子。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Suddenly Mr. Sloane and the lady walked down the steps and mounted their horses.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly Mr. Sloane and the lady walked down the steps and mounted their horses.","zh":"斯隆先生和那位女士突然走下了台阶，登上他们的马。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come on,” said Mr. Sloane to Tom, “we’re late. We’ve got to go.” And then to me: “Tell him we couldn’t wait, will you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come on,” said Mr. Sloane to Tom, “we’re late.","zh":"“走吧，”斯隆先生对汤姆说，“我们迟到啦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We’ve got to go.”","zh":"赶快走。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then to me: “Tell him we couldn’t wait, will you?”","zh":"然后又对我说：“跟他说我们没时间等了，好吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom and I shook hands, the rest of us exchanged a cool nod, and they trotted quickly down the drive, disappearing under the August foliage just as Gatsby, with hat and light overcoat in hand, came out the front door.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom and I shook hands, the rest of us exchanged a cool nod, and they trotted quickly down the drive, disappearing under the August foliage just as Gatsby, with hat and light overcoat in hand, came out the front door.","zh":"汤姆和我握手道别，另外两人跟我冷淡地点了点头，然后他们沿着车道一溜快跑，消失在八月的树荫里。这时盖茨比手里拿着帽子和薄外套，正好走出前门。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom was evidently perturbed at Daisy’s running around alone, for on the following Saturday night he came with her to Gatsby’s party. Perhaps his presence gave the evening its peculiar quality of oppressiveness—it stands out in my memory from Gatsby’s other parties that summer. There were the same people, or at least the same sort of people, the same profusion of champagne, the same many-coloured, many-keyed commotion, but I felt an unpleasantness in the air, a pervading harshness that hadn’t been there before. Or perhaps I had merely grown used to it, grown to accept West Egg as a world complete in itself, with its own standards and its own great figures, second to nothing because it had no consciousness of being so, and now I was looking at it again, through Daisy’s eyes. It is invariably saddening to look through new eyes at things upon which you have expended your own powers of adjustment.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom was evidently perturbed at Daisy’s running around alone, for on the following Saturday night he came with her to Gatsby’s party.","zh":"汤姆显然不放心黛熙一个人出来玩，因为接下来那个星期六晚上，他陪黛熙来参加盖茨比的宴会。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps his presence gave the evening its peculiar quality of oppressiveness—it stands out in my memory from Gatsby’s other parties that summer.","zh":"也许他的出席使那天晚上的气氛变得特别压抑——那年夏天我在盖茨比家参加了不少宴会，这次印象尤其深刻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were the same people, or at least the same sort of people, the same profusion of champagne, the same many-coloured, many-keyed commotion, but I felt an unpleasantness in the air, a pervading harshness that hadn’t been there before.","zh":"人还是那些人，至少还是那类人，香槟还是源源不断地漫溢着，还是五颜六色、七嘴八舌的喧闹，但我觉得现场有一种不愉快的感觉，充盈着一种沉闷的氛围。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Or perhaps I had merely grown used to it, grown to accept West Egg as a world complete in itself, with its own standards and its own great figures, second to nothing because it had no consciousness of being so, and now I was looking at it again, through Daisy’s eyes.","zh":"或许是因为我早已习惯了这样的场合，渐渐认为西卵自成天地，有其自身的风俗和独特的人物，是独一无二的好地方，但现在我却通过黛熙的眼睛来重新认识它。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is invariably saddening to look through new eyes at things upon which you have expended your own powers of adjustment.","zh":"如果你用新的眼光来看待你费了很大劲才适应的事物，感到难受总是不可避免的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They arrived at twilight, and, as we strolled out among the sparkling hundreds, Daisy’s voice was playing murmurous tricks in her throat.","sentences":[{"en":"They arrived at twilight, and, as we strolled out among the sparkling hundreds, Daisy’s voice was playing murmurous tricks in her throat.","zh":"他们来时已是黄昏。我们在数百位耀眼的客人中漫步，黛熙的喉咙不断弹奏出婉转动听的呢喃。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“These things excite me so,” she whispered. “If you want to kiss me any time during the evening, Nick, just let me know and I’ll be glad to arrange it for you. Just mention my name. Or present a green card. I’m giving out green—”","sentences":[{"en":"“These things excite me so,” she whispered.","zh":"“这种场合让我很兴奋，”她低声说，“如果你今晚想要亲我，尼克，请随时跟我说，我会很乐意替你安排的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“If you want to kiss me any time during the evening, Nick, just let me know and I’ll be glad to arrange it for you.","zh":"“这种场合让我很兴奋，”她低声说，“如果你今晚想要亲我，尼克，请随时跟我说，我会很乐意替你安排的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Just mention my name.","zh":"你只要喊我的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Or present a green card.","zh":"或者出示一张绿卡片。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m giving out green—”","zh":"我正在散发绿…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look around,” suggested Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"“Look around,” suggested Gatsby.","zh":"“请四处看看，”盖茨比提议说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m looking around. I’m having a marvellous—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m looking around.","zh":"“我一直在看呀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m having a marvellous—”","zh":"我觉得真是太…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You must see the faces of many people you’ve heard about.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You must see the faces of many people you’ve heard about.”","zh":"“你肯定看到许多闻名已久的人物。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom’s arrogant eyes roamed the crowd.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom’s arrogant eyes roamed the crowd.","zh":"汤姆傲慢的眼睛扫视着人群。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We don’t go around very much,” he said; “in fact, I was just thinking I don’t know a soul here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We don’t go around very much,” he said; “in fact, I was just thinking I don’t know a soul here.”","zh":"“我们很少出来玩，”他说，“其实我刚才还觉得这里一个认识的人都没有。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Perhaps you know that lady.” Gatsby indicated a gorgeous, scarcely human orchid of a woman who sat in state under a white-plum tree. Tom and Daisy stared, with that peculiarly unreal feeling that accompanies the recognition of a hitherto ghostly celebrity of the movies.","sentences":[{"en":"“Perhaps you know that lady.”","zh":"“也许你认识那位女士。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby indicated a gorgeous, scarcely human orchid of a woman who sat in state under a white-plum tree.","zh":"盖茨比指着一个明艳照人、美若兰花的女人，她雍容地坐在一株白梅树下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom and Daisy stared, with that peculiarly unreal feeling that accompanies the recognition of a hitherto ghostly celebrity of the movies.","zh":"汤姆和黛熙望过去，认出那是某个向来只在大银幕上见到的电影明星，简直不敢相信这是真的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s lovely,” said Daisy.","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s lovely,” said Daisy.","zh":"“她好美啊，”黛熙说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The man bending over her is her director.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The man bending over her is her director.”","zh":"“在她面前弯着腰那人是她的导演。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He took them ceremoniously from group to group:","sentences":[{"en":"He took them ceremoniously from group to group:","zh":"他郑重其事地带他们认识一群又一群的宾客。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Mrs. Buchanan… and Mr. Buchanan—” After an instant’s hesitation he added: “the polo player.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Mrs. Buchanan… and Mr. Buchanan—” After an instant’s hesitation he added: “the polo player.”","zh":"“这位是布坎南太太…这位是布坎南先生…”略微犹豫之后，他立即补充说，“马球高手。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh no,” objected Tom quickly, “not me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh no,” objected Tom quickly, “not me.”","zh":"“谬赞啦，”汤姆赶紧谦让，“我算不上。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But evidently the sound of it pleased Gatsby for Tom remained “the polo player” for the rest of the evening.","sentences":[{"en":"But evidently the sound of it pleased Gatsby for Tom remained “the polo player” for the rest of the evening.","zh":"但盖茨比显然很喜欢这个称号，因为那天晚上他逢人便说汤姆是“马球高手”。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve never met so many celebrities,” Daisy exclaimed. “I liked that man—what was his name?—with the sort of blue nose.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve never met so many celebrities,” Daisy exclaimed.","zh":"“我从来没见到过这么多名人，”黛熙惊喜地说，“我喜欢那个人，他叫什么名字？鼻子有点发青那个。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I liked that man—what was his name?—with the sort of blue nose.”","zh":"“我从来没见到过这么多名人，”黛熙惊喜地说，“我喜欢那个人，他叫什么名字？鼻子有点发青那个。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby identified him, adding that he was a small producer.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby identified him, adding that he was a small producer.","zh":"盖茨比说出那人的名字，又说他只是个小制片人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I liked him anyhow.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I liked him anyhow.”","zh":"“嗯，反正我喜欢他。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’d a little rather not be the polo player,” said Tom pleasantly, “I’d rather look at all these famous people in—in oblivion.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’d a little rather not be the polo player,” said Tom pleasantly, “I’d rather look at all these famous people in—in oblivion.”","zh":"“我宁愿自己不是马球高手，”汤姆高兴地说，“我宁愿当一个景仰这些著名人物的…无名小卒。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy and Gatsby danced. I remember being surprised by his graceful, conservative foxtrot—I had never seen him dance before. Then they sauntered over to my house and sat on the steps for half an hour, while at her request I remained watchfully in the garden. “In case there’s a fire or a flood,” she explained, “or any act of God.”","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy and Gatsby danced.","zh":"黛熙和盖茨比跳舞了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I remember being surprised by his graceful, conservative foxtrot—I had never seen him dance before.","zh":"我记得当时很吃惊，因为他的狐步舞跳得既优雅又合拍——而在此之前我从未见他跳过舞。然后他们漫步到我家，在台阶上坐了半个小时，而我则应黛熙的要求，在花园里望风。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then they sauntered over to my house and sat on the steps for half an hour, while at her request I remained watchfully in the garden.","zh":"我记得当时很吃惊，因为他的狐步舞跳得既优雅又合拍——而在此之前我从未见他跳过舞。然后他们漫步到我家，在台阶上坐了半个小时，而我则应黛熙的要求，在花园里望风。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“In case there’s a fire or a flood,” she explained, “or any act of God.”","zh":"“以防走火或者发洪水，”她解释说，“或者有什么天灾。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom appeared from his oblivion as we were sitting down to supper together. “Do you mind if I eat with some people over here?” he said. “A fellow’s getting off some funny stuff.”","sentences":[{"en":"Tom appeared from his oblivion as we were sitting down to supper together.","zh":"我们一起坐下来吃晚餐时，汤姆这位无名小卒出现了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you mind if I eat with some people over here?” he said.","zh":"“你介意我去陪那些人吃饭吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“A fellow’s getting off some funny stuff.”","zh":"他说，“那边有个家伙说话很风趣。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Go ahead,” answered Daisy genially, “and if you want to take down any addresses here’s my little gold pencil.”… She looked around after a moment and told me the girl was “common but pretty,” and I knew that except for the half-hour she’d been alone with Gatsby she wasn’t having a good time.","sentences":[{"en":"“Go ahead,” answered Daisy genially, “and if you want to take down any addresses here’s my little gold pencil.”…","zh":"“去呀，”黛熙善解人意地说，“把我这支小金笔拿去，你想记下地址的时候可以用。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked around after a moment and told me the girl was “common but pretty,” and I knew that except for the half-hour she’d been alone with Gatsby she wasn’t having a good time.","zh":"过了片刻，她望望四周，告诉我那个女孩“粗俗但很漂亮”，我知道除了和盖茨比独处那半个小时，她其实过得并不快乐。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We were at a particularly tipsy table. That was my fault—Gatsby had been called to the phone, and I’d enjoyed these same people only two weeks before. But what had amused me then turned septic on the air now.","sentences":[{"en":"We were at a particularly tipsy table.","zh":"我们这桌人喝得特别醉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That was my fault—Gatsby had been called to the phone, and I’d enjoyed these same people only two weeks before.","zh":"这都怪我——盖茨比被叫去听电话，而两个星期前刚认识那些人的时候，我觉得他们还挺有趣的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But what had amused me then turned septic on the air now.","zh":"但原本让我感兴趣的东西这时已经变得索然无味。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How do you feel, Miss Baedeker?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How do you feel, Miss Baedeker?”","zh":"“你还好吧，贝德克小姐？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The girl addressed was trying, unsuccessfully, to slump against my shoulder. At this inquiry she sat up and opened her eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"The girl addressed was trying, unsuccessfully, to slump against my shoulder.","zh":"我问候的那女孩正要向我的肩膀靠过来，但还没靠到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At this inquiry she sat up and opened her eyes.","zh":"听到这句话，她立刻坐直了，睁开了眼睛。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wha’?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wha’?”","zh":"“什么啊？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A massive and lethargic woman, who had been urging Daisy to play golf with her at the local club tomorrow, spoke in Miss Baedeker’s defence:","sentences":[{"en":"A massive and lethargic woman, who had been urging Daisy to play golf with her at the local club tomorrow, spoke in Miss Baedeker’s defence:","zh":"有个昏昏欲睡的大块头女人刚才一直在敦促黛熙明天陪她到本地的俱乐部打高尔夫球，这时她替贝德克小姐打圆场说：“哎呀，她没事的啦。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, she’s all right now. When she’s had five or six cocktails she always starts screaming like that. I tell her she ought to leave it alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, she’s all right now.","zh":"有个昏昏欲睡的大块头女人刚才一直在敦促黛熙明天陪她到本地的俱乐部打高尔夫球，这时她替贝德克小姐打圆场说：“哎呀，她没事的啦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When she’s had five or six cocktails she always starts screaming like that.","zh":"她要是喝上五六杯鸡尾酒，就会像这样大喊大叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I tell her she ought to leave it alone.”","zh":"我早就跟她说过不能多喝酒的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I do leave it alone,” affirmed the accused hollowly.","sentences":[{"en":"“I do leave it alone,” affirmed the accused hollowly.","zh":"“我确实没多喝呀，”受指责的那位茫然地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We heard you yelling, so I said to Doc Civet here: ‘There’s somebody that needs your help, Doc.’ ”","sentences":[{"en":"“We heard you yelling, so I said to Doc Civet here: ‘There’s somebody that needs your help, Doc.’ ”","zh":"“那次我们听见你在大叫，所以我对这里的西维特医生说：‘有个人需要你的帮助，医生。’”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s much obliged, I’m sure,” said another friend, without gratitude, “but you got her dress all wet when you stuck her head in the pool.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s much obliged, I’m sure,” said another friend, without gratitude, “but you got her dress all wet when you stuck her head in the pool.”","zh":"“她很领你的情，这是肯定的，”另外一位朋友毫不感激地说，“可是当时你把她的头按到游泳池里，把她的裙子都弄湿了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Anything I hate is to get my head stuck in a pool,” mumbled Miss Baedeker. “They almost drowned me once over in New Jersey.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Anything I hate is to get my head stuck in a pool,” mumbled Miss Baedeker.","zh":"“我最讨厌的事情就是别人把我的头按到游泳池里，”贝德克小姐口齿不清地说，“有一次在新泽西他们差点把我淹死。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“They almost drowned me once over in New Jersey.”","zh":"“我最讨厌的事情就是别人把我的头按到游泳池里，”贝德克小姐口齿不清地说，“有一次在新泽西他们差点把我淹死。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Then you ought to leave it alone,” countered Doctor Civet.","sentences":[{"en":"“Then you ought to leave it alone,” countered Doctor Civet.","zh":"“那么你应该戒酒，”西维特医生反驳说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Speak for yourself!” cried Miss Baedeker violently. “Your hand shakes. I wouldn’t let you operate on me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Speak for yourself!” cried Miss Baedeker violently.","zh":"“说说你自己吧！”贝德克小姐激动地喊道，“你的手抖个不停。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Your hand shakes.","zh":"“说说你自己吧！”贝德克小姐激动地喊道，“你的手抖个不停。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I wouldn’t let you operate on me!”","zh":"我就算要做手术也不找你开刀！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was like that. Almost the last thing I remember was standing with Daisy and watching the moving-picture director and his Star. They were still under the white-plum tree and their faces were touching except for a pale, thin ray of moonlight between. It occurred to me that he had been very slowly bending toward her all evening to attain this proximity, and even while I watched I saw him stoop one ultimate degree and kiss at her cheek.","sentences":[{"en":"It was like that.","zh":"情形大概就是这样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Almost the last thing I remember was standing with Daisy and watching the moving-picture director and his Star.","zh":"我记得到最后我和黛熙站在一起看着那位电影导演和他的明星。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were still under the white-plum tree and their faces were touching except for a pale, thin ray of moonlight between.","zh":"他们仍在白梅树下，两张脸凑得很近，中间只隔着一道淡淡的月光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It occurred to me that he had been very slowly bending toward her all evening to attain this proximity, and even while I watched I saw him stoop one ultimate degree and kiss at her cheek.","zh":"我怀疑那导演整晚都在以非常缓慢的速度朝女明星弯下腰去，到现在终于靠得这么近了。然后我看见他弯下最后一度，亲上了她的脸颊。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I like her,” said Daisy, “I think she’s lovely.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I like her,” said Daisy, “I think she’s lovely.”","zh":"“我喜欢她，”黛熙说，“我觉得她很漂亮。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But the rest offended her—and inarguably because it wasn’t a gesture but an emotion. She was appalled by West Egg, this unprecedented “place” that Broadway had begotten upon a Long Island fishing village—appalled by its raw vigour that chafed under the old euphemisms and by the too obtrusive fate that herded its inhabitants along a shortcut from nothing to nothing. She saw something awful in the very simplicity she failed to understand.","sentences":[{"en":"But the rest offended her—and inarguably because it wasn’t a gesture but an emotion.","zh":"但别的一切都让她反感——她也说不出个所以然来，因为她的反感并不针对具体的东西，而是一种整体的感觉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was appalled by West Egg, this unprecedented “place” that Broadway had begotten upon a Long Island fishing village—appalled by its raw vigour that chafed under the old euphemisms and by the too obtrusive fate that herded its inhabitants along a shortcut from nothing to nothing.","zh":"她厌恶西卵，几个百老汇名流的光临就让这个长岛渔村硬生生地变成前所未有的“胜地”。她厌恶那种与老派社交礼仪龃龉不合的粗俗习气，厌恶西卵居民那种原本家徒四壁而后富可敌国的过于突兀的命运。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She saw something awful in the very simplicity she failed to understand.","zh":"她无法理解这种简单的现象，所以觉得实在是太可怕了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I sat on the front steps with them while they waited for their car. It was dark here in front; only the bright door sent ten square feet of light volleying out into the soft black morning. Sometimes a shadow moved against a dressing-room blind above, gave way to another shadow, an indefinite procession of shadows, who rouged and powdered in an invisible glass.","sentences":[{"en":"I sat on the front steps with them while they waited for their car.","zh":"我陪他们坐在前门的台阶上等车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was dark here in front; only the bright door sent ten square feet of light volleying out into the soft black morning.","zh":"这里很暗，只有明亮的前门发出十平方英尺的光线，击破了黎明前的幽黑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes a shadow moved against a dressing-room blind above, gave way to another shadow, an indefinite procession of shadows, who rouged and powdered in an invisible glass.","zh":"楼上更衣室的百叶窗上不时有人影闪过，这些络绎不绝的人影大概是在对着一面看不见的镜子涂脂抹粉吧。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who is this Gatsby anyhow?” demanded Tom suddenly. “Some big bootlegger?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who is this Gatsby anyhow?” demanded Tom suddenly.","zh":"“这个盖茨比到底是什么人？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Some big bootlegger?”","zh":"汤姆突然气势汹汹地问，“一个大私酒贩子？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where’d you hear that?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where’d you hear that?”","zh":"“你在哪里听来的？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I didn’t hear it. I imagined it. A lot of these newly rich people are just big bootleggers, you know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I didn’t hear it.","zh":"“这不是我听来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I imagined it.","zh":"是我想到的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A lot of these newly rich people are just big bootleggers, you know.”","zh":"许多这种暴发户其实都是大私酒贩子，你也知道的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Not Gatsby,” I said shortly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Not Gatsby,” I said shortly.","zh":"“盖茨比不是这种人，”我懒得多说。他沉默了片刻。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was silent for a moment. The pebbles of the drive crunched under his feet.","sentences":[{"en":"He was silent for a moment.","zh":"“盖茨比不是这种人，”我懒得多说。他沉默了片刻。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The pebbles of the drive crunched under his feet.","zh":"车道的碎石被他踩得吱嘎响。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, he certainly must have strained himself to get this menagerie together.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, he certainly must have strained himself to get this menagerie together.”","zh":"“他肯定花了很大力气才把这些九流三教的人请到一起。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A breeze stirred the grey haze of Daisy’s fur collar.","sentences":[{"en":"A breeze stirred the grey haze of Daisy’s fur collar.","zh":"微风吹得黛熙的灰皮领上的细毛像薄雾般轻轻晃动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“At least they are more interesting than the people we know,” she said with an effort.","sentences":[{"en":"“At least they are more interesting than the people we know,” she said with an effort.","zh":"“这些人至少比我们认识那些有趣多了，”她不自然地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You didn’t look so interested.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You didn’t look so interested.”","zh":"“刚才你好像不怎么高兴啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I was.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I was.”","zh":"“谁说的，我很高兴。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom laughed and turned to me.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom laughed and turned to me.","zh":"汤姆哈哈大笑，扭头看着我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you notice Daisy’s face when that girl asked her to put her under a cold shower?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you notice Daisy’s face when that girl asked her to put her under a cold shower?”","zh":"“你刚才注意到黛熙的脸色吗？就是那个喝醉的女孩请黛熙替她冲冷水澡那会儿。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy began to sing with the music in a husky, rhythmic whisper, bringing out a meaning in each word that it had never had before and would never have again. When the melody rose her voice broke up sweetly, following it, in a way contralto voices have, and each change tipped out a little of her warm human magic upon the air.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy began to sing with the music in a husky, rhythmic whisper, bringing out a meaning in each word that it had never had before and would never have again.","zh":"黛熙开始跟着音乐轻轻地歌唱，她的歌喉婉转而动听，把每个字都唱得具有一种以前从未有过、将来也不会再有的意义。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When the melody rose her voice broke up sweetly, following it, in a way contralto voices have, and each change tipped out a little of her warm human magic upon the air.","zh":"她曼妙的歌声随着曲调的高低而变化，其音色之纯美足以媲美女低音歌唱家，时而低回时而激昂地将她温馨的魅力挥洒给夜空。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Lots of people come who haven’t been invited,” she said suddenly. “That girl hadn’t been invited. They simply force their way in and he’s too polite to object.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Lots of people come who haven’t been invited,” she said suddenly.","zh":"“这里有许多人是不请自来的，”她突然说，“那女孩就没受到邀请。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“That girl hadn’t been invited.","zh":"“这里有许多人是不请自来的，”她突然说，“那女孩就没受到邀请。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They simply force their way in and he’s too polite to object.”","zh":"他们直接闯上门来，他又不好意思拒绝。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’d like to know who he is and what he does,” insisted Tom. “And I think I’ll make a point of finding out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’d like to know who he is and what he does,” insisted Tom.","zh":"“我想知道他是什么人，做什么事，”汤姆旧话重提，“我想我会搞清楚的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And I think I’ll make a point of finding out.”","zh":"“我想知道他是什么人，做什么事，”汤姆旧话重提，“我想我会搞清楚的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I can tell you right now,” she answered. “He owned some drugstores, a lot of drugstores. He built them up himself.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I can tell you right now,” she answered.","zh":"“我现在就可以告诉你，”她回答说，“他是开药房的，有很多家大药房。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He owned some drugstores, a lot of drugstores.","zh":"“我现在就可以告诉你，”她回答说，“他是开药房的，有很多家大药房。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He built them up himself.”","zh":"那些都是他亲手创办的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The dilatory limousine came rolling up the drive.","sentences":[{"en":"The dilatory limousine came rolling up the drive.","zh":"那辆姗姗来迟的豪华轿车缓缓地驶过来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Good night, Nick,” said Daisy.","sentences":[{"en":"“Good night, Nick,” said Daisy.","zh":"“晚安，尼克，”黛熙说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her glance left me and sought the lighted top of the steps, where “Three O’Clock in the Morning,” a neat, sad little waltz of that year, was drifting out the open door. After all, in the very casualness of Gatsby’s party there were romantic possibilities totally absent from her world. What was it up there in the song that seemed to be calling her back inside? What would happen now in the dim, incalculable hours? Perhaps some unbelievable guest would arrive, a person infinitely rare and to be marvelled at, some authentically radiant young girl who with one fresh glance at Gatsby, one moment of magical encounter, would blot out those five years of unwavering devotion.","sentences":[{"en":"Her glance left me and sought the lighted top of the steps, where “Three O’Clock in the Morning,” a neat, sad little waltz of that year, was drifting out the open door.","zh":"她的目光离开我，直奔光线明亮的台阶上端而去，那年流行的伤感华尔兹舞曲《凌晨三点钟》正从前门飘扬而出。终归到底，盖茨比的宴会虽然不讲繁文缛节，却有着罗曼蒂克的可能性，而这在她的世界里是完全没有的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"After all, in the very casualness of Gatsby’s party there were romantic possibilities totally absent from her world.","zh":"她的目光离开我，直奔光线明亮的台阶上端而去，那年流行的伤感华尔兹舞曲《凌晨三点钟》正从前门飘扬而出。终归到底，盖茨比的宴会虽然不讲繁文缛节，却有着罗曼蒂克的可能性，而这在她的世界里是完全没有的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"What was it up there in the song that seemed to be calling her back inside?","zh":"这首动听的乐曲不就引得她忍不住想要回到里面吗？在随后几个小时，那昏暗的大厅里会发生什么事情呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"What would happen now in the dim, incalculable hours?","zh":"这首动听的乐曲不就引得她忍不住想要回到里面吗？在随后几个小时，那昏暗的大厅里会发生什么事情呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Perhaps some unbelievable guest would arrive, a person infinitely rare and to be marvelled at, some authentically radiant young girl who with one fresh glance at Gatsby, one moment of magical encounter, would blot out those five years of unwavering devotion.","zh":"也许会有一位不可思议的宾客，一个倾城倾国的佳人，一个明艳动人的少女，向盖茨比投去倾慕的眼神，然后刹那间的神奇邂逅就会把五年的坚贞不渝一笔勾销。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I stayed late that night. Gatsby asked me to wait until he was free, and I lingered in the garden until the inevitable swimming party had run up, chilled and exalted, from the black beach, until the lights were extinguished in the guestrooms overhead. When he came down the steps at last the tanned skin was drawn unusually tight on his face, and his eyes were bright and tired.","sentences":[{"en":"I stayed late that night.","zh":"那晚我待了很久。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby asked me to wait until he was free, and I lingered in the garden until the inevitable swimming party had run up, chilled and exalted, from the black beach, until the lights were extinguished in the guestrooms overhead.","zh":"盖茨比让我等到他有空再聊几句，于是我在花园里流连，直到那些下海游泳的客人浑身哆嗦、嘻嘻哈哈地从黝黑的沙滩跑上来，直到楼上那些客房的灯光都熄灭了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he came down the steps at last the tanned skin was drawn unusually tight on his face, and his eyes were bright and tired.","zh":"然后他终于从台阶上走下来，他那晒得发黄的皮肤在脸上绷得异乎寻常的紧，眼睛还是很亮，但有点倦意。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She didn’t like it,” he said immediately.","sentences":[{"en":"“She didn’t like it,” he said immediately.","zh":"“她不喜欢这场宴会，”他迫不及待地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course she did.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course she did.”","zh":"“她当然喜欢啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She didn’t like it,” he insisted. “She didn’t have a good time.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She didn’t like it,” he insisted.","zh":"“她不喜欢的，”他固执地说，“她今晚玩得不是很高兴。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She didn’t have a good time.”","zh":"“她不喜欢的，”他固执地说，“她今晚玩得不是很高兴。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was silent, and I guessed at his unutterable depression.","sentences":[{"en":"He was silent, and I guessed at his unutterable depression.","zh":"他沉默了半晌，我猜他心里大概有什么说不出的苦恼。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I feel far away from her,” he said. “It’s hard to make her understand.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I feel far away from her,” he said.","zh":"“我感觉和她离得很远，”他说，“很难让她明白我的想法。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s hard to make her understand.”","zh":"“我感觉和她离得很远，”他说，“很难让她明白我的想法。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You mean about the dance?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You mean about the dance?”","zh":"“你是说跳舞的事情吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The dance?” He dismissed all the dances he had given with a snap of his fingers. “Old sport, the dance is unimportant.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The dance?”","zh":"“跳舞？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He dismissed all the dances he had given with a snap of his fingers.","zh":"他打个响指，把他开过的所有舞会都取消了，“老兄，跳舞并不重要。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Old sport, the dance is unimportant.”","zh":"他打个响指，把他开过的所有舞会都取消了，“老兄，跳舞并不重要。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He wanted nothing less of Daisy than that she should go to Tom and say: “I never loved you.” After she had obliterated four years with that sentence they could decide upon the more practical measures to be taken. One of them was that, after she was free, they were to go back to Louisville and be married from her house—just as if it were five years ago.","sentences":[{"en":"He wanted nothing less of Daisy than that she should go to Tom and say: “I never loved you.”","zh":"他对黛熙没别的要求，只希望她走到汤姆面前并说：“我从来没有爱过你。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After she had obliterated four years with that sentence they could decide upon the more practical measures to be taken.","zh":"在她用这句话抹杀过去四年之后，他们就能决定要采取哪些更为实际的步骤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One of them was that, after she was free, they were to go back to Louisville and be married from her house—just as if it were five years ago.","zh":"其中一个步骤是，等她恢复自由，他们将会重返路易斯维尔，在她家举办婚礼——仿佛一切回到了五年前。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And she doesn’t understand,” he said. “She used to be able to understand. We’d sit for hours—”","sentences":[{"en":"“And she doesn’t understand,” he said.","zh":"“她不理解，”他说，“她以前很善解人意的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“She used to be able to understand.","zh":"我们常常坐上几个小时…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We’d sit for hours—”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He broke off and began to walk up and down a desolate path of fruit rinds and discarded favours and crushed flowers.","sentences":[{"en":"He broke off and began to walk up and down a desolate path of fruit rinds and discarded favours and crushed flowers.","zh":"他说到这里就停了，开始凄凉地在满地果皮、客人收下又丢弃的礼物和被踩烂的花朵之间走来走去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I wouldn’t ask too much of her,” I ventured. “You can’t repeat the past.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wouldn’t ask too much of her,” I ventured.","zh":"“还是别要求她太多吧，”我斗胆提议，“人是无法回到从前的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You can’t repeat the past.”","zh":"“还是别要求她太多吧，”我斗胆提议，“人是无法回到从前的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Can’t repeat the past?” he cried incredulously. “Why of course you can!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Can’t repeat the past?” he cried incredulously.","zh":"“无法回到从前？”他不以为然地喊道，“当然是可以回去的！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Why of course you can!”","zh":"“无法回到从前？”他不以为然地喊道，“当然是可以回去的！”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He looked around him wildly, as if the past were lurking here in the shadow of his house, just out of reach of his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"He looked around him wildly, as if the past were lurking here in the shadow of his house, just out of reach of his hand.","zh":"他神经兮兮地东张西望，仿佛“从前”就躲在他的房子的阴影里，只要伸出手就能抓到。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m going to fix everything just the way it was before,” he said, nodding determinedly. “She’ll see.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m going to fix everything just the way it was before,” he said, nodding determinedly.","zh":"“我会把所有事情安排得像从前那样，”他坚决地点着头说，“她会明白的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She’ll see.”","zh":"“我会把所有事情安排得像从前那样，”他坚决地点着头说，“她会明白的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He talked a lot about the past, and I gathered that he wanted to recover something, some idea of himself perhaps, that had gone into loving Daisy. His life had been confused and disordered since then, but if he could once return to a certain starting place and go over it all slowly, he could find out what that thing was…","sentences":[{"en":"He talked a lot about the past, and I gathered that he wanted to recover something, some idea of himself perhaps, that had gone into loving Daisy.","zh":"他说了许多从前的事，我觉得他是想找回某种他和黛熙恋爱时丢失的东西，也许是他对自己的某些看法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His life had been confused and disordered since then, but if he could once return to a certain starting place and go over it all slowly, he could find out what that thing was…","zh":"他的生活在那以后变得混乱不堪，但如果他能回到某个起点，慢慢地重新再来，他就能找到丢失的到底是什么…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"… One autumn night, five years before, they had been walking down the street when the leaves were falling, and they came to a place where there were no trees and the sidewalk was white with moonlight. They stopped here and turned toward each other. Now it was a cool night with that mysterious excitement in it which comes at the two changes of the year. The quiet lights in the houses were humming out into the darkness and there was a stir and bustle among the stars. Out of the corner of his eye Gatsby saw that the blocks of the sidewalks really formed a ladder and mounted to a secret place above the trees—he could climb to it, if he climbed alone, and once there he could suck on the pap of life, gulp down the incomparable milk of wonder.","sentences":[{"en":"…","zh":"五年前的某个秋夜，他们在街上走啊走，落叶纷纷飘下，他们走到一个没有树的地方，人行道上洒满了皎洁的月光。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One autumn night, five years before, they had been walking down the street when the leaves were falling, and they came to a place where there were no trees and the sidewalk was white with moonlight.","zh":"五年前的某个秋夜，他们在街上走啊走，落叶纷纷飘下，他们走到一个没有树的地方，人行道上洒满了皎洁的月光。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They stopped here and turned toward each other.","zh":"他们在那里停下脚步，转身彼此对视。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now it was a cool night with that mysterious excitement in it which comes at the two changes of the year.","zh":"夜凉如水，空气中弥漫着每年夏秋之交特有的神秘而兴奋的气息。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The quiet lights in the houses were humming out into the darkness and there was a stir and bustle among the stars.","zh":"安静的灯光从几处屋宇中透射出来，打破了黑暗的夜色，天上的星星也不肯安宁，片刻不停地闪烁着。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Out of the corner of his eye Gatsby saw that the blocks of the sidewalks really formed a ladder and mounted to a secret place above the trees—he could climb to it, if he climbed alone, and once there he could suck on the pap of life, gulp down the incomparable milk of wonder.","zh":"借眼角的余光望去，盖茨比看见一段一段的人行道变成了梯子，直通到树梢上方某个秘密的地方——只要他独自往上爬，他就能爬上去；爬到顶部之后，他就能吮吸生活的乳头，大口大口地喝下那无与伦比的神奇奶汁。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His heart beat faster as Daisy’s white face came up to his own. He knew that when he kissed this girl, and forever wed his unutterable visions to her perishable breath, his mind would never romp again like the mind of God. So he waited, listening for a moment longer to the tuning-fork that had been struck upon a star. Then he kissed her. At his lips’ touch she blossomed for him like a flower and the incarnation was complete.","sentences":[{"en":"His heart beat faster as Daisy’s white face came up to his own.","zh":"眼看黛熙白皙的面庞向他的脸凑过来，他的心越跳越快。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He knew that when he kissed this girl, and forever wed his unutterable visions to her perishable breath, his mind would never romp again like the mind of God.","zh":"他深深地知道，只要他亲吻这个女孩，让他那些无法言喻的梦想和她容易消失的呼吸永远地结合起来，他的精神就再也不能像上帝那样自由自在、毫无羁绊了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So he waited, listening for a moment longer to the tuning-fork that had been struck upon a star.","zh":"所以他等待着，再次静静地倾听自己内心的声音。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he kissed her.","zh":"然后他亲吻了她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At his lips’ touch she blossomed for him like a flower and the incarnation was complete.","zh":"在他的嘴唇的触碰之下，黛熙像花朵般为他盛放，而他从此也就脱胎换骨，完全变成了另外一个人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Through all he said, even through his appalling sentimentality, I was reminded of something—an elusive rhythm, a fragment of lost words, that I had heard somewhere a long time ago. For a moment a phrase tried to take shape in my mouth and my lips parted like a dumb man’s, as though there was more struggling upon them than a wisp of startled air. But they made no sound, and what I had almost remembered was uncommunicable forever.","sentences":[{"en":"Through all he said, even through his appalling sentimentality, I was reminded of something—an elusive rhythm, a fragment of lost words, that I had heard somewhere a long time ago.","zh":"听完他说的这番话，听完他伤感的回忆，我似乎想起了什么——某段飘忽不定的乐曲，几句早已遗忘的歌词，也许是很久以前在某个地方听过的歌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a moment a phrase tried to take shape in my mouth and my lips parted like a dumb man’s, as though there was more struggling upon them than a wisp of startled air.","zh":"刹那间，有句话试图通过我的嘴跑出来，而我的双唇像哑巴那样张开，仿佛除了一丝受惊的空气，还有什么在它们之上挣扎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But they made no sound, and what I had almost remembered was uncommunicable forever.","zh":"但它们终于没有发出声音，而我几乎就要想起来的东西，也变得永远不可言传。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-7","n":7,"title":"Chapter VII","titleZh":"第七章","paragraphs":[{"en":"It was when curiosity about Gatsby was at its highest that the lights in his house failed to go on one Saturday night—and, as obscurely as it had begun, his career as Trimalchio was over. Only gradually did I become aware that the automobiles which turned expectantly into his drive stayed for just a minute and then drove sulkily away. Wondering if he were sick I went over to find out—an unfamiliar butler with a villainous face squinted at me suspiciously from the door.","sentences":[{"en":"It was when curiosity about Gatsby was at its highest that the lights in his house failed to go on one Saturday night—and, as obscurely as it had begun, his career as Trimalchio was over.","zh":"就在人们对盖茨比的好奇达到顶点期间，有个星期六晚上，他家的灯光竟然没有亮起——如同当初莫名其妙开始那样，他的特里马乔生涯莫名其妙结束了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Only gradually did I become aware that the automobiles which turned expectantly into his drive stayed for just a minute and then drove sulkily away.","zh":"起初我倒没注意，后来才发现那些轿车满怀希望地驶入他的车道，只待上不到一分钟，就大失所望地离开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wondering if he were sick I went over to find out—an unfamiliar butler with a villainous face squinted at me suspiciously from the door.","zh":"我怀疑他可能病了，于是走过去想要看个究竟——有个面目狰狞的陌生男佣打开门，狐疑地斜眼看着我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is Mr. Gatsby sick?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Is Mr. Gatsby sick?”","zh":"“盖茨比先生病了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nope.” After a pause he added “sir” in a dilatory, grudging way.","sentences":[{"en":"“Nope.”","zh":"“没有。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After a pause he added “sir” in a dilatory, grudging way.","zh":"过了片刻，他才勉为其难地补上“先生”两个字。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I hadn’t seen him around, and I was rather worried. Tell him Mr. Carraway came over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I hadn’t seen him around, and I was rather worried.","zh":"“我最近没看到他，所以有点担心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell him Mr. Carraway came over.”","zh":"请跟他说卡拉威先生来过。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who?” he demanded rudely.","sentences":[{"en":"“Who?” he demanded rudely.","zh":"“什么先生？”他相当无礼地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Carraway.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Carraway.”","zh":"“卡拉威。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Carraway. All right, I’ll tell him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Carraway.","zh":"“卡拉威。好的，我会跟他说的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"All right, I’ll tell him.”","zh":"“卡拉威。好的，我会跟他说的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Abruptly he slammed the door.","sentences":[{"en":"Abruptly he slammed the door.","zh":"他猛然砰地把门关上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"My Finn informed me that Gatsby had dismissed every servant in his house a week ago and replaced them with half a dozen others, who never went into West Egg village to be bribed by the tradesmen, but ordered moderate supplies over the telephone. The grocery boy reported that the kitchen looked like a pigsty, and the general opinion in the village was that the new people weren’t servants at all.","sentences":[{"en":"My Finn informed me that Gatsby had dismissed every servant in his house a week ago and replaced them with half a dozen others, who never went into West Egg village to be bribed by the tradesmen, but ordered moderate supplies over the telephone.","zh":"我的芬兰女佣告诉我，盖茨比上星期解雇了家里所有佣人，另外请了五六个来，这些人从不为了回扣到西卵村的商店买东西，而是通过电话订购数量不多的日常用品和食物。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The grocery boy reported that the kitchen looked like a pigsty, and the general opinion in the village was that the new people weren’t servants at all.","zh":"杂货店的小伙子说厨房脏得像猪圈，村民普遍认为这些新来的根本不是佣人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Next day Gatsby called me on the phone.","sentences":[{"en":"Next day Gatsby called me on the phone.","zh":"第二天盖茨比给我打电话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Going away?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Going away?”","zh":"“你要出远门啦？”我问。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"“你要出远门啦？”我问。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, old sport.”","zh":"“没有，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I hear you fired all your servants.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I hear you fired all your servants.”","zh":"“听说你解雇了所有的佣人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I wanted somebody who wouldn’t gossip. Daisy comes over quite often—in the afternoons.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wanted somebody who wouldn’t gossip.","zh":"“我需要不会说闲话的佣人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy comes over quite often—in the afternoons.”","zh":"黛熙最近经常来——都是在下午。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"So the whole caravansary had fallen in like a card house at the disapproval in her eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"So the whole caravansary had fallen in like a card house at the disapproval in her eyes.","zh":"原来这整座大酒店会像纸牌搭的房子那样倒掉，只是因为黛熙看不顺眼。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They’re some people Wolfshiem wanted to do something for. They’re all brothers and sisters. They used to run a small hotel.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They’re some people Wolfshiem wanted to do something for.","zh":"“他们是沃夫希姆的手下，正好要找事情做。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They’re all brothers and sisters.","zh":"他们都是兄弟姐妹，原来开过一家小旅馆。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"They used to run a small hotel.”","zh":"他们都是兄弟姐妹，原来开过一家小旅馆。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I see.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I see.”","zh":"“我明白了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was calling up at Daisy’s request—would I come to lunch at her house tomorrow? Miss Baker would be there. Half an hour later Daisy herself telephoned and seemed relieved to find that I was coming. Something was up. And yet I couldn’t believe that they would choose this occasion for a scene—especially for the rather harrowing scene that Gatsby had outlined in the garden.","sentences":[{"en":"He was calling up at Daisy’s request—would I come to lunch at her house tomorrow?","zh":"他打电话来是受黛熙之托——我明天能到她家吃午饭吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Miss Baker would be there.","zh":"贝克小姐也会去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Half an hour later Daisy herself telephoned and seemed relieved to find that I was coming.","zh":"半小时后，黛熙亲自打来电话，发现我愿意去，她似乎很欣慰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something was up.","zh":"可能会有事发生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And yet I couldn’t believe that they would choose this occasion for a scene—especially for the rather harrowing scene that Gatsby had outlined in the garden.","zh":"可是我不敢相信他们会选择这样的场合来摊牌——他们居然准备落实盖茨比那晚在花园里提出的计划，让黛熙和汤姆从此恩断义绝。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The next day was broiling, almost the last, certainly the warmest, of the summer. As my train emerged from the tunnel into sunlight, only the hot whistles of the National Biscuit Company broke the simmering hush at noon. The straw seats of the car hovered on the edge of combustion; the woman next to me perspired delicately for a while into her white shirtwaist, and then, as her newspaper dampened under her fingers, lapsed despairingly into deep heat with a desolate cry. Her pocketbook slapped to the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day was broiling, almost the last, certainly the warmest, of the summer.","zh":"隔日天气很热，虽然暑气将尽，但那天肯定是当年夏季最热的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As my train emerged from the tunnel into sunlight, only the hot whistles of the National Biscuit Company broke the simmering hush at noon.","zh":"当我乘坐的火车从隧道驶入阳光里，只有国民饼干公司火辣的哨声打破了正午炙热的静寂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The straw seats of the car hovered on the edge of combustion; the woman next to me perspired delicately for a while into her white shirtwaist, and then, as her newspaper dampened under her fingers, lapsed despairingly into deep heat with a desolate cry.","zh":"车厢里的稻草座席简直就要起火，坐在我身边的那个女人起初还矜持地任由汗水浸湿她的束腰衬衣，后来她的报纸也被顺着手指流下的汗水弄湿，这时她热得整个人都蔫下来了，发出绝望的哀叹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her pocketbook slapped to the floor.","zh":"她的钱包啪地一响掉在地上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, my!” she gasped.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, my!” she gasped.","zh":"“哎呀！”她惊呼。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I picked it up with a weary bend and handed it back to her, holding it at arm’s length and by the extreme tip of the corners to indicate that I had no designs upon it—but everyone near by, including the woman, suspected me just the same.","sentences":[{"en":"I picked it up with a weary bend and handed it back to her, holding it at arm’s length and by the extreme tip of the corners to indicate that I had no designs upon it—but everyone near by, including the woman, suspected me just the same.","zh":"我吃力地弯下腰，把它捡起来，递还给她。我拈着钱包的一角，把手伸得长长的，表示我对它并无非分之想——但周围的每个乘客，包括那位女士，还是怀疑我想将其据为己有。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hot!” said the conductor to familiar faces. “Some weather!… Hot!… Hot!… Hot!… Is it hot enough for you? Is it hot? Is it… ?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hot!” said the conductor to familiar faces.","zh":"“好热啊！”售票员对那些熟悉的面孔说，“这鬼天气…","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Some weather!…","zh":"“好热啊！”售票员对那些熟悉的面孔说，“这鬼天气…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hot!…","zh":"“好热啊！”售票员对那些熟悉的面孔说，“这鬼天气…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hot!…","zh":"好热！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hot!…","zh":"好热！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it hot enough for you?","zh":"好热啊！你们觉得热吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it hot?","zh":"热不热呀？热…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it… ?”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"My commutation ticket came back to me with a dark stain from his hand. That anyone should care in this heat whose flushed lips he kissed, whose head made damp the pyjama pocket over his heart!","sentences":[{"en":"My commutation ticket came back to me with a dark stain from his hand.","zh":"我的车票回到我手上时，已经多出他的手留下的黑印。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That anyone should care in this heat whose flushed lips he kissed, whose head made damp the pyjama pocket over his heart!","zh":"天气这么热，怎么还会有人关心他亲吻过谁的红唇，谁的眼泪流湿了他胸前的睡衣口袋呢！","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"… Through the hall of the Buchanans’ house blew a faint wind, carrying the sound of the telephone bell out to Gatsby and me as we waited at the door.","sentences":[{"en":"…","zh":"盖茨比和我站在布坎南家门口等待着，这时门厅里吹出微弱的风，带来一阵电话的铃声。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Through the hall of the Buchanans’ house blew a faint wind, carrying the sound of the telephone bell out to Gatsby and me as we waited at the door.","zh":"盖茨比和我站在布坎南家门口等待着，这时门厅里吹出微弱的风，带来一阵电话的铃声。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The master’s body?” roared the butler into the mouthpiece. “I’m sorry, madame, but we can’t furnish it—it’s far too hot to touch this noon!”","sentences":[{"en":"“The master’s body?” roared the butler into the mouthpiece.","zh":"“我家主人的尸体？”管家对着话筒大声说，“对不起，太太，我们交不出来…今天中午太热了，碰都没法碰！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m sorry, madame, but we can’t furnish it—it’s far too hot to touch this noon!”","zh":"“我家主人的尸体？”管家对着话筒大声说，“对不起，太太，我们交不出来…今天中午太热了，碰都没法碰！”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"What he really said was: “Yes… Yes… I’ll see.”","sentences":[{"en":"What he really said was: “Yes…","zh":"其实他说的是：“是的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes…","zh":"是的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll see.”","zh":"我看看。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He set down the receiver and came toward us, glistening slightly, to take our stiff straw hats.","sentences":[{"en":"He set down the receiver and came toward us, glistening slightly, to take our stiff straw hats.","zh":"他放下听筒，向我们走过来，看上去有点冒汗，伸手接过我们的硬草帽。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Madame expects you in the salon!” he cried, needlessly indicating the direction. In this heat every extra gesture was an affront to the common store of life.","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame expects you in the salon!” he cried, needlessly indicating the direction.","zh":"“夫人在客厅恭候两位！”他响亮地说，毫无必要地指出了方向。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In this heat every extra gesture was an affront to the common store of life.","zh":"在这么热的天，每个多余的动作都是对生命能量的浪费。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The room, shadowed well with awnings, was dark and cool. Daisy and Jordan lay upon an enormous couch, like silver idols weighing down their own white dresses against the singing breeze of the fans.","sentences":[{"en":"The room, shadowed well with awnings, was dark and cool.","zh":"由于窗户外面都装了遮阳篷，客厅里很阴凉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy and Jordan lay upon an enormous couch, like silver idols weighing down their own white dresses against the singing breeze of the fans.","zh":"黛熙和乔丹躺在巨大的沙发上，好像两身银像，各自压住自己的白色长裙，以免被嘶嘶响的电风扇吹动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We can’t move,” they said together.","sentences":[{"en":"“We can’t move,” they said together.","zh":"“恕我们不能站起来招呼你们啦，”她们异口同声地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Jordan’s fingers, powdered white over their tan, rested for a moment in mine.","sentences":[{"en":"Jordan’s fingers, powdered white over their tan, rested for a moment in mine.","zh":"乔丹涂了白粉的棕色手指在我手心搁了片刻。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And Mr. Thomas Buchanan, the athlete?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“And Mr. Thomas Buchanan, the athlete?”","zh":"“马球高手托马斯·布坎南先生呢？”我问。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"“马球高手托马斯·布坎南先生呢？”我问。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Simultaneously I heard his voice, gruff, muffled, husky, at the hall telephone.","sentences":[{"en":"Simultaneously I heard his voice, gruff, muffled, husky, at the hall telephone.","zh":"话音刚落，我就听到他的声音，粗着嗓子低声地在门厅里接电话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby stood in the centre of the crimson carpet and gazed around with fascinated eyes. Daisy watched him and laughed, her sweet, exciting laugh; a tiny gust of powder rose from her bosom into the air.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby stood in the centre of the crimson carpet and gazed around with fascinated eyes.","zh":"盖茨比站在绯红色的地毯中央，好奇地四处看看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy watched him and laughed, her sweet, exciting laugh; a tiny gust of powder rose from her bosom into the air.","zh":"黛熙望着他，发出甜腻而兴奋的笑声，有些细小的粉末从她胸口冉冉升起。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The rumour is,” whispered Jordan, “that that’s Tom’s girl on the telephone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The rumour is,” whispered Jordan, “that that’s Tom’s girl on the telephone.”","zh":"“有人造谣说，”乔丹压低声音说，“打电话来的是汤姆的相好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We were silent. The voice in the hall rose high with annoyance: “Very well, then, I won’t sell you the car at all… I’m under no obligations to you at all… and as for your bothering me about it at lunch time, I won’t stand that at all!”","sentences":[{"en":"We were silent.","zh":"我们默不作声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The voice in the hall rose high with annoyance: “Very well, then, I won’t sell you the car at all…","zh":"门厅里的声音变得愤激起来：“非常好，我根本就不想把车卖给你…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m under no obligations to you at all… and as for your bothering me about it at lunch time, I won’t stand that at all!”","zh":"我又不欠你什么东西…下次别在午餐时间来骚扰我，否则我对你不客气！”“他挂上话筒说给我们听的，”黛熙嗤之以鼻地说。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Holding down the receiver,” said Daisy cynically.","sentences":[{"en":"“Holding down the receiver,” said Daisy cynically.","zh":"我又不欠你什么东西…下次别在午餐时间来骚扰我，否则我对你不客气！”“他挂上话筒说给我们听的，”黛熙嗤之以鼻地说。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, he’s not,” I assured her. “It’s a bona-fide deal. I happen to know about it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, he’s not,” I assured her.","zh":"“不是啦，”我安慰她说，“这门生意如假包换。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s a bona-fide deal.","zh":"“不是啦，”我安慰她说，“这门生意如假包换。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I happen to know about it.”","zh":"我正好有所了解。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom flung open the door, blocked out its space for a moment with his thick body, and hurried into the room.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom flung open the door, blocked out its space for a moment with his thick body, and hurried into the room.","zh":"汤姆猛地推开房门，庞大的身躯霎时把门口堵住，然后阔步走进客厅。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Mr. Gatsby!” He put out his broad, flat hand with well-concealed dislike. “I’m glad to see you, sir… Nick…”","sentences":[{"en":"“Mr. Gatsby!”","zh":"“盖茨比先生！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He put out his broad, flat hand with well-concealed dislike.","zh":"他很好地掩饰了他的憎恶，伸出他那扁平的大手，“很高兴见到你，先生…尼克…","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m glad to see you, sir…","zh":"他很好地掩饰了他的憎恶，伸出他那扁平的大手，“很高兴见到你，先生…尼克…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Nick…”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Make us a cold drink,” cried Daisy.","sentences":[{"en":"“Make us a cold drink,” cried Daisy.","zh":"“给我们弄点冷饮来啊，”黛熙大声地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As he left the room again she got up and went over to Gatsby and pulled his face down, kissing him on the mouth.","sentences":[{"en":"As he left the room again she got up and went over to Gatsby and pulled his face down, kissing him on the mouth.","zh":"看到汤姆又走出客厅，她赶紧站起来，走到盖茨比身边，捧着他的脸往下拉，向他的嘴亲过去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You know I love you,” she murmured.","sentences":[{"en":"“You know I love you,” she murmured.","zh":"“我爱你，你知道的，”她喃喃地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You forget there’s a lady present,” said Jordan.","sentences":[{"en":"“You forget there’s a lady present,” said Jordan.","zh":"“别忘了有女客在场，”乔丹说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy looked around doubtfully.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy looked around doubtfully.","zh":"黛熙转过头来，满是不解的神色。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You kiss Nick too.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You kiss Nick too.”","zh":"“你也可以亲亲尼克呀。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What a low, vulgar girl!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What a low, vulgar girl!”","zh":"“这女人多么低俗！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t care!” cried Daisy, and began to clog on the brick fireplace. Then she remembered the heat and sat down guiltily on the couch just as a freshly laundered nurse leading a little girl came into the room.","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t care!” cried Daisy, and began to clog on the brick fireplace.","zh":"“我不管！”黛熙昂然自若地说，随即在砖砌的壁炉前跳起舞来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she remembered the heat and sat down guiltily on the couch just as a freshly laundered nurse leading a little girl came into the room.","zh":"然后她想起来天太热，又羞赧地坐到沙发上，这时有个穿着整洁的保姆领着一个小女孩走进客厅。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Bles-sed pre-cious,” she crooned, holding out her arms. “Come to your own mother that loves you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bles-sed pre-cious,” she crooned, holding out her arms.","zh":"“乖——宝贝，”她哄着说，同时伸出了双手，“来妈妈这里，妈妈最爱你啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Come to your own mother that loves you.”","zh":"“乖——宝贝，”她哄着说，同时伸出了双手，“来妈妈这里，妈妈最爱你啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The child, relinquished by the nurse, rushed across the room and rooted shyly into her mother’s dress.","sentences":[{"en":"The child, relinquished by the nurse, rushed across the room and rooted shyly into her mother’s dress.","zh":"保姆把手松开，那孩子从客厅门口冲过来，害羞地把头埋进她母亲的裙子里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The bles-sed pre-cious! Did mother get powder on your old yellowy hair? Stand up now, and say—How-de-do.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The bles-sed pre-cious!","zh":"“乖乖的宝贝啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did mother get powder on your old yellowy hair?","zh":"妈妈的粉有没有沾到你黄黄的头发呀？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Stand up now, and say—How-de-do.”","zh":"快站起来，跟客人说‘你好’。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby and I in turn leaned down and took the small reluctant hand. Afterward he kept looking at the child with surprise. I don’t think he had ever really believed in its existence before.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby and I in turn leaned down and took the small reluctant hand.","zh":"盖茨比和我轮流弯下腰，握住那只畏缩的小手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Afterward he kept looking at the child with surprise.","zh":"然后他一直惊奇地盯着那孩子看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t think he had ever really believed in its existence before.","zh":"我想他以前并不相信这个孩子真的存在。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I got dressed before luncheon,” said the child, turning eagerly to Daisy.","sentences":[{"en":"“I got dressed before luncheon,” said the child, turning eagerly to Daisy.","zh":"“我还没吃午饭就穿上漂亮衣服了，”那孩子说，热切地转身给黛熙看。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s because your mother wanted to show you off.” Her face bent into the single wrinkle of the small white neck. “You dream, you. You absolute little dream.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s because your mother wanted to show you off.”","zh":"“那是因为你妈妈需要你来长脸呀，”她弯下腰去亲亲那女孩细细的白皙脖子，“你真美啊，你绝对是个小美人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her face bent into the single wrinkle of the small white neck.","zh":"“那是因为你妈妈需要你来长脸呀，”她弯下腰去亲亲那女孩细细的白皙脖子，“你真美啊，你绝对是个小美人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You dream, you.","zh":"“那是因为你妈妈需要你来长脸呀，”她弯下腰去亲亲那女孩细细的白皙脖子，“你真美啊，你绝对是个小美人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You absolute little dream.”","zh":"“那是因为你妈妈需要你来长脸呀，”她弯下腰去亲亲那女孩细细的白皙脖子，“你真美啊，你绝对是个小美人。”","scope":"block"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes,” admitted the child calmly. “Aunt Jordan’s got on a white dress too.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” admitted the child calmly.","zh":"“是的，”那孩子镇定地承认，“乔丹阿姨也穿着白裙子。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Aunt Jordan’s got on a white dress too.”","zh":"“是的，”那孩子镇定地承认，“乔丹阿姨也穿着白裙子。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How do you like mother’s friends?” Daisy turned her around so that she faced Gatsby. “Do you think they’re pretty?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How do you like mother’s friends?”","zh":"“你喜欢妈妈的朋友吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy turned her around so that she faced Gatsby.","zh":"黛熙把她转过来，让她面对着盖茨比，“你觉得他们漂亮吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Do you think they’re pretty?”","zh":"黛熙把她转过来，让她面对着盖茨比，“你觉得他们漂亮吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where’s Daddy?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where’s Daddy?”","zh":"“爸爸在哪里？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She doesn’t look like her father,” explained Daisy. “She looks like me. She’s got my hair and shape of the face.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She doesn’t look like her father,” explained Daisy.","zh":"“她长得不像她父亲，”黛熙解释说，“她长得像我。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She looks like me.","zh":"“她长得不像她父亲，”黛熙解释说，“她长得像我。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She’s got my hair and shape of the face.”","zh":"她的头发和脸型都像我。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy sat back upon the couch. The nurse took a step forward and held out her hand.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy sat back upon the couch.","zh":"黛熙又往后靠到沙发上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The nurse took a step forward and held out her hand.","zh":"保姆向前踏上一步，伸出她的手。“来吧，小帕。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come, Pammy.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, Pammy.”","zh":"“再见，乖女儿。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Goodbye, sweetheart!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Goodbye, sweetheart!”","zh":"“再见，乖女儿。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"With a reluctant backward glance the well-disciplined child held to her nurse’s hand and was pulled out the door, just as Tom came back, preceding four gin rickeys that clicked full of ice.","sentences":[{"en":"With a reluctant backward glance the well-disciplined child held to her nurse’s hand and was pulled out the door, just as Tom came back, preceding four gin rickeys that clicked full of ice.","zh":"那个很有家教的女孩被保姆拉着，恋恋不舍地回头望，被拉出了客厅。这时汤姆正好回来，端着四杯装满冰块的金酒。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby took up his drink.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby took up his drink.","zh":"盖茨比拿起他的酒杯。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They certainly look cool,” he said, with visible tension.","sentences":[{"en":"“They certainly look cool,” he said, with visible tension.","zh":"“看上去蛮冰凉的，”他说，显得很紧张。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We drank in long, greedy swallows.","sentences":[{"en":"We drank in long, greedy swallows.","zh":"我们慢慢地、贪婪地喝着酒。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I read somewhere that the sun’s getting hotter every year,” said Tom genially. “It seems that pretty soon the earth’s going to fall into the sun—or wait a minute—it’s just the opposite—the sun’s getting colder every year.","sentences":[{"en":"“I read somewhere that the sun’s getting hotter every year,” said Tom genially.","zh":"“我在什么地方看到有人写文章说，太阳一年年变得越来越热，”汤姆友善地说，“好像过不了多久，地球就会掉进太阳里——哦，不对，我说错了。恰好相反，太阳是一年年变得越来越冷。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It seems that pretty soon the earth’s going to fall into the sun—or wait a minute—it’s just the opposite—the sun’s getting colder every year.","zh":"“我在什么地方看到有人写文章说，太阳一年年变得越来越热，”汤姆友善地说，“好像过不了多久，地球就会掉进太阳里——哦，不对，我说错了。恰好相反，太阳是一年年变得越来越冷。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come outside,” he suggested to Gatsby, “I’d like you to have a look at the place.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come outside,” he suggested to Gatsby, “I’d like you to have a look at the place.”","zh":"“到外面去吧，”他动员盖茨比说，“我想让你看看这个地方。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I went with them out to the veranda. On the green Sound, stagnant in the heat, one small sail crawled slowly toward the fresher sea. Gatsby’s eyes followed it momentarily; he raised his hand and pointed across the bay.","sentences":[{"en":"I went with them out to the veranda.","zh":"我随他们走到外面的阳台。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the green Sound, stagnant in the heat, one small sail crawled slowly toward the fresher sea.","zh":"碧绿的海湾在闷热的空气中波澜不兴，但见一艘小小的帆船慢慢地向远海爬去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby’s eyes followed it momentarily; he raised his hand and pointed across the bay.","zh":"盖茨比目送它航行了片刻，然后举起手，指着海湾彼岸。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m right across from you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m right across from you.”","zh":"“我就住在你家正对面。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“So you are.”","sentences":[{"en":"“So you are.”","zh":"“是啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Our eyes lifted over the rose-beds and the hot lawn and the weedy refuse of the dog-days alongshore. Slowly the white wings of the boat moved against the blue cool limit of the sky. Ahead lay the scalloped ocean and the abounding blessed isles.","sentences":[{"en":"Our eyes lifted over the rose-beds and the hot lawn and the weedy refuse of the dog-days alongshore.","zh":"我们的眼睛越过玫瑰花丛、炎热的草坪和海边无精打采的杂草。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Slowly the white wings of the boat moved against the blue cool limit of the sky.","zh":"那艘小船的白翅膀在湛蓝的天空下缓缓移动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ahead lay the scalloped ocean and the abounding blessed isles.","zh":"前方是扇贝般的海面和许多美丽的小岛。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There’s sport for you,” said Tom, nodding. “I’d like to be out there with him for about an hour.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There’s sport for you,” said Tom, nodding.","zh":"“这是多好的运动啊，”汤姆点着头说，“我真想去跟他玩上个把小时。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’d like to be out there with him for about an hour.”","zh":"“这是多好的运动啊，”汤姆点着头说，“我真想去跟他玩上个把小时。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We had luncheon in the dining-room, darkened too against the heat, and drank down nervous gaiety with the cold ale.","sentences":[{"en":"We had luncheon in the dining-room, darkened too against the heat, and drank down nervous gaiety with the cold ale.","zh":"午饭是在餐厅吃的，那里也很阴凉，大家强颜欢笑地喝着冰凉的麦芽酒。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’ll we do with ourselves this afternoon?” cried Daisy, “and the day after that, and the next thirty years?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’ll we do with ourselves this afternoon?” cried Daisy, “and the day after that, and the next thirty years?”","zh":"“今天下午大家做什么好呢？”黛熙大声说，“明天呢？今后三十年呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t be morbid,” Jordan said. “Life starts all over again when it gets crisp in the fall.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t be morbid,” Jordan said.","zh":"“别担心，”乔丹说，“等到秋高气爽，生活又会重新开始。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Life starts all over again when it gets crisp in the fall.”","zh":"“别担心，”乔丹说，“等到秋高气爽，生活又会重新开始。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But it’s so hot,” insisted Daisy, on the verge of tears, “and everything’s so confused. Let’s all go to town!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But it’s so hot,” insisted Daisy, on the verge of tears, “and everything’s so confused.","zh":"“但这天太热了，”黛熙固执地说，眼泪就要夺眶而出，“什么事都是乱七八糟的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let’s all go to town!”","zh":"我们到城里去吧！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her voice struggled on through the heat, beating against it, moulding its senselessness into forms.","sentences":[{"en":"Her voice struggled on through the heat, beating against it, moulding its senselessness into forms.","zh":"她的声音在闷热中挣扎，不停地拍打着它，把无影无踪的它变得有形有状。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve heard of making a garage out of a stable,” Tom was saying to Gatsby, “but I’m the first man who ever made a stable out of a garage.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve heard of making a garage out of a stable,” Tom was saying to Gatsby, “but I’m the first man who ever made a stable out of a garage.”","zh":"“我曾听说有人把马房改成车库，”汤姆对盖茨比说，“但把车库改成马房的，在下还是第一个。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who wants to go to town?” demanded Daisy insistently. Gatsby’s eyes floated toward her. “Ah,” she cried, “you look so cool.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who wants to go to town?” demanded Daisy insistently.","zh":"“谁要去城里？”黛熙毫不动摇地说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby’s eyes floated toward her.","zh":"盖茨比的眼光向她飘过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Ah,” she cried, “you look so cool.”","zh":"“哎呀，”她高兴地说，“你看上去真酷。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Their eyes met, and they stared together at each other, alone in space. With an effort she glanced down at the table.","sentences":[{"en":"Their eyes met, and they stared together at each other, alone in space.","zh":"他们的眼神相遇了，开始凝望着对方，旁若无人的样子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With an effort she glanced down at the table.","zh":"黛熙勉强把眼光降到餐桌上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You always look so cool,” she repeated.","sentences":[{"en":"“You always look so cool,” she repeated.","zh":"“你总是这么酷，”她又情不自禁地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She had told him that she loved him, and Tom Buchanan saw. He was astounded. His mouth opened a little, and he looked at Gatsby, and then back at Daisy as if he had just recognized her as someone he knew a long time ago.","sentences":[{"en":"She had told him that she loved him, and Tom Buchanan saw.","zh":"她刚才说过她爱盖茨比，现在汤姆·布坎南亲眼看到了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was astounded.","zh":"他惊呆了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His mouth opened a little, and he looked at Gatsby, and then back at Daisy as if he had just recognized her as someone he knew a long time ago.","zh":"他微微张开了嘴巴，看看盖茨比，又看看黛熙，仿佛刚刚认出黛熙就是他很久以前认识的某个人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You resemble the advertisement of the man,” she went on innocently. “You know the advertisement of the man—”","sentences":[{"en":"“You resemble the advertisement of the man,” she went on innocently.","zh":"“你很像广告里那个人，”她毫无察觉地接着说，“你知道的，广告里那个人…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You know the advertisement of the man—”","zh":"“你很像广告里那个人，”她毫无察觉地接着说，“你知道的，广告里那个人…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All right,” broke in Tom quickly, “I’m perfectly willing to go to town. Come on—we’re all going to town.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right,” broke in Tom quickly, “I’m perfectly willing to go to town.","zh":"“好啦，”汤姆赶紧插口说，“我完全同意去城里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come on—we’re all going to town.”","zh":"走吧——我们大家都去城里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He got up, his eyes still flashing between Gatsby and his wife. No one moved.","sentences":[{"en":"He got up, his eyes still flashing between Gatsby and his wife.","zh":"他站起来，眼睛仍在盖茨比和黛熙之间瞟来瞟去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No one moved.","zh":"没有人动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come on!” His temper cracked a little. “What’s the matter, anyhow? If we’re going to town, let’s start.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come on!”","zh":"“走啊！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His temper cracked a little.","zh":"他有点生气了，“到底怎么回事？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What’s the matter, anyhow?","zh":"他有点生气了，“到底怎么回事？","scope":"group"},{"en":"If we’re going to town, let’s start.”","zh":"如果想去城里，那就动身啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His hand, trembling with his effort at self-control, bore to his lips the last of his glass of ale. Daisy’s voice got us to our feet and out on to the blazing gravel drive.","sentences":[{"en":"His hand, trembling with his effort at self-control, bore to his lips the last of his glass of ale.","zh":"他强压心里的怒气，用有点发抖的手拿起杯子，把剩下的麦芽酒一饮而尽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy’s voice got us to our feet and out on to the blazing gravel drive.","zh":"黛熙开口让我们站起来，大家都走到外面热气腾腾的车道上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Are we just going to go?” she objected. “Like this? Aren’t we going to let anyone smoke a cigarette first?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Are we just going to go?” she objected.","zh":"“我们就这样走吗？”她反对说，“这样就走了啊？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Like this?","zh":"“我们就这样走吗？”她反对说，“这样就走了啊？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Aren’t we going to let anyone smoke a cigarette first?”","zh":"也不让人先抽根烟？”“午饭的时候每个人都抽了很多烟。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Everybody smoked all through lunch.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Everybody smoked all through lunch.”","zh":"也不让人先抽根烟？”“午饭的时候每个人都抽了很多烟。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, let’s have fun,” she begged him. “It’s too hot to fuss.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, let’s have fun,” she begged him.","zh":"“哎呀，你开心点好不好，”黛熙恳求他，“天气这么热，你就别发火了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s too hot to fuss.”","zh":"“哎呀，你开心点好不好，”黛熙恳求他，“天气这么热，你就别发火了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He didn’t answer.","sentences":[{"en":"He didn’t answer.","zh":"“哎呀，你开心点好不好，”黛熙恳求他，“天气这么热，你就别发火了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Have it your own way,” she said. “Come on, Jordan.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Have it your own way,” she said.","zh":"他没有回答。“随便你吧，”她说，“走吧，乔丹。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Come on, Jordan.”","zh":"他没有回答。“随便你吧，”她说，“走吧，乔丹。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They went upstairs to get ready while we three men stood there shuffling the hot pebbles with our feet. A silver curve of the moon hovered already in the western sky. Gatsby started to speak, changed his mind, but not before Tom wheeled and faced him expectantly.","sentences":[{"en":"They went upstairs to get ready while we three men stood there shuffling the hot pebbles with our feet.","zh":"她们到楼上去准备，我们三个大男人站在车道上，用脚把滚烫的石子拨来拨去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A silver curve of the moon hovered already in the western sky.","zh":"一弯银月已经悬挂在西天。盖茨比想要说话，又改变了主意，但这时汤姆已经转过身来，期待地看着他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Gatsby started to speak, changed his mind, but not before Tom wheeled and faced him expectantly.","zh":"一弯银月已经悬挂在西天。盖茨比想要说话，又改变了主意，但这时汤姆已经转过身来，期待地看着他。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Have you got your stables here?” asked Gatsby with an effort.","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you got your stables here?” asked Gatsby with an effort.","zh":"“你这个地方有马房吗？”盖茨比勉强地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“About a quarter of a mile down the road.”","sentences":[{"en":"“About a quarter of a mile down the road.”","zh":"“沿着这条路过去，走大概四分之一英里就到了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh.”","zh":"“哦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A pause.","sentences":[{"en":"A pause.","zh":"大家默默无言。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t see the idea of going to town,” broke out Tom savagely. “Women get these notions in their heads—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t see the idea of going to town,” broke out Tom savagely.","zh":"“真不知道为什么要到城里去，”汤姆毫无风度地说，“女人的头脑里总是有这些古怪的想法…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Women get these notions in their heads—”","zh":"“真不知道为什么要到城里去，”汤姆毫无风度地说，“女人的头脑里总是有这些古怪的想法…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Shall we take anything to drink?” called Daisy from an upper window.","sentences":[{"en":"“Shall we take anything to drink?” called Daisy from an upper window.","zh":"“我们应该带些喝的吧？”黛熙在楼上的窗户喊道。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll get some whisky,” answered Tom. He went inside.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll get some whisky,” answered Tom.","zh":"“我去弄点威士忌，”汤姆回答说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went inside.","zh":"他进了屋子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby turned to me rigidly:","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby turned to me rigidly:","zh":"盖茨比动作生硬地转向我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I can’t say anything in his house, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I can’t say anything in his house, old sport.”","zh":"“在他家里我什么话也不能说，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s got an indiscreet voice,” I remarked. “It’s full of—” I hesitated.","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s got an indiscreet voice,” I remarked.","zh":"“她这人说话不经头脑的，”我说，“她的声音充满了…”我欲言又止。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s full of—” I hesitated.","zh":"“她这人说话不经头脑的，”我说，“她的声音充满了…”我欲言又止。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Her voice is full of money,” he said suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Her voice is full of money,” he said suddenly.","zh":"“她的声音充满了金钱，”他突然说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That was it. I’d never understood before. It was full of money—that was the inexhaustible charm that rose and fell in it, the jingle of it, the cymbals’ song of it… High in a white palace the king’s daughter, the golden girl…","sentences":[{"en":"That was it.","zh":"正是如此。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’d never understood before.","zh":"我以前没想到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was full of money—that was the inexhaustible charm that rose and fell in it, the jingle of it, the cymbals’ song of it…","zh":"黛熙的声音确实充满了金钱——她那抑扬顿挫、银铃般叮当悦耳、铙钹般清脆动听的声音蕴含着的，正是这种无穷的魅力…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"High in a white palace the king’s daughter, the golden girl…","zh":"仿佛她是白色宫殿里高高在上的公主，是黄金铸就的女郎…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom came out of the house wrapping a quart bottle in a towel, followed by Daisy and Jordan wearing small tight hats of metallic cloth and carrying light capes over their arms.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom came out of the house wrapping a quart bottle in a towel, followed by Daisy and Jordan wearing small tight hats of metallic cloth and carrying light capes over their arms.","zh":"汤姆从屋子里走出来，手里抓住一个用毛巾包住的大瓶子，跟在他身后的是黛熙和乔丹，她们头上都戴着闪亮的小帽子，手臂上披着薄纱。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Shall we all go in my car?” suggested Gatsby. He felt the hot, green leather of the seat. “I ought to have left it in the shade.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Shall we all go in my car?” suggested Gatsby.","zh":"“大家都坐我的车去吧？”盖茨比提议说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He felt the hot, green leather of the seat.","zh":"他摸了摸滚烫的绿皮座椅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I ought to have left it in the shade.”","zh":"“我应该把它停在阴凉的地方。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is it standard shift?” demanded Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is it standard shift?” demanded Tom.","zh":"“你这辆车是手排挡吧？”汤姆问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“是的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, you take my coupé and let me drive your car to town.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you take my coupé and let me drive your car to town.”","zh":"“很好，你开我的跑车，让我开你的车到城里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The suggestion was distasteful to Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"The suggestion was distasteful to Gatsby.","zh":"这个提议让盖茨比很郁闷。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t think there’s much gas,” he objected.","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t think there’s much gas,” he objected.","zh":"“我怕汽油可能不够用，”他表示反对。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Plenty of gas,” said Tom boisterously. He looked at the gauge. “And if it runs out I can stop at a drugstore. You can buy anything at a drugstore nowadays.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Plenty of gas,” said Tom boisterously.","zh":"“汽油还有很多，”汤姆粗声说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked at the gauge.","zh":"他看了看油表。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“And if it runs out I can stop at a drugstore.","zh":"“就算用光了，就找个药店呗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You can buy anything at a drugstore nowadays.”","zh":"现在药店里什么都有卖。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A pause followed this apparently pointless remark. Daisy looked at Tom frowning, and an indefinable expression, at once definitely unfamiliar and vaguely recognizable, as if I had only heard it described in words, passed over Gatsby’s face.","sentences":[{"en":"A pause followed this apparently pointless remark.","zh":"听完这句显然毫无意义的话，大家默不作声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy looked at Tom frowning, and an indefinable expression, at once definitely unfamiliar and vaguely recognizable, as if I had only heard it described in words, passed over Gatsby’s face.","zh":"黛熙皱眉看着汤姆，盖茨比脸上闪过一丝阴晴不定的表情。这种表情我觉得非常陌生，又隐约能够认出来，仿佛我只听人用言语描述过。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come on, Daisy,” said Tom, pressing her with his hand toward Gatsby’s car. “I’ll take you in this circus wagon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come on, Daisy,” said Tom, pressing her with his hand toward Gatsby’s car.","zh":"“走吧，黛熙，”汤姆说着用手将黛熙往盖茨比的车上推，“我开这辆马戏团的花车带你。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll take you in this circus wagon.”","zh":"“走吧，黛熙，”汤姆说着用手将黛熙往盖茨比的车上推，“我开这辆马戏团的花车带你。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He opened the door, but she moved out from the circle of his arm.","sentences":[{"en":"He opened the door, but she moved out from the circle of his arm.","zh":"他打开车门，但黛熙走出了他的臂弯。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You take Nick and Jordan. We’ll follow you in the coupé.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You take Nick and Jordan.","zh":"“你带尼克和乔丹吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We’ll follow you in the coupé.”","zh":"我们开跑车跟在你们后面。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She walked close to Gatsby, touching his coat with her hand. Jordan and Tom and I got into the front seat of Gatsby’s car, Tom pushed the unfamiliar gears tentatively, and we shot off into the oppressive heat, leaving them out of sight behind.","sentences":[{"en":"She walked close to Gatsby, touching his coat with her hand.","zh":"她走到盖茨比身边，拉着他的外套。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Jordan and Tom and I got into the front seat of Gatsby’s car, Tom pushed the unfamiliar gears tentatively, and we shot off into the oppressive heat, leaving them out of sight behind.","zh":"乔丹、汤姆和我坐进了盖茨比那辆车的前排座位，汤姆试探着推动那不熟悉的挡位杆，于是我们冲进了逼人的热浪之中，将他们甩得不见踪影。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you see that?” demanded Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you see that?” demanded Tom.","zh":"“你看到了吗？”汤姆气鼓鼓地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“See what?”","sentences":[{"en":"“See what?”","zh":"“看到什么？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He looked at me keenly, realizing that Jordan and I must have known all along.","sentences":[{"en":"He looked at me keenly, realizing that Jordan and I must have known all along.","zh":"他冷冷地望着我，看来已经明白乔丹和我早就知道了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You think I’m pretty dumb, don’t you?” he suggested. “Perhaps I am, but I have a—almost a second sight, sometimes, that tells me what to do. Maybe you don’t believe that, but science—”","sentences":[{"en":"“You think I’m pretty dumb, don’t you?” he suggested.","zh":"“你认为我是个白痴，对吧？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Perhaps I am, but I have a—almost a second sight, sometimes, that tells me what to do.","zh":"他说，“也许我确实是，但我有——我有一种第二知觉，它有时候会告诉我该怎么办。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Maybe you don’t believe that, but science—”","zh":"说了你也许不信，但科学…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He paused. The immediate contingency overtook him, pulled him back from the edge of theoretical abyss.","sentences":[{"en":"He paused.","zh":"他说到这里停了下来。眼前紧急的情况占了上风，将他从理论的深渊边缘拉回来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The immediate contingency overtook him, pulled him back from the edge of theoretical abyss.","zh":"他说到这里停了下来。眼前紧急的情况占了上风，将他从理论的深渊边缘拉回来。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve made a small investigation of this fellow,” he continued. “I could have gone deeper if I’d known—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve made a small investigation of this fellow,” he continued.","zh":"“我对这个家伙做过一番小小的调查，”他接着说，“调查本来可以更深入的，只可惜我…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I could have gone deeper if I’d known—”","zh":"“我对这个家伙做过一番小小的调查，”他接着说，“调查本来可以更深入的，只可惜我…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do you mean you’ve been to a medium?” inquired Jordan humorously.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you mean you’ve been to a medium?” inquired Jordan humorously.","zh":"“你是说你请灵媒了吗？”乔丹幽默地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What?” Confused, he stared at us as we laughed. “A medium?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“什么？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Confused, he stared at us as we laughed.","zh":"看到我们哈哈大笑，他大惑不解地说，“灵媒？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“A medium?”","zh":"看到我们哈哈大笑，他大惑不解地说，“灵媒？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“About Gatsby.”","sentences":[{"en":"“About Gatsby.”","zh":"“问盖茨比的底细啊。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“About Gatsby! No, I haven’t. I said I’d been making a small investigation of his past.”","sentences":[{"en":"“About Gatsby!","zh":"“问盖茨比的底细？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No, I haven’t.","zh":"不，我没有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I said I’d been making a small investigation of his past.”","zh":"我是说我对他的经历做过一番小小的调查。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And you found he was an Oxford man,” said Jordan helpfully.","sentences":[{"en":"“And you found he was an Oxford man,” said Jordan helpfully.","zh":"“然后你发现他是牛津大学毕业的，”乔丹帮腔说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“An Oxford man!” He was incredulous. “Like hell he is! He wears a pink suit.”","sentences":[{"en":"“An Oxford man!”","zh":"“牛津大学毕业的！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was incredulous.","zh":"他完全不信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Like hell he is!","zh":"“就凭他那副鸟样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He wears a pink suit.”","zh":"你看他的西装都是红色的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nevertheless he’s an Oxford man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nevertheless he’s an Oxford man.”","zh":"“可他就是牛津毕业的呀。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oxford, New Mexico,” snorted Tom contemptuously, “or something like that.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oxford, New Mexico,” snorted Tom contemptuously, “or something like that.”","zh":"“新墨西哥州的牛津吧，”汤姆嗤之以鼻地说，“或者什么叫这个名字的烂野鸡大学。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Listen, Tom. If you’re such a snob, why did you invite him to lunch?” demanded Jordan crossly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Listen, Tom.","zh":"“喂，汤姆，既然你这么瞧不起他，干吗还请他到你家吃午饭呢？”乔丹生气地质问他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"If you’re such a snob, why did you invite him to lunch?” demanded Jordan crossly.","zh":"“喂，汤姆，既然你这么瞧不起他，干吗还请他到你家吃午饭呢？”乔丹生气地质问他。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Daisy invited him; she knew him before we were married—God knows where!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Daisy invited him; she knew him before we were married—God knows where!”","zh":"“是黛熙请的，她在我们结婚前就认识他了——天知道是在什么地方！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We were all irritable now with the fading ale, and aware of it we drove for a while in silence. Then as Doctor T. J. Eckleburg’s faded eyes came into sight down the road, I remembered Gatsby’s caution about gasoline.","sentences":[{"en":"We were all irritable now with the fading ale, and aware of it we drove for a while in silence.","zh":"这时我们都有点心浮气躁，因为麦芽酒的后劲上来了。由于意识到这一点，我们默默地开着车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then as Doctor T. J. Eckleburg’s faded eyes came into sight down the road, I remembered Gatsby’s caution about gasoline.","zh":"等到艾克堡医生那双褪色的眼睛在马路的尽头出现时，我想起了盖茨比的警告，怕汽油不够用。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ve got enough to get us to town,” said Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ve got enough to get us to town,” said Tom.","zh":"“剩下的油足够开到城里了，”汤姆说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But there’s a garage right here,” objected Jordan. “I don’t want to get stalled in this baking heat.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But there’s a garage right here,” objected Jordan.","zh":"“但那边就有个汽修厂，”乔丹表示反对，“天气这么烤人，我可不想车开到半路走不了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I don’t want to get stalled in this baking heat.”","zh":"“但那边就有个汽修厂，”乔丹表示反对，“天气这么烤人，我可不想车开到半路走不了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom threw on both brakes impatiently, and we slid to an abrupt dusty stop under Wilson’s sign. After a moment the proprietor emerged from the interior of his establishment and gazed hollow-eyed at the car.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom threw on both brakes impatiently, and we slid to an abrupt dusty stop under Wilson’s sign.","zh":"汤姆暴躁地猛踩刹车，车子突然激起阵阵尘土，停在威尔逊的招牌下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After a moment the proprietor emerged from the interior of his establishment and gazed hollow-eyed at the car.","zh":"过了片刻，老板从汽修厂走出来，两眼无神地盯着轿车看。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Let’s have some gas!” cried Tom roughly. “What do you think we stopped for—to admire the view?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let’s have some gas!” cried Tom roughly.","zh":"“给我们加点油！”汤姆粗鲁地大喊，“你以为我们停下来干什么…欣赏风景吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What do you think we stopped for—to admire the view?”","zh":"“给我们加点油！”汤姆粗鲁地大喊，“你以为我们停下来干什么…欣赏风景吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m sick,” said Wilson without moving. “Been sick all day.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m sick,” said Wilson without moving.","zh":"“我生病了，”威尔逊毫不动弹地说，“今天一天都很难受。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Been sick all day.”","zh":"“我生病了，”威尔逊毫不动弹地说，“今天一天都很难受。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s the matter?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the matter?”","zh":"“怎么回事？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m all run down.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m all run down.”","zh":"“我累坏了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, shall I help myself?” Tom demanded. “You sounded well enough on the phone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, shall I help myself?”","zh":"“难道要我自己动手吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom demanded.","zh":"汤姆质问他，“刚才在电话里你听上去很精神。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You sounded well enough on the phone.”","zh":"汤姆质问他，“刚才在电话里你听上去很精神。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"With an effort Wilson left the shade and support of the doorway and, breathing hard, unscrewed the cap of the tank. In the sunlight his face was green.","sentences":[{"en":"With an effort Wilson left the shade and support of the doorway and, breathing hard, unscrewed the cap of the tank.","zh":"威尔逊吃力地离开阴凉处，不再靠着门框，喘着气拧开油箱的盖子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the sunlight his face was green.","zh":"他的脸在阳光下是绿色的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I didn’t mean to interrupt your lunch,” he said. “But I need money pretty bad, and I was wondering what you were going to do with your old car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I didn’t mean to interrupt your lunch,” he said.","zh":"“我也不想打扰你吃午饭，”他说，“但我特别需要钱，我想知道你准备怎么处理你的旧车。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“But I need money pretty bad, and I was wondering what you were going to do with your old car.”","zh":"“我也不想打扰你吃午饭，”他说，“但我特别需要钱，我想知道你准备怎么处理你的旧车。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How do you like this one?” inquired Tom. “I bought it last week.”","sentences":[{"en":"“How do you like this one?” inquired Tom.","zh":"“你觉得这辆怎么样？”汤姆问，“我上星期才买的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I bought it last week.”","zh":"“你觉得这辆怎么样？”汤姆问，“我上星期才买的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s a nice yellow one,” said Wilson, as he strained at the handle.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s a nice yellow one,” said Wilson, as he strained at the handle.","zh":"“很漂亮的黄色轿车，”威尔逊说，使劲地摇动把手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Like to buy it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Like to buy it?”","zh":"“你想买吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Big chance,” Wilson smiled faintly. “No, but I could make some money on the other.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Big chance,” Wilson smiled faintly.","zh":"“非常想啊，”威尔逊孱弱地笑了，“其实不想啦，但另外那辆可以让我赚点钱。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“No, but I could make some money on the other.”","zh":"“非常想啊，”威尔逊孱弱地笑了，“其实不想啦，但另外那辆可以让我赚点钱。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What do you want money for, all of a sudden?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What do you want money for, all of a sudden?”","zh":"“你要钱干什么，这么突然？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve been here too long. I want to get away. My wife and I want to go West.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve been here too long.","zh":"“我在这里待得太久了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I want to get away.","zh":"我想要离开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My wife and I want to go West.”","zh":"我太太和我想到西部去。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Your wife does,” exclaimed Tom, startled.","sentences":[{"en":"“Your wife does,” exclaimed Tom, startled.","zh":"“你太太想去？”汤姆惊得叫了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s been talking about it for ten years.” He rested for a moment against the pump, shading his eyes. “And now she’s going whether she wants to or not. I’m going to get her away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s been talking about it for ten years.”","zh":"“她说了有十年啦，”他一只手扶着油泵休息了片刻，一只手替眼睛挡住阳光。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He rested for a moment against the pump, shading his eyes.","zh":"“她说了有十年啦，”他一只手扶着油泵休息了片刻，一只手替眼睛挡住阳光。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And now she’s going whether she wants to or not.","zh":"“现在她不管想不想都得去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m going to get her away.”","zh":"我要带她离开这里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The coupé flashed by us with a flurry of dust and the flash of a waving hand.","sentences":[{"en":"The coupé flashed by us with a flurry of dust and the flash of a waving hand.","zh":"跑车从我们身边疾驰而过，激起一溜灰尘，车上有人挥着手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What do I owe you?” demanded Tom harshly.","sentences":[{"en":"“What do I owe you?” demanded Tom harshly.","zh":"“多少钱？”汤姆恶狠狠地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I just got wised up to something funny the last two days,” remarked Wilson. “That’s why I want to get away. That’s why I been bothering you about the car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I just got wised up to something funny the last two days,” remarked Wilson.","zh":"“我前两天才发现事情有点不对劲，”威尔逊说，“所以我想要离开。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“That’s why I want to get away.","zh":"“我前两天才发现事情有点不对劲，”威尔逊说，“所以我想要离开。","scope":"group"},{"en":"That’s why I been bothering you about the car.”","zh":"所以才会打扰你，问你那辆车的事。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What do I owe you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What do I owe you?”","zh":"“多少钱？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Dollar twenty.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Dollar twenty.”","zh":"“一块二。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The relentless beating heat was beginning to confuse me and I had a bad moment there before I realized that so far his suspicions hadn’t alighted on Tom. He had discovered that Myrtle had some sort of life apart from him in another world, and the shock had made him physically sick. I stared at him and then at Tom, who had made a parallel discovery less than an hour before—and it occurred to me that there was no difference between men, in intelligence or race, so profound as the difference between the sick and the well. Wilson was so sick that he looked guilty, unforgivably guilty—as if he had just got some poor girl with child.","sentences":[{"en":"The relentless beating heat was beginning to confuse me and I had a bad moment there before I realized that so far his suspicions hadn’t alighted on Tom.","zh":"在热浪无休无止的拍打之下，我开始有点糊涂了；我先是感到大事不妙，然后才明白威尔逊的疑心迄今尚未落到汤姆身上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had discovered that Myrtle had some sort of life apart from him in another world, and the shock had made him physically sick.","zh":"他已经发现梅朵背着他，在别的世界有某种生活，他惊慌得生起病来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I stared at him and then at Tom, who had made a parallel discovery less than an hour before—and it occurred to me that there was no difference between men, in intelligence or race, so profound as the difference between the sick and the well.","zh":"我看看他，又看看汤姆；不到一个小时之前，汤姆也发现了相同的事情——我突然想到，人与人之间的差别，无论是智力的高低还是种族的不同，都不如生病与健康的差别来得复杂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wilson was so sick that he looked guilty, unforgivably guilty—as if he had just got some poor girl with child.","zh":"威尔逊病得十分厉害，看上去一副罪不可赦的样子——好像他刚刚搞大了某个无知少女的肚子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll let you have that car,” said Tom. “I’ll send it over tomorrow afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll let you have that car,” said Tom.","zh":"“我会把车卖给你的，”汤姆说，“明天下午我派人送过来。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll send it over tomorrow afternoon.”","zh":"“我会把车卖给你的，”汤姆说，“明天下午我派人送过来。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That locality was always vaguely disquieting, even in the broad glare of afternoon, and now I turned my head as though I had been warned of something behind. Over the ash-heaps the giant eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg kept their vigil, but I perceived, after a moment, that other eyes were regarding us with peculiar intensity from less than twenty feet away.","sentences":[{"en":"That locality was always vaguely disquieting, even in the broad glare of afternoon, and now I turned my head as though I had been warned of something behind.","zh":"这地方总是让人隐隐感到不安，哪怕在光天化日之下，这时我觉得后面好像有点不对劲，于是转过头去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Over the ash-heaps the giant eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg kept their vigil, but I perceived, after a moment, that other eyes were regarding us with peculiar intensity from less than twenty feet away.","zh":"在众多垃圾堆的上方，艾克堡医生的巨眼依然监视着这里，但过了一会，我发现不到二十英尺开外，另外有双眼睛正在特别专注地看着我们。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"In one of the windows over the garage the curtains had been moved aside a little, and Myrtle Wilson was peering down at the car. So engrossed was she that she had no consciousness of being observed, and one emotion after another crept into her face like objects into a slowly developing picture. Her expression was curiously familiar—it was an expression I had often seen on women’s faces, but on Myrtle Wilson’s face it seemed purposeless and inexplicable until I realized that her eyes, wide with jealous terror, were fixed not on Tom, but on Jordan Baker, whom she took to be his wife.","sentences":[{"en":"In one of the windows over the garage the curtains had been moved aside a little, and Myrtle Wilson was peering down at the car.","zh":"汽修厂楼上有扇窗户的帘子被拉开了一点点，梅朵·威尔逊俯视着那辆轿车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So engrossed was she that she had no consciousness of being observed, and one emotion after another crept into her face like objects into a slowly developing picture.","zh":"她看得很出神，都没发现有人正在看着她，一种接一种的感情偷偷爬上她的脸庞，就像冲照片时各种东西慢慢地显露出来那样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her expression was curiously familiar—it was an expression I had often seen on women’s faces, but on Myrtle Wilson’s face it seemed purposeless and inexplicable until I realized that her eyes, wide with jealous terror, were fixed not on Tom, but on Jordan Baker, whom she took to be his wife.","zh":"她的表情既熟悉又奇怪——我常常在女人的脸上看到这种表情，但它出现在梅朵·威尔逊脸上显得毫无意义和不可理解，然后我明白了，原来她那双因妒忌和惊恐而睁得很大的眼睛盯着的不是汤姆，而是乔丹·贝克。她误以为乔丹就是汤姆的妻子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"There is no confusion like the confusion of a simple mind, and as we drove away Tom was feeling the hot whips of panic. His wife and his mistress, until an hour ago secure and inviolate, were slipping precipitately from his control. Instinct made him step on the accelerator with the double purpose of overtaking Daisy and leaving Wilson behind, and we sped along toward Astoria at fifty miles an hour, until, among the spidery girders of the elevated, we came in sight of the easygoing blue coupé.","sentences":[{"en":"There is no confusion like the confusion of a simple mind, and as we drove away Tom was feeling the hot whips of panic.","zh":"头脑简单的人不犯浑则已，犯起浑来就非同小可；等到我们驱车离开时，汤姆急得如热锅上的蚂蚁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His wife and his mistress, until an hour ago secure and inviolate, were slipping precipitately from his control.","zh":"他的妻子和情妇在一个小时前似乎还对他死心塌地，但现在很快就要与他分道扬镳了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instinct made him step on the accelerator with the double purpose of overtaking Daisy and leaving Wilson behind, and we sped along toward Astoria at fifty miles an hour, until, among the spidery girders of the elevated, we came in sight of the easygoing blue coupé.","zh":"本能促使他猛踩油门，我怀疑他既是为了追上前方的黛熙，也是为了远离身后的威尔逊。于是我们以五十英里的时速朝阿斯陀利亚疾驰而去，然后在高架铁路蜘蛛网般的支架之间，我们看见了那辆不徐不疾的蓝色跑车。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Those big movies around Fiftieth Street are cool,” suggested Jordan. “I love New York on summer afternoons when everyone’s away. There’s something very sensuous about it—overripe, as if all sorts of funny fruits were going to fall into your hands.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Those big movies around Fiftieth Street are cool,” suggested Jordan.","zh":"“第五十街附近那些大电影院很凉快的，”乔丹提议说，“我喜欢夏日午后的纽约，大街上冷冷清清的，有一种非常诱惑的感觉——熟透的感觉，就好像各种稀奇古怪的果实随时会掉进你手里。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I love New York on summer afternoons when everyone’s away.","zh":"“第五十街附近那些大电影院很凉快的，”乔丹提议说，“我喜欢夏日午后的纽约，大街上冷冷清清的，有一种非常诱惑的感觉——熟透的感觉，就好像各种稀奇古怪的果实随时会掉进你手里。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"There’s something very sensuous about it—overripe, as if all sorts of funny fruits were going to fall into your hands.”","zh":"“第五十街附近那些大电影院很凉快的，”乔丹提议说，“我喜欢夏日午后的纽约，大街上冷冷清清的，有一种非常诱惑的感觉——熟透的感觉，就好像各种稀奇古怪的果实随时会掉进你手里。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The word “sensuous” had the effect of further disquieting Tom, but before he could invent a protest the coupé came to a stop, and Daisy signalled us to draw up alongside.","sentences":[{"en":"The word “sensuous” had the effect of further disquieting Tom, but before he could invent a protest the coupé came to a stop, and Daisy signalled us to draw up alongside.","zh":"“诱惑”这两个字让汤姆更加不安，但他还没来得及说什么，跑车已经停了下来，黛熙示意我们停到旁边。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Where are we going?” she cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where are we going?” she cried.","zh":"“我们去哪呢？”她大声说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How about the movies?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How about the movies?”","zh":"“去看电影怎么样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s so hot,” she complained. “You go. We’ll ride around and meet you after.” With an effort her wit rose faintly. “We’ll meet you on some corner. I’ll be the man smoking two cigarettes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s so hot,” she complained.","zh":"“天气太热了啊，”她表示不满，“你们去吧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You go.","zh":"“天气太热了啊，”她表示不满，“你们去吧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"We’ll ride around and meet you after.”","zh":"我们就兜兜风，然后再跟你们会合。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With an effort her wit rose faintly.","zh":"接着她勉强又憋出两句开玩笑的话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“We’ll meet you on some corner.","zh":"“我们约好在某个街角碰面吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll be the man smoking two cigarettes.”","zh":"你们要是看见一个男人吸着两根香烟，那就是我。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We can’t argue about it here,” Tom said impatiently, as a truck gave out a cursing whistle behind us. “You follow me to the south side of Central Park, in front of the Plaza.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We can’t argue about it here,” Tom said impatiently, as a truck gave out a cursing whistle behind us.","zh":"“别在这里吵架好不好，”汤姆暴躁地说，这时有辆货车在我们后面按响了咒骂的喇叭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“You follow me to the south side of Central Park, in front of the Plaza.”","zh":"“你们跟我来，到中央公园南边，广场酒店前面。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Several times he turned his head and looked back for their car, and if the traffic delayed them he slowed up until they came into sight. I think he was afraid they would dart down a side-street and out of his life forever.","sentences":[{"en":"Several times he turned his head and looked back for their car, and if the traffic delayed them he slowed up until they came into sight.","zh":"他数次回头去望他们的车，如果他们被交通灯拦下，他就会减速，直到他们进入视线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think he was afraid they would dart down a side-street and out of his life forever.","zh":"我想他当时很害怕他们会拐进某条小巷，永远地驶出他的生活。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But they didn’t. And we all took the less explicable step of engaging the parlour of a suite in the Plaza Hotel.","sentences":[{"en":"But they didn’t.","zh":"但他们没有那么做。比去看电影更不可思议的是，我们居然坐进了广场酒店某个套房的客厅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And we all took the less explicable step of engaging the parlour of a suite in the Plaza Hotel.","zh":"但他们没有那么做。比去看电影更不可思议的是，我们居然坐进了广场酒店某个套房的客厅。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The prolonged and tumultuous argument that ended by herding us into that room eludes me, though I have a sharp physical memory that, in the course of it, my underwear kept climbing like a damp snake around my legs and intermittent beads of sweat raced cool across my back. The notion originated with Daisy’s suggestion that we hire five bathrooms and take cold baths, and then assumed more tangible form as “a place to have a mint julep.” Each of us said over and over that it was a “crazy idea”—we all talked at once to a baffled clerk and thought, or pretended to think, that we were being very funny…","sentences":[{"en":"The prolonged and tumultuous argument that ended by herding us into that room eludes me, though I have a sharp physical memory that, in the course of it, my underwear kept climbing like a damp snake around my legs and intermittent beads of sweat raced cool across my back.","zh":"走进房间之前那阵漫长而混乱的争吵我已全然忘了，我只深深地记得，在这个过程中，我的内裤像一条黏糊糊的蛇，不停地在我的双腿间爬来爬去，冰凉的汗珠在我后背滚滚而下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The notion originated with Daisy’s suggestion that we hire five bathrooms and take cold baths, and then assumed more tangible form as “a place to have a mint julep.”","zh":"当时黛熙先是提议我们租五个浴室洗冷水澡，然后又提出更为可行的建议，“找个地方喝点冰镇薄荷酒”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Each of us said over and over that it was a “crazy idea”—we all talked at once to a baffled clerk and thought, or pretended to think, that we were being very funny…","zh":"每当有人提出新的想法，其他人就会反复地说“这个主意不好”——我们七嘴八舌地把酒店前台搞得不知如何是好，却以为，或者假装以为，我们这样很好玩…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The room was large and stifling, and, though it was already four o’clock, opening the windows admitted only a gust of hot shrubbery from the Park. Daisy went to the mirror and stood with her back to us, fixing her hair.","sentences":[{"en":"The room was large and stifling, and, though it was already four o’clock, opening the windows admitted only a gust of hot shrubbery from the Park.","zh":"房间很宽敞，也很闷热；虽然已经是下午四点，可是打开窗户后，乘隙而入的只有自公园灌木丛吹来的热风。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy went to the mirror and stood with her back to us, fixing her hair.","zh":"黛熙走到镜前，背对着我们，站着梳理她的头发。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s a swell suite,” whispered Jordan respectfully, and everyone laughed.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s a swell suite,” whispered Jordan respectfully, and everyone laughed.","zh":"“这套房好漂亮哟，”乔丹装出乡巴佬进城的样子，敬仰地赞叹说，引得每个人都哈哈大笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Open another window,” commanded Daisy, without turning around.","sentences":[{"en":"“Open another window,” commanded Daisy, without turning around.","zh":"“再打开一扇窗，”黛熙头也不回地下命令。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There aren’t any more.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There aren’t any more.”","zh":"“没有窗啦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, we’d better telephone for an axe—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, we’d better telephone for an axe—”","zh":"“那么打电话让他们送把斧头…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The thing to do is to forget about the heat,” said Tom impatiently. “You make it ten times worse by crabbing about it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The thing to do is to forget about the heat,” said Tom impatiently.","zh":"“最好别再喊热了，”汤姆不耐烦地说，“你这样嚷个不停只会让天气热上十倍。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You make it ten times worse by crabbing about it.”","zh":"“最好别再喊热了，”汤姆不耐烦地说，“你这样嚷个不停只会让天气热上十倍。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He unrolled the bottle of whisky from the towel and put it on the table.","sentences":[{"en":"He unrolled the bottle of whisky from the towel and put it on the table.","zh":"他解开毛巾，把那瓶威士忌取出来，放在桌子上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why not let her alone, old sport?” remarked Gatsby. “You’re the one that wanted to come to town.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why not let her alone, old sport?” remarked Gatsby.","zh":"“你能别说她吗，老兄？”盖茨比淡定地说，“说要进城的人也是你。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’re the one that wanted to come to town.”","zh":"“你能别说她吗，老兄？”盖茨比淡定地说，“说要进城的人也是你。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was a moment of silence. The telephone book slipped from its nail and splashed to the floor, whereupon Jordan whispered, “Excuse me”—but this time no one laughed.","sentences":[{"en":"There was a moment of silence.","zh":"大家都不说话了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The telephone book slipped from its nail and splashed to the floor, whereupon Jordan whispered, “Excuse me”—but this time no one laughed.","zh":"挂在钉子上的电话簿突然啪地掉在地上，乔丹立刻低声下气地说：“对不起”——但这次没有人笑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll pick it up,” I offered.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll pick it up,” I offered.","zh":"“我来捡，”我主动说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got it.” Gatsby examined the parted string, muttered “Hum!” in an interested way, and tossed the book on a chair.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got it.”","zh":"“还是我来吧。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby examined the parted string, muttered “Hum!” in an interested way, and tossed the book on a chair.","zh":"盖茨比查看那根断开的绳子，“嗯！”了一声，好像觉得很有意思，然后把电话簿丢到椅子上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s a great expression of yours, isn’t it?” said Tom sharply.","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s a great expression of yours, isn’t it?” said Tom sharply.","zh":"“这是你的口头禅，对吧？”汤姆冷冷地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What is?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is?”","zh":"“什么口头禅？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All this ‘old sport’ business. Where’d you pick that up?”","sentences":[{"en":"“All this ‘old sport’ business.","zh":"“你满嘴都是‘老兄’。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where’d you pick that up?”","zh":"这是从哪里学来的？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Now see here, Tom,” said Daisy, turning around from the mirror, “if you’re going to make personal remarks I won’t stay here a minute. Call up and order some ice for the mint julep.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now see here, Tom,” said Daisy, turning around from the mirror, “if you’re going to make personal remarks I won’t stay here a minute.","zh":"“喂，看着我，汤姆，”黛熙从镜前转过身来说，“如果你准备进行人身攻击，我马上就离开这里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Call up and order some ice for the mint julep.”","zh":"快打电话叫服务员送点冰块来喝薄荷酒。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As Tom took up the receiver the compressed heat exploded into sound and we were listening to the portentous chords of Mendelssohn’s Wedding March from the ballroom below.","sentences":[{"en":"As Tom took up the receiver the compressed heat exploded into sound and we were listening to the portentous chords of Mendelssohn’s Wedding March from the ballroom below.","zh":"汤姆刚拿起话筒，压抑而炎热的空气中突然响起激情澎湃的音乐，我们侧耳细听，原来是门德尔松的《婚礼进行曲》，从楼下的舞厅传来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Imagine marrying anybody in this heat!” cried Jordan dismally.","sentences":[{"en":"“Imagine marrying anybody in this heat!” cried Jordan dismally.","zh":"“这么热的天，居然还有人结婚！”乔丹惊恐地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Still—I was married in the middle of June,” Daisy remembered. “Louisville in June! Somebody fainted. Who was it fainted, Tom?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Still—I was married in the middle of June,” Daisy remembered.","zh":"“你可别说——我就是在六月中旬结的婚，”黛熙回忆说，“六月的路易斯维尔！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Louisville in June!","zh":"“你可别说——我就是在六月中旬结的婚，”黛熙回忆说，“六月的路易斯维尔！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Somebody fainted.","zh":"有人热晕过去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who was it fainted, Tom?”","zh":"晕过去那个人是谁呀，汤姆？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Biloxi,” he answered shortly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Biloxi,” he answered shortly.","zh":"“毕洛西，”他没好气地回答。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“A man named Biloxi. ‘Blocks’ Biloxi, and he made boxes—that’s a fact—and he was from Biloxi, Tennessee.”","sentences":[{"en":"“A man named Biloxi. ‘Blocks’ Biloxi, and he made boxes—that’s a fact—and he was from Biloxi, Tennessee.”","zh":"他的外号叫‘方块’，是个做纸盒的。真的，不骗你。他来自田纳西州的毕洛西。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They carried him into my house,” appended Jordan, “because we lived just two doors from the church. And he stayed three weeks, until Daddy told him he had to get out. The day after he left Daddy died.” After a moment she added as if she might have sounded irreverent, “There wasn’t any connection.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They carried him into my house,” appended Jordan, “because we lived just two doors from the church.","zh":"“他们把他抬到我家，”乔丹添油加醋地说，“因为我家和教堂只隔着两座房子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he stayed three weeks, until Daddy told him he had to get out.","zh":"他赖了三个星期，后来我爸将他赶走了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The day after he left Daddy died.”","zh":"他走后隔日，我爸就去世了。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After a moment she added as if she might have sounded irreverent, “There wasn’t any connection.”","zh":"隔了片刻，她补充道：“这两件事没有任何联系。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I used to know a Bill Biloxi from Memphis,” I remarked.","sentences":[{"en":"“I used to know a Bill Biloxi from Memphis,” I remarked.","zh":"“我认识孟菲斯的比尔·毕洛西，”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That was his cousin. I knew his whole family history before he left. He gave me an aluminium putter that I use today.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That was his cousin.","zh":"“那是他的堂弟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I knew his whole family history before he left.","zh":"他走前把整个家族的历史都说给我了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He gave me an aluminium putter that I use today.”","zh":"他送了我一根高尔夫球杆，我现在还在用呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The music had died down as the ceremony began and now a long cheer floated in at the window, followed by intermittent cries of “Yea—ea—ea!” and finally by a burst of jazz as the dancing began.","sentences":[{"en":"The music had died down as the ceremony began and now a long cheer floated in at the window, followed by intermittent cries of “Yea—ea—ea!” and finally by a burst of jazz as the dancing began.","zh":"音乐声渐渐消歇，仪式正式启动，一阵持续很久的欢呼声飘进窗户，随之而来的是断断续续的叫好声，然后是激情澎湃的爵士乐，宣告舞会已经开始。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’re getting old,” said Daisy. “If we were young we’d rise and dance.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We’re getting old,” said Daisy.","zh":"“我们老啦，”黛熙说，“如果我们还年轻，我们就会站起来跳舞。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“If we were young we’d rise and dance.”","zh":"“我们老啦，”黛熙说，“如果我们还年轻，我们就会站起来跳舞。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Remember Biloxi,” Jordan warned her. “Where’d you know him, Tom?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Remember Biloxi,” Jordan warned her.","zh":"“别忘了毕洛西的前车之鉴，”乔丹警告她，“你是怎么认识他的，汤姆？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Where’d you know him, Tom?”","zh":"“别忘了毕洛西的前车之鉴，”乔丹警告她，“你是怎么认识他的，汤姆？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Biloxi?” He concentrated with an effort. “I didn’t know him. He was a friend of Daisy’s.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Biloxi?”","zh":"“毕洛西？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He concentrated with an effort.","zh":"汤姆努力回忆着，“我以前没有见过他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I didn’t know him.","zh":"汤姆努力回忆着，“我以前没有见过他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was a friend of Daisy’s.”","zh":"他是黛熙的朋友。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He was not,” she denied. “I’d never seen him before. He came down in the private car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He was not,” she denied.","zh":"“才不是呢，”黛熙否认，“我以前从没见过他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’d never seen him before.","zh":"“才不是呢，”黛熙否认，“我以前从没见过他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He came down in the private car.”","zh":"他是坐你包的火车来的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, he said he knew you. He said he was raised in Louisville. Asa Bird brought him around at the last minute and asked if we had room for him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, he said he knew you.","zh":"“是的，他说他认识你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He said he was raised in Louisville.","zh":"他说他是在路易斯维尔长大的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Asa Bird brought him around at the last minute and asked if we had room for him.”","zh":"火车快开的时候，阿萨·伯德把他带过来，问是否有位子给他。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Jordan smiled.","sentences":[{"en":"Jordan smiled.","zh":"乔丹笑了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He was probably bumming his way home. He told me he was president of your class at Yale.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He was probably bumming his way home.","zh":"“他可能是为了搭便车回家吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He told me he was president of your class at Yale.”","zh":"他跟我说他是你在耶鲁的班长。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom and I looked at each other blankly.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom and I looked at each other blankly.","zh":"汤姆和我茫然地看着对方。“毕洛西？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Biloxi?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Biloxi?”","zh":"汤姆和我茫然地看着对方。“毕洛西？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“First place, we didn’t have any president—”","sentences":[{"en":"“First place, we didn’t have any president—”","zh":"“首先，我们没有班长…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby’s foot beat a short, restless tattoo and Tom eyed him suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby’s foot beat a short, restless tattoo and Tom eyed him suddenly.","zh":"盖茨比的脚不耐烦地在地上转来转去，汤姆突然望着他。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“By the way, Mr. Gatsby, I understand you’re an Oxford man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“By the way, Mr. Gatsby, I understand you’re an Oxford man.”","zh":"“对了，盖茨比先生，听说你是牛津毕业的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Not exactly.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not exactly.”","zh":"“倒也不能这么说。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, yes, I understand you went to Oxford.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, yes, I understand you went to Oxford.”","zh":"“是吗？我听说你去过牛津呢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes—I went there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes—I went there.”","zh":"“是的——我是去过。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A pause. Then Tom’s voice, incredulous and insulting:","sentences":[{"en":"A pause.","zh":"大家默不作声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Tom’s voice, incredulous and insulting:","zh":"然后汤姆用怀疑和侮辱的口气说：“你去那里的时间，大概跟毕洛西去纽黑文差不多。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You must have gone there about the time Biloxi went to New Haven.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You must have gone there about the time Biloxi went to New Haven.”","zh":"然后汤姆用怀疑和侮辱的口气说：“你去那里的时间，大概跟毕洛西去纽黑文差不多。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Another pause. A waiter knocked and came in with crushed mint and ice but the silence was unbroken by his “thank you” and the soft closing of the door. This tremendous detail was to be cleared up at last.","sentences":[{"en":"Another pause.","zh":"又是一阵沉默。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A waiter knocked and came in with crushed mint and ice but the silence was unbroken by his “thank you” and the soft closing of the door.","zh":"有个服务员敲敲门，端着捣碎的薄荷叶和冰块走进来，但直到他说了“谢谢”并轻轻地关上房门，大家都没有说话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This tremendous detail was to be cleared up at last.","zh":"有个服务员敲敲门，端着捣碎的薄荷叶和冰块走进来，但直到他说了“谢谢”并轻轻地关上房门，大家都没有说话。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I told you I went there,” said Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"“I told you I went there,” said Gatsby.","zh":"“我刚才跟你说我去过那里，”盖茨比说，","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I heard you, but I’d like to know when.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I heard you, but I’d like to know when.”","zh":"“我听到了，但我想知道是什么时候。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was in nineteen-nineteen, I only stayed five months. That’s why I can’t really call myself an Oxford man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was in nineteen-nineteen, I only stayed five months.","zh":"“那是在1919年，我只待了五个月。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That’s why I can’t really call myself an Oxford man.”","zh":"所以其实不能说我是牛津毕业的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom glanced around to see if we mirrored his unbelief. But we were all looking at Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom glanced around to see if we mirrored his unbelief.","zh":"汤姆四下环顾，想看我们的脸是否反映出他的怀疑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But we were all looking at Gatsby.","zh":"但我们都在望着盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was an opportunity they gave to some of the officers after the armistice,” he continued. “We could go to any of the universities in England or France.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was an opportunity they gave to some of the officers after the armistice,” he continued.","zh":"“那是停战后他们为部分军官安排的机会，”他接着说，“我们可以去英国或者法国的任何大学。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“We could go to any of the universities in England or France.”","zh":"“那是停战后他们为部分军官安排的机会，”他接着说，“我们可以去英国或者法国的任何大学。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I wanted to get up and slap him on the back. I had one of those renewals of complete faith in him that I’d experienced before.","sentences":[{"en":"I wanted to get up and slap him on the back.","zh":"我真想站起来，拍拍他的后背，为他叫好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I had one of those renewals of complete faith in him that I’d experienced before.","zh":"我对他的信心又完全恢复了，以前也有过几次这样的情况。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy rose, smiling faintly, and went to the table.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy rose, smiling faintly, and went to the table.","zh":"黛熙站起来，强作欢颜，走到桌子旁边。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Open the whisky, Tom,” she ordered, “and I’ll make you a mint julep. Then you won’t seem so stupid to yourself… Look at the mint!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Open the whisky, Tom,” she ordered, “and I’ll make you a mint julep.","zh":"“把威士忌打开，汤姆，”她发布命令似的说，“我来给你弄点冰镇薄荷酒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then you won’t seem so stupid to yourself…","zh":"然后你就不会这么丢人现眼了…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Look at the mint!”","zh":"你看看这些薄荷叶子！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wait a minute,” snapped Tom, “I want to ask Mr. Gatsby one more question.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wait a minute,” snapped Tom, “I want to ask Mr. Gatsby one more question.”","zh":"“且慢，”汤姆喝道，“我还有话要问盖茨比先生。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Go on,” Gatsby said politely.","sentences":[{"en":"“Go on,” Gatsby said politely.","zh":"“请讲，”盖茨比礼貌地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What kind of a row are you trying to cause in my house anyhow?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What kind of a row are you trying to cause in my house anyhow?”","zh":"“你去我家到底是想闹什么事？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They were out in the open at last and Gatsby was content.","sentences":[{"en":"They were out in the open at last and Gatsby was content.","zh":"他们终于翻脸了，这正中盖茨比下怀。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He isn’t causing a row,” Daisy looked desperately from one to the other. “You’re causing a row. Please have a little self-control.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He isn’t causing a row,” Daisy looked desperately from one to the other.","zh":"“他没有闹事，”黛熙绝望地来回看着他们俩，“闹事的人是你。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’re causing a row.","zh":"“他没有闹事，”黛熙绝望地来回看着他们俩，“闹事的人是你。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Please have a little self-control.”","zh":"请你自重一点好不好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Self-control!” repeated Tom incredulously. “I suppose the latest thing is to sit back and let Mr. Nobody from Nowhere make love to your wife. Well, if that’s the idea you can count me out… Nowadays people begin by sneering at family life and family institutions, and next they’ll throw everything overboard and have intermarriage between black and white.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Self-control!” repeated Tom incredulously.","zh":"“你居然要我自重！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I suppose the latest thing is to sit back and let Mr. Nobody from Nowhere make love to your wife.","zh":"汤姆不敢置信地说，“难道现在最时髦的事情就是袖手旁观放任来路不明的无名小卒跟你的太太做爱吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, if that’s the idea you can count me out…","zh":"哼，如果这样才算时髦，你尽可认为我很古板…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nowadays people begin by sneering at family life and family institutions, and next they’ll throw everything overboard and have intermarriage between black and white.”","zh":"这年头大家开始蔑视家庭生活和家庭制度了，我看接下去规矩都要被废掉，连黑人和白人也可以通婚了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Flushed with his impassioned gibberish, he saw himself standing alone on the last barrier of civilization.","sentences":[{"en":"Flushed with his impassioned gibberish, he saw himself standing alone on the last barrier of civilization.","zh":"他脸上涨得通红，满嘴胡说八道，好像他自己正在独自守卫着文明社会最后一道防线。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’re all white here,” murmured Jordan.","sentences":[{"en":"“We’re all white here,” murmured Jordan.","zh":"他脸上涨得通红，满嘴胡说八道，好像他自己正在独自守卫着文明社会最后一道防线。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I know I’m not very popular. I don’t give big parties. I suppose you’ve got to make your house into a pigsty in order to have any friends—in the modern world.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know I’m not very popular.","zh":"“这里大家都是白人，”乔丹嘀咕说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t give big parties.","zh":"“我知道我人缘不好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I suppose you’ve got to make your house into a pigsty in order to have any friends—in the modern world.”","zh":"我没有大办宴席。我看在这个现代社会，你非得把家里变成猪圈才能交到朋友。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Angry as I was, as we all were, I was tempted to laugh whenever he opened his mouth. The transition from libertine to prig was so complete.","sentences":[{"en":"Angry as I was, as we all were, I was tempted to laugh whenever he opened his mouth.","zh":"我虽然很生气，大家都很生气，但他每次张开嘴巴，我都忍不住想笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The transition from libertine to prig was so complete.","zh":"这人满肚子男盗女娼，竟然能够装得如此道貌岸然。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got something to tell you, old sport—” began Gatsby. But Daisy guessed at his intention.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got something to tell you, old sport—” began Gatsby.","zh":"“我有话要告诉你，老兄…”盖茨比开口了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Daisy guessed at his intention.","zh":"但黛熙猜到了他的用意。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Please don’t!” she interrupted helplessly. “Please let’s all go home. Why don’t we all go home?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Please don’t!” she interrupted helplessly.","zh":"“别说！”她无助地拦住了话头，“我们大家都回去吧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Please let’s all go home.","zh":"“别说！”她无助地拦住了话头，“我们大家都回去吧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why don’t we all go home?”","zh":"我们都回家了，好不好？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s a good idea,” I got up. “Come on, Tom. Nobody wants a drink.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s a good idea,” I got up.","zh":"“好啊，”我站起来，“走吧，汤姆。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Come on, Tom.","zh":"“好啊，”我站起来，“走吧，汤姆。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Nobody wants a drink.”","zh":"没有人想喝酒。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want to know what Mr. Gatsby has to tell me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want to know what Mr. Gatsby has to tell me.”","zh":"“我倒想听听盖茨比先生有什么话要对我说。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Your wife doesn’t love you,” said Gatsby. “She’s never loved you. She loves me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Your wife doesn’t love you,” said Gatsby.","zh":"“你的太太并不爱你，”盖茨比说，“她从来没有爱过你。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She’s never loved you.","zh":"“你的太太并不爱你，”盖茨比说，“她从来没有爱过你。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She loves me.”","zh":"她爱的是我。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You must be crazy!” exclaimed Tom automatically.","sentences":[{"en":"“You must be crazy!” exclaimed Tom automatically.","zh":"“你肯定疯掉了！”汤姆脱口而出。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby sprang to his feet, vivid with excitement.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby sprang to his feet, vivid with excitement.","zh":"盖茨比猛然站起来，显得非常激动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She never loved you, do you hear?” he cried. “She only married you because I was poor and she was tired of waiting for me. It was a terrible mistake, but in her heart she never loved anyone except me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“She never loved you, do you hear?” he cried.","zh":"“她从来没有爱过你，你听到了吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“She only married you because I was poor and she was tired of waiting for me.","zh":"他大喊，“她会嫁给你，只是因为当时我很穷，她又不想等我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a terrible mistake, but in her heart she never loved anyone except me!”","zh":"这是个可怕的错误，但在她心里，她从未爱过别人，她只爱我！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At this point Jordan and I tried to go, but Tom and Gatsby insisted with competitive firmness that we remain—as though neither of them had anything to conceal and it would be a privilege to partake vicariously of their emotions.","sentences":[{"en":"At this point Jordan and I tried to go, but Tom and Gatsby insisted with competitive firmness that we remain—as though neither of them had anything to conceal and it would be a privilege to partake vicariously of their emotions.","zh":"这时我和乔丹都想走，但汤姆和盖茨比争先恐后地硬要我们留下——仿佛他们都没有不可告人的秘密，仿佛能够见证他们的争风吃醋也是一种荣幸。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Sit down, Daisy,” Tom’s voice groped unsuccessfully for the paternal note. “What’s been going on? I want to hear all about it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sit down, Daisy,” Tom’s voice groped unsuccessfully for the paternal note.","zh":"“坐下，黛熙，”汤姆想要装出父亲教育女儿的口气，但装得不像，“到底怎么回事？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What’s been going on?","zh":"“坐下，黛熙，”汤姆想要装出父亲教育女儿的口气，但装得不像，“到底怎么回事？","scope":"group"},{"en":"I want to hear all about it.”","zh":"你从头到尾说给我听。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I told you what’s been going on,” said Gatsby. “Going on for five years—and you didn’t know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I told you what’s been going on,” said Gatsby.","zh":"“我已经告诉你怎么回事，”盖茨比说，“已经有五年了——你什么都不知道。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Going on for five years—and you didn’t know.”","zh":"“我已经告诉你怎么回事，”盖茨比说，“已经有五年了——你什么都不知道。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom turned to Daisy sharply.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom turned to Daisy sharply.","zh":"汤姆转过身严厉地看着黛熙。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’ve been seeing this fellow for five years?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’ve been seeing this fellow for five years?”","zh":"“你跟这个家伙来往了五年？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Not seeing,” said Gatsby. “No, we couldn’t meet. But both of us loved each other all that time, old sport, and you didn’t know. I used to laugh sometimes”—but there was no laughter in his eyes—“to think that you didn’t know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not seeing,” said Gatsby.","zh":"“不是交往，”盖茨比说，“我们无法见面。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“No, we couldn’t meet.","zh":"“不是交往，”盖茨比说，“我们无法见面。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But both of us loved each other all that time, old sport, and you didn’t know.","zh":"但在这段时间里我们彼此相爱，老兄，而你什么都不知道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I used to laugh sometimes”—but there was no laughter in his eyes—“to think that you didn’t know.”","zh":"我常常想笑”——但他眼里毫无笑意——“因为你什么都不知道。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh—that’s all.” Tom tapped his thick fingers together like a clergyman and leaned back in his chair.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh—that’s all.”","zh":"“哦——原来不过如此。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom tapped his thick fingers together like a clergyman and leaned back in his chair.","zh":"汤姆粗壮的十指像牧师那样合了起来，向后靠着椅背。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re crazy!” he exploded. “I can’t speak about what happened five years ago, because I didn’t know Daisy then—and I’ll be damned if I see how you got within a mile of her unless you brought the groceries to the back door. But all the rest of that’s a God damned lie. Daisy loved me when she married me and she loves me now.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re crazy!” he exploded.","zh":"“你疯掉了！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I can’t speak about what happened five years ago, because I didn’t know Daisy then—and I’ll be damned if I see how you got within a mile of her unless you brought the groceries to the back door.","zh":"他破口大骂，“五年前的事我不管，因为那时我还没有认识黛熙——我真他妈不明白你怎么能接近她，除非你是从后门给她家送杂货的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But all the rest of that’s a God damned lie.","zh":"但别的都他妈是一派胡言。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Daisy loved me when she married me and she loves me now.”","zh":"黛熙嫁给我的时候很爱我，她现在也爱我。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No,” said Gatsby, shaking his head.","sentences":[{"en":"“No,” said Gatsby, shaking his head.","zh":"“不，”盖茨比摇摇头说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She does, though. The trouble is that sometimes she gets foolish ideas in her head and doesn’t know what she’s doing.” He nodded sagely. “And what’s more, I love Daisy too. Once in a while I go off on a spree and make a fool of myself, but I always come back, and in my heart I love her all the time.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She does, though.","zh":"“随便你怎么说，反正她确实爱我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The trouble is that sometimes she gets foolish ideas in her head and doesn’t know what she’s doing.”","zh":"问题在于，有时候她脑袋里会有些愚蠢的念头，也不知道她自己在干什么。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He nodded sagely.","zh":"问题在于，有时候她脑袋里会有些愚蠢的念头，也不知道她自己在干什么。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“And what’s more, I love Daisy too.","zh":"他自以为是地点点头，“更重要的是，我也爱黛熙。我偶尔也会寻欢作乐，干些傻事，但我总是会回来，我心里一直是爱着她的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Once in a while I go off on a spree and make a fool of myself, but I always come back, and in my heart I love her all the time.”","zh":"他自以为是地点点头，“更重要的是，我也爱黛熙。我偶尔也会寻欢作乐，干些傻事，但我总是会回来，我心里一直是爱着她的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re revolting,” said Daisy. She turned to me, and her voice, dropping an octave lower, filled the room with thrilling scorn: “Do you know why we left Chicago? I’m surprised that they didn’t treat you to the story of that little spree.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re revolting,” said Daisy.","zh":"“你真恶心，”黛熙说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She turned to me, and her voice, dropping an octave lower, filled the room with thrilling scorn: “Do you know why we left Chicago?","zh":"她转身看着我，压低了声音，让整个房间充满了颤抖的谴责：“你知道我们为什么离开芝加哥吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m surprised that they didn’t treat you to the story of that little spree.”","zh":"我真奇怪大家没有把他那些风流韵事说给你听。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby walked over and stood beside her.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby walked over and stood beside her.","zh":"盖茨比走过去，站在她身边。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Daisy, that’s all over now,” he said earnestly. “It doesn’t matter any more. Just tell him the truth—that you never loved him—and it’s all wiped out forever.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Daisy, that’s all over now,” he said earnestly.","zh":"“黛熙，旧事不必再提了，”他满怀期待地说，“那已经无所谓。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It doesn’t matter any more.","zh":"“黛熙，旧事不必再提了，”他满怀期待地说，“那已经无所谓。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Just tell him the truth—that you never loved him—and it’s all wiped out forever.”","zh":"只要告诉他真相，说你从来没有爱过他，那些事就被永远地抹掉了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She looked at him blindly. “Why—how could I love him—possibly?”","sentences":[{"en":"She looked at him blindly.","zh":"她茫然地看着盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why—how could I love him—possibly?”","zh":"“是啊，我怎么可能爱过他呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You never loved him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You never loved him.”","zh":"“你没有爱过他。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She hesitated. Her eyes fell on Jordan and me with a sort of appeal, as though she realized at last what she was doing—and as though she had never, all along, intended doing anything at all. But it was done now. It was too late.","sentences":[{"en":"She hesitated.","zh":"她犹豫了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her eyes fell on Jordan and me with a sort of appeal, as though she realized at last what she was doing—and as though she had never, all along, intended doing anything at all.","zh":"她眼带哀求地看着乔丹和我，仿佛她终于明白她在做什么——仿佛她一直以来根本什么事也不想做。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But it was done now.","zh":"但事情已经做了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was too late.","zh":"后悔也来不及了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I never loved him,” she said, with perceptible reluctance.","sentences":[{"en":"“I never loved him,” she said, with perceptible reluctance.","zh":"“我没有爱过他，”她说，显得很勉强。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Not at Kapiolani?” demanded Tom suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Not at Kapiolani?” demanded Tom suddenly.","zh":"“在卡皮奥兰尼时你不爱我吗？”汤姆突然问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No.”","zh":"“不爱。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"From the ballroom beneath, muffled and suffocating chords were drifting up on hot waves of air.","sentences":[{"en":"From the ballroom beneath, muffled and suffocating chords were drifting up on hot waves of air.","zh":"楼下舞厅里沉闷而令人窒息的音乐声不停地顺着空气的热浪飘上来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Not that day I carried you down from the Punch Bowl to keep your shoes dry?” There was a husky tenderness in his tone… “Daisy?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not that day I carried you down from the Punch Bowl to keep your shoes dry?”","zh":"“那天为了让你的鞋不沾水，我背着你走下酒钵山，当时你也不爱我吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a husky tenderness in his tone…","zh":"他哑着嗓子温柔地说，“黛熙？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Daisy?”","zh":"他哑着嗓子温柔地说，“黛熙？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Please don’t.” Her voice was cold, but the rancour was gone from it. She looked at Gatsby. “There, Jay,” she said—but her hand as she tried to light a cigarette was trembling. Suddenly she threw the cigarette and the burning match on the carpet.","sentences":[{"en":"“Please don’t.”","zh":"“请别说了，”她冷冷地说，但话音里的怨恨已经消失。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her voice was cold, but the rancour was gone from it.","zh":"“请别说了，”她冷冷地说，但话音里的怨恨已经消失。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She looked at Gatsby.","zh":"她看着盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“There, Jay,” she said—but her hand as she tried to light a cigarette was trembling.","zh":"“你看，杰伊，”她强作镇定地说——但她那想要去点香烟的手却一直在发抖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suddenly she threw the cigarette and the burning match on the carpet.","zh":"突然间，她把香烟和燃烧着的火柴丢到地毯上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, you want too much!” she cried to Gatsby. “I love you now—isn’t that enough? I can’t help what’s past.” She began to sob helplessly. “I did love him once—but I loved you too.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, you want too much!” she cried to Gatsby.","zh":"“唉，你想要的太多了！”她哭喊着对盖茨比说，“现在我爱你——这还不够吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I love you now—isn’t that enough?","zh":"“唉，你想要的太多了！”她哭喊着对盖茨比说，“现在我爱你——这还不够吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"I can’t help what’s past.”","zh":"过去发生的事情我没法改变。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She began to sob helplessly.","zh":"她开始无助地哭起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I did love him once—but I loved you too.”","zh":"“以前我是爱过他——但我也爱你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby’s eyes opened and closed.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby’s eyes opened and closed.","zh":"盖茨比的眼睛睁开又闭上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You loved me too?” he repeated.","sentences":[{"en":"“You loved me too?” he repeated.","zh":"“你也爱我？”他喃喃地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Even that’s a lie,” said Tom savagely. “She didn’t know you were alive. Why—there’s things between Daisy and me that you’ll never know, things that neither of us can ever forget.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Even that’s a lie,” said Tom savagely.","zh":"“连这句话也是骗你的，”汤姆恶狠狠地说，“她早就忘了有你这个人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She didn’t know you were alive.","zh":"“连这句话也是骗你的，”汤姆恶狠狠地说，“她早就忘了有你这个人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why—there’s things between Daisy and me that you’ll never know, things that neither of us can ever forget.”","zh":"哼——黛熙和我之间的事你永远不会知道，那些事是我们永远无法忘记的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The words seemed to bite physically into Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"The words seemed to bite physically into Gatsby.","zh":"这些话似乎刺痛了盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want to speak to Daisy alone,” he insisted. “She’s all excited now—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want to speak to Daisy alone,” he insisted.","zh":"“我想要跟黛熙单独谈谈，”他语气坚决地说，“她现在太激动了…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She’s all excited now—”","zh":"“我想要跟黛熙单独谈谈，”他语气坚决地说，“她现在太激动了…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Even alone I can’t say I never loved Tom,” she admitted in a pitiful voice. “It wouldn’t be true.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Even alone I can’t say I never loved Tom,” she admitted in a pitiful voice.","zh":"“单独谈我也不能说我没有爱过汤姆，”她痛苦地坦白说，“那不是真话。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It wouldn’t be true.”","zh":"“单独谈我也不能说我没有爱过汤姆，”她痛苦地坦白说，“那不是真话。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course it wouldn’t,” agreed Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course it wouldn’t,” agreed Tom.","zh":"“那当然不是真话，”汤姆赞许地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She turned to her husband.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned to her husband.","zh":"她转身面对她的丈夫。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“As if it mattered to you,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“As if it mattered to you,” she said.","zh":"“别装得你好像很在乎似的，”她说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course it matters. I’m going to take better care of you from now on.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course it matters.","zh":"“我当然在乎啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m going to take better care of you from now on.”","zh":"从现在开始我要好好照顾你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You don’t understand,” said Gatsby, with a touch of panic. “You’re not going to take care of her any more.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You don’t understand,” said Gatsby, with a touch of panic.","zh":"“你怎么还不明白，”盖茨比有点惊慌地说，“你再也没有机会照顾她了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’re not going to take care of her any more.”","zh":"“你怎么还不明白，”盖茨比有点惊慌地说，“你再也没有机会照顾她了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m not?” Tom opened his eyes wide and laughed. He could afford to control himself now. “Why’s that?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m not?”","zh":"“真的吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom opened his eyes wide and laughed.","zh":"汤姆睁大了眼睛，哈哈地笑起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He could afford to control himself now.","zh":"现在他已经淡定了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why’s that?”","zh":"“为什么呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Daisy’s leaving you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Daisy’s leaving you.”","zh":"“黛熙要离开你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nonsense.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nonsense.”","zh":"“无稽之谈。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I am, though,” she said with a visible effort.","sentences":[{"en":"“I am, though,” she said with a visible effort.","zh":"“但我是要离开你，”黛熙很勉强地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s not leaving me!” Tom’s words suddenly leaned down over Gatsby. “Certainly not for a common swindler who’d have to steal the ring he put on her finger.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s not leaving me!”","zh":"“她不会离开我！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom’s words suddenly leaned down over Gatsby.","zh":"汤姆突然盛气凌人地对盖茨比说，“她肯定不会为了一个连结婚戒指也要去偷来的大骗子离开我。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Certainly not for a common swindler who’d have to steal the ring he put on her finger.”","zh":"汤姆突然盛气凌人地对盖茨比说，“她肯定不会为了一个连结婚戒指也要去偷来的大骗子离开我。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I won’t stand this!” cried Daisy. “Oh, please let’s get out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I won’t stand this!” cried Daisy.","zh":"“你怎能这么说呢！”黛熙哭着说，“求求你，我们走吧。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Oh, please let’s get out.”","zh":"“你怎能这么说呢！”黛熙哭着说，“求求你，我们走吧。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who are you, anyhow?” broke out Tom. “You’re one of that bunch that hangs around with Meyer Wolfshiem—that much I happen to know. I’ve made a little investigation into your affairs—and I’ll carry it further tomorrow.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who are you, anyhow?” broke out Tom.","zh":"“你到底是什么人？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“You’re one of that bunch that hangs around with Meyer Wolfshiem—that much I happen to know.","zh":"汤姆又是破口大骂，“你是梅耶·沃夫希姆的猪朋狗友——目前我就知道这么多。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve made a little investigation into your affairs—and I’ll carry it further tomorrow.”","zh":"我摸过你的底细——明天我还会继续打听。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You can suit yourself about that, old sport,” said Gatsby steadily.","sentences":[{"en":"“You can suit yourself about that, old sport,” said Gatsby steadily.","zh":"“随你的便，老兄，”盖茨比镇定地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I found out what your ‘drugstores’ were.” He turned to us and spoke rapidly. “He and this Wolfshiem bought up a lot of side-street drugstores here and in Chicago and sold grain alcohol over the counter. That’s one of his little stunts. I picked him for a bootlegger the first time I saw him, and I wasn’t far wrong.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I found out what your ‘drugstores’ were.”","zh":"“我已经揭穿你那些‘药房’的老底。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He turned to us and spoke rapidly.","zh":"他转过身看着我们，快速地说，“他和这位沃夫希姆在这里和芝加哥的小巷收购了许多药房，公然把酒精摆到柜台上卖。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He and this Wolfshiem bought up a lot of side-street drugstores here and in Chicago and sold grain alcohol over the counter.","zh":"他转过身看着我们，快速地说，“他和这位沃夫希姆在这里和芝加哥的小巷收购了许多药房，公然把酒精摆到柜台上卖。","scope":"group"},{"en":"That’s one of his little stunts.","zh":"这是他的鬼把戏之一。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I picked him for a bootlegger the first time I saw him, and I wasn’t far wrong.”","zh":"我第一次见到他就知道他是个私酒贩子，我猜得没错吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What about it?” said Gatsby politely. “I guess your friend Walter Chase wasn’t too proud to come in on it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What about it?” said Gatsby politely.","zh":"“那又怎么样？”盖茨比礼貌地说，“你的朋友瓦尔特·蔡斯不也做这行吗？他可不觉得丢人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I guess your friend Walter Chase wasn’t too proud to come in on it.”","zh":"“那又怎么样？”盖茨比礼貌地说，“你的朋友瓦尔特·蔡斯不也做这行吗？他可不觉得丢人。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And you left him in the lurch, didn’t you? You let him go to jail for a month over in New Jersey. God! You ought to hear Walter on the subject of you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And you left him in the lurch, didn’t you?","zh":"“你弄了个圈套让他钻，对吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You let him go to jail for a month over in New Jersey.","zh":"你让他在新泽西坐了一个月的牢。天哪！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"God!","zh":"你应该听听瓦尔特对你的评价。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You ought to hear Walter on the subject of you.”","zh":"你应该听听瓦尔特对你的评价。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He came to us dead broke. He was very glad to pick up some money, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He came to us dead broke.","zh":"“他来找我们的时候几乎破产了。他非常高兴可以白捡一些钱，老兄。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was very glad to pick up some money, old sport.”","zh":"“他来找我们的时候几乎破产了。他非常高兴可以白捡一些钱，老兄。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t you call me ‘old sport’!” cried Tom. Gatsby said nothing. “Walter could have you up on the betting laws too, but Wolfshiem scared him into shutting his mouth.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t you call me ‘old sport’!” cried Tom.","zh":"“别叫我‘老兄’！”汤姆大声说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby said nothing.","zh":"盖茨比没有回话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Walter could have you up on the betting laws too, but Wolfshiem scared him into shutting his mouth.”","zh":"“瓦尔特本来想揭发你违法赌博的，但沃夫希姆恐吓他，要他闭嘴。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That unfamiliar yet recognizable look was back again in Gatsby’s face.","sentences":[{"en":"That unfamiliar yet recognizable look was back again in Gatsby’s face.","zh":"那种陌生然而可以辨认的表情又回到了盖茨比脸上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That drugstore business was just small change,” continued Tom slowly, “but you’ve got something on now that Walter’s afraid to tell me about.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That drugstore business was just small change,” continued Tom slowly, “but you’ve got something on now that Walter’s afraid to tell me about.”","zh":"“药房的生意只是小儿科，”汤姆慢慢地接着说，“你现在做的事才厉害，连瓦尔特都不敢对我说。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I glanced at Daisy, who was staring terrified between Gatsby and her husband, and at Jordan, who had begun to balance an invisible but absorbing object on the tip of her chin. Then I turned back to Gatsby—and was startled at his expression. He looked—and this is said in all contempt for the babbled slander of his garden—as if he had “killed a man.” For a moment the set of his face could be described in just that fantastic way.","sentences":[{"en":"I glanced at Daisy, who was staring terrified between Gatsby and her husband, and at Jordan, who had begun to balance an invisible but absorbing object on the tip of her chin.","zh":"我望向黛熙，她正惊恐地看着盖茨比和她丈夫。我又看着乔丹，她又开始平衡下巴上某样看不见但很有趣的物品。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then I turned back to Gatsby—and was startled at his expression.","zh":"然后我望着盖茨比——被他的表情吓了一跳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked—and this is said in all contempt for the babbled slander of his garden—as if he had “killed a man.”","zh":"虽然我很讨厌人们在他花园里散布的那些谣言，但他的表情特别凶恶，看上去确实像是“杀过人”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a moment the set of his face could be described in just that fantastic way.","zh":"恨不得把汤姆杀死的神情在他脸上盘桓了片刻。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It passed, and he began to talk excitedly to Daisy, denying everything, defending his name against accusations that had not been made. But with every word she was drawing further and further into herself, so he gave that up, and only the dead dream fought on as the afternoon slipped away, trying to touch what was no longer tangible, struggling unhappily, undespairingly, toward that lost voice across the room.","sentences":[{"en":"It passed, and he began to talk excitedly to Daisy, denying everything, defending his name against accusations that had not been made.","zh":"这种表情消失之后，他开始激动地向黛熙说话，矢口否认一切，为尚未有人提出的罪名辩白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But with every word she was drawing further and further into herself, so he gave that up, and only the dead dream fought on as the afternoon slipped away, trying to touch what was no longer tangible, struggling unhappily, undespairingly, toward that lost voice across the room.","zh":"但他说得越多，黛熙越是听不进去，越是往后退得离他更远，所以他放弃了，只剩下业已死去的梦想随着午后时光的流逝继续在挣扎，还拼命地想要去触碰那再也不可企及的，还痛苦而又不绝望地想追上房间对面那已消失的声音。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The voice begged again to go.","sentences":[{"en":"The voice begged again to go.","zh":"那声音又求着要走。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Please, Tom! I can’t stand this any more.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Please, Tom!","zh":"“求求你，汤姆！我再也受不了啦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I can’t stand this any more.”","zh":"“求求你，汤姆！我再也受不了啦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Her frightened eyes told that whatever intentions, whatever courage she had had, were definitely gone.","sentences":[{"en":"Her frightened eyes told that whatever intentions, whatever courage she had had, were definitely gone.","zh":"她惊恐的双眼表明，她原来的决心和勇气无论有多大，现在全都消失了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You two start on home, Daisy,” said Tom. “In Mr. Gatsby’s car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You two start on home, Daisy,” said Tom.","zh":"“你们俩回家去吧，黛熙，”汤姆说，“坐盖茨比先生的车。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“In Mr. Gatsby’s car.”","zh":"“你们俩回家去吧，黛熙，”汤姆说，“坐盖茨比先生的车。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She looked at Tom, alarmed now, but he insisted with magnanimous scorn.","sentences":[{"en":"She looked at Tom, alarmed now, but he insisted with magnanimous scorn.","zh":"她望着汤姆，显得很是惶惑，但他坚持这种大方的轻蔑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Go on. He won’t annoy you. I think he realizes that his presumptuous little flirtation is over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go on.","zh":"“去吧。他不敢再对你怎样的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He won’t annoy you.","zh":"“去吧。他不敢再对你怎样的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I think he realizes that his presumptuous little flirtation is over.”","zh":"我想他已经明白，癞蛤蟆终究是吃不上天鹅肉的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They were gone, without a word, snapped out, made accidental, isolated, like ghosts, even from our pity.","sentences":[{"en":"They were gone, without a word, snapped out, made accidental, isolated, like ghosts, even from our pity.","zh":"他们转头就走，片言不留地离开，就这样像幽灵般意外地、决绝地不辞而别，连我们的同情也弃之不顾。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"After a moment Tom got up and began wrapping the unopened bottle of whisky in the towel.","sentences":[{"en":"After a moment Tom got up and began wrapping the unopened bottle of whisky in the towel.","zh":"过了片刻，汤姆站起来，开始用毛巾把那瓶尚未打开的威士忌包起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Want any of this stuff? Jordan?… Nick?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Want any of this stuff?","zh":"“想来点这玩意吗？乔丹？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Jordan?…","zh":"尼克，你呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Nick?”","zh":"尼克，你呢？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I didn’t answer.","sentences":[{"en":"I didn’t answer.","zh":"我没有回答。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nick?” He asked again.","sentences":[{"en":"“Nick?”","zh":"“尼克，你呢？”他又问。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He asked again.","zh":"“尼克，你呢？”他又问。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“什么？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Want any?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Want any?”","zh":"“想来点吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No… I just remembered that today’s my birthday.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No… I just remembered that today’s my birthday.”","zh":"“不了…我刚想起来今天是我的生日。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was thirty. Before me stretched the portentous, menacing road of a new decade.","sentences":[{"en":"I was thirty.","zh":"我三十岁了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Before me stretched the portentous, menacing road of a new decade.","zh":"又一条艰难凶险的十年之路摆在我面前。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was seven o’clock when we got into the coupé with him and started for Long Island. Tom talked incessantly, exulting and laughing, but his voice was as remote from Jordan and me as the foreign clamour on the sidewalk or the tumult of the elevated overhead. Human sympathy has its limits, and we were content to let all their tragic arguments fade with the city lights behind. Thirty—the promise of a decade of loneliness, a thinning list of single men to know, a thinning briefcase of enthusiasm, thinning hair. But there was Jordan beside me, who, unlike Daisy, was too wise ever to carry well-forgotten dreams from age to age. As we passed over the dark bridge her wan face fell lazily against my coat’s shoulder and the formidable stroke of thirty died away with the reassuring pressure of her hand.","sentences":[{"en":"It was seven o’clock when we got into the coupé with him and started for Long Island.","zh":"到了晚上七点，我们随着他坐进跑车，启程赶回长岛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom talked incessantly, exulting and laughing, but his voice was as remote from Jordan and me as the foreign clamour on the sidewalk or the tumult of the elevated overhead.","zh":"汤姆不停地说话，意气风发，哈哈大笑。但在我和乔丹听来，他的声音遥远如同人行道上嘈杂的人声，或者火车从头顶高架铁路驶过的轰隆声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Human sympathy has its limits, and we were content to let all their tragic arguments fade with the city lights behind.","zh":"人类的同情心是有限的，所以我们乐于将他们那场可悲的争吵连同城市的灯火抛诸脑后。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thirty—the promise of a decade of loneliness, a thinning list of single men to know, a thinning briefcase of enthusiasm, thinning hair.","zh":"我三十岁啦——眼看又是十年的孤独，单身的朋友将会渐渐变少，澎湃的激情必将缓缓淡薄，而我的头发也将会日渐稀疏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But there was Jordan beside me, who, unlike Daisy, was too wise ever to carry well-forgotten dreams from age to age.","zh":"但我身边还有乔丹，她不像黛熙那么傻，不会把早该遗忘的梦想年复一年地藏在心里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As we passed over the dark bridge her wan face fell lazily against my coat’s shoulder and the formidable stroke of thirty died away with the reassuring pressure of her hand.","zh":"当我们驶过昏暗的大桥时，她那苍白的脸娇慵地靠在我的肩膀上，紧紧地握住我的手，我感到非常欣慰，也就慢慢忘记我的三十岁生日毁于这件可怕的事情。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"So we drove on toward death through the cooling twilight.","sentences":[{"en":"So we drove on toward death through the cooling twilight.","zh":"我们就这样在凉爽的暮色中向着前方的死亡驶去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"The young Greek, Michaelis, who ran the coffee joint beside the ash-heaps was the principal witness at the inquest. He had slept through the heat until after five, when he strolled over to the garage, and found George Wilson sick in his office—really sick, pale as his own pale hair and shaking all over. Michaelis advised him to go to bed, but Wilson refused, saying that he’d miss a lot of business if he did. While his neighbour was trying to persuade him a violent racket broke out overhead.","sentences":[{"en":"The young Greek, Michaelis, who ran the coffee joint beside the ash-heaps was the principal witness at the inquest.","zh":"警方前来盘问时的主要目击证人是米迦勒斯，这个年轻的希腊人在垃圾场旁边经营一家咖啡馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had slept through the heat until after five, when he strolled over to the garage, and found George Wilson sick in his office—really sick, pale as his own pale hair and shaking all over.","zh":"那天他在闷热中睡到下午五点才起床，然后漫步走到汽修厂，发现乔治·威尔逊病恹恹地坐在账房里——病得很厉害，脸色像他的头发那般苍白，而且浑身发抖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Michaelis advised him to go to bed, but Wilson refused, saying that he’d miss a lot of business if he did.","zh":"米迦勒斯建议他上床休息，但威尔逊不肯接受，他说去休息会少做很多生意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"While his neighbour was trying to persuade him a violent racket broke out overhead.","zh":"他的邻居正在进行劝说时，楼上传来激烈的吵闹声。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve got my wife locked in up there,” explained Wilson calmly. “She’s going to stay there till the day after tomorrow, and then we’re going to move away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve got my wife locked in up there,” explained Wilson calmly.","zh":"“我把我太太关在楼上了，”威尔逊冷静地说，“她会在那里待到后天，然后我们就离开这里。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She’s going to stay there till the day after tomorrow, and then we’re going to move away.”","zh":"“我把我太太关在楼上了，”威尔逊冷静地说，“她会在那里待到后天，然后我们就离开这里。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Michaelis was astonished; they had been neighbours for four years, and Wilson had never seemed faintly capable of such a statement. Generally he was one of these worn-out men: when he wasn’t working, he sat on a chair in the doorway and stared at the people and the cars that passed along the road. When anyone spoke to him he invariably laughed in an agreeable, colourless way. He was his wife’s man and not his own.","sentences":[{"en":"Michaelis was astonished; they had been neighbours for four years, and Wilson had never seemed faintly capable of such a statement.","zh":"米迦勒斯目瞪口呆；他们做了四年邻居，威尔逊半点也不像是会说出这番话的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Generally he was one of these worn-out men: when he wasn’t working, he sat on a chair in the doorway and stared at the people and the cars that passed along the road.","zh":"平常他总是忙得筋疲力尽，在不干活的时候，他会搬张椅子坐在门口，望着路上过往的行人和车辆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When anyone spoke to him he invariably laughed in an agreeable, colourless way.","zh":"每当有人跟他说话，他总是无精打采地笑笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was his wife’s man and not his own.","zh":"他什么事都听老婆的，从不自己做主。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"So naturally Michaelis tried to find out what had happened, but Wilson wouldn’t say a word—instead he began to throw curious, suspicious glances at his visitor and ask him what he’d been doing at certain times on certain days. Just as the latter was getting uneasy, some workmen came past the door bound for his restaurant, and Michaelis took the opportunity to get away, intending to come back later. But he didn’t. He supposed he forgot to, that’s all. When he came outside again, a little after seven, he was reminded of the conversation because he heard Mrs. Wilson’s voice, loud and scolding, downstairs in the garage.","sentences":[{"en":"So naturally Michaelis tried to find out what had happened, but Wilson wouldn’t say a word—instead he began to throw curious, suspicious glances at his visitor and ask him what he’d been doing at certain times on certain days.","zh":"所以米迦勒斯自然想弄清到底怎么回事，但威尔逊什么都不肯说——反倒开始疑神疑鬼地审视他的邻居，盘问他在某日某时做了什么事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just as the latter was getting uneasy, some workmen came past the door bound for his restaurant, and Michaelis took the opportunity to get away, intending to come back later.","zh":"米迦勒斯越听越不自在，这时正好有几个工人从门口向他的餐馆走去，他赶紧趁机告辞，想着过会再回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he didn’t.","zh":"但他没有回去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He supposed he forgot to, that’s all.","zh":"他说他只是忘记了，没有别的原因。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he came outside again, a little after seven, he was reminded of the conversation because he heard Mrs. Wilson’s voice, loud and scolding, downstairs in the garage.","zh":"他七点过后又走到外面，并想起了刚才的对话，因为他听见威尔逊太太的声音，在汽修厂楼下破口大骂。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Beat me!” he heard her cry. “Throw me down and beat me, you dirty little coward!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Beat me!” he heard her cry.","zh":"“你打我啊！”他听见她喊，“把我扔下楼啊，你打我啊，你这个肮脏的懦夫！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Throw me down and beat me, you dirty little coward!”","zh":"“你打我啊！”他听见她喊，“把我扔下楼啊，你打我啊，你这个肮脏的懦夫！”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A moment later she rushed out into the dusk, waving her hands and shouting—before he could move from his door the business was over.","sentences":[{"en":"A moment later she rushed out into the dusk, waving her hands and shouting—before he could move from his door the business was over.","zh":"她随即冲进夜幕之中，挥舞着双手，嘴里大喊大叫——他还没来得及离开自己的门口，惨剧已经发生了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The “death car” as the newspapers called it, didn’t stop; it came out of the gathering darkness, wavered tragically for a moment, and then disappeared around the next bend. Mavro Michaelis wasn’t even sure of its colour—he told the first policeman that it was light green. The other car, the one going toward New York, came to rest a hundred yards beyond, and its driver hurried back to where Myrtle Wilson, her life violently extinguished, knelt in the road and mingled her thick dark blood with the dust.","sentences":[{"en":"The “death car” as the newspapers called it, didn’t stop; it came out of the gathering darkness, wavered tragically for a moment, and then disappeared around the next bend.","zh":"那辆“死亡之车”——报纸是这么称呼它的——并没有停下来，它从渐浓的夜色里冲出来，肇事后稍微减缓了车速，然后拐了个弯就消失得无影无踪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mavro Michaelis wasn’t even sure of its colour—he told the first policeman that it was light green.","zh":"玛福罗·米迦勒斯甚至连车身什么颜色都没看清——他对第一个警察说是浅绿色的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The other car, the one going toward New York, came to rest a hundred yards beyond, and its driver hurried back to where Myrtle Wilson, her life violently extinguished, knelt in the road and mingled her thick dark blood with the dust.","zh":"另外一辆前往纽约的轿车在开出上百码之后停住，开车的人匆匆回到梅朵·威尔逊身边，这时她已经被撞得当场毙命，扑倒在路上，浓稠的黑血和尘土混在一起。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Michaelis and this man reached her first, but when they had torn open her shirtwaist, still damp with perspiration, they saw that her left breast was swinging loose like a flap, and there was no need to listen for the heart beneath. The mouth was wide open and ripped a little at the corners, as though she had choked a little in giving up the tremendous vitality she had stored so long.","sentences":[{"en":"Michaelis and this man reached her first, but when they had torn open her shirtwaist, still damp with perspiration, they saw that her left breast was swinging loose like a flap, and there was no need to listen for the heart beneath.","zh":"米迦勒斯和这个人最先赶到她身旁，可是撕开她仍然汗津津的衬衣之后，他们发现她左边的乳房已经和身体分开，摇摇晃晃地挂着，没有必要再去听她的心跳了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The mouth was wide open and ripped a little at the corners, as though she had choked a little in giving up the tremendous vitality she had stored so long.","zh":"她的嘴巴张得很开，嘴角有点裂开，仿佛是被她毕生积蓄的巨大活力冲出来时划破的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"We saw the three or four automobiles and the crowd when we were still some distance away.","sentences":[{"en":"We saw the three or four automobiles and the crowd when we were still some distance away.","zh":"看到三四辆轿车和围观的人群时，我们还隔得很远。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wreck!” said Tom. “That’s good. Wilson’ll have a little business at last.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wreck!” said Tom.","zh":"“车祸！”汤姆说，“那很好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“That’s good.","zh":"“车祸！”汤姆说，“那很好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Wilson’ll have a little business at last.”","zh":"威尔逊总算有生意可做了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He slowed down, but still without any intention of stopping, until, as we came nearer, the hushed, intent faces of the people at the garage door made him automatically put on the brakes.","sentences":[{"en":"He slowed down, but still without any intention of stopping, until, as we came nearer, the hushed, intent faces of the people at the garage door made him automatically put on the brakes.","zh":"他减缓了车速，但仍然完全没有停车的打算，后来开到近处，看见汽修厂门口许多肃穆专注的脸庞，他才不自觉地踩下了刹车。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ll take a look,” he said doubtfully, “just a look.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ll take a look,” he said doubtfully, “just a look.”","zh":"“我们看看怎么回事，”他有点狐疑，“看看就走。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I became aware now of a hollow, wailing sound which issued incessantly from the garage, a sound which as we got out of the coupé and walked toward the door resolved itself into the words “Oh, my God!” uttered over and over in a gasping moan.","sentences":[{"en":"I became aware now of a hollow, wailing sound which issued incessantly from the garage, a sound which as we got out of the coupé and walked toward the door resolved itself into the words “Oh, my God!” uttered over and over in a gasping moan.","zh":"这时我听见汽修厂不停地传出一阵含混的哀嚎。我们下了跑车，向汽修厂门口走过去，这时才听清原来是有人哭得上气不接下气，反反复复地喊着“我的上帝啊！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There’s some bad trouble here,” said Tom excitedly.","sentences":[{"en":"“There’s some bad trouble here,” said Tom excitedly.","zh":"“看来出大事了，”汤姆兴奋地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He reached up on tiptoes and peered over a circle of heads into the garage, which was lit only by a yellow light in a swinging metal basket overhead. Then he made a harsh sound in his throat, and with a violent thrusting movement of his powerful arms pushed his way through.","sentences":[{"en":"He reached up on tiptoes and peered over a circle of heads into the garage, which was lit only by a yellow light in a swinging metal basket overhead.","zh":"他踮起脚尖，隔着前面的人头向汽修厂里面望去，那里只亮着一盏昏黄的电灯，挂在摇摇晃晃的铁丝罩里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he made a harsh sound in his throat, and with a violent thrusting movement of his powerful arms pushed his way through.","zh":"然后他发出一声惊呼，强壮的双手猛地左右开路，拨动人群钻了进去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The circle closed up again with a running murmur of expostulation; it was a minute before I could see anything at all. Then new arrivals deranged the line, and Jordan and I were pushed suddenly inside.","sentences":[{"en":"The circle closed up again with a running murmur of expostulation; it was a minute before I could see anything at all.","zh":"围观的人群骂骂咧咧，很快又合上了，我根本来不及看清里面的情况。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then new arrivals deranged the line, and Jordan and I were pushed suddenly inside.","zh":"然后又有新来者把圈子打破，我和乔丹突然被挤了进去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Myrtle Wilson’s body, wrapped in a blanket, and then in another blanket, as though she suffered from a chill in the hot night, lay on a worktable by the wall, and Tom, with his back to us, was bending over it, motionless. Next to him stood a motorcycle policeman taking down names with much sweat and correction in a little book. At first I couldn’t find the source of the high, groaning words that echoed clamorously through the bare garage—then I saw Wilson standing on the raised threshold of his office, swaying back and forth and holding to the doorposts with both hands. Some man was talking to him in a low voice and attempting, from time to time, to lay a hand on his shoulder, but Wilson neither heard nor saw. His eyes would drop slowly from the swinging light to the laden table by the wall, and then jerk back to the light again, and he gave out incessantly his high, horrible call:","sentences":[{"en":"Myrtle Wilson’s body, wrapped in a blanket, and then in another blanket, as though she suffered from a chill in the hot night, lay on a worktable by the wall, and Tom, with his back to us, was bending over it, motionless.","zh":"梅朵·威尔逊的尸体裹着毛毯，然后外面又包着毛毯，仿佛在这个炎热的夜晚她还着了凉。尸体摆在墙边的工作台上，汤姆背对着我们，弯腰看着它，浑身纹丝不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Next to him stood a motorcycle policeman taking down names with much sweat and correction in a little book.","zh":"站在他身边的是一位巡警，他满头大汗，拿着小本子涂涂改改地记录着人名。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At first I couldn’t find the source of the high, groaning words that echoed clamorously through the bare garage—then I saw Wilson standing on the raised threshold of his office, swaying back and forth and holding to the doorposts with both hands.","zh":"那撕心裂肺的哭喊声在四壁萧然的汽修厂里面来回激荡，起初我找不到它的来源——然后我看见威尔逊站在比外面高出一节的账房门槛上，双手抓住门框，哭得前俯后仰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some man was talking to him in a low voice and attempting, from time to time, to lay a hand on his shoulder, but Wilson neither heard nor saw.","zh":"有个人正在轻轻地跟他说话，时不时伸手去拍拍他的肩膀，但威尔逊不听也不看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His eyes would drop slowly from the swinging light to the laden table by the wall, and then jerk back to the light again, and he gave out incessantly his high, horrible call:","zh":"他的眼睛慢慢地从摇晃的电灯往下看到墙边摆放着尸体的工作台，跟着又突然朝上看着电灯，片刻不停地、痛不欲生地哀嚎着：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, my Ga-od! Oh, my Ga-od! Oh, Ga-od! Oh, my Ga-od!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, my Ga-od!","zh":"“我的上——帝啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, my Ga-od!","zh":"我的上——帝啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, Ga-od!","zh":"我的上——帝啊！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, my Ga-od!”","zh":"我的上——帝啊！”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Presently Tom lifted his head with a jerk and, after staring around the garage with glazed eyes, addressed a mumbled incoherent remark to the policeman.","sentences":[{"en":"Presently Tom lifted his head with a jerk and, after staring around the garage with glazed eyes, addressed a mumbled incoherent remark to the policeman.","zh":"这时汤姆突然抬起头来，茫然地扫视了汽修厂之后，含含糊糊地对那警察说了几个字。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“M-a-v—” the policeman was saying, “—o—”","sentences":[{"en":"“M-a-v—” the policeman was saying, “—o—”","zh":"“玛——”那警察正在说着，“——佛…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, r—” corrected the man, “M-a-v-r-o—”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, r—” corrected the man, “M-a-v-r-o—”","zh":"“不对，是福，”希腊人纠正他说，“玛福罗…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Listen to me!” muttered Tom fiercely.","sentences":[{"en":"“Listen to me!” muttered Tom fiercely.","zh":"“我跟你说话呢！”汤姆厉声说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“r—” said the policeman, “o—”","sentences":[{"en":"“r—” said the policeman, “o—”","zh":"“福——”警察说，“——罗…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“g—”","sentences":[{"en":"“g—”","zh":"“希——”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“g—” He looked up as Tom’s broad hand fell sharply on his shoulder. “What you want, fella?”","sentences":[{"en":"“g—” He looked up as Tom’s broad hand fell sharply on his shoulder.","zh":"“希——”这时汤姆的大手猛拍了拍他的肩膀，于是他抬起头问，“你想干什么，伙计？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What you want, fella?”","zh":"“希——”这时汤姆的大手猛拍了拍他的肩膀，于是他抬起头问，“你想干什么，伙计？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What happened?—that’s what I want to know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What happened?—that’s what I want to know.”","zh":"“怎么回事？——我想知道。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Auto hit her. Ins’antly killed.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Auto hit her.","zh":"“她被车撞了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ins’antly killed.”","zh":"当场撞死。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Instantly killed,” repeated Tom, staring.","sentences":[{"en":"“Instantly killed,” repeated Tom, staring.","zh":"“当场撞死，”汤姆呆呆地重复着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She ran out ina road. Son-of-a-bitch didn’t even stopus car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She ran out ina road.","zh":"“她跑到马路中间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Son-of-a-bitch didn’t even stopus car.”","zh":"那婊子养的连停都不停一下。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There was two cars,” said Michaelis, “one comin’, one goin’, see?”","sentences":[{"en":"“There was two cars,” said Michaelis, “one comin’, one goin’, see?”","zh":"“有两辆车，”米迦勒斯说，“一辆开过来，一辆开过去，明白了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Going where?” asked the policeman keenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Going where?” asked the policeman keenly.","zh":"“往哪个方向开？”警察机灵地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“One goin’ each way. Well, she”—his hand rose toward the blankets but stopped halfway and fell to his side—“she ran out there an’ the one comin’ from N’York knock right into her, goin’ thirty or forty miles an hour.”","sentences":[{"en":"“One goin’ each way.","zh":"“两辆是对开的啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, she”—his hand rose toward the blankets but stopped halfway and fell to his side—“she ran out there an’ the one comin’ from N’York knock right into her, goin’ thirty or forty miles an hour.”","zh":"是这样的，她”——他的手抬起来向毛毯指去，但半途又停住，掉到他身边——“她冲出去，从纽约开来的那辆车把她撞了个正着，时速估计有三十到四十英里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s the name of this place here?” demanded the officer.","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the name of this place here?” demanded the officer.","zh":"“这个地方叫什么名字？”警察问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hasn’t got any name.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hasn’t got any name.”","zh":"“这里没有名字。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A pale well-dressed negro stepped near.","sentences":[{"en":"A pale well-dressed negro stepped near.","zh":"有个肤色较浅、穿着很讲究的黑人走过来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was a yellow car,” he said, “big yellow car. New.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was a yellow car,” he said, “big yellow car.","zh":"“那辆车是黄色的，”他说，“很大的黄色轿车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"New.”","zh":"是新的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“See the accident?” asked the policeman.","sentences":[{"en":"“See the accident?” asked the policeman.","zh":"“你看到事故了吗？”警察问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, but the car passed me down the road, going faster’n forty. Going fifty, sixty.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, but the car passed me down the road, going faster’n forty.","zh":"“没有，但那辆车后来从我边上开过，我看时速不止四十英里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Going fifty, sixty.”","zh":"五六十英里都有了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Come here and let’s have your name. Look out now. I want to get his name.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come here and let’s have your name.","zh":"“到这里来，让我们记下你的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Look out now.","zh":"让开点。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I want to get his name.”","zh":"我要记下他的名字。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Some words of this conversation must have reached Wilson, swaying in the office door, for suddenly a new theme found voice among his grasping cries:","sentences":[{"en":"Some words of this conversation must have reached Wilson, swaying in the office door, for suddenly a new theme found voice among his grasping cries:","zh":"这番谈话中有几个字肯定被正在账房门口前后摇摆着的威尔逊听到了，因为突然间，他呼天抢地的哭喊有了新的内容：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You don’t have to tell me what kind of car it was! I know what kind of car it was!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You don’t have to tell me what kind of car it was!","zh":"“不用你们来告诉我那辆车是什么样子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I know what kind of car it was!”","zh":"我知道那辆车是什么样子！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Watching Tom, I saw the wad of muscle back of his shoulder tighten under his coat. He walked quickly over to Wilson and, standing in front of him, seized him firmly by the upper arms.","sentences":[{"en":"Watching Tom, I saw the wad of muscle back of his shoulder tighten under his coat.","zh":"我看着汤姆，发现他肩后的肌肉在外套下面收缩了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He walked quickly over to Wilson and, standing in front of him, seized him firmly by the upper arms.","zh":"他赶紧向威尔逊走过去，站到他面前，用力地抓住他的上臂。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’ve got to pull yourself together,” he said with soothing gruffness.","sentences":[{"en":"“You’ve got to pull yourself together,” he said with soothing gruffness.","zh":"“你要振作起来，”他用粗豪的声音安慰地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Wilson’s eyes fell upon Tom; he started up on his tiptoes and then would have collapsed to his knees had not Tom held him upright.","sentences":[{"en":"Wilson’s eyes fell upon Tom; he started up on his tiptoes and then would have collapsed to his knees had not Tom held him upright.","zh":"威尔逊看到是汤姆，惊得脚尖都踮起来了，接着又双腿发软，差点瘫倒在地，幸亏汤姆把他扶住了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Listen,” said Tom, shaking him a little. “I just got here a minute ago, from New York. I was bringing you that coupé we’ve been talking about. That yellow car I was driving this afternoon wasn’t mine—do you hear? I haven’t seen it all afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Listen,” said Tom, shaking him a little.","zh":"“听着，”汤姆轻轻地摇着他说，“我一分钟前刚从纽约来到这里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I just got here a minute ago, from New York.","zh":"“听着，”汤姆轻轻地摇着他说，“我一分钟前刚从纽约来到这里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I was bringing you that coupé we’ve been talking about.","zh":"我把前面我们谈到的那辆跑车开过来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That yellow car I was driving this afternoon wasn’t mine—do you hear?","zh":"今天下午那辆黄色的轿车不是我的——你听到了吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I haven’t seen it all afternoon.”","zh":"我整个下午都没有看到它。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Only the negro and I were near enough to hear what he said, but the policeman caught something in the tone and looked over with truculent eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"Only the negro and I were near enough to hear what he said, but the policeman caught something in the tone and looked over with truculent eyes.","zh":"只有那个黑人和我站得足够近，能听清他说的话，但那警察发觉汤姆的语气有点不对劲，于是把严厉的眼光投过来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s all that?” he demanded.","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s all that?” he demanded.","zh":"“怎么回事？”他质问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m a friend of his.” Tom turned his head but kept his hands firm on Wilson’s body. “He says he knows the car that did it… It was a yellow car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m a friend of his.”","zh":"“我是他的朋友，”汤姆转过头说，但他的双手依然紧紧地扶着威尔逊的身体，“他说他认得那辆肇事的车…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Tom turned his head but kept his hands firm on Wilson’s body.","zh":"“我是他的朋友，”汤姆转过头说，但他的双手依然紧紧地扶着威尔逊的身体，“他说他认得那辆肇事的车…","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He says he knows the car that did it…","zh":"“我是他的朋友，”汤姆转过头说，但他的双手依然紧紧地扶着威尔逊的身体，“他说他认得那辆肇事的车…","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was a yellow car.”","zh":"那是一辆黄色的轿车。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Some dim impulse moved the policeman to look suspiciously at Tom.","sentences":[{"en":"Some dim impulse moved the policeman to look suspiciously at Tom.","zh":"那警察隐隐觉得有点蹊跷，于是怀疑地看着汤姆。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And what colour’s your car?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And what colour’s your car?”","zh":"“你的车是什么颜色？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s a blue car, a coupé.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s a blue car, a coupé.”","zh":"“蓝色的，是跑车。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We’ve come straight from New York,” I said.","sentences":[{"en":"“We’ve come straight from New York,” I said.","zh":"“我们刚从纽约过来，”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Someone who had been driving a little behind us confirmed this, and the policeman turned away.","sentences":[{"en":"Someone who had been driving a little behind us confirmed this, and the policeman turned away.","zh":"有个人刚才开车跟在我们后面，他证实了我的话，于是警察又转过身去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Now, if you’ll let me have that name again correct—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now, if you’ll let me have that name again correct—”","zh":"“来，看看你的名字有没有写对…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Picking up Wilson like a doll, Tom carried him into the office, set him down in a chair, and came back.","sentences":[{"en":"Picking up Wilson like a doll, Tom carried him into the office, set him down in a chair, and came back.","zh":"汤姆像提着玩具般把威尔逊提进账房，安排他坐在椅子上，然后走回来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“If somebody’ll come here and sit with him,” he snapped authoritatively. He watched while the two men standing closest glanced at each other and went unwillingly into the room. Then Tom shut the door on them and came down the single step, his eyes avoiding the table. As he passed close to me he whispered: “Let’s get out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If somebody’ll come here and sit with him,” he snapped authoritatively.","zh":"“就没有人过来照顾他吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He watched while the two men standing closest glanced at each other and went unwillingly into the room.","zh":"他威严地盯着两个站得最近的人说。他们彼此对视，不情不愿地走进了账房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Tom shut the door on them and came down the single step, his eyes avoiding the table.","zh":"汤姆等他们进去就把门关上，踏下那一级台阶，刻意不去看那张工作台。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he passed close to me he whispered: “Let’s get out.”","zh":"经过我身边时，他低声说：“我们走吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Self-consciously, with his authoritative arms breaking the way, we pushed through the still gathering crowd, passing a hurried doctor, case in hand, who had been sent for in wild hope half an hour ago.","sentences":[{"en":"Self-consciously, with his authoritative arms breaking the way, we pushed through the still gathering crowd, passing a hurried doctor, case in hand, who had been sent for in wild hope half an hour ago.","zh":"他有点不自在，那双权威的胳膊把仍在围观的人群推开，我们跟着走了出去。这时正好有个行色匆匆的医生走过来，他手里提着药箱，这是半小时前有人情急之下去请来的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Tom drove slowly until we were beyond the bend—then his foot came down hard, and the coupé raced along through the night. In a little while I heard a low husky sob, and saw that the tears were overflowing down his face.","sentences":[{"en":"Tom drove slowly until we were beyond the bend—then his foot came down hard, and the coupé raced along through the night.","zh":"汤姆开得很慢，直到我们过了弯道——然后他的脚猛踩油门，跑车飞也似的在夜色里穿行。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In a little while I heard a low husky sob, and saw that the tears were overflowing down his face.","zh":"顷刻间我听到一阵粗哑的哽噎声，看到泪水在他脸上滚滚而下。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The God damned coward!” he whimpered. “He didn’t even stop his car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The God damned coward!” he whimpered.","zh":"“那该死的懦夫！”他咒骂说，“他连把车停下都不敢。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He didn’t even stop his car.”","zh":"“那该死的懦夫！”他咒骂说，“他连把车停下都不敢。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"The Buchanans’ house floated suddenly toward us through the dark rustling trees. Tom stopped beside the porch and looked up at the second floor, where two windows bloomed with light among the vines.","sentences":[{"en":"The Buchanans’ house floated suddenly toward us through the dark rustling trees.","zh":"布坎南公馆突然浮现在我们面前，周围是黝黑而萧瑟的树木。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tom stopped beside the porch and looked up at the second floor, where two windows bloomed with light among the vines.","zh":"汤姆把车停在门廊旁边，抬头望着二楼，但见葡萄藤中有两个窗户灯火通明。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Daisy’s home,” he said. As we got out of the car he glanced at me and frowned slightly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Daisy’s home,” he said.","zh":"“黛熙到家了，”他说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As we got out of the car he glanced at me and frowned slightly.","zh":"我们下车时，他瞟了我一眼，轻轻地皱起眉头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I ought to have dropped you in West Egg, Nick. There’s nothing we can do tonight.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I ought to have dropped you in West Egg, Nick.","zh":"“我应该在西卵让你下车的，尼克。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There’s nothing we can do tonight.”","zh":"今晚我们没有事可做了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A change had come over him, and he spoke gravely, and with decision. As we walked across the moonlight gravel to the porch he disposed of the situation in a few brisk phrases.","sentences":[{"en":"A change had come over him, and he spoke gravely, and with decision.","zh":"他整个人都变了，说话很严肃，口气也特别坚决。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As we walked across the moonlight gravel to the porch he disposed of the situation in a few brisk phrases.","zh":"我们在月光中沿着碎石路走到门廊，他仅用三言两语就化解了这个难题。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll telephone for a taxi to take you home, and while you’re waiting you and Jordan better go in the kitchen and have them get you some supper—if you want any.” He opened the door. “Come in.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll telephone for a taxi to take you home, and while you’re waiting you and Jordan better go in the kitchen and have them get you some supper—if you want any.”","zh":"“我打电话叫出租车来送你回家，等车来的时候，你和乔丹最好到厨房去，让佣人给你们弄点晚饭吃——假如你们想吃的话。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He opened the door.","zh":"他打开门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Come in.”","zh":"“进来吧。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, thanks. But I’d be glad if you’d order me the taxi. I’ll wait outside.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, thanks.","zh":"“我不进去了，谢谢。那就麻烦你帮我叫出租车吧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But I’d be glad if you’d order me the taxi.","zh":"“我不进去了，谢谢。那就麻烦你帮我叫出租车吧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll wait outside.”","zh":"我在外面等就好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Jordan put her hand on my arm.","sentences":[{"en":"Jordan put her hand on my arm.","zh":"乔丹拉住我的手臂。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Won’t you come in, Nick?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Won’t you come in, Nick?”","zh":"“你就不进来了吗，尼克？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No, thanks.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, thanks.”","zh":"“不啦，谢谢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was feeling a little sick and I wanted to be alone. But Jordan lingered for a moment more.","sentences":[{"en":"I was feeling a little sick and I wanted to be alone.","zh":"我心里有点不舒服，想要一个人待着。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Jordan lingered for a moment more.","zh":"但乔丹又逗留了片刻。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s only half-past nine,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s only half-past nine,” she said.","zh":"“现在才九点半，”她说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I’d be damned if I’d go in; I’d had enough of all of them for one day, and suddenly that included Jordan too. She must have seen something of this in my expression, for she turned abruptly away and ran up the porch steps into the house. I sat down for a few minutes with my head in my hands, until I heard the phone taken up inside and the butler’s voice calling a taxi. Then I walked slowly down the drive away from the house, intending to wait by the gate.","sentences":[{"en":"I’d be damned if I’d go in; I’d had enough of all of them for one day, and suddenly that included Jordan too.","zh":"我宁可被打死也不愿进去，这些人的嘴脸我今天已经看够了，突然间那也包括乔丹在内。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She must have seen something of this in my expression, for she turned abruptly away and ran up the porch steps into the house.","zh":"她肯定从我的脸色上看到了什么，因为她猛地转过身去，快步登上门廊的台阶，走进了屋里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I sat down for a few minutes with my head in my hands, until I heard the phone taken up inside and the butler’s voice calling a taxi.","zh":"我双手抱头坐了几分钟，然后听到里面有人打电话，是那管家在叫出租车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then I walked slowly down the drive away from the house, intending to wait by the gate.","zh":"于是我慢慢地沿着车道走开，远离那座房子，打算到门口去等。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I hadn’t gone twenty yards when I heard my name and Gatsby stepped from between two bushes into the path. I must have felt pretty weird by that time, because I could think of nothing except the luminosity of his pink suit under the moon.","sentences":[{"en":"I hadn’t gone twenty yards when I heard my name and Gatsby stepped from between two bushes into the path.","zh":"走不到二十码，我听见有人喊我的名字，盖茨比从两株灌木之后现身，踏进了车道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I must have felt pretty weird by that time, because I could think of nothing except the luminosity of his pink suit under the moon.","zh":"我当时肯定觉得特别怪异，因为我现在还能想起来他那套粉红色西装在月光下闪闪发光的样子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What are you doing?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“What are you doing?”","zh":"“你在干什么？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Just standing here, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Just standing here, old sport.”","zh":"“就是站在这里，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Somehow, that seemed a despicable occupation. For all I knew he was going to rob the house in a moment; I wouldn’t have been surprised to see sinister faces, the faces of “Wolfshiem’s people,” behind him in the dark shrubbery.","sentences":[{"en":"Somehow, that seemed a despicable occupation.","zh":"反正那看起来像是不可告人的勾当。因为我总觉得他就要去洗劫这家人，就算他身后的灌木丛露出许多邪恶的脸，“沃夫希姆的手下”的脸，我也不会感到意外。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For all I knew he was going to rob the house in a moment; I wouldn’t have been surprised to see sinister faces, the faces of “Wolfshiem’s people,” behind him in the dark shrubbery.","zh":"反正那看起来像是不可告人的勾当。因为我总觉得他就要去洗劫这家人，就算他身后的灌木丛露出许多邪恶的脸，“沃夫希姆的手下”的脸，我也不会感到意外。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you see any trouble on the road?” he asked after a minute.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you see any trouble on the road?” he asked after a minute.","zh":"“你在路上看到什么麻烦事了吗？”他隔了半晌问。“是的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"他欲言又止。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He hesitated.","sentences":[{"en":"He hesitated.","zh":"他欲言又止。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Was she killed?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Was she killed?”","zh":"“她死了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“死了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I thought so; I told Daisy I thought so. It’s better that the shock should all come at once. She stood it pretty well.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought so; I told Daisy I thought so.","zh":"“我想也是，我跟黛熙说那人肯定被撞死了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s better that the shock should all come at once.","zh":"先让她有个心理准备比较好，免得到时她会太过吃惊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She stood it pretty well.”","zh":"但她倒是表现得很勇敢。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He spoke as if Daisy’s reaction was the only thing that mattered.","sentences":[{"en":"He spoke as if Daisy’s reaction was the only thing that mattered.","zh":"听他的口气，好像黛熙的反应才是最重要的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I got to West Egg by a side road,” he went on, “and left the car in my garage. I don’t think anybody saw us, but of course I can’t be sure.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I got to West Egg by a side road,” he went on, “and left the car in my garage.","zh":"“我抄小路回了西卵，”他继续说，“把车停在我的车库里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t think anybody saw us, but of course I can’t be sure.”","zh":"我想应该没有人看见我们，但我也不能确定。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I disliked him so much by this time that I didn’t find it necessary to tell him he was wrong.","sentences":[{"en":"I disliked him so much by this time that I didn’t find it necessary to tell him he was wrong.","zh":"这时我已经极其讨厌他，所以觉得没有必要指出他错了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who was the woman?” he inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Who was the woman?” he inquired.","zh":"“那女人是谁？”他问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Her name was Wilson. Her husband owns the garage. How the devil did it happen?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Her name was Wilson.","zh":"“她姓威尔逊。她的丈夫是那家汽修厂的老板。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her husband owns the garage.","zh":"“她姓威尔逊。她的丈夫是那家汽修厂的老板。","scope":"group"},{"en":"How the devil did it happen?”","zh":"事情到底是怎么发生的？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I tried to swing the wheel—” He broke off, and suddenly I guessed at the truth.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I tried to swing the wheel—” He broke off, and suddenly I guessed at the truth.","zh":"“哎，我想把方向盘抢过来——”他的话音戛然而止，突然间我猜到了真相。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Was Daisy driving?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Was Daisy driving?”","zh":"“车是黛熙开的？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes,” he said after a moment, “but of course I’ll say I was. You see, when we left New York she was very nervous and she thought it would steady her to drive—and this woman rushed out at us just as we were passing a car coming the other way. It all happened in a minute, but it seemed to me that she wanted to speak to us, thought we were somebody she knew. Well, first Daisy turned away from the woman toward the other car, and then she lost her nerve and turned back. The second my hand reached the wheel I felt the shock—it must have killed her instantly.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” he said after a moment, “but of course I’ll say I was.","zh":"“是的，”他沉默片刻之后说，“但我当然会说是我开的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You see, when we left New York she was very nervous and she thought it would steady her to drive—and this woman rushed out at us just as we were passing a car coming the other way.","zh":"是这样的，我们离开纽约时，她非常紧张，她觉得开车能让情绪镇定下来——这个女人冲出来的时候，我们正好和对面一辆车擦身而过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It all happened in a minute, but it seemed to me that she wanted to speak to us, thought we were somebody she knew.","zh":"事情发生得太快，但我觉得她似乎是想要跟我们说话，好像我们是她认识的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, first Daisy turned away from the woman toward the other car, and then she lost her nerve and turned back.","zh":"哎，黛熙起初打了方向盘想避开那个女人，但看到对面的车就要撞上来，她吓得又把方向盘打回去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The second my hand reached the wheel I felt the shock—it must have killed her instantly.”","zh":"在伸手去抓方向盘的刹那间，我感到车身一震——肯定当场就把她撞死了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It ripped her open—”","sentences":[{"en":"“It ripped her open—”","zh":"“把她胸口撞开一个大洞…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t tell me, old sport.” He winced. “Anyhow—Daisy stepped on it. I tried to make her stop, but she couldn’t, so I pulled on the emergency brake. Then she fell over into my lap and I drove on.","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t tell me, old sport.”","zh":"“别说了，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He winced.","zh":"他畏缩地说，“反正——黛熙拼命地踩油门。我让她停车，但她不肯，所以我拉动了手刹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Anyhow—Daisy stepped on it.","zh":"他畏缩地说，“反正——黛熙拼命地踩油门。我让她停车，但她不肯，所以我拉动了手刹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I tried to make her stop, but she couldn’t, so I pulled on the emergency brake.","zh":"他畏缩地说，“反正——黛熙拼命地踩油门。我让她停车，但她不肯，所以我拉动了手刹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she fell over into my lap and I drove on.","zh":"然后她昏倒在我膝盖上，我就把车开走了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’ll be all right tomorrow,” he said presently. “I’m just going to wait here and see if he tries to bother her about that unpleasantness this afternoon. She’s locked herself into her room, and if he tries any brutality she’s going to turn the light out and on again.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’ll be all right tomorrow,” he said presently.","zh":"“她明天就没事啦，”他随即又说，“我只是想在这里守着，看他会不会因为下午不愉快的事情而怪罪她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m just going to wait here and see if he tries to bother her about that unpleasantness this afternoon.","zh":"“她明天就没事啦，”他随即又说，“我只是想在这里守着，看他会不会因为下午不愉快的事情而怪罪她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She’s locked herself into her room, and if he tries any brutality she’s going to turn the light out and on again.”","zh":"她把自己的房间锁起来了，如果他准备动粗，她就会把灯关掉再打开。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He won’t touch her,” I said. “He’s not thinking about her.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He won’t touch her,” I said.","zh":"“他不会碰她的，”我说，“他现在脑子里没空想她。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He’s not thinking about her.”","zh":"“他不会碰她的，”我说，“他现在脑子里没空想她。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t trust him, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t trust him, old sport.”","zh":"“我信不过他，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How long are you going to wait?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How long are you going to wait?”","zh":"“你准备等多久？”“有必要的话我会等到天亮。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“All night, if necessary. Anyhow, till they all go to bed.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All night, if necessary.","zh":"“你准备等多久？”“有必要的话我会等到天亮。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Anyhow, till they all go to bed.”","zh":"反正要等到他们都上床睡觉。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A new point of view occurred to me. Suppose Tom found out that Daisy had been driving. He might think he saw a connection in it—he might think anything. I looked at the house; there were two or three bright windows downstairs and the pink glow from Daisy’s room on the ground floor.","sentences":[{"en":"A new point of view occurred to me.","zh":"这时我突然有个新的想法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suppose Tom found out that Daisy had been driving.","zh":"假设汤姆发现开车的人是黛熙，他可能会怀疑这里面有阴谋——他可能会胡乱猜测。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He might think he saw a connection in it—he might think anything.","zh":"假设汤姆发现开车的人是黛熙，他可能会怀疑这里面有阴谋——他可能会胡乱猜测。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I looked at the house; there were two or three bright windows downstairs and the pink glow from Daisy’s room on the ground floor.","zh":"我向那座房子望去，楼下两三个宽敞的窗户亮着灯，黛熙在二楼的卧房透出粉红的光线。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You wait here,” I said. “I’ll see if there’s any sign of a commotion.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You wait here,” I said.","zh":"“你在这里等着，”我说，“我去看看有没有吵架的迹象。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll see if there’s any sign of a commotion.”","zh":"“你在这里等着，”我说，“我去看看有没有吵架的迹象。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I walked back along the border of the lawn, traversed the gravel softly, and tiptoed up the veranda steps. The drawing-room curtains were open, and I saw that the room was empty. Crossing the porch where we had dined that June night three months before, I came to a small rectangle of light which I guessed was the pantry window. The blind was drawn, but I found a rift at the sill.","sentences":[{"en":"I walked back along the border of the lawn, traversed the gravel softly, and tiptoed up the veranda steps.","zh":"我沿着草坪边缘走回去，轻轻地踏过碎石路，踮起脚尖走上露台的台阶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The drawing-room curtains were open, and I saw that the room was empty.","zh":"客厅的窗帘是拉开的，我看到里面没有人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Crossing the porch where we had dined that June night three months before, I came to a small rectangle of light which I guessed was the pantry window.","zh":"我绕过三个月前那个六月晚上我们吃饭的餐厅外面的门廊，来到一小片长方形的光线下面，我猜透出灯光的窗户里面是厨房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The blind was drawn, but I found a rift at the sill.","zh":"百叶窗帘被拉起来了，但我发现窗台处有道缝隙。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Daisy and Tom were sitting opposite each other at the kitchen table, with a plate of cold fried chicken between them, and two bottles of ale. He was talking intently across the table at her, and in his earnestness his hand had fallen upon and covered her own. Once in a while she looked up at him and nodded in agreement.","sentences":[{"en":"Daisy and Tom were sitting opposite each other at the kitchen table, with a plate of cold fried chicken between them, and two bottles of ale.","zh":"黛熙和汤姆面对面地坐在厨房的桌子上，两人之间摆着一盘冷炸鸡，还有两瓶麦芽酒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was talking intently across the table at her, and in his earnestness his hand had fallen upon and covered her own.","zh":"他神情专注地朝桌子对面的她说话，说到动情之处，不由自主地拉住了黛熙的手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once in a while she looked up at him and nodded in agreement.","zh":"她时不时抬起眼看他，频频点头表示同意。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They weren’t happy, and neither of them had touched the chicken or the ale—and yet they weren’t unhappy either. There was an unmistakable air of natural intimacy about the picture, and anybody would have said that they were conspiring together.","sentences":[{"en":"They weren’t happy, and neither of them had touched the chicken or the ale—and yet they weren’t unhappy either.","zh":"他们看上去并不高兴，没有人去碰鸡肉或麦芽酒——但也不能说他们不高兴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was an unmistakable air of natural intimacy about the picture, and anybody would have said that they were conspiring together.","zh":"反正毋庸置疑的是，这个画面是很亲密温馨的，任谁看到了都会说他们是在推心置腹地密谋什么事情。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"As I tiptoed from the porch I heard my taxi feeling its way along the dark road toward the house. Gatsby was waiting where I had left him in the drive.","sentences":[{"en":"As I tiptoed from the porch I heard my taxi feeling its way along the dark road toward the house.","zh":"踮着脚尖离开门廊时，我听见出租车正在黑暗中向这座房子驶过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gatsby was waiting where I had left him in the drive.","zh":"盖茨比仍在车道上刚才那个地方等着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Is it all quiet up there?” he asked anxiously.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is it all quiet up there?” he asked anxiously.","zh":"“里面很安静吧？”他焦急地问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes, it’s all quiet.” I hesitated. “You’d better come home and get some sleep.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, it’s all quiet.”","zh":"“是的，很安静。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I hesitated.","zh":"我迟疑地说，“你还是回家睡觉吧。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’d better come home and get some sleep.”","zh":"我迟疑地说，“你还是回家睡觉吧。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He shook his head.","sentences":[{"en":"He shook his head.","zh":"他摇摇头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want to wait here till Daisy goes to bed. Good night, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want to wait here till Daisy goes to bed.","zh":"“我要在这里守到黛熙去睡觉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good night, old sport.”","zh":"晚安，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He put his hands in his coat pockets and turned back eagerly to his scrutiny of the house, as though my presence marred the sacredness of the vigil. So I walked away and left him standing there in the moonlight—watching over nothing.","sentences":[{"en":"He put his hands in his coat pockets and turned back eagerly to his scrutiny of the house, as though my presence marred the sacredness of the vigil.","zh":"他把手插进外衣的口袋，背过身去，继续紧张地监视那座房子，仿佛我的在场有损他的守望的神圣性。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So I walked away and left him standing there in the moonlight—watching over nothing.","zh":"所以我只好走开了，留下他在月光下伫立——徒劳地守候着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-8","n":8,"title":"Chapter VIII","titleZh":"第八章","paragraphs":[{"en":"I couldn’t sleep all night; a foghorn was groaning incessantly on the Sound, and I tossed half-sick between grotesque reality and savage, frightening dreams. Toward dawn I heard a taxi go up Gatsby’s drive, and immediately I jumped out of bed and began to dress—I felt that I had something to tell him, something to warn him about, and morning would be too late.","sentences":[{"en":"I couldn’t sleep all night; a foghorn was groaning incessantly on the Sound, and I tossed half-sick between grotesque reality and savage, frightening dreams.","zh":"我彻夜难眠，海湾里有个雾号不停地悲鸣，我生病似的在怪诞的现实和狰狞的梦境之间辗转反侧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Toward dawn I heard a taxi go up Gatsby’s drive, and immediately I jumped out of bed and began to dress—I felt that I had something to tell him, something to warn him about, and morning would be too late.","zh":"天快亮时，我听见有辆出租车开上盖茨比的车道，便立刻从床上跳起来，开始穿上衣服——我觉得我有话要告诉他，要赶紧提醒他某些事情，等到天亮就太晚了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Crossing his lawn, I saw that his front door was still open and he was leaning against a table in the hall, heavy with dejection or sleep.","sentences":[{"en":"Crossing his lawn, I saw that his front door was still open and he was leaning against a table in the hall, heavy with dejection or sleep.","zh":"穿过他的草坪时，我看到他的前门依然敞开着，他靠着门厅里的桌子站着，表情很沉重，可能是因为情绪低落，或者整晚没睡。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nothing happened,” he said wanly. “I waited, and about four o’clock she came to the window and stood there for a minute and then turned out the light.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nothing happened,” he said wanly.","zh":"“没有什么事，”他凄楚地说，“我等到差不多四点，她走到窗边，站了片刻，然后把电灯关掉了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I waited, and about four o’clock she came to the window and stood there for a minute and then turned out the light.”","zh":"“没有什么事，”他凄楚地说，“我等到差不多四点，她走到窗边，站了片刻，然后把电灯关掉了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His house had never seemed so enormous to me as it did that night when we hunted through the great rooms for cigarettes. We pushed aside curtains that were like pavilions, and felt over innumerable feet of dark wall for electric light switches—once I tumbled with a sort of splash upon the keys of a ghostly piano. There was an inexplicable amount of dust everywhere, and the rooms were musty, as though they hadn’t been aired for many days. I found the humidor on an unfamiliar table, with two stale, dry cigarettes inside. Throwing open the French windows of the drawing-room, we sat smoking out into the darkness.","sentences":[{"en":"His house had never seemed so enormous to me as it did that night when we hunted through the great rooms for cigarettes.","zh":"我们摸黑在许多宽敞的房间里搜罗香烟，这时我才发现他的房子原来是这么大。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We pushed aside curtains that were like pavilions, and felt over innumerable feet of dark wall for electric light switches—once I tumbled with a sort of splash upon the keys of a ghostly piano.","zh":"我们掀起许多大帐篷似的窗帘，在黑暗中摸着无数英尺长的墙壁去找电灯开关——有一次我差点摔倒，幸好扶住了一架幽灵般的钢琴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was an inexplicable amount of dust everywhere, and the rooms were musty, as though they hadn’t been aired for many days.","zh":"到处的灰尘多得不可思议，而且那些房间都很闷，好像很多天没有透过气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I found the humidor on an unfamiliar table, with two stale, dry cigarettes inside.","zh":"最后我在一张陌生的桌子上找到烟盒，里面有两根干瘪的香烟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Throwing open the French windows of the drawing-room, we sat smoking out into the darkness.","zh":"我们把客厅的落地窗打开，坐在黑暗中抽了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You ought to go away,” I said. “It’s pretty certain they’ll trace your car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You ought to go away,” I said.","zh":"“你应该离开这里，”我说，“他们肯定会查出来那是你的车。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s pretty certain they’ll trace your car.”","zh":"“你应该离开这里，”我说，“他们肯定会查出来那是你的车。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Go away now, old sport?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go away now, old sport?”","zh":"“现在离开这里，老兄？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Go to Atlantic City for a week, or up to Montreal.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go to Atlantic City for a week, or up to Montreal.”","zh":"“去大西城住几天吧，或者到北边的蒙特利尔。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He wouldn’t consider it. He couldn’t possibly leave Daisy until he knew what she was going to do. He was clutching at some last hope and I couldn’t bear to shake him free.","sentences":[{"en":"He wouldn’t consider it.","zh":"他不肯走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He couldn’t possibly leave Daisy until he knew what she was going to do.","zh":"在不知道黛熙接下来要怎么做之前，他是不可能离开的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was clutching at some last hope and I couldn’t bear to shake him free.","zh":"他这是抓住最后的希望不放，我也不忍心劝他松手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was this night that he told me the strange story of his youth with Dan Cody—told it to me because “Jay Gatsby” had broken up like glass against Tom’s hard malice, and the long secret extravaganza was played out. I think that he would have acknowledged anything now, without reserve, but he wanted to talk about Daisy.","sentences":[{"en":"It was this night that he told me the strange story of his youth with Dan Cody—told it to me because “Jay Gatsby” had broken up like glass against Tom’s hard malice, and the long secret extravaganza was played out.","zh":"正是在那天晚上，他跟我说起来他年轻时追随达恩·科迪的奇闻轶事——他会告诉我，是因为在汤姆的恶意打击之下，“杰伊·盖茨比”这个形象已经像玻璃般碎裂，这出长久以来引人注目的大戏终于落幕。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think that he would have acknowledged anything now, without reserve, but he wanted to talk about Daisy.","zh":"我以为他会毫无保留地将往事和盘托出，但他只想聊聊黛熙。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She was the first “nice” girl he had ever known. In various unrevealed capacities he had come in contact with such people, but always with indiscernible barbed wire between. He found her excitingly desirable. He went to her house, at first with other officers from Camp Taylor, then alone. It amazed him—he had never been in such a beautiful house before. But what gave it an air of breathless intensity, was that Daisy lived there—it was as casual a thing to her as his tent out at camp was to him. There was a ripe mystery about it, a hint of bedrooms upstairs more beautiful and cool than other bedrooms, of gay and radiant activities taking place through its corridors, and of romances that were not musty and laid away already in lavender but fresh and breathing and redolent of this year’s shining motorcars and of dances whose flowers were scarcely withered. It excited him, too, that many men had already loved Daisy—it increased her value in his eyes. He felt their presence all about the house, pervading the air with the shades and echoes of still vibrant emotions.","sentences":[{"en":"She was the first “nice” girl he had ever known.","zh":"黛熙是他认识的第一位“大家闺秀”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In various unrevealed capacities he had come in contact with such people, but always with indiscernible barbed wire between.","zh":"他从前也曾多次在未表明身份的情况下接触过这类人，但和她们之间总是隔着无形的铁丝网。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He found her excitingly desirable.","zh":"他发现黛熙正是他的梦中情人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went to her house, at first with other officers from Camp Taylor, then alone.","zh":"他常常登门拜访，起初是和泰勒军营其他军官结伴，后来是独自去的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It amazed him—he had never been in such a beautiful house before.","zh":"黛熙的家让他惊奇不已——他从未见过如此华丽的豪宅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But what gave it an air of breathless intensity, was that Daisy lived there—it was as casual a thing to her as his tent out at camp was to him.","zh":"但它之所以有那种令人屏声息气的紧张气氛，却是因为黛熙住在这里——尽管在她看来这地方平淡无奇，就像他看军营外的帐篷那样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a ripe mystery about it, a hint of bedrooms upstairs more beautiful and cool than other bedrooms, of gay and radiant activities taking place through its corridors, and of romances that were not musty and laid away already in lavender but fresh and breathing and redolent of this year’s shining motorcars and of dances whose flowers were scarcely withered.","zh":"他总觉得这座房子很神秘，似乎楼上的卧室是他前所未见的豪华与凉爽，而走廊里总有许多欢乐而美好的活动，还有很多浪漫的爱情故事，不是早已是陈年旧事的那种，而是鲜活的、清新的、芬芳的，像闪亮的新款汽车，像舞会上永不凋谢的花朵。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It excited him, too, that many men had already loved Daisy—it increased her value in his eyes.","zh":"他也因为有许多男人爱过黛熙而兴奋——黛熙在他眼里因此而变得更有价值。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He felt their presence all about the house, pervading the air with the shades and echoes of still vibrant emotions.","zh":"他觉得她家里到处都有他们的存在，空气中依然弥漫着那些感情的痕迹和回声。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But he knew that he was in Daisy’s house by a colossal accident. However glorious might be his future as Jay Gatsby, he was at present a penniless young man without a past, and at any moment the invisible cloak of his uniform might slip from his shoulders. So he made the most of his time. He took what he could get, ravenously and unscrupulously—eventually he took Daisy one still October night, took her because he had no real right to touch her hand.","sentences":[{"en":"But he knew that he was in Daisy’s house by a colossal accident.","zh":"但他知道，他能走进黛熙家里纯属偶然。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However glorious might be his future as Jay Gatsby, he was at present a penniless young man without a past, and at any moment the invisible cloak of his uniform might slip from his shoulders.","zh":"无论杰伊·盖茨比的前途有多么光明，他目前只是个身无分文、家世贫贱的年轻人，而那套军装给他带来的无形魅力也随时可能消退。所以他尽可能地利用他和黛熙相处的时间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So he made the most of his time.","zh":"他贪得无厌地、毫无原则地攫取所有他能得到的东西——终于，在某个安静的十月之夜，他迫不及待地占有了黛熙，占有了她的身体，因为他其实连跟她拉手的资格都没有。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He took what he could get, ravenously and unscrupulously—eventually he took Daisy one still October night, took her because he had no real right to touch her hand.","zh":"他贪得无厌地、毫无原则地攫取所有他能得到的东西——终于，在某个安静的十月之夜，他迫不及待地占有了黛熙，占有了她的身体，因为他其实连跟她拉手的资格都没有。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He might have despised himself, for he had certainly taken her under false pretences. I don’t mean that he had traded on his phantom millions, but he had deliberately given Daisy a sense of security; he let her believe that he was a person from much the same strata as herself—that he was fully able to take care of her. As a matter of fact, he had no such facilities—he had no comfortable family standing behind him, and he was liable at the whim of an impersonal government to be blown anywhere about the world.","sentences":[{"en":"He might have despised himself, for he had certainly taken her under false pretences.","zh":"他可能会瞧不起自己，因为他肯定是用欺骗的手段占有她的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t mean that he had traded on his phantom millions, but he had deliberately given Daisy a sense of security; he let her believe that he was a person from much the same strata as herself—that he was fully able to take care of her.","zh":"我倒不是说他假装成百万富翁，而是说他刻意给黛熙营造一种安全感，让黛熙相信他的家世也是那么显赫——他完全有能力把自己照顾好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As a matter of fact, he had no such facilities—he had no comfortable family standing behind him, and he was liable at the whim of an impersonal government to be blown anywhere about the world.","zh":"事实上，他没有这些能力——他和黛熙门不当户不对，而且毫无人性的政府随时可能将他派到世界上任何一个角落。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But he didn’t despise himself and it didn’t turn out as he had imagined. He had intended, probably, to take what he could and go—but now he found that he had committed himself to the following of a grail. He knew that Daisy was extraordinary, but he didn’t realize just how extraordinary a “nice” girl could be. She vanished into her rich house, into her rich, full life, leaving Gatsby—nothing. He felt married to her, that was all.","sentences":[{"en":"But he didn’t despise himself and it didn’t turn out as he had imagined.","zh":"但他没有瞧不起自己，事情的发展也跟他想象的不同。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had intended, probably, to take what he could and go—but now he found that he had committed himself to the following of a grail.","zh":"他起初可能只是逢场作戏——但后来却发现自己弄假成真。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He knew that Daisy was extraordinary, but he didn’t realize just how extraordinary a “nice” girl could be.","zh":"他原本也知道黛熙不落俗套，但没想到一位“大家闺秀”竟然是如此的不落俗套。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She vanished into her rich house, into her rich, full life, leaving Gatsby—nothing.","zh":"她若无其事地回到她那富裕的家，那富裕的生活，彻底消失了，留给盖茨比的是——失落的心情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He felt married to her, that was all.","zh":"他觉得离不开她了，这就是全部的结果。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When they met again, two days later, it was Gatsby who was breathless, who was, somehow, betrayed. Her porch was bright with the bought luxury of star-shine; the wicker of the settee squeaked fashionably as she turned toward him and he kissed her curious and lovely mouth. She had caught a cold, and it made her voice huskier and more charming than ever, and Gatsby was overwhelmingly aware of the youth and mystery that wealth imprisons and preserves, of the freshness of many clothes, and of Daisy, gleaming like silver, safe and proud above the hot struggles of the poor.","sentences":[{"en":"When they met again, two days later, it was Gatsby who was breathless, who was, somehow, betrayed.","zh":"再次相遇已是两日之后，当时盖茨比患得患失，好像他反倒吃亏了似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her porch was bright with the bought luxury of star-shine; the wicker of the settee squeaked fashionably as she turned toward him and he kissed her curious and lovely mouth.","zh":"现成的灿烂星光照亮了她家的阳台，在柳条长椅悦耳的吱嘎声中，她转身面对他，他情不自禁地吻上那美妙的嘴唇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had caught a cold, and it made her voice huskier and more charming than ever, and Gatsby was overwhelmingly aware of the youth and mystery that wealth imprisons and preserves, of the freshness of many clothes, and of Daisy, gleaming like silver, safe and proud above the hot struggles of the poor.","zh":"她早先染了风寒，声音变得比平时更加嘶哑，也更加动人，盖茨比深深地体会到，惊人的财富能够锁住和保留青春与神秘，华美的衣服能够让人面貌焕然一新，而像白银般光彩照人的黛熙安逸而骄傲，人间的困苦挣扎完全与她无缘。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"“I can’t describe to you how surprised I was to find out I loved her, old sport. I even hoped for a while that she’d throw me over, but she didn’t, because she was in love with me too. She thought I knew a lot because I knew different things from her… Well, there I was, way off my ambitions, getting deeper in love every minute, and all of a sudden I didn’t care. What was the use of doing great things if I could have a better time telling her what I was going to do?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I can’t describe to you how surprised I was to find out I loved her, old sport.","zh":"“我无法向你描述当时发现爱上她之后我有多么吃惊，老兄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I even hoped for a while that she’d throw me over, but she didn’t, because she was in love with me too.","zh":"我甚至曾经希望她会甩掉我，可是她没有，因为她也爱上我了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She thought I knew a lot because I knew different things from her…","zh":"她以为我的知识很渊博，因为我懂的东西和她完全不同…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, there I was, way off my ambitions, getting deeper in love every minute, and all of a sudden I didn’t care.","zh":"唉，我就这样忘掉了所有的雄心壮志，在爱河中越陷越深，而且突然间我并不在乎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was the use of doing great things if I could have a better time telling her what I was going to do?”","zh":"既然跟她畅想未来能让我得到更大的快乐，去做那些伟大的事情又有什么用呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"On the last afternoon before he went abroad, he sat with Daisy in his arms for a long, silent time. It was a cold fall day, with fire in the room and her cheeks flushed. Now and then she moved and he changed his arm a little, and once he kissed her dark shining hair. The afternoon had made them tranquil for a while, as if to give them a deep memory for the long parting the next day promised. They had never been closer in their month of love, nor communicated more profoundly one with another, than when she brushed silent lips against his coat’s shoulder or when he touched the end of her fingers, gently, as though she were asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"On the last afternoon before he went abroad, he sat with Daisy in his arms for a long, silent time.","zh":"在他奔赴海外之前最后那个下午，他抱着黛熙，两人静静地坐了很长时间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a cold fall day, with fire in the room and her cheeks flushed.","zh":"那是个寒冷的秋日，房间里生着火，她脸颊红扑扑的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now and then she moved and he changed his arm a little, and once he kissed her dark shining hair.","zh":"她偶尔挪动身体，他随之稍微调整手臂的位置，中间还亲了她乌黑发亮的秀发。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The afternoon had made them tranquil for a while, as if to give them a deep memory for the long parting the next day promised.","zh":"那个下午让他们得到了短暂的安宁，似乎是为了给他们留下深刻的记忆，以便面对第二天即将开始的长久分离。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had never been closer in their month of love, nor communicated more profoundly one with another, than when she brushed silent lips against his coat’s shoulder or when he touched the end of her fingers, gently, as though she were asleep.","zh":"在相恋的那个月里，他们从未如此亲密无间，也从未如此心心相印：她沉默的嘴唇轻轻地摩擦着他穿着外套的肩膀，而他则轻轻地触碰她的指尖，仿佛当她已经睡着似的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"He did extraordinarily well in the war. He was a captain before he went to the front, and following the Argonne battles he got his majority and the command of the divisional machine-guns. After the armistice he tried frantically to get home, but some complication or misunderstanding sent him to Oxford instead. He was worried now—there was a quality of nervous despair in Daisy’s letters. She didn’t see why he couldn’t come. She was feeling the pressure of the world outside, and she wanted to see him and feel his presence beside her and be reassured that she was doing the right thing after all.","sentences":[{"en":"He did extraordinarily well in the war.","zh":"战争期间他的表现非常出色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was a captain before he went to the front, and following the Argonne battles he got his majority and the command of the divisional machine-guns.","zh":"在上前线之前，他已经是上尉军衔，阿贡森林战役之后，又得以升任少校，负责指挥师部的机枪连。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After the armistice he tried frantically to get home, but some complication or misunderstanding sent him to Oxford instead.","zh":"战争结束，他心急如焚地想要回国，但由于某些意外的情况或者误解，他被派去了牛津大学。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was worried now—there was a quality of nervous despair in Daisy’s letters.","zh":"这时他很担心——黛熙在信里表示对他非常失望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She didn’t see why he couldn’t come.","zh":"黛熙不明白他为何不能回去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was feeling the pressure of the world outside, and she wanted to see him and feel his presence beside her and be reassured that she was doing the right thing after all.","zh":"她感到外界的压力，她想见到他，想有他陪伴在身边，让她相信自己做的事情到底是正确的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For Daisy was young and her artificial world was redolent of orchids and pleasant, cheerful snobbery and orchestras which set the rhythm of the year, summing up the sadness and suggestiveness of life in new tunes. All night the saxophones wailed the hopeless comment of the “Beale Street Blues” while a hundred pairs of golden and silver slippers shuffled the shining dust. At the grey tea hour there were always rooms that throbbed incessantly with this low, sweet fever, while fresh faces drifted here and there like rose petals blown by the sad horns around the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"For Daisy was young and her artificial world was redolent of orchids and pleasant, cheerful snobbery and orchestras which set the rhythm of the year, summing up the sadness and suggestiveness of life in new tunes.","zh":"因为黛熙是个妙龄少女，而她所处的又是纸醉金迷、寻欢作乐的势利世界。在这个世界里，轻歌曼舞尽日不息，声色犬马终年无休。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All night the saxophones wailed the hopeless comment of the “Beale Street Blues” while a hundred pairs of golden and silver slippers shuffled the shining dust.","zh":"萨克斯管彻夜吹奏着如泣如诉的《毕尔街蓝调》，上百双金色、银色的舞鞋踢起闪亮的灰尘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the grey tea hour there were always rooms that throbbed incessantly with this low, sweet fever, while fresh faces drifted here and there like rose petals blown by the sad horns around the floor.","zh":"到了茶歇时间，这首低沉而甜蜜的热门歌曲依旧不断地回荡着，而许多新鲜的面孔宛如被那些铜管吹落在地面的玫瑰花瓣，在舞厅里到处飘来飘去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Through this twilight universe Daisy began to move again with the season; suddenly she was again keeping half a dozen dates a day with half a dozen men, and drowsing asleep at dawn with the beads and chiffon of an evening-dress tangled among dying orchids on the floor beside her bed. And all the time something within her was crying for a decision. She wanted her life shaped now, immediately—and the decision must be made by some force—of love, of money, of unquestionable practicality—that was close at hand.","sentences":[{"en":"Through this twilight universe Daisy began to move again with the season; suddenly she was again keeping half a dozen dates a day with half a dozen men, and drowsing asleep at dawn with the beads and chiffon of an evening-dress tangled among dying orchids on the floor beside her bed.","zh":"在这个暧昧的宇宙里，黛熙又开始抛头露面；突然间她又每天和五六个男人约会，天快亮时才昏沉沉睡去，而缀着珠子的雪纺纱晚礼服连同干枯的兰花，被乱七八糟地丢在床边的地板上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And all the time something within her was crying for a decision.","zh":"她内心一直迫切地想要做出决定。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wanted her life shaped now, immediately—and the decision must be made by some force—of love, of money, of unquestionable practicality—that was close at hand.","zh":"她想要现在就解决她的终身大事，马上就解决；而帮她做出决定的力量——是爱情也好，是金钱也好——必须是非常现实而且近在眼前的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That force took shape in the middle of spring with the arrival of Tom Buchanan. There was a wholesome bulkiness about his person and his position, and Daisy was flattered. Doubtless there was a certain struggle and a certain relief. The letter reached Gatsby while he was still at Oxford.","sentences":[{"en":"That force took shape in the middle of spring with the arrival of Tom Buchanan.","zh":"那股力量终于在孟春时节由于汤姆·布坎南的到来而出现了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a wholesome bulkiness about his person and his position, and Daisy was flattered.","zh":"他相貌堂堂，家世显赫，这让黛熙觉得非常有面子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Doubtless there was a certain struggle and a certain relief.","zh":"她毫无疑问是纠结过，但后来又感到如释重负。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The letter reached Gatsby while he was still at Oxford.","zh":"收到她的信时，盖茨比还在牛津。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"It was dawn now on Long Island and we went about opening the rest of the windows downstairs, filling the house with grey-turning, gold-turning light. The shadow of a tree fell abruptly across the dew and ghostly birds began to sing among the blue leaves. There was a slow, pleasant movement in the air, scarcely a wind, promising a cool, lovely day.","sentences":[{"en":"It was dawn now on Long Island and we went about opening the rest of the windows downstairs, filling the house with grey-turning, gold-turning light.","zh":"长岛天已亮了，我们打开楼下其他的窗户，让客厅里充满渐渐变成白色、又渐渐变成金色的光芒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The shadow of a tree fell abruptly across the dew and ghostly birds began to sing among the blue leaves.","zh":"有一棵树的影子突然横伸在露珠之上，幽灵般的鸟儿开始在墨绿色的树叶里歌唱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a slow, pleasant movement in the air, scarcely a wind, promising a cool, lovely day.","zh":"空气缓缓地、令人愉悦地流动着，也算不上是风，预示着今天将是个凉爽而美好的日子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t think she ever loved him.” Gatsby turned around from a window and looked at me challengingly. “You must remember, old sport, she was very excited this afternoon. He told her those things in a way that frightened her—that made it look as if I was some kind of cheap sharper. And the result was she hardly knew what she was saying.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t think she ever loved him.”","zh":"“我不认为她爱过他，”站在窗边的盖茨比转过身来，带着自信满满的眼神看着我，“你要知道，老兄，她今天下午太激动了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Gatsby turned around from a window and looked at me challengingly.","zh":"“我不认为她爱过他，”站在窗边的盖茨比转过身来，带着自信满满的眼神看着我，“你要知道，老兄，她今天下午太激动了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You must remember, old sport, she was very excited this afternoon.","zh":"“我不认为她爱过他，”站在窗边的盖茨比转过身来，带着自信满满的眼神看着我，“你要知道，老兄，她今天下午太激动了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He told her those things in a way that frightened her—that made it look as if I was some kind of cheap sharper.","zh":"他说的那些话让她有点害怕——让她觉得我好像是个无耻的骗子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the result was she hardly knew what she was saying.”","zh":"结果弄得她语无伦次的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He sat down gloomily.","sentences":[{"en":"He sat down gloomily.","zh":"他苦闷地坐下来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course she might have loved him just for a minute, when they were first married—and loved me more even then, do you see?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course she might have loved him just for a minute, when they were first married—and loved me more even then, do you see?”","zh":"“当然，她也可能短暂地爱过他，在他们刚结婚的时候——哪怕在那个时候，她也是更爱我，你明白吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Suddenly he came out with a curious remark.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly he came out with a curious remark.","zh":"突然间，他说出一句很奇怪的话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“In any case,” he said, “it was just personal.”","sentences":[{"en":"“In any case,” he said, “it was just personal.”","zh":"“反正，”他说，“这是我个人的事情。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"What could you make of that, except to suspect some intensity in his conception of the affair that couldn’t be measured?","sentences":[{"en":"What could you make of that, except to suspect some intensity in his conception of the affair that couldn’t be measured?","zh":"你觉得这句话除了表明他对这场恋爱投入了无法估量的感情和想象，还能有什么别的解释呢？","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He came back from France when Tom and Daisy were still on their wedding trip, and made a miserable but irresistible journey to Louisville on the last of his army pay. He stayed there a week, walking the streets where their footsteps had clicked together through the November night and revisiting the out-of-the-way places to which they had driven in her white car. Just as Daisy’s house had always seemed to him more mysterious and gay than other houses, so his idea of the city itself, even though she was gone from it, was pervaded with a melancholy beauty.","sentences":[{"en":"He came back from France when Tom and Daisy were still on their wedding trip, and made a miserable but irresistible journey to Louisville on the last of his army pay.","zh":"他从法国回来时，汤姆和黛熙仍在度蜜月，他情不自禁地用所剩无几的军饷，踏上了前往路易斯维尔的伤心之旅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stayed there a week, walking the streets where their footsteps had clicked together through the November night and revisiting the out-of-the-way places to which they had driven in her white car.","zh":"他在那里待了一个星期，踏遍那些他们曾在十一月的夜晚并肩走过的街道，重游了他们曾开着她的白色跑车去过的旧地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just as Daisy’s house had always seemed to him more mysterious and gay than other houses, so his idea of the city itself, even though she was gone from it, was pervaded with a melancholy beauty.","zh":"就像黛熙家的房子在他看来比其他房子更加神秘和美好那样，在他看来，这座城市弥漫着伤感之美，尽管她已经远走高飞。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He left feeling that if he had searched harder, he might have found her—that he was leaving her behind. The day-coach—he was penniless now—was hot. He went out to the open vestibule and sat down on a folding-chair, and the station slid away and the backs of unfamiliar buildings moved by. Then out into the spring fields, where a yellow trolley raced them for a minute with people in it who might once have seen the pale magic of her face along the casual street.","sentences":[{"en":"He left feeling that if he had searched harder, he might have found her—that he was leaving her behind.","zh":"离开时他隐隐觉得，如果再努力一点，他也许能找到她——而现在是他把她抛弃了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The day-coach—he was penniless now—was hot.","zh":"硬座车厢——他已经身无分文——很热。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went out to the open vestibule and sat down on a folding-chair, and the station slid away and the backs of unfamiliar buildings moved by.","zh":"他走到火车末端敞开的地方，找了张折叠椅坐下，车站渐渐远去，许多陌生建筑的背面在两边移动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then out into the spring fields, where a yellow trolley raced them for a minute with people in it who might once have seen the pale magic of her face along the casual street.","zh":"然后火车开进春日的田野，有辆黄色的电车并排行驶了片刻，车里的乘客也许曾在街上偶然见到她那张苍白而充满魅力的脸。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The track curved and now it was going away from the sun, which, as it sank lower, seemed to spread itself in benediction over the vanishing city where she had drawn her breath. He stretched out his hand desperately as if to snatch only a wisp of air, to save a fragment of the spot that she had made lovely for him. But it was all going by too fast now for his blurred eyes and he knew that he had lost that part of it, the freshest and the best, forever.","sentences":[{"en":"The track curved and now it was going away from the sun, which, as it sank lower, seemed to spread itself in benediction over the vanishing city where she had drawn her breath.","zh":"铁轨拐了个弯，这时火车背对着太阳向东前进。太阳渐渐西沉，漫天的余晖似乎正在祝福她生活过的这座正在消失的城市。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stretched out his hand desperately as if to snatch only a wisp of air, to save a fragment of the spot that she had made lovely for him.","zh":"他绝望地伸出双手，仿佛只是为了抓住些许空气留作纪念，以便记住这个因为有她而变得美丽的地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But it was all going by too fast now for his blurred eyes and he knew that he had lost that part of it, the freshest and the best, forever.","zh":"但在他模糊的泪眼中，一切消失得太快，他知道他已经失去了这座城市的一部分，那最鲜活、最美好的部分，永远地失去了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was nine o’clock when we finished breakfast and went out on the porch. The night had made a sharp difference in the weather and there was an autumn flavour in the air. The gardener, the last one of Gatsby’s former servants, came to the foot of the steps.","sentences":[{"en":"It was nine o’clock when we finished breakfast and went out on the porch.","zh":"九点时我们吃完早餐，走到外面的门廊上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The night had made a sharp difference in the weather and there was an autumn flavour in the air.","zh":"气候一夜之间发生了变化，空气里已经有了秋天的味道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The gardener, the last one of Gatsby’s former servants, came to the foot of the steps.","zh":"那个园丁，盖茨比原来那批仆人中仅剩的一个，走到台阶下面。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m going to drain the pool today, Mr. Gatsby. Leaves’ll start falling pretty soon, and then there’s always trouble with the pipes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m going to drain the pool today, Mr. Gatsby.","zh":"“我今天准备把游泳池的水放干，盖茨比先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Leaves’ll start falling pretty soon, and then there’s always trouble with the pipes.”","zh":"树叶很快就会落下来，它们会把水管塞住的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t do it today,” Gatsby answered. He turned to me apologetically. “You know, old sport, I’ve never used that pool all summer?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t do it today,” Gatsby answered.","zh":"“今天先别放，”盖茨比回答说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He turned to me apologetically.","zh":"他扭头看着我，略带歉意地说：“你知道的，老兄，我整个夏天都没用过游泳池。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You know, old sport, I’ve never used that pool all summer?”","zh":"他扭头看着我，略带歉意地说：“你知道的，老兄，我整个夏天都没用过游泳池。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I looked at my watch and stood up.","sentences":[{"en":"I looked at my watch and stood up.","zh":"我看看手表，站了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Twelve minutes to my train.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Twelve minutes to my train.”","zh":"“我那班车十二分钟后开。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I didn’t want to go to the city. I wasn’t worth a decent stroke of work, but it was more than that—I didn’t want to leave Gatsby. I missed that train, and then another, before I could get myself away.","sentences":[{"en":"I didn’t want to go to the city.","zh":"我并不想到城里去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wasn’t worth a decent stroke of work, but it was more than that—I didn’t want to leave Gatsby.","zh":"那天我根本没有心情上班，但还有别的原因——我不想离开盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I missed that train, and then another, before I could get myself away.","zh":"我错过了那班火车，接着又错过了一班，终于还是走了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll call you up,” I said finally.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll call you up,” I said finally.","zh":"“我会给你打电话的，”我最后说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Do, old sport.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do, old sport.”","zh":"“一定要打，老兄。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ll call you about noon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll call you about noon.”","zh":"“我中午打给你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We walked slowly down the steps.","sentences":[{"en":"We walked slowly down the steps.","zh":"我们慢慢走下台阶。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I suppose Daisy’ll call too.” He looked at me anxiously, as if he hoped I’d corroborate this.","sentences":[{"en":"“I suppose Daisy’ll call too.”","zh":"“我想黛熙也会打过来，”他紧张地看着我，似乎是指望我会证实他的话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He looked at me anxiously, as if he hoped I’d corroborate this.","zh":"“我想黛熙也会打过来，”他紧张地看着我，似乎是指望我会证实他的话。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I suppose so.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I suppose so.”","zh":"“我想也是。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, goodbye.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, goodbye.”","zh":"“好吧，再见。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We shook hands and I started away. Just before I reached the hedge I remembered something and turned around.","sentences":[{"en":"We shook hands and I started away.","zh":"握手之后，我就走开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just before I reached the hedge I remembered something and turned around.","zh":"就快走到篱笆时，我想起某件事，于是转过身去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“They’re a rotten crowd,” I shouted across the lawn. “You’re worth the whole damn bunch put together.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They’re a rotten crowd,” I shouted across the lawn.","zh":"“他们都是烂人，”我隔着草坪大声说，“那帮混蛋全部加起来也没你高贵。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’re worth the whole damn bunch put together.”","zh":"“他们都是烂人，”我隔着草坪大声说，“那帮混蛋全部加起来也没你高贵。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I’ve always been glad I said that. It was the only compliment I ever gave him, because I disapproved of him from beginning to end. First he nodded politely, and then his face broke into that radiant and understanding smile, as if we’d been in ecstatic cahoots on that fact all the time. His gorgeous pink rag of a suit made a bright spot of colour against the white steps, and I thought of the night when I first came to his ancestral home, three months before. The lawn and drive had been crowded with the faces of those who guessed at his corruption—and he had stood on those steps, concealing his incorruptible dream, as he waved them goodbye.","sentences":[{"en":"I’ve always been glad I said that.","zh":"我总是很高兴我说出了那句话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the only compliment I ever gave him, because I disapproved of him from beginning to end.","zh":"那是我对他仅有的恭维，因为我自始至终是看他不顺眼的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"First he nodded politely, and then his face broke into that radiant and understanding smile, as if we’d been in ecstatic cahoots on that fact all the time.","zh":"他先是礼貌地点点头，随即脸上绽放出那种灿烂而会意的笑容，仿佛这是我们多年以来心照不宣的事实。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His gorgeous pink rag of a suit made a bright spot of colour against the white steps, and I thought of the night when I first came to his ancestral home, three months before.","zh":"他那套华丽的粉红色西装在白色台阶的映衬下格外醒目，我想起了三个月前初次拜访这座古旧大宅的那个夜晚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The lawn and drive had been crowded with the faces of those who guessed at his corruption—and he had stood on those steps, concealing his incorruptible dream, as he waved them goodbye.","zh":"当时草坪和车道上挤满了人，暗地里猜测他的为人是多么的龌龊——而他就站在这些台阶之上，隐藏着他纯洁的梦想，挥手向他们道别。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I thanked him for his hospitality. We were always thanking him for that—I and the others.","sentences":[{"en":"I thanked him for his hospitality.","zh":"我感谢他的热情招待。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We were always thanking him for that—I and the others.","zh":"我们总是为此感谢他——我和其他人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Goodbye,” I called. “I enjoyed breakfast, Gatsby.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Goodbye,” I called.","zh":"“再见，”我喊道，“谢谢你的早餐，盖茨比。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I enjoyed breakfast, Gatsby.”","zh":"“再见，”我喊道，“谢谢你的早餐，盖茨比。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"Up in the city, I tried for a while to list the quotations on an interminable amount of stock, then I fell asleep in my swivel-chair. Just before noon the phone woke me, and I started up with sweat breaking out on my forehead. It was Jordan Baker; she often called me up at this hour because the uncertainty of her own movements between hotels and clubs and private houses made her hard to find in any other way. Usually her voice came over the wire as something fresh and cool, as if a divot from a green golf-links had come sailing in at the office window, but this morning it seemed harsh and dry.","sentences":[{"en":"Up in the city, I tried for a while to list the quotations on an interminable amount of stock, then I fell asleep in my swivel-chair.","zh":"进城之后，我勉强抄了一会无穷无尽的股票行情，随后坐在转椅上睡着了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just before noon the phone woke me, and I started up with sweat breaking out on my forehead.","zh":"快到中午时，电话把我吵醒，我吓得额头直冒冷汗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Jordan Baker; she often called me up at this hour because the uncertainty of her own movements between hotels and clubs and private houses made her hard to find in any other way.","zh":"电话是乔丹打来的；她经常在这个点打给我，因为她行踪飘忽，要么在酒店，要么在俱乐部，要么在某些人家里，要不是这样我很难跟她取得联系。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Usually her voice came over the wire as something fresh and cool, as if a divot from a green golf-links had come sailing in at the office window, but this morning it seemed harsh and dry.","zh":"平常她在电话里的声音是很清凉的，仿佛有片草皮从某个高尔夫球场飘进我办公室的窗户，但今天听起来很干涩。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve left Daisy’s house,” she said. “I’m at Hempstead, and I’m going down to Southampton this afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve left Daisy’s house,” she said.","zh":"“我离开黛熙的家了，”她说，“现在我在汉普斯塔德，今天下午要去南安普敦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m at Hempstead, and I’m going down to Southampton this afternoon.”","zh":"“我离开黛熙的家了，”她说，“现在我在汉普斯塔德，今天下午要去南安普敦。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Probably it had been tactful to leave Daisy’s house, but the act annoyed me, and her next remark made me rigid.","sentences":[{"en":"Probably it had been tactful to leave Daisy’s house, but the act annoyed me, and her next remark made me rigid.","zh":"也许这时离开黛熙家不失为明智之举，但这个举动惹恼了我，而她下句话更让我生气。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You weren’t so nice to me last night.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You weren’t so nice to me last night.”","zh":"“你昨晚对我不是很好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How could it have mattered then?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How could it have mattered then?”","zh":"“在当时那种情况下有什么关系呢？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Silence for a moment. Then:","sentences":[{"en":"Silence for a moment.","zh":"“在当时那种情况下有什么关系呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then:","zh":"“在当时那种情况下有什么关系呢？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“However—I want to see you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“However—I want to see you.”","zh":"她沉默了片刻。然后说：“算了——我想见你。”“我也想见你。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I want to see you, too.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want to see you, too.”","zh":"她沉默了片刻。然后说：“算了——我想见你。”“我也想见你。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Suppose I don’t go to Southampton, and come into town this afternoon?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Suppose I don’t go to Southampton, and come into town this afternoon?”","zh":"“我今天下午不去南安普敦，到城里来找你怎么样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No—I don’t think this afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No—I don’t think this afternoon.”","zh":"“不要了——今天下午不行。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Very well.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well.”","zh":"“非常好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s impossible this afternoon. Various—”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s impossible this afternoon.","zh":"“今天下午不方便。有很多…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Various—”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We talked like that for a while, and then abruptly we weren’t talking any longer. I don’t know which of us hung up with a sharp click, but I know I didn’t care. I couldn’t have talked to her across a tea-table that day if I never talked to her again in this world.","sentences":[{"en":"We talked like that for a while, and then abruptly we weren’t talking any longer.","zh":"我们就这样聊了一会，然后突然间无话可说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t know which of us hung up with a sharp click, but I know I didn’t care.","zh":"我不知道是谁先把电话啪地挂掉，但我知道我无所谓。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I couldn’t have talked to her across a tea-table that day if I never talked to her again in this world.","zh":"那天我没有办法隔着茶桌和她说话，就算她因此和我绝交我也没有办法。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I called Gatsby’s house a few minutes later, but the line was busy. I tried four times; finally an exasperated central told me the wire was being kept open for long distance from Detroit. Taking out my timetable, I drew a small circle around the three-fifty train. Then I leaned back in my chair and tried to think. It was just noon.","sentences":[{"en":"I called Gatsby’s house a few minutes later, but the line was busy.","zh":"几分钟后，我给盖茨比家打电话，但电话占线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I tried four times; finally an exasperated central told me the wire was being kept open for long distance from Detroit.","zh":"我试了四回，最后总机被我惹急了，跟我说这条线路正在专门等候底特律打来的长途电话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Taking out my timetable, I drew a small circle around the three-fifty train.","zh":"我拿出列车时刻表，在三点五十分那班车上画了个小圈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then I leaned back in my chair and tried to think.","zh":"然后我又靠在椅背上，想要理清思绪。现在是中午，时候还早。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was just noon.","zh":"然后我又靠在椅背上，想要理清思绪。现在是中午，时候还早。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"When I passed the ash-heaps on the train that morning I had crossed deliberately to the other side of the car. I supposed there’d be a curious crowd around there all day with little boys searching for dark spots in the dust, and some garrulous man telling over and over what had happened, until it became less and less real even to him and he could tell it no longer, and Myrtle Wilson’s tragic achievement was forgotten. Now I want to go back a little and tell what happened at the garage after we left there the night before.","sentences":[{"en":"When I passed the ash-heaps on the train that morning I had crossed deliberately to the other side of the car.","zh":"那天早晨，当我乘坐的火车路过垃圾场时，我故意走到车厢的另一边，避免看到出事的地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I supposed there’d be a curious crowd around there all day with little boys searching for dark spots in the dust, and some garrulous man telling over and over what had happened, until it became less and less real even to him and he could tell it no longer, and Myrtle Wilson’s tragic achievement was forgotten.","zh":"我觉得应该会有很多好奇的人整天围在那里，几个小男孩寻找泥地上黑色的血迹，还有人添油加醋反复讲述那次事故，后来越说越玄乎，连自己也不信，于是不再说下去，梅朵·威尔逊的悲剧下场也就被抛到九霄云外。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now I want to go back a little and tell what happened at the garage after we left there the night before.","zh":"现在我想倒回去讲述那夜我们离开之后汽修厂发生的事情。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"They had difficulty in locating the sister, Catherine. She must have broken her rule against drinking that night, for when she arrived she was stupid with liquor and unable to understand that the ambulance had already gone to Flushing. When they convinced her of this, she immediately fainted, as if that was the intolerable part of the affair. Someone, kind or curious, took her in his car and drove her in the wake of her sister’s body.","sentences":[{"en":"They had difficulty in locating the sister, Catherine.","zh":"大家费了好大周折才找到死者的妹妹凯瑟琳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She must have broken her rule against drinking that night, for when she arrived she was stupid with liquor and unable to understand that the ambulance had already gone to Flushing.","zh":"当晚她肯定破了她自己不喝酒的惯例，因为到达汽修厂时她已经醉得晕头转向，人们说救护车已经前往法拉盛，她完全无法理解。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When they convinced her of this, she immediately fainted, as if that was the intolerable part of the affair.","zh":"等到大家让她听明白这一点时，她立刻昏了过去，仿佛这是整个事故中最难以忍受的部分。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Someone, kind or curious, took her in his car and drove her in the wake of her sister’s body.","zh":"有个人可能是出于好心或者好奇，开车带上她，追赶她姐姐的尸体去了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Until long after midnight a changing crowd lapped up against the front of the garage, while George Wilson rocked himself back and forth on the couch inside. For a while the door of the office was open, and everyone who came into the garage glanced irresistibly through it. Finally someone said it was a shame, and closed the door. Michaelis and several other men were with him; first, four or five men, later two or three men. Still later Michaelis had to ask the last stranger to wait there fifteen minutes longer, while he went back to his own place and made a pot of coffee. After that, he stayed there alone with Wilson until dawn.","sentences":[{"en":"Until long after midnight a changing crowd lapped up against the front of the garage, while George Wilson rocked himself back and forth on the couch inside.","zh":"午夜过后很久，依旧有络绎不绝的人来到汽修厂前面围观，而威尔逊还在里面的沙发上前后摇晃他自己的身体。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a while the door of the office was open, and everyone who came into the garage glanced irresistibly through it.","zh":"有一阵账房的门被打开了，每个人都走进车库，忍不住朝里面看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Finally someone said it was a shame, and closed the door.","zh":"最后有人说这太过分了，并把门关上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Michaelis and several other men were with him; first, four or five men, later two or three men.","zh":"米迦勒斯和其他几个人陪着威尔逊；起初有四五个人，后来变成两三个。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Still later Michaelis had to ask the last stranger to wait there fifteen minutes longer, while he went back to his own place and made a pot of coffee.","zh":"再后来米迦勒斯不得不恳请最后那位陌生人多留十五分钟，而他则回到自己的地方，煮了一壶咖啡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After that, he stayed there alone with Wilson until dawn.","zh":"在那之后，他一个人陪着威尔逊到天亮。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"About three o’clock the quality of Wilson’s incoherent muttering changed—he grew quieter and began to talk about the yellow car. He announced that he had a way of finding out whom the yellow car belonged to, and then he blurted out that a couple of months ago his wife had come from the city with her face bruised and her nose swollen.","sentences":[{"en":"About three o’clock the quality of Wilson’s incoherent muttering changed—he grew quieter and began to talk about the yellow car.","zh":"三点左右，威尔逊不再断断续续地嘟囔了——他变得越来越镇定，开始谈起那辆黄色的轿车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He announced that he had a way of finding out whom the yellow car belonged to, and then he blurted out that a couple of months ago his wife had come from the city with her face bruised and her nose swollen.","zh":"他宣称他有办法找出谁是那辆黄色轿车的主人，然后他又连珠炮般地说两个月前他妻子从城里回来时鼻青脸肿的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But when he heard himself say this, he flinched and began to cry “Oh, my God!” again in his groaning voice. Michaelis made a clumsy attempt to distract him.","sentences":[{"en":"But when he heard himself say this, he flinched and began to cry “Oh, my God!” again in his groaning voice.","zh":"但听到自己说出这句话时，他气得发抖，又开始用哽噎的声音大喊“我的上帝啊”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Michaelis made a clumsy attempt to distract him.","zh":"米迦勒斯赶紧想办法分散他的注意力。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How long have you been married, George? Come on there, try and sit still a minute, and answer my question. How long have you been married?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How long have you been married, George?","zh":"“你们结婚多久啦，乔治？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come on there, try and sit still a minute, and answer my question.","zh":"别这样，安静地坐一会，回答我的问题。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How long have you been married?”","zh":"你们结婚多久啦？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Twelve years.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Twelve years.”","zh":"“十二年。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Ever had any children? Come on, George, sit still—I asked you a question. Did you ever have any children?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ever had any children?","zh":"“生过孩子吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come on, George, sit still—I asked you a question.","zh":"喂，乔治，别乱动——我有个问题要问你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did you ever have any children?”","zh":"你们生过孩子吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The hard brown beetles kept thudding against the dull light, and whenever Michaelis heard a car go tearing along the road outside it sounded to him like the car that hadn’t stopped a few hours before. He didn’t like to go into the garage, because the work bench was stained where the body had been lying, so he moved uncomfortably around the office—he knew every object in it before morning—and from time to time sat down beside Wilson trying to keep him more quiet.","sentences":[{"en":"The hard brown beetles kept thudding against the dull light, and whenever Michaelis heard a car go tearing along the road outside it sounded to him like the car that hadn’t stopped a few hours before.","zh":"许多硬壳的棕色虫子不停地攻击着昏暗的电灯，每当听到外面有汽车呼啸而过，米迦勒斯总以为是几个小时前那辆肇事逃逸的轿车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He didn’t like to go into the garage, because the work bench was stained where the body had been lying, so he moved uncomfortably around the office—he knew every object in it before morning—and from time to time sat down beside Wilson trying to keep him more quiet.","zh":"他不喜欢走到外面的汽修厂，因为摆放过尸体的工作台上血迹斑斑，所以他浑身不舒服地在账房里走来走去——天还没亮，他已经很熟悉里面的每样东西了，并时不时地在威尔逊身边坐下，劝他安静下来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Have you got a church you go to sometimes, George? Maybe even if you haven’t been there for a long time? Maybe I could call up the church and get a priest to come over and he could talk to you, see?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you got a church you go to sometimes, George?","zh":"“你平时去教堂吗，乔治？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Maybe even if you haven’t been there for a long time?","zh":"你可能很久没有去教堂里吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Maybe I could call up the church and get a priest to come over and he could talk to you, see?”","zh":"要不这样吧，我打电话到教堂去，请个牧师过来跟你聊聊，你觉得呢？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Don’t belong to any.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t belong to any.”","zh":"“我不信教的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You ought to have a church, George, for times like this. You must have gone to church once. Didn’t you get married in a church? Listen, George, listen to me. Didn’t you get married in a church?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You ought to have a church, George, for times like this.","zh":"“你应该信教的，乔治，尤其是在这样的时候。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You must have gone to church once.","zh":"你肯定去过教堂啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Didn’t you get married in a church?","zh":"你不是在教堂里结婚的吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Listen, George, listen to me.","zh":"听着，乔治，听我说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Didn’t you get married in a church?”","zh":"你不是在教堂里结婚的吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That was a long time ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That was a long time ago.”","zh":"“那是很久以前的事了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The effort of answering broke the rhythm of his rocking—for a moment he was silent. Then the same half-knowing, half-bewildered look came back into his faded eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"The effort of answering broke the rhythm of his rocking—for a moment he was silent.","zh":"回答这些问题所费的精神打断了他摇晃的节奏——他暂时安静下来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the same half-knowing, half-bewildered look came back into his faded eyes.","zh":"那种迷离恍惚的神色又回到了他萎靡的眼里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look in the drawer there,” he said, pointing at the desk.","sentences":[{"en":"“Look in the drawer there,” he said, pointing at the desk.","zh":"“打开那个抽屉看看，”他指着写字台说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Which drawer?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Which drawer?”","zh":"“哪个抽屉？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That drawer—that one.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That drawer—that one.”","zh":"“那个抽屉——那个。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Michaelis opened the drawer nearest his hand. There was nothing in it but a small, expensive dog-leash, made of leather and braided silver. It was apparently new.","sentences":[{"en":"Michaelis opened the drawer nearest his hand.","zh":"米迦勒斯打开离他的手最近的抽屉。里面只有一条贵重的狗链，是皮做的，还镶着白银。","scope":"group"},{"en":"There was nothing in it but a small, expensive dog-leash, made of leather and braided silver.","zh":"米迦勒斯打开离他的手最近的抽屉。里面只有一条贵重的狗链，是皮做的，还镶着白银。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was apparently new.","zh":"它显然是新的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This?” he inquired, holding it up.","sentences":[{"en":"“This?” he inquired, holding it up.","zh":"“这件东西吗？”他拿起狗链问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Wilson stared and nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"Wilson stared and nodded.","zh":"威尔逊怔怔地点点头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I found it yesterday afternoon. She tried to tell me about it, but I knew it was something funny.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I found it yesterday afternoon.","zh":"“这是我昨天下午发现的。她试图狡辩，但我知道它肯定有古怪。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She tried to tell me about it, but I knew it was something funny.”","zh":"“这是我昨天下午发现的。她试图狡辩，但我知道它肯定有古怪。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You mean your wife bought it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You mean your wife bought it?”","zh":"“你是怪你太太买了它吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She had it wrapped in tissue paper on her bureau.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She had it wrapped in tissue paper on her bureau.”","zh":"“她用纸巾把它包起来，放在梳妆台上。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Michaelis didn’t see anything odd in that, and he gave Wilson a dozen reasons why his wife might have bought the dog-leash. But conceivably Wilson had heard some of these same explanations before, from Myrtle, because he began saying “Oh, my God!” again in a whisper—his comforter left several explanations in the air.","sentences":[{"en":"Michaelis didn’t see anything odd in that, and he gave Wilson a dozen reasons why his wife might have bought the dog-leash.","zh":"米迦勒斯可不觉得这有什么古怪，他给了威尔逊十几个理由，说明这条狗链也许真是他太太买的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But conceivably Wilson had heard some of these same explanations before, from Myrtle, because he began saying “Oh, my God!” again in a whisper—his comforter left several explanations in the air.","zh":"但威尔逊显然已经从梅朵口中听过这些解释，因为他又开始低声地说“我的上帝啊”——米迦勒斯又安慰着提出了几个解释，但他完全听不进去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Then he killed her,” said Wilson. His mouth dropped open suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Then he killed her,” said Wilson.","zh":"“我看她是他杀的，”威尔逊说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His mouth dropped open suddenly.","zh":"他的嘴巴突然张开了。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Who did?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who did?”","zh":"他的嘴巴突然张开了。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I have a way of finding out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I have a way of finding out.”","zh":"“谁？”“我有办法找出来的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re morbid, George,” said his friend. “This has been a strain to you and you don’t know what you’re saying. You’d better try and sit quiet till morning.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re morbid, George,” said his friend.","zh":"“你生病了，乔治，”他的朋友说，“你的精神太紧张了，别胡思乱想啦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“This has been a strain to you and you don’t know what you’re saying.","zh":"“你生病了，乔治，”他的朋友说，“你的精神太紧张了，别胡思乱想啦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"You’d better try and sit quiet till morning.”","zh":"你最好想办法安静下来，等天亮了再说。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He murdered her.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He murdered her.”","zh":"“他谋杀了她。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was an accident, George.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was an accident, George.”","zh":"“那是意外，乔治。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Wilson shook his head. His eyes narrowed and his mouth widened slightly with the ghost of a superior “Hm!”","sentences":[{"en":"Wilson shook his head.","zh":"威尔逊摇着头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His eyes narrowed and his mouth widened slightly with the ghost of a superior “Hm!”","zh":"他皱起眉头，微微张开嘴巴，有气无力地“哼”了一声。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I know,” he said definitely. “I’m one of these trusting fellas and I don’t think any harm to nobody, but when I get to know a thing I know it. It was the man in that car. She ran out to speak to him and he wouldn’t stop.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know,” he said definitely.","zh":"“我知道，”他坚定地说，“我很容易相信别人，也没想过要伤害任何人，但有些事情我要是弄明白了，我心里会有数的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m one of these trusting fellas and I don’t think any harm to nobody, but when I get to know a thing I know it.","zh":"“我知道，”他坚定地说，“我很容易相信别人，也没想过要伤害任何人，但有些事情我要是弄明白了，我心里会有数的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was the man in that car.","zh":"车里肯定是那个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She ran out to speak to him and he wouldn’t stop.”","zh":"她冲出去想要跟他说话，可是他不肯停车。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Michaelis had seen this too, but it hadn’t occurred to him that there was any special significance in it. He believed that Mrs. Wilson had been running away from her husband, rather than trying to stop any particular car.","sentences":[{"en":"Michaelis had seen this too, but it hadn’t occurred to him that there was any special significance in it.","zh":"米迦勒斯也看到这个场面，但他原来没想到这里面有什么特别的意义。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He believed that Mrs. Wilson had been running away from her husband, rather than trying to stop any particular car.","zh":"当时他认为威尔逊太太冲出去是为了逃离她的丈夫，而不是试图拦住某辆车。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“How could she of been like that?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How could she of been like that?”","zh":"“她怎么会搞成这样？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“She’s a deep one,” said Wilson, as if that answered the question. “Ah-h-h—”","sentences":[{"en":"“She’s a deep one,” said Wilson, as if that answered the question.","zh":"“她这个人城府很深，”威尔逊答非所问地说，“唉…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Ah-h-h—”","zh":"“她这个人城府很深，”威尔逊答非所问地说，“唉…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He began to rock again, and Michaelis stood twisting the leash in his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"He began to rock again, and Michaelis stood twisting the leash in his hand.","zh":"他又开始摇晃，米迦勒斯站在旁边，手里揉着那条狗链。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Maybe you got some friend that I could telephone for, George?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Maybe you got some friend that I could telephone for, George?”","zh":"“你有没有什么朋友，乔治？我帮你打电话给他们。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"This was a forlorn hope—he was almost sure that Wilson had no friend: there was not enough of him for his wife. He was glad a little later when he noticed a change in the room, a blue quickening by the window, and realized that dawn wasn’t far off. About five o’clock it was blue enough outside to snap off the light.","sentences":[{"en":"This was a forlorn hope—he was almost sure that Wilson had no friend: there was not enough of him for his wife.","zh":"这是个渺茫的希望——他几乎可以肯定威尔逊没有朋友：他连自己的老婆都管不住。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was glad a little later when he noticed a change in the room, a blue quickening by the window, and realized that dawn wasn’t far off.","zh":"片刻之后他又高兴起来，因为他发现房间里有了变化，窗外的天空渐渐变蓝，黎明已经不远了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"About five o’clock it was blue enough outside to snap off the light.","zh":"大概五点钟的时候，外面的天已经蓝得可以把灯关掉。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Wilson’s glazed eyes turned out to the ash-heaps, where small grey clouds took on fantastic shapes and scurried here and there in the faint dawn wind.","sentences":[{"en":"Wilson’s glazed eyes turned out to the ash-heaps, where small grey clouds took on fantastic shapes and scurried here and there in the faint dawn wind.","zh":"威尔逊无神的双眼望向外面的垃圾场，那边有几片奇形怪状的阴云，被微弱的晨风吹得飘来飘去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I spoke to her,” he muttered, after a long silence. “I told her she might fool me but she couldn’t fool God. I took her to the window”—with an effort he got up and walked to the rear window and leaned with his face pressed against it—“and I said ‘God knows what you’ve been doing, everything you’ve been doing. You may fool me, but you can’t fool God!’ ”","sentences":[{"en":"“I spoke to her,” he muttered, after a long silence.","zh":"“我跟她谈过，”沉默良久之后，他咕哝着说，“我说她也许可以愚弄我，但她愚弄不了上帝。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I told her she might fool me but she couldn’t fool God.","zh":"“我跟她谈过，”沉默良久之后，他咕哝着说，“我说她也许可以愚弄我，但她愚弄不了上帝。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I took her to the window”—with an effort he got up and walked to the rear window and leaned with his face pressed against it—“and I said ‘God knows what you’ve been doing, everything you’ve been doing.","zh":"我把她拉到窗边”——他勉为其难地站起来，走到后窗边上，把脸贴着窗上的玻璃——“我说：‘上帝知道你在做什么，知道你做过的每件事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You may fool me, but you can’t fool God!’ ”","zh":"你可以愚弄我，但你愚弄不了上帝！’”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Standing behind him, Michaelis saw with a shock that he was looking at the eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg, which had just emerged, pale and enormous, from the dissolving night.","sentences":[{"en":"Standing behind him, Michaelis saw with a shock that he was looking at the eyes of Doctor T. J. Eckleburg, which had just emerged, pale and enormous, from the dissolving night.","zh":"米迦勒斯站在他身后，吃惊地发现他正在看着艾克堡医生的眼睛。那双苍白而巨大的眼睛刚刚从消失的夜色中显露出来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“God sees everything,” repeated Wilson.","sentences":[{"en":"“God sees everything,” repeated Wilson.","zh":"“上帝看到一切，”威尔逊又说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s an advertisement,” Michaelis assured him. Something made him turn away from the window and look back into the room. But Wilson stood there a long time, his face close to the window pane, nodding into the twilight.","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s an advertisement,” Michaelis assured him.","zh":"“那是个广告牌啊，”米迦勒斯开解他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something made him turn away from the window and look back into the room.","zh":"他觉得心里隐隐有点不舒服，于是把眼光收回来，重新看着账房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Wilson stood there a long time, his face close to the window pane, nodding into the twilight.","zh":"但威尔逊站在那里久久不动，他的脸紧贴着后窗的玻璃，不停地向着晨曦点头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"By six o’clock Michaelis was worn out, and grateful for the sound of a car stopping outside. It was one of the watchers of the night before who had promised to come back, so he cooked breakfast for three, which he and the other man ate together. Wilson was quieter now, and Michaelis went home to sleep; when he awoke four hours later and hurried back to the garage, Wilson was gone.","sentences":[{"en":"By six o’clock Michaelis was worn out, and grateful for the sound of a car stopping outside.","zh":"到六点米迦勒斯已经累得不行，听到有辆轿车停在外面，他心里很是感激。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was one of the watchers of the night before who had promised to come back, so he cooked breakfast for three, which he and the other man ate together.","zh":"来者是昨晚到这里看热闹的，他答应过会回来帮忙。于是米迦勒斯去做了三个人的早餐，他和那个人把东西吃掉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wilson was quieter now, and Michaelis went home to sleep; when he awoke four hours later and hurried back to the garage, Wilson was gone.","zh":"看到威尔逊情绪比较平稳，米迦勒斯就回家睡觉去了。四个小时后，他醒过来，匆匆赶到汽修厂，这时威尔逊已经走了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His movements—he was on foot all the time—were afterward traced to Port Roosevelt and then to Gad’s Hill, where he bought a sandwich that he didn’t eat, and a cup of coffee. He must have been tired and walking slowly, for he didn’t reach Gad’s Hill until noon. Thus far there was no difficulty in accounting for his time—there were boys who had seen a man “acting sort of crazy,” and motorists at whom he stared oddly from the side of the road. Then for three hours he disappeared from view. The police, on the strength of what he said to Michaelis, that he “had a way of finding out,” supposed that he spent that time going from garage to garage thereabout, inquiring for a yellow car. On the other hand, no garage man who had seen him ever came forward, and perhaps he had an easier, surer way of finding out what he wanted to know. By half-past two he was in West Egg, where he asked someone the way to Gatsby’s house. So by that time he knew Gatsby’s name.","sentences":[{"en":"His movements—he was on foot all the time—were afterward traced to Port Roosevelt and then to Gad’s Hill, where he bought a sandwich that he didn’t eat, and a cup of coffee.","zh":"他的行踪——他始终是步行的——后来被人查了出来：先是去了罗斯福港，然后到嘉德山庄。他在那里买了个没有吃的三明治和一杯咖啡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He must have been tired and walking slowly, for he didn’t reach Gad’s Hill until noon.","zh":"他肯定很累，而且走得很慢，因为他走到嘉德山庄已是正午。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus far there was no difficulty in accounting for his time—there were boys who had seen a man “acting sort of crazy,” and motorists at whom he stared oddly from the side of the road.","zh":"他到此为止的行踪并不难查明——有几个孩子说看到有个人“疯疯癫癫的”，几个开车的人也说曾看见他在路边盯着他们看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then for three hours he disappeared from view.","zh":"随后三个小时他就消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The police, on the strength of what he said to Michaelis, that he “had a way of finding out,” supposed that he spent that time going from garage to garage thereabout, inquiring for a yellow car.","zh":"警察根据他对米迦勒斯说过的话，说“他有办法找出来的”，推断他这段时间是在走访附近的汽修厂，打听那部黄色轿车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the other hand, no garage man who had seen him ever came forward, and perhaps he had an easier, surer way of finding out what he wanted to know.","zh":"可是又没有哪个汽修厂的人说见过他，也许他有更简单、更确定的方法，可以找到他想知道的答案。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By half-past two he was in West Egg, where he asked someone the way to Gatsby’s house.","zh":"下午两点半时他已经走到西卵，问人盖茨比家怎么走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So by that time he knew Gatsby’s name.","zh":"所以那时他已经知道盖茨比的名字了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"At two o’clock Gatsby put on his bathing-suit and left word with the butler that if anyone phoned word was to be brought to him at the pool. He stopped at the garage for a pneumatic mattress that had amused his guests during the summer, and the chauffeur helped him to pump it up. Then he gave instructions that the open car wasn’t to be taken out under any circumstances—and this was strange, because the front right fender needed repair.","sentences":[{"en":"At two o’clock Gatsby put on his bathing-suit and left word with the butler that if anyone phoned word was to be brought to him at the pool.","zh":"下午两点时，盖茨比穿上他的泳装，吩咐管家如果有人打电话来，就到游泳池通知他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stopped at the garage for a pneumatic mattress that had amused his guests during the summer, and the chauffeur helped him to pump it up.","zh":"他先到车库去拿一只那年夏天给许多客人用过的气垫，司机帮他把气充好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he gave instructions that the open car wasn’t to be taken out under any circumstances—and this was strange, because the front right fender needed repair.","zh":"然后他叮嘱司机千万不能把那辆敞篷车开出去——这个要求很怪，因为右前方的挡泥板需要修理。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby shouldered the mattress and started for the pool. Once he stopped and shifted it a little, and the chauffeur asked him if he needed help, but he shook his head and in a moment disappeared among the yellowing trees.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby shouldered the mattress and started for the pool.","zh":"盖茨比扛着气垫，向游泳池走去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once he stopped and shifted it a little, and the chauffeur asked him if he needed help, but he shook his head and in a moment disappeared among the yellowing trees.","zh":"他路上停下来过一次，稍微调整了垫子的位置，司机问他要不要帮忙，但他摇摇头，随即消失在那些叶子正在变黄的树木里。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"No telephone message arrived, but the butler went without his sleep and waited for it until four o’clock—until long after there was anyone to give it to if it came. I have an idea that Gatsby himself didn’t believe it would come, and perhaps he no longer cared. If that was true he must have felt that he had lost the old warm world, paid a high price for living too long with a single dream. He must have looked up at an unfamiliar sky through frightening leaves and shivered as he found what a grotesque thing a rose is and how raw the sunlight was upon the scarcely created grass. A new world, material without being real, where poor ghosts, breathing dreams like air, drifted fortuitously about… like that ashen, fantastic figure gliding toward him through the amorphous trees.","sentences":[{"en":"No telephone message arrived, but the butler went without his sleep and waited for it until four o’clock—until long after there was anyone to give it to if it came.","zh":"没有人打电话来，但管家没有去午睡，一直等到下午四点——那时候就算有电话打进来，盖茨比也早已接不到了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I have an idea that Gatsby himself didn’t believe it would come, and perhaps he no longer cared.","zh":"我总是想，盖茨比本人并不相信电话会响，他也许觉得无所谓。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If that was true he must have felt that he had lost the old warm world, paid a high price for living too long with a single dream.","zh":"如果我的设想没有错，那么他肯定已经明白他失去了原来那个温暖的世界，已经为怀有一个梦想太久而付出高昂的代价。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He must have looked up at an unfamiliar sky through frightening leaves and shivered as he found what a grotesque thing a rose is and how raw the sunlight was upon the scarcely created grass.","zh":"他肯定抬起过头，透过那些可怕的树叶，发现天空是如此的陌生；而当他发现玫瑰是如此的丑陋，照耀着稀疏青草的阳光是如此的残酷，他肯定会感到不寒而栗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A new world, material without being real, where poor ghosts, breathing dreams like air, drifted fortuitously about… like that ashen, fantastic figure gliding toward him through the amorphous trees.","zh":"他宛如处于一个新的世界，一个具体而又虚假的世界，在这里，可怜的幽灵呼吸着空气般的梦想，漫无目的地飘来荡去…就像那个脸色灰白、形迹可疑的人，他正在枝叶蔓生的树丛中，偷偷摸摸地向他走过来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The chauffeur—he was one of Wolfshiem’s protégés—heard the shots—afterwards he could only say that he hadn’t thought anything much about them. I drove from the station directly to Gatsby’s house and my rushing anxiously up the front steps was the first thing that alarmed anyone. But they knew then, I firmly believe. With scarcely a word said, four of us, the chauffeur, butler, gardener, and I hurried down to the pool.","sentences":[{"en":"The chauffeur—he was one of Wolfshiem’s protégés—heard the shots—afterwards he could only say that he hadn’t thought anything much about them.","zh":"司机——他也是沃夫希姆的手下——听到了枪声，后来他说他没有联想太多。我从火车站雇了车直接赶到盖茨比家，听到我急急忙忙冲上前门台阶的脚步声，他们才反应过来可能出了事。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I drove from the station directly to Gatsby’s house and my rushing anxiously up the front steps was the first thing that alarmed anyone.","zh":"司机——他也是沃夫希姆的手下——听到了枪声，后来他说他没有联想太多。我从火车站雇了车直接赶到盖茨比家，听到我急急忙忙冲上前门台阶的脚步声，他们才反应过来可能出了事。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But they knew then, I firmly believe.","zh":"但我坚信他们那时已经知道了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With scarcely a word said, four of us, the chauffeur, butler, gardener, and I hurried down to the pool.","zh":"我们四个人，司机、管家、园丁和我，默默不语地赶到游泳池。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was a faint, barely perceptible movement of the water as the fresh flow from one end urged its way toward the drain at the other. With little ripples that were hardly the shadows of waves, the laden mattress moved irregularly down the pool. A small gust of wind that scarcely corrugated the surface was enough to disturb its accidental course with its accidental burden. The touch of a cluster of leaves revolved it slowly, tracing, like the leg of transit, a thin red circle in the water.","sentences":[{"en":"There was a faint, barely perceptible movement of the water as the fresh flow from one end urged its way toward the drain at the other.","zh":"游泳池里的水轻轻地荡漾着，因为清水从一头流进来，又从一头排出去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With little ripples that were hardly the shadows of waves, the laden mattress moved irregularly down the pool.","zh":"那只负重的气垫毫无规律地漂浮着，所到之处激起淡淡的涟漪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A small gust of wind that scarcely corrugated the surface was enough to disturb its accidental course with its accidental burden.","zh":"一阵微风吹来，几乎吹不皱水面，却扰乱了它偶然的航程，尽管它还负载着偶然的重担。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The touch of a cluster of leaves revolved it slowly, tracing, like the leg of transit, a thin red circle in the water.","zh":"几片树叶落在它上面，使它慢慢地旋转，像圆规的腿那样，在水里画出一个淡红色的圆圈。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was after we started with Gatsby toward the house that the gardener saw Wilson’s body a little way off in the grass, and the holocaust was complete.","sentences":[{"en":"It was after we started with Gatsby toward the house that the gardener saw Wilson’s body a little way off in the grass, and the holocaust was complete.","zh":"直到我们抬起盖茨比往屋子走之后，园丁才看见威尔逊的尸体，就躺在不远处的草丛里，这场浩劫就此告终。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]},{"id":"ch-9","n":9,"title":"Chapter IX","titleZh":"第九章","paragraphs":[{"en":"After two years I remember the rest of that day, and that night and the next day, only as an endless drill of police and photographers and newspaper men in and out of Gatsby’s front door. A rope stretched across the main gate and a policeman by it kept out the curious, but little boys soon discovered that they could enter through my yard, and there were always a few of them clustered open-mouthed about the pool. Someone with a positive manner, perhaps a detective, used the expression “madman” as he bent over Wilson’s body that afternoon, and the adventitious authority of his voice set the key for the newspaper reports next morning.","sentences":[{"en":"After two years I remember the rest of that day, and that night and the next day, only as an endless drill of police and photographers and newspaper men in and out of Gatsby’s front door.","zh":"时隔两年，当时的情形我已不是很清楚，只记得那天下午、晚上和第二天，络绎不绝的警察、摄影师和记者在盖茨比家进进出出。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A rope stretched across the main gate and a policeman by it kept out the curious, but little boys soon discovered that they could enter through my yard, and there were always a few of them clustered open-mouthed about the pool.","zh":"大门拉起一条绳子，有个警察守在旁边，挡住想看热闹的人，但附近的小孩很快发现他们可以从我的草坪进去，因此游泳池边总是有几个目瞪口呆的孩子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Someone with a positive manner, perhaps a detective, used the expression “madman” as he bent over Wilson’s body that afternoon, and the adventitious authority of his voice set the key for the newspaper reports next morning.","zh":"有个气定神闲的人——可能是个侦探——在弯腰视察威尔逊的尸体时，使用了“疯子”这个词，这句言之凿凿的无心快语奠定了隔日媒体的报道基调。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Most of those reports were a nightmare—grotesque, circumstantial, eager, and untrue. When Michaelis’s testimony at the inquest brought to light Wilson’s suspicions of his wife I thought the whole tale would shortly be served up in racy pasquinade—but Catherine, who might have said anything, didn’t say a word. She showed a surprising amount of character about it too—looked at the coroner with determined eyes under that corrected brow of hers, and swore that her sister had never seen Gatsby, that her sister was completely happy with her husband, that her sister had been into no mischief whatever. She convinced herself of it, and cried into her handkerchief, as if the very suggestion was more than she could endure. So Wilson was reduced to a man “deranged by grief” in order that the case might remain in its simplest form. And it rested there.","sentences":[{"en":"Most of those reports were a nightmare—grotesque, circumstantial, eager, and untrue.","zh":"那些报道大多数是噩梦——荒诞不经、琐碎无聊、兴致勃勃、无中生有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Michaelis’s testimony at the inquest brought to light Wilson’s suspicions of his wife I thought the whole tale would shortly be served up in racy pasquinade—but Catherine, who might have said anything, didn’t say a word.","zh":"当米迦勒斯供认威尔逊怀疑他太太红杏出墙的证词曝光之后，我原本以为这个事件很快会演变成桃色新闻——但凯瑟琳非但没有胡说八道，居然还守口如瓶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She showed a surprising amount of character about it too—looked at the coroner with determined eyes under that corrected brow of hers, and swore that her sister had never seen Gatsby, that her sister was completely happy with her husband, that her sister had been into no mischief whatever.","zh":"她也展现出惊人的勇气——她那双眼睛在修整过的眉毛之下坚定地看着警察局派来的法医，发誓她姐姐从未见过盖茨比，她姐姐的婚姻生活非常美满，又说她姐姐从来没有做过越轨的事情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She convinced herself of it, and cried into her handkerchief, as if the very suggestion was more than she could endure.","zh":"她说得连自己都信了，用手帕捂着脸哭了起来，仿佛这是她万万不能接受的污蔑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So Wilson was reduced to a man “deranged by grief” in order that the case might remain in its simplest form.","zh":"所以威尔逊被说成是“因悲哀而行为失常”，于是这件案子变成了最简单的命案，就这样不了了之。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And it rested there.","zh":"所以威尔逊被说成是“因悲哀而行为失常”，于是这件案子变成了最简单的命案，就这样不了了之。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"But all this part of it seemed remote and unessential. I found myself on Gatsby’s side, and alone. From the moment I telephoned news of the catastrophe to West Egg village, every surmise about him, and every practical question, was referred to me. At first I was surprised and confused; then, as he lay in his house and didn’t move or breathe or speak, hour upon hour, it grew upon me that I was responsible, because no one else was interested—interested, I mean, with that intense personal interest to which everyone has some vague right at the end.","sentences":[{"en":"But all this part of it seemed remote and unessential.","zh":"但其实所有这些都是无关紧要的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I found myself on Gatsby’s side, and alone.","zh":"最让我失望的是，站在盖茨比那边的只有我自己，只有我一个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From the moment I telephoned news of the catastrophe to West Egg village, every surmise about him, and every practical question, was referred to me.","zh":"从我打电话到西卵村报告惨剧的消息开始，但凡有关于他的猜测或者具体问题，人们都会跑来问我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At first I was surprised and confused; then, as he lay in his house and didn’t move or breathe or speak, hour upon hour, it grew upon me that I was responsible, because no one else was interested—interested, I mean, with that intense personal interest to which everyone has some vague right at the end.","zh":"起初我既诧异又困惑，后来随着时间的流逝，看到他无声无息，安然地躺在他的房子里，我渐渐明白了：大家都来找我，是因为没有别的人感兴趣——我的意思是说，别人完全没有兴趣来料理他的后事。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I called up Daisy half an hour after we found him, called her instinctively and without hesitation. But she and Tom had gone away early that afternoon, and taken baggage with them.","sentences":[{"en":"I called up Daisy half an hour after we found him, called her instinctively and without hesitation.","zh":"我们发现他的尸体之后不到半个小时，我本能地、毫不迟疑地给黛熙打电话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she and Tom had gone away early that afternoon, and taken baggage with them.","zh":"但她和汤姆那天下午早些时候出门了，而且还带着许多行李。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Left no address?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Left no address?”","zh":"“没说去哪里吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No.”","zh":"“没有。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Say when they’d be back?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Say when they’d be back?”","zh":"“有说什么时候回来吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“No.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No.”","zh":"“没有。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Any idea where they are? How I could reach them?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Any idea where they are?","zh":"“知道他们在哪里吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How I could reach them?”","zh":"我怎样才能找到他们？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t know. Can’t say.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t know.","zh":"“我不知道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Can’t say.”","zh":"说不上来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I wanted to get somebody for him. I wanted to go into the room where he lay and reassure him: “I’ll get somebody for you, Gatsby. Don’t worry. Just trust me and I’ll get somebody for you—”","sentences":[{"en":"I wanted to get somebody for him.","zh":"我想替他找个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wanted to go into the room where he lay and reassure him: “I’ll get somebody for you, Gatsby.","zh":"我真想走进他躺着的房间，安慰他说：“我会替你找个人来的，盖茨比。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Don’t worry.","zh":"别担心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just trust me and I’ll get somebody for you—”","zh":"包在我身上，我会给你找个人——”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Meyer Wolfshiem’s name wasn’t in the phone book. The butler gave me his office address on Broadway, and I called Information, but by the time I had the number it was long after five, and no one answered the phone.","sentences":[{"en":"Meyer Wolfshiem’s name wasn’t in the phone book.","zh":"梅耶·沃夫希姆的名字并不在电话簿里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The butler gave me his office address on Broadway, and I called Information, but by the time I had the number it was long after five, and no one answered the phone.","zh":"管家给了我他在百老汇的地址，我打电话到查号台，但等我拿到号码，时间早就过了五点，那边没人接电话。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Will you ring again?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Will you ring again?”","zh":"“你能再帮我接通吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’ve rung three times.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve rung three times.”","zh":"“我已经接通三次了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It’s very important.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s very important.”","zh":"“我有很重要的事情。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Sorry. I’m afraid no one’s there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sorry.","zh":"“对不起。那边恐怕没有人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’m afraid no one’s there.”","zh":"“对不起。那边恐怕没有人。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I went back to the drawing-room and thought for an instant that they were chance visitors, all these official people who suddenly filled it. But, though they drew back the sheet and looked at Gatsby with shocked eyes, his protest continued in my brain:","sentences":[{"en":"I went back to the drawing-room and thought for an instant that they were chance visitors, all these official people who suddenly filled it.","zh":"我回到客厅，突然发现里面挤满了人，开始还以为是顺道来访的宾客，随即发现其实是政府的工作人员。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, though they drew back the sheet and looked at Gatsby with shocked eyes, his protest continued in my brain:","zh":"可是，当他们掀起那块薄布，惊恐地看着盖茨比，我仿佛听到他的抗议：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look here, old sport, you’ve got to get somebody for me. You’ve got to try hard. I can’t go through this alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look here, old sport, you’ve got to get somebody for me.","zh":"“喂，老兄，你得帮我找个人啊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You’ve got to try hard.","zh":"你要努力去找。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I can’t go through this alone.”","zh":"我一个人应付不来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Someone started to ask me questions, but I broke away and going upstairs looked hastily through the unlocked parts of his desk—he’d never told me definitely that his parents were dead. But there was nothing—only the picture of Dan Cody, a token of forgotten violence, staring down from the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"Someone started to ask me questions, but I broke away and going upstairs looked hastily through the unlocked parts of his desk—he’d never told me definitely that his parents were dead.","zh":"有人开始问我问题，但我脱身走到楼上去，匆匆翻查他的书桌那些没上锁的抽屉——他从来没有明确地跟我说过他的父母已经去世。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But there was nothing—only the picture of Dan Cody, a token of forgotten violence, staring down from the wall.","zh":"但那里什么都没有——只有达恩·科迪的照片，象征着那早已被遗忘的风云岁月，从墙上望下来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Next morning I sent the butler to New York with a letter to Wolfshiem, which asked for information and urged him to come out on the next train. That request seemed superfluous when I wrote it. I was sure he’d start when he saw the newspapers, just as I was sure there’d be a wire from Daisy before noon—but neither a wire nor Mr. Wolfshiem arrived; no one arrived except more police and photographers and newspaper men. When the butler brought back Wolfshiem’s answer I began to have a feeling of defiance, of scornful solidarity between Gatsby and me against them all.","sentences":[{"en":"Next morning I sent the butler to New York with a letter to Wolfshiem, which asked for information and urged him to come out on the next train.","zh":"隔日清早，我派管家到纽约送信给沃夫希姆，我在信里向他打听消息，也敦促他赶紧坐火车过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That request seemed superfluous when I wrote it.","zh":"其实我在写信时就觉得这个请求是多余的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was sure he’d start when he saw the newspapers, just as I was sure there’d be a wire from Daisy before noon—but neither a wire nor Mr. Wolfshiem arrived; no one arrived except more police and photographers and newspaper men.","zh":"我原本以为他看到报纸肯定就会动身，也以为中午之前肯定能收到黛熙的电报——但电报和沃夫希姆先生都没有来，谁也没有来，除了越来越多的警察、摄影师和记者。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When the butler brought back Wolfshiem’s answer I began to have a feeling of defiance, of scornful solidarity between Gatsby and me against them all.","zh":"当看完管家带回来的沃夫希姆的回信，有种愤慨在我心里油然而生，我要和盖茨比联合起来，鄙夷地对抗他们所有人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Dear Mr. Carraway. This has been one of the most terrible shocks of my life to me I hardly can believe it that it is true at all. Such a mad act as that man did should make us all think. I cannot come down now as I am tied up in some very important business and cannot get mixed up in this thing now. If there is anything I can do a little later let me know in a letter by Edgar. I hardly know where I am when I hear about a thing like this and am completely knocked down and out.","sentences":[{"en":"Dear Mr. Carraway.","zh":"亲爱的卡拉威先生：这是有生以来最让我感到震惊的事情，我简直不敢相信这是真的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This has been one of the most terrible shocks of my life to me I hardly can believe it that it is true at all.","zh":"亲爱的卡拉威先生：这是有生以来最让我感到震惊的事情，我简直不敢相信这是真的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Such a mad act as that man did should make us all think.","zh":"这人的疯狂行为值得我们大家深思。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I cannot come down now as I am tied up in some very important business and cannot get mixed up in this thing now.","zh":"我现在没法过来，因为手头有非常重要的生意要处理，不能让这件事给耽误了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If there is anything I can do a little later let me know in a letter by Edgar.","zh":"如果稍后有需要效劳的地方，请让埃德加送信告知我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I hardly know where I am when I hear about a thing like this and am completely knocked down and out.","zh":"听到这样的事情，我简直不知道身在何处，悲伤得难以自持。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Yours truly","sentences":[{"en":"Yours truly","zh":"你真诚的朋友梅耶·沃夫希姆","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Meyer Wolfshiem","sentences":[{"en":"Meyer Wolfshiem","zh":"然后他又用潦草的笔迹补充：","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"and then hasty addenda beneath:","sentences":[{"en":"and then hasty addenda beneath:","zh":"然后他又用潦草的笔迹补充：","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Let me know about the funeral etc do not know his family at all.","sentences":[{"en":"Let me know about the funeral etc do not know his family at all.","zh":"葬礼的事情请让我知道。我根本不认识他的家人。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When the phone rang that afternoon and Long Distance said Chicago was calling I thought this would be Daisy at last. But the connection came through as a man’s voice, very thin and far away.","sentences":[{"en":"When the phone rang that afternoon and Long Distance said Chicago was calling I thought this would be Daisy at last.","zh":"那天下午电话响起，总机说是芝加哥打来的长途电话，我以为黛熙终于打过来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the connection came through as a man’s voice, very thin and far away.","zh":"但话筒里传来的是男人的声音，听上去很轻，很遥远。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This is Slagle speaking…”","sentences":[{"en":"“This is Slagle speaking…”","zh":"“我是斯拉格…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes?” The name was unfamiliar.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes?”","zh":"“请讲，”这个名字听起来很陌生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The name was unfamiliar.","zh":"“请讲，”这个名字听起来很陌生。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hell of a note, isn’t it? Get my wire?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hell of a note, isn’t it?","zh":"“太让人意外了，对吧？收到我的电报了吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Get my wire?”","zh":"“太让人意外了，对吧？收到我的电报了吗？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There haven’t been any wires.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There haven’t been any wires.”","zh":"“什么电报也没有收到。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Young Parke’s in trouble,” he said rapidly. “They picked him up when he handed the bonds over the counter. They got a circular from New York giving ’em the numbers just five minutes before. What d’you know about that, hey? You never can tell in these hick towns—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Young Parke’s in trouble,” he said rapidly.","zh":"“帕克那小子出事了，”他语速很快地说，“他把债券摆上柜台的时候被抓个正着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“They picked him up when he handed the bonds over the counter.","zh":"“帕克那小子出事了，”他语速很快地说，“他把债券摆上柜台的时候被抓个正着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They got a circular from New York giving ’em the numbers just five minutes before.","zh":"他们之前五分钟刚刚收到纽约的通告，上面写着那些号码。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What d’you know about that, hey?","zh":"喂，你能想象得到吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You never can tell in these hick towns—”","zh":"你怎么也想不到在这种乡下地方…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Hello!” I interrupted breathlessly. “Look here—this isn’t Mr. Gatsby. Mr. Gatsby’s dead.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hello!”","zh":"“喂！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I interrupted breathlessly.","zh":"我赶紧打断他的话头，“听我说——我不是盖茨比先生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Look here—this isn’t Mr. Gatsby.","zh":"我赶紧打断他的话头，“听我说——我不是盖茨比先生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Mr. Gatsby’s dead.”","zh":"盖茨比先生死了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was a long silence on the other end of the wire, followed by an exclamation… then a quick squawk as the connection was broken.","sentences":[{"en":"There was a long silence on the other end of the wire, followed by an exclamation… then a quick squawk as the connection was broken.","zh":"电话那端沉默了很久，随即传来一声惊叫…然后在匆促的咒骂声中，电话被挂断了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"I think it was on the third day that a telegram signed Henry C. Gatz arrived from a town in Minnesota. It said only that the sender was leaving immediately and to postpone the funeral until he came.","sentences":[{"en":"I think it was on the third day that a telegram signed Henry C. Gatz arrived from a town in Minnesota.","zh":"我想应该是在第三天，有封署名亨利·盖兹的电报从明尼苏达州某个小城发过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It said only that the sender was leaving immediately and to postpone the funeral until he came.","zh":"上面只说发报人已经动身赶来，丧事等他到了之后再办。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was Gatsby’s father, a solemn old man, very helpless and dismayed, bundled up in a long cheap ulster against the warm September day. His eyes leaked continuously with excitement, and when I took the bag and umbrella from his hands he began to pull so incessantly at his sparse grey beard that I had difficulty in getting off his coat. He was on the point of collapse, so I took him into the music-room and made him sit down while I sent for something to eat. But he wouldn’t eat, and the glass of milk spilled from his trembling hand.","sentences":[{"en":"It was Gatsby’s father, a solemn old man, very helpless and dismayed, bundled up in a long cheap ulster against the warm September day.","zh":"那是盖茨比的父亲，一个表情沉重的老人，看上去非常无奈和消沉，身上裹着阿尔斯特长外套，尽管九月的天气依然很暖和。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His eyes leaked continuously with excitement, and when I took the bag and umbrella from his hands he began to pull so incessantly at his sparse grey beard that I had difficulty in getting off his coat.","zh":"他的眼睛不断露出惊奇的神色；我从他手上接过布袋和雨伞后，他就不断地轻抚他那稀疏的灰白胡子，所以我也没办法帮他把外套脱掉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was on the point of collapse, so I took him into the music-room and made him sit down while I sent for something to eat.","zh":"我看他站不稳的样子，于是扶他到音乐室，让他坐下，同时让佣人去弄点吃的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he wouldn’t eat, and the glass of milk spilled from his trembling hand.","zh":"但他不肯吃东西，手里拿着玻璃杯直发抖，牛奶都洒出来了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I saw it in the Chicago newspaper,” he said. “It was all in the Chicago newspaper. I started right away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I saw it in the Chicago newspaper,” he said.","zh":"“我在芝加哥的报纸上看到消息，”他说，“芝加哥的报纸全都是关于这件事的新闻。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It was all in the Chicago newspaper.","zh":"“我在芝加哥的报纸上看到消息，”他说，“芝加哥的报纸全都是关于这件事的新闻。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I started right away.”","zh":"我立刻就出发了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I didn’t know how to reach you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I didn’t know how to reach you.”","zh":"“我当时不知道怎样找到你。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His eyes, seeing nothing, moved ceaselessly about the room.","sentences":[{"en":"His eyes, seeing nothing, moved ceaselessly about the room.","zh":"他的眼神很茫然，不停地扫视着这个房间。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It was a madman,” he said. “He must have been mad.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It was a madman,” he said.","zh":"“那人是个疯子，”他说，“那人肯定是个疯子。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He must have been mad.”","zh":"“那人是个疯子，”他说，“那人肯定是个疯子。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wouldn’t you like some coffee?” I urged him.","sentences":[{"en":"“Wouldn’t you like some coffee?”","zh":"“你想喝点咖啡吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I urged him.","zh":"我问他。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I don’t want anything. I’m all right now, Mr.—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t want anything.","zh":"“我什么都不要。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’m all right now, Mr.—”","zh":"我没事，卡…卡…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Carraway.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Carraway.”","zh":"“卡拉威。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I’m all right now. Where have they got Jimmy?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I’m all right now.","zh":"“唉，我没事。他们把小詹放哪了？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Where have they got Jimmy?”","zh":"“唉，我没事。他们把小詹放哪了？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I took him into the drawing-room, where his son lay, and left him there. Some little boys had come up on the steps and were looking into the hall; when I told them who had arrived, they went reluctantly away.","sentences":[{"en":"I took him into the drawing-room, where his son lay, and left him there.","zh":"我把他带到客厅，他的儿子就躺在那里，然后留下他一个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some little boys had come up on the steps and were looking into the hall; when I told them who had arrived, they went reluctantly away.","zh":"有几个小男孩爬上台阶，正在往客厅里面看；我告诉他们来的人是谁，他们这才一步两回头地走开。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"After a little while Mr. Gatz opened the door and came out, his mouth ajar, his face flushed slightly, his eyes leaking isolated and unpunctual tears. He had reached an age where death no longer has the quality of ghastly surprise, and when he looked around him now for the first time and saw the height and splendour of the hall and the great rooms opening out from it into other rooms, his grief began to be mixed with an awed pride. I helped him to a bedroom upstairs; while he took off his coat and vest I told him that all arrangements had been deferred until he came.","sentences":[{"en":"After a little while Mr. Gatz opened the door and came out, his mouth ajar, his face flushed slightly, his eyes leaking isolated and unpunctual tears.","zh":"不久之后，盖兹先生打开房门走出来，他的嘴巴是张开的，脸上有点红，泪珠滚滚而下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had reached an age where death no longer has the quality of ghastly surprise, and when he looked around him now for the first time and saw the height and splendour of the hall and the great rooms opening out from it into other rooms, his grief began to be mixed with an awed pride.","zh":"他已经到了不再为死亡感到错愕的年纪，这时他第一次环顾四周，看到门厅如此宽敞豪华，门厅之后是连绵不绝的大房间，他的悲哀开始混进些许敬畏的骄傲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I helped him to a bedroom upstairs; while he took off his coat and vest I told him that all arrangements had been deferred until he came.","zh":"我扶着他走进楼上的卧室，在他脱下外套和马甲时，我告诉他所有安排已经推迟，等他来决定。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I didn’t know what you’d want, Mr. Gatsby—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I didn’t know what you’d want, Mr. Gatsby—”","zh":"“我不知道你有什么想法，盖茨比先生…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Gatz is my name.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Gatz is my name.”","zh":"“我姓盖兹。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“—Mr. Gatz. I thought you might want to take the body West.”","sentences":[{"en":"“—Mr. Gatz.","zh":"“——盖兹先生，我觉得你可能想把尸体运到西部。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I thought you might want to take the body West.”","zh":"“——盖兹先生，我觉得你可能想把尸体运到西部。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He shook his head.","sentences":[{"en":"He shook his head.","zh":"他摇摇头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Jimmy always liked it better down East. He rose up to his position in the East. Were you a friend of my boy’s, Mr.—?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Jimmy always liked it better down East.","zh":"“小詹向来更喜欢东部。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He rose up to his position in the East.","zh":"他是在东部发迹的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Were you a friend of my boy’s, Mr.—?”","zh":"你是我家孩子的朋友吗，卡…卡…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“We were close friends.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We were close friends.”","zh":"“我们是好朋友。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He had a big future before him, you know. He was only a young man, but he had a lot of brain power here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He had a big future before him, you know.","zh":"“他本来有很好的前途，你知道的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was only a young man, but he had a lot of brain power here.”","zh":"他只是个年轻人，但他的脑力很好。”他边说边戳着自己的脑袋，我点头表示同意。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He touched his head impressively, and I nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"He touched his head impressively, and I nodded.","zh":"他只是个年轻人，但他的脑力很好。”他边说边戳着自己的脑袋，我点头表示同意。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“If he’d of lived, he’d of been a great man. A man like James J. Hill. He’d of helped build up the country.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If he’d of lived, he’d of been a great man.","zh":"“如果他能活下去，他会变成了不起的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A man like James J. Hill.","zh":"像詹姆斯·希尔那样的大人物。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He’d of helped build up the country.”","zh":"他会帮助建设这个国家的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“That’s true,” I said, uncomfortably.","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s true,” I said, uncomfortably.","zh":"“你说得对，”我不自在地说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He fumbled at the embroidered coverlet, trying to take it from the bed, and lay down stiffly—was instantly asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"He fumbled at the embroidered coverlet, trying to take it from the bed, and lay down stiffly—was instantly asleep.","zh":"他笨手笨脚地去弄那绣花的床罩，想把它拉掉，然后硬邦邦地躺下——立刻就睡着了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That night an obviously frightened person called up, and demanded to know who I was before he would give his name.","sentences":[{"en":"That night an obviously frightened person called up, and demanded to know who I was before he would give his name.","zh":"那晚有个明显很害怕的人打电话来，不肯说出他的名字，非要先问我是谁。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“This is Mr. Carraway,” I said.","sentences":[{"en":"“This is Mr. Carraway,” I said.","zh":"“我是卡拉威先生，”我说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh!” He sounded relieved. “This is Klipspringer.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh!”","zh":"“啊！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sounded relieved.","zh":"他如释重负地说，“我是克里普斯普林格。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“This is Klipspringer.”","zh":"他如释重负地说，“我是克里普斯普林格。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I was relieved too, for that seemed to promise another friend at Gatsby’s grave. I didn’t want it to be in the papers and draw a sightseeing crowd, so I’d been calling up a few people myself. They were hard to find.","sentences":[{"en":"I was relieved too, for that seemed to promise another friend at Gatsby’s grave.","zh":"我也如释重负，因为看来盖茨比墓前将会多一个朋友。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I didn’t want it to be in the papers and draw a sightseeing crowd, so I’d been calling up a few people myself.","zh":"我不希望葬礼变成报纸上的新闻，引来许多看热闹的人，所以我亲自打过电话给几个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were hard to find.","zh":"他们很难找到。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The funeral’s tomorrow,” I said. “Three o’clock, here at the house. I wish you’d tell anybody who’d be interested.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The funeral’s tomorrow,” I said.","zh":"“葬礼定在明天，”我说，“下午三点，在这座房子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Three o’clock, here at the house.","zh":"“葬礼定在明天，”我说，“下午三点，在这座房子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I wish you’d tell anybody who’d be interested.”","zh":"我希望你能通知其他感兴趣的人。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, I will,” he broke out hastily. “Of course I’m not likely to see anybody, but if I do.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I will,” he broke out hastily.","zh":"“我会的啦，”他赶紧接口说，“当然，我不太可能见到什么人。但见到的话，我会通知的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Of course I’m not likely to see anybody, but if I do.”","zh":"“我会的啦，”他赶紧接口说，“当然，我不太可能见到什么人。但见到的话，我会通知的。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"His tone made me suspicious.","sentences":[{"en":"His tone made me suspicious.","zh":"他的口气让我起疑。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Of course you’ll be there yourself.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Of course you’ll be there yourself.”","zh":"“你自己肯定会来的吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, I’ll certainly try. What I called up about is—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I’ll certainly try.","zh":"“嗯，我会争取的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What I called up about is—”","zh":"我打电话来是想…”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Wait a minute,” I interrupted. “How about saying you’ll come?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wait a minute,” I interrupted.","zh":"“且慢，”我打断他的话，“你就答应来吧，怎么样？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“How about saying you’ll come?”","zh":"“且慢，”我打断他的话，“你就答应来吧，怎么样？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, the fact is—the truth of the matter is that I’m staying with some people up here in Greenwich, and they rather expect me to be with them tomorrow. In fact, there’s a sort of picnic or something. Of course I’ll do my best to get away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, the fact is—the truth of the matter is that I’m staying with some people up here in Greenwich, and they rather expect me to be with them tomorrow.","zh":"“哎呀，其实——实际上，我目前和几个朋友在格林尼治，他们相当希望我明天陪他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In fact, there’s a sort of picnic or something.","zh":"其实明天他们会去野炊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Of course I’ll do my best to get away.”","zh":"当然，我会尽量争取来的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I ejaculated an unrestrained “Huh!” and he must have heard me, for he went on nervously:","sentences":[{"en":"I ejaculated an unrestrained “Huh!” and he must have heard me, for he went on nervously:","zh":"我忍不住发出了“哼！”的声音，他肯定听见了，因为他接下来很紧张地说：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What I called up about was a pair of shoes I left there. I wonder if it’d be too much trouble to have the butler send them on. You see, they’re tennis shoes, and I’m sort of helpless without them. My address is care of B. F.—”","sentences":[{"en":"“What I called up about was a pair of shoes I left there.","zh":"“我打电话来，是因为我留了一双鞋在那边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I wonder if it’d be too much trouble to have the butler send them on.","zh":"我在想，如果不是太麻烦的话，请让管家把它们寄给我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You see, they’re tennis shoes, and I’m sort of helpless without them.","zh":"你知道吗，那双是网球鞋，没有它们我真不知道该怎么办。我的地址是…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"My address is care of B. F.—”","zh":"你知道吗，那双是网球鞋，没有它们我真不知道该怎么办。我的地址是…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I didn’t hear the rest of the name, because I hung up the receiver.","sentences":[{"en":"I didn’t hear the rest of the name, because I hung up the receiver.","zh":"我没有听到他下面的话，因为我把听筒挂掉了。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"After that I felt a certain shame for Gatsby—one gentleman to whom I telephoned implied that he had got what he deserved. However, that was my fault, for he was one of those who used to sneer most bitterly at Gatsby on the courage of Gatsby’s liquor, and I should have known better than to call him.","sentences":[{"en":"After that I felt a certain shame for Gatsby—one gentleman to whom I telephoned implied that he had got what he deserved.","zh":"在那之后，我真替盖茨比感到不值——某位接到我电话的绅士竟然含沙射影地表示盖茨比死有余辜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, that was my fault, for he was one of those who used to sneer most bitterly at Gatsby on the courage of Gatsby’s liquor, and I should have known better than to call him.","zh":"然而这是我的错，因为以前有些人经常借盖茨比的酒壮胆，然后恶毒地咒骂盖茨比，而他是骂得最恶毒的人之一，我本来不应该打给他的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The morning of the funeral I went up to New York to see Meyer Wolfshiem; I couldn’t seem to reach him any other way. The door that I pushed open, on the advice of an elevator boy, was marked “The Swastika Holding Company,” and at first there didn’t seem to be anyone inside. But when I’d shouted “hello” several times in vain, an argument broke out behind a partition, and presently a lovely Jewess appeared at an interior door and scrutinized me with black hostile eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"The morning of the funeral I went up to New York to see Meyer Wolfshiem; I couldn’t seem to reach him any other way.","zh":"举行葬礼那天早晨，我去纽约城里找沃夫希姆；用其他方法我根本联系不到他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The door that I pushed open, on the advice of an elevator boy, was marked “The Swastika Holding Company,” and at first there didn’t seem to be anyone inside.","zh":"根据负责开电梯那男孩的指引，我推开那扇挂着“卍控股公司”招牌的门，刚开始里面好像没人在。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when I’d shouted “hello” several times in vain, an argument broke out behind a partition, and presently a lovely Jewess appeared at an interior door and scrutinized me with black hostile eyes.","zh":"可是当我喊了几声“喂”也没人应答之后，隔板后面传出几句争执的声音，然后有个美貌的犹太女人出现在里间的门口，乌黑的眼睛充满敌意地看着我。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nobody’s in,” she said. “Mr. Wolfshiem’s gone to Chicago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nobody’s in,” she said.","zh":"“里面没有人，”她说，“沃夫希姆先生去芝加哥了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Mr. Wolfshiem’s gone to Chicago.”","zh":"“里面没有人，”她说，“沃夫希姆先生去芝加哥了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The first part of this was obviously untrue, for someone had begun to whistle “The Rosary,” tunelessly, inside.","sentences":[{"en":"The first part of this was obviously untrue, for someone had begun to whistle “The Rosary,” tunelessly, inside.","zh":"前半句显然是假话，因为里面已经有人开始跑调地用口哨吹起了“玫瑰经”。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Please say that Mr. Carraway wants to see him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Please say that Mr. Carraway wants to see him.”","zh":"“请跟他说卡拉威先生求见。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I can’t get him back from Chicago, can I?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I can’t get him back from Chicago, can I?”","zh":"“我又不能让他从芝加哥回来，对吧？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"At this moment a voice, unmistakably Wolfshiem’s, called “Stella!” from the other side of the door.","sentences":[{"en":"At this moment a voice, unmistakably Wolfshiem’s, called “Stella!” from the other side of the door.","zh":"这时门后有人大喊：“斯泰娜！”，那毫无疑问就是沃夫希姆的声音。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Leave your name on the desk,” she said quickly. “I’ll give it to him when he gets back.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave your name on the desk,” she said quickly.","zh":"“请在前台留下你的名字，”她匆匆地说，“等他回来我就告诉他。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’ll give it to him when he gets back.”","zh":"“请在前台留下你的名字，”她匆匆地说，“等他回来我就告诉他。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“But I know he’s there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But I know he’s there.”","zh":"“但我知道他就在这里。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She took a step toward me and began to slide her hands indignantly up and down her hips.","sentences":[{"en":"She took a step toward me and began to slide her hands indignantly up and down her hips.","zh":"她向我踏上一步，双手叉腰，做出很生气的样子。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You young men think you can force your way in here any time,” she scolded. “We’re getting sickantired of it. When I say he’s in Chicago, he’s in Chicago.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You young men think you can force your way in here any time,” she scolded.","zh":"“你们这些年轻人以为随时都可以到这里来，”她气势汹汹说，“我们他妈的已经受够了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“We’re getting sickantired of it.","zh":"“你们这些年轻人以为随时都可以到这里来，”她气势汹汹说，“我们他妈的已经受够了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When I say he’s in Chicago, he’s in Chicago.”","zh":"我说他在芝加哥，他就在芝加哥。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I mentioned Gatsby.","sentences":[{"en":"I mentioned Gatsby.","zh":"我提起了盖茨比的名字。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh-h!” She looked at me over again. “Will you just—What was your name?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh-h!”","zh":"“啊！”她又从头到脚打量我，“你能…","scope":"group"},{"en":"She looked at me over again.","zh":"“啊！”她又从头到脚打量我，“你能…","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Will you just—What was your name?”","zh":"请问你贵姓？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She vanished. In a moment Meyer Wolfshiem stood solemnly in the doorway, holding out both hands. He drew me into his office, remarking in a reverent voice that it was a sad time for all of us, and offered me a cigar.","sentences":[{"en":"She vanished.","zh":"她消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In a moment Meyer Wolfshiem stood solemnly in the doorway, holding out both hands.","zh":"片刻之后，沃夫希姆肃穆地站在走廊里，两只手都伸出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He drew me into his office, remarking in a reverent voice that it was a sad time for all of us, and offered me a cigar.","zh":"他拉着我走进他的办公室，用虔敬的口吻说现在我们大家都很伤心，并递给我一根雪茄。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“My memory goes back to when first I met him,” he said. “A young major just out of the army and covered over with medals he got in the war. He was so hard up he had to keep on wearing his uniform because he couldn’t buy some regular clothes. First time I saw him was when he came into Winebrenner’s poolroom at Forty-third Street and asked for a job. He hadn’t eat anything for a couple of days. ‘Come on have some lunch with me,’ I said. He ate more than four dollars’ worth of food in half an hour.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My memory goes back to when first I met him,” he said.","zh":"“我的记忆回到了初次和他见面的时候，”他说，“他是个刚从部队退役的年轻少校，胸前挂满了在战争中得到的军功章。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“A young major just out of the army and covered over with medals he got in the war.","zh":"“我的记忆回到了初次和他见面的时候，”他说，“他是个刚从部队退役的年轻少校，胸前挂满了在战争中得到的军功章。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was so hard up he had to keep on wearing his uniform because he couldn’t buy some regular clothes.","zh":"他当时非常穷，整天穿着军装，因为他买不起便服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"First time I saw him was when he came into Winebrenner’s poolroom at Forty-third Street and asked for a job.","zh":"我第一次和他见面时，他走进第四十三街的维恩布伦纳撞球厅，想找点活干。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He hadn’t eat anything for a couple of days. ‘Come on have some lunch with me,’ I said.","zh":"他已经有好几天没吃过东西。‘走吧，我带你去吃午饭，’我说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He ate more than four dollars’ worth of food in half an hour.”","zh":"他半个小时内吃掉了四块钱的饭菜。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Did you start him in business?” I inquired.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you start him in business?”","zh":"“他做生意是你提携的吧？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I inquired.","zh":"我问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Start him! I made him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Start him!","zh":"“何止提携！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I made him.”","zh":"他是我一手栽培的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh.”","zh":"“哦。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I raised him up out of nothing, right out of the gutter. I saw right away he was a fine-appearing, gentlemanly young man, and when he told me he was at Oggsford I knew I could use him good. I got him to join the American Legion and he used to stand high there. Right off he did some work for a client of mine up to Albany. We were so thick like that in everything”—he held up two bulbous fingers—“always together.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I raised him up out of nothing, right out of the gutter.","zh":"“他原本身无分文，是我从阴沟里硬把他栽培起来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw right away he was a fine-appearing, gentlemanly young man, and when he told me he was at Oggsford I knew I could use him good.","zh":"我立刻看出来他是个长相英俊、温文尔雅的年轻人，他跟我说他念过‘牛精’之后，我就知道他值得好好培养。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I got him to join the American Legion and he used to stand high there.","zh":"我让他加入了美国退伍军人联合会，他以前在那里地位很高。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Right off he did some work for a client of mine up to Albany.","zh":"他刚出道就北上奥尔巴尼帮我的客户解决了某些难题。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We were so thick like that in everything”—he held up two bulbous fingers—“always together.”","zh":"我们无论做什么事总是这么亲密无间，”——他伸出两根胖手指——“总是在一起。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I wondered if this partnership had included the World’s Series transaction in 1919.","sentences":[{"en":"I wondered if this partnership had included the World’s Series transaction in 1919.","zh":"我在想1919年的世界棒球大赛舞弊案是否也是他们联手干的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Now he’s dead,” I said after a moment. “You were his closest friend, so I know you’ll want to come to his funeral this afternoon.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now he’s dead,” I said after a moment.","zh":"“现在他去世了，”我隔了片刻之后说，“你是他最亲近的朋友，所以我觉得你今天下午应该愿意去参加他的葬礼。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You were his closest friend, so I know you’ll want to come to his funeral this afternoon.”","zh":"“现在他去世了，”我隔了片刻之后说，“你是他最亲近的朋友，所以我觉得你今天下午应该愿意去参加他的葬礼。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’d like to come.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’d like to come.”","zh":"“现在他去世了，”我隔了片刻之后说，“你是他最亲近的朋友，所以我觉得你今天下午应该愿意去参加他的葬礼。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Well, come then.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, come then.”","zh":"“我倒是想去。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"The hair in his nostrils quivered slightly, and as he shook his head his eyes filled with tears.","sentences":[{"en":"The hair in his nostrils quivered slightly, and as he shook his head his eyes filled with tears.","zh":"“好啊，那就去啊。”他含泪摇摇头，鼻毛随之轻轻地抖动。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I can’t do it—I can’t get mixed up in it,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“I can’t do it—I can’t get mixed up in it,” he said.","zh":"“我不能去——我不能受这件事牵连，”他说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“There’s nothing to get mixed up in. It’s all over now.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There’s nothing to get mixed up in.","zh":"“不会牵连到你的。这件事已经结束了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s all over now.”","zh":"“不会牵连到你的。这件事已经结束了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“When a man gets killed I never like to get mixed up in it in any way. I keep out. When I was a young man it was different—if a friend of mine died, no matter how, I stuck with them to the end. You may think that’s sentimental, but I mean it—to the bitter end.”","sentences":[{"en":"“When a man gets killed I never like to get mixed up in it in any way.","zh":"“反正我不想受人命案子牵连。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I keep out.","zh":"我要置身事外。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When I was a young man it was different—if a friend of mine died, no matter how, I stuck with them to the end.","zh":"年轻时我倒不是这样的——那时如果我的朋友死了，不管是怎么死的，我都会陪他们到最后。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You may think that’s sentimental, but I mean it—to the bitter end.”","zh":"你也许会认为这是感情用事，但我不骗你——我会陪他们走完痛苦的人生路。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I saw that for some reason of his own he was determined not to come, so I stood up.","sentences":[{"en":"I saw that for some reason of his own he was determined not to come, so I stood up.","zh":"我明白他决定不去也是有理由的，所以站了起来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Are you a college man?” he inquired suddenly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you a college man?” he inquired suddenly.","zh":"“你念过大学，对吧？”他突然问。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"For a moment I thought he was going to suggest a “gonnegtion,” but he only nodded and shook my hand.","sentences":[{"en":"For a moment I thought he was going to suggest a “gonnegtion,” but he only nodded and shook my hand.","zh":"刹那间我以为他准备要跟我搞“光系”，但他只是点点头，跟我握手道别。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Let us learn to show our friendship for a man when he is alive and not after he is dead,” he suggested. “After that my own rule is to let everything alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let us learn to show our friendship for a man when he is alive and not after he is dead,” he suggested.","zh":"“我们要明白，讲交情要在人活着的时候讲，人死就没有交情了，”他意味深长地说，“我自己的原则是，人死我就什么都不管了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“After that my own rule is to let everything alone.”","zh":"“我们要明白，讲交情要在人活着的时候讲，人死就没有交情了，”他意味深长地说，“我自己的原则是，人死我就什么都不管了。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When I left his office the sky had turned dark and I got back to West Egg in a drizzle. After changing my clothes I went next door and found Mr. Gatz walking up and down excitedly in the hall. His pride in his son and in his son’s possessions was continually increasing and now he had something to show me.","sentences":[{"en":"When I left his office the sky had turned dark and I got back to West Egg in a drizzle.","zh":"离开他的办公室时，天变黑了；等我回到西卵已经飘起毛毛细雨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After changing my clothes I went next door and found Mr. Gatz walking up and down excitedly in the hall.","zh":"换好衣服之后，我走到隔壁，发现盖兹先生兴奋地在门厅里走来走去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His pride in his son and in his son’s possessions was continually increasing and now he had something to show me.","zh":"他越来越为他儿子和他儿子的产业感到自豪，这时他有东西要给我看。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Jimmy sent me this picture.” He took out his wallet with trembling fingers. “Look there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Jimmy sent me this picture.”","zh":"“小詹给我寄了这张照片，”他用颤抖的手指递过他的钱包，“你看。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He took out his wallet with trembling fingers.","zh":"“小詹给我寄了这张照片，”他用颤抖的手指递过他的钱包，“你看。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Look there.”","zh":"“小詹给我寄了这张照片，”他用颤抖的手指递过他的钱包，“你看。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"It was a photograph of the house, cracked in the corners and dirty with many hands. He pointed out every detail to me eagerly. “Look there!” and then sought admiration from my eyes. He had shown it so often that I think it was more real to him now than the house itself.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a photograph of the house, cracked in the corners and dirty with many hands.","zh":"那是这座房子的照片，四角已经裂开，被很多人摸得很脏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He pointed out every detail to me eagerly.","zh":"他热切地向我指出每个细节。他会说“你看！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Look there!” and then sought admiration from my eyes.","zh":"，然后看我眼里有没有赞赏的意思。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had shown it so often that I think it was more real to him now than the house itself.","zh":"他把照片给人看过那么多次，我想在他眼里，照片可能比房子本身还要真实。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Jimmy sent it to me. I think it’s a very pretty picture. It shows up well.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Jimmy sent it to me.","zh":"“小詹把它寄给我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think it’s a very pretty picture.","zh":"我觉得它是很漂亮的照片。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It shows up well.”","zh":"拍得很好。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Very well. Had you seen him lately?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well.","zh":"“非常好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Had you seen him lately?”","zh":"你后来有见过他吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“He come out to see me two years ago and bought me the house I live in now. Of course we was broke up when he run off from home, but I see now there was a reason for it. He knew he had a big future in front of him. And ever since he made a success he was very generous with me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He come out to see me two years ago and bought me the house I live in now.","zh":"“两年前他去看过我，给我买了现在住的房子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Of course we was broke up when he run off from home, but I see now there was a reason for it.","zh":"当然，从前他离家出走的时候，我们感到很伤心，但现在我明白他是有道理的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He knew he had a big future in front of him.","zh":"他知道他前面有远大的未来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And ever since he made a success he was very generous with me.”","zh":"自从发达之后，他对我非常慷慨。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He seemed reluctant to put away the picture, held it for another minute, lingeringly, before my eyes. Then he returned the wallet and pulled from his pocket a ragged old copy of a book called Hopalong Cassidy.","sentences":[{"en":"He seemed reluctant to put away the picture, held it for another minute, lingeringly, before my eyes.","zh":"他似乎不舍得把照片收起来，又拿着它在我眼前摇晃了一分钟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he returned the wallet and pulled from his pocket a ragged old copy of a book called Hopalong Cassidy.","zh":"随后他把钱包放回去，从口袋里掏出一本破旧的书，叫做《霍巴隆·卡西迪》。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Look here, this is a book he had when he was a boy. It just shows you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look here, this is a book he had when he was a boy.","zh":"“你看，这是他小时候读的书。你一看就明白。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It just shows you.”","zh":"“你看，这是他小时候读的书。你一看就明白。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He opened it at the back cover and turned it around for me to see. On the last flyleaf was printed the word schedule, and the date September 12, 1906. And underneath:","sentences":[{"en":"He opened it at the back cover and turned it around for me to see.","zh":"他打开封底，转过来给我看。最后那张空白页上有“作息表”三个字，日期是“1902年9月12日”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"On the last flyleaf was printed the word schedule, and the date September 12, 1906.","zh":"他打开封底，转过来给我看。最后那张空白页上有“作息表”三个字，日期是“1902年9月12日”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And underneath:","zh":"下面写着：","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Rise from bed | 6:00 | a.m. |","sentences":[{"en":"| Rise from bed | 6:00 | a.m. |","zh":"起床…6:00","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| --- | --- | --- |","sentences":[{"en":"| --- | --- | --- |","zh":"哑铃锻炼和爬墙练习…6:15–6:30","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Dumbell exercise and wall-scaling | 6:15⁠–⁠6:30 | “ |","sentences":[{"en":"| Dumbell exercise and wall-scaling | 6:15⁠–⁠6:30 | “ |","zh":"哑铃锻炼和爬墙练习…6:15–6:30","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Study electricity, etc. | 7:15⁠–⁠8:15 | “ |","sentences":[{"en":"| Study electricity, etc. | 7:15⁠–⁠8:15 | “ |","zh":"研究电学等等…7:15–8:15","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Work | 8:30⁠–⁠4:30 | p.m. |","sentences":[{"en":"| Work | 8:30⁠–⁠4:30 | p.m. |","zh":"工作…8:30–16:30","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Baseball and sports | 4:30⁠–⁠5:00 | “ |","sentences":[{"en":"| Baseball and sports | 4:30⁠–⁠5:00 | “ |","zh":"棒球和其他运动…16:30–17:00","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Practise elocution, poise and how to attain it | 5:00⁠–⁠6:00 | “ |","sentences":[{"en":"| Practise elocution, poise and how to attain it | 5:00⁠–⁠6:00 | “ |","zh":"练习演讲和社交礼仪…17:00–18:00","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"| Study needed inventions | 7:00⁠–⁠9:00 | “ |","sentences":[{"en":"| Study needed inventions | 7:00⁠–⁠9:00 | “ |","zh":"研究有用的新发明…19:00–21:00","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"General Resolves","sentences":[{"en":"General Resolves","zh":"总体目标","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"No wasting time at Shafters or [a name, indecipherable]","sentences":[{"en":"No wasting time at Shafters or [a name, indecipherable]","zh":"绝不浪费时间去沙福特家或者【某个姓，字迹看不清楚】","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"No more smokeing or chewing.","sentences":[{"en":"No more smokeing or chewing.","zh":"绝不吸卷烟或者嚼烟叶","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Bath every other day","sentences":[{"en":"Bath every other day","zh":"每两日洗一次澡","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Read one improving book or magazine per week","sentences":[{"en":"Read one improving book or magazine per week","zh":"每周读一本有益的书或者杂志","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Save $5.00 [crossed out] $3.00 per week","sentences":[{"en":"Save $5.00 [crossed out] $3.00 per week","zh":"每周储存五块钱【划掉】三块钱","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Be better to parents","sentences":[{"en":"Be better to parents","zh":"更加孝顺父母","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I came across this book by accident,” said the old man. “It just shows you, don’t it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I came across this book by accident,” said the old man.","zh":"“这本书是我无意间发现的，”老人说，“你一看就明白了，对吧？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It just shows you, don’t it?”","zh":"“这本书是我无意间发现的，”老人说，“你一看就明白了，对吧？”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“It just shows you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It just shows you.”","zh":"“是的。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Jimmy was bound to get ahead. He always had some resolves like this or something. Do you notice what he’s got about improving his mind? He was always great for that. He told me I et like a hog once, and I beat him for it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Jimmy was bound to get ahead.","zh":"“小詹注定要发达的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He always had some resolves like this or something.","zh":"他总是有这样的决心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you notice what he’s got about improving his mind?","zh":"你发现他很注意提高自己的修养了吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was always great for that.","zh":"你发现他很注意提高自己的修养了吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"He told me I et like a hog once, and I beat him for it.”","zh":"有一次他说我吃饭像猪一样，我还打了他一顿。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He was reluctant to close the book, reading each item aloud and then looking eagerly at me. I think he rather expected me to copy down the list for my own use.","sentences":[{"en":"He was reluctant to close the book, reading each item aloud and then looking eagerly at me.","zh":"他不舍得把这本书合上，而是大声地把每一项念出来，然后热切地看着我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think he rather expected me to copy down the list for my own use.","zh":"我想他是相当期望我会把这张表格抄下来自己用。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"A little before three the Lutheran minister arrived from Flushing, and I began to look involuntarily out the windows for other cars. So did Gatsby’s father. And as the time passed and the servants came in and stood waiting in the hall, his eyes began to blink anxiously, and he spoke of the rain in a worried, uncertain way. The minister glanced several times at his watch, so I took him aside and asked him to wait for half an hour. But it wasn’t any use. Nobody came.","sentences":[{"en":"A little before three the Lutheran minister arrived from Flushing, and I began to look involuntarily out the windows for other cars.","zh":"在此之前不久，有个路德派牧师从法拉盛赶过来，我开始不由自主地向窗外望去，看看有没有别的车来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"So did Gatsby’s father.","zh":"在此之前不久，有个路德派牧师从法拉盛赶过来，我开始不由自主地向窗外望去，看看有没有别的车来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And as the time passed and the servants came in and stood waiting in the hall, his eyes began to blink anxiously, and he spoke of the rain in a worried, uncertain way.","zh":"盖茨比的父亲也是这样。等到过了三点，几个佣人都走进来了，站在门厅里等，他开始着急地眨着眼睛，担心地说不知道雨要下多久。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The minister glanced several times at his watch, so I took him aside and asked him to wait for half an hour.","zh":"牧师也不耐烦地看了几次手表，所以我把他拉到旁边，请他再等半个小时。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But it wasn’t any use.","zh":"但这完全没有用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nobody came.","zh":"谁也没有来。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"About five o’clock our procession of three cars reached the cemetery and stopped in a thick drizzle beside the gate—first a motor hearse, horribly black and wet, then Mr. Gatz and the minister and me in the limousine, and a little later four or five servants and the postman from West Egg, in Gatsby’s station wagon, all wet to the skin. As we started through the gate into the cemetery I heard a car stop and then the sound of someone splashing after us over the soggy ground. I looked around. It was the man with owl-eyed glasses whom I had found marvelling over Gatsby’s books in the library one night three months before.","sentences":[{"en":"About five o’clock our procession of three cars reached the cemetery and stopped in a thick drizzle beside the gate—first a motor hearse, horribly black and wet, then Mr. Gatz and the minister and me in the limousine, and a little later four or five servants and the postman from West Egg, in Gatsby’s station wagon, all wet to the skin.","zh":"五点钟时，我们一排三辆车开到了墓园，冒着瓢泼大雨停在大门口——最前面是灵车，又黑又湿，看上去很可怕；跟着是那辆豪华车，盖兹先生、牧师和我坐在里面，最后是盖茨比的旅行车，坐着四五个佣人和西卵的邮差；我们大家浑身都湿透了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As we started through the gate into the cemetery I heard a car stop and then the sound of someone splashing after us over the soggy ground.","zh":"就在我们开始走进墓园的大门时，我听到有辆车停下来，然后又听到有人踩着水追赶我们的声音。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I looked around.","zh":"我回头去看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the man with owl-eyed glasses whom I had found marvelling over Gatsby’s books in the library one night three months before.","zh":"原来是那个戴着猫头鹰眼镜的人，三个月前的某个晚上，我曾经见到他在盖茨比的书房对着那些书称赞不已。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I’d never seen him since then. I don’t know how he knew about the funeral, or even his name. The rain poured down his thick glasses, and he took them off and wiped them to see the protecting canvas unrolled from Gatsby’s grave.","sentences":[{"en":"I’d never seen him since then.","zh":"自那以后我再也没有见过他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t know how he knew about the funeral, or even his name.","zh":"我不知道他从何处得知葬礼在今天举行，甚至也不知道他的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The rain poured down his thick glasses, and he took them off and wiped them to see the protecting canvas unrolled from Gatsby’s grave.","zh":"大雨倾倒在他的眼镜上，他把眼镜摘下来，擦去雨水，看佣人把防水的布铺开，遮住盖茨比的坟头。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I tried to think about Gatsby then for a moment, but he was already too far away, and I could only remember, without resentment, that Daisy hadn’t sent a message or a flower. Dimly I heard someone murmur “Blessed are the dead that the rain falls on,” and then the owl-eyed man said “Amen to that,” in a brave voice.","sentences":[{"en":"I tried to think about Gatsby then for a moment, but he was already too far away, and I could only remember, without resentment, that Daisy hadn’t sent a message or a flower.","zh":"我努力地回忆着盖茨比的音容笑貌，但他已经离得太远，我只能想起，毫不怨恨地想起，黛熙没有送信或者送花来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Dimly I heard someone murmur “Blessed are the dead that the rain falls on,” and then the owl-eyed man said “Amen to that,” in a brave voice.","zh":"隐隐约约之间我听到有人低声说“愿上帝保佑这位淋雨的死者”，然后那位猫头鹰眼镜先生响亮地说：“但愿如此，阿门！”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We straggled down quickly through the rain to the cars. Owl-eyes spoke to me by the gate.","sentences":[{"en":"We straggled down quickly through the rain to the cars.","zh":"我们在雨中踉跄地朝几辆车跑过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Owl-eyes spoke to me by the gate.","zh":"猫头鹰眼镜先生在大门口跟我聊了几句。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I couldn’t get to the house,” he remarked.","sentences":[{"en":"“I couldn’t get to the house,” he remarked.","zh":"“我没能赶到别墅去吊丧，”他说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Neither could anybody else.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Neither could anybody else.”","zh":"“别人也都没有去。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Go on!” He started. “Why, my God! they used to go there by the hundreds.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go on!”","zh":"“不会吧！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He started.","zh":"他吃惊地说，“唉，我的上帝！他们以前一去就是几百人。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Why, my God! they used to go there by the hundreds.”","zh":"他吃惊地说，“唉，我的上帝！他们以前一去就是几百人。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He took off his glasses and wiped them again, outside and in.","sentences":[{"en":"He took off his glasses and wiped them again, outside and in.","zh":"他摘下眼镜，又里里外外地擦了一遍。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“The poor son-of-a-bitch,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“The poor son-of-a-bitch,” he said.","zh":"“这婊子养的真可怜，”他说。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"One of my most vivid memories is of coming back West from prep school and later from college at Christmas time. Those who went farther than Chicago would gather in the old dim Union Station at six o’clock of a December evening, with a few Chicago friends, already caught up into their own holiday gaieties, to bid them a hasty goodbye. I remember the fur coats of the girls returning from Miss This-or-That’s and the chatter of frozen breath and the hands waving overhead as we caught sight of old acquaintances, and the matchings of invitations: “Are you going to the Ordways’? the Herseys’? the Schultzes’?” and the long green tickets clasped tight in our gloved hands. And last the murky yellow cars of the Chicago, Milwaukee and St. Paul railroad looking cheerful as Christmas itself on the tracks beside the gate.","sentences":[{"en":"One of my most vivid memories is of coming back West from prep school and later from college at Christmas time.","zh":"我印象中最难忘的事，是在念预科学校和后来念大学期间，每逢圣诞回西部的经历。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Those who went farther than Chicago would gather in the old dim Union Station at six o’clock of a December evening, with a few Chicago friends, already caught up into their own holiday gaieties, to bid them a hasty goodbye.","zh":"每年十二月某夜六点，那些家住芝加哥以西的人，会聚集在古老昏暗的联合车站，而芝加哥本地的同学则已经沉浸在节日氛围里，欢乐地和他们道别。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I remember the fur coats of the girls returning from Miss This-or-That’s and the chatter of frozen breath and the hands waving overhead as we caught sight of old acquaintances, and the matchings of invitations: “Are you going to the Ordways’? the Herseys’? the Schultzes’?” and the long green tickets clasped tight in our gloved hands.","zh":"我记得车站里有很多从各所女校回来的、穿着皮衣的女生，大家冒着白气热火朝天地闲聊，每当看到熟人就兴奋地把手举到头顶挥舞，还会相互攀比接到的邀请，“你会去奥德威家吗？赫什邀请了你吗？舒茨呢？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And last the murky yellow cars of the Chicago, Milwaukee and St. Paul railroad looking cheerful as Christmas itself on the tracks beside the gate.","zh":"，而戴手套的手里紧紧抓着长条绿车票。我还记得车站大门旁边停着许多芝加哥—密尔沃基—圣保罗铁道公司的专线车，橘黄色的车厢看上去特别有欢乐的圣诞气氛。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"When we pulled out into the winter night and the real snow, our snow, began to stretch out beside us and twinkle against the windows, and the dim lights of small Wisconsin stations moved by, a sharp wild brace came suddenly into the air. We drew in deep breaths of it as we walked back from dinner through the cold vestibules, unutterably aware of our identity with this country for one strange hour, before we melted indistinguishably into it again.","sentences":[{"en":"When we pulled out into the winter night and the real snow, our snow, began to stretch out beside us and twinkle against the windows, and the dim lights of small Wisconsin stations moved by, a sharp wild brace came suddenly into the air.","zh":"当列车驶入冬夜，真正的雪，故乡的雪，开始从我们身边延伸而去，反射着车窗透出的光芒，沿途驶过威斯康星州境内许多灯光黯淡的小站，车厢里突然变得清冷起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We drew in deep breaths of it as we walked back from dinner through the cold vestibules, unutterably aware of our identity with this country for one strange hour, before we melted indistinguishably into it again.","zh":"在餐车吃过晚饭，穿过那些寒冷的车厢走回座位时，我们深深地吸入凛冽的气息，恍然明白这片土地才是我们的故乡。直到一个小时之后，当我们再次习惯了清新寒冷的空气，这种奇妙的感觉才渐渐消失。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"That’s my Middle West—not the wheat or the prairies or the lost Swede towns, but the thrilling returning trains of my youth, and the street lamps and sleigh bells in the frosty dark and the shadows of holly wreaths thrown by lighted windows on the snow. I am part of that, a little solemn with the feel of those long winters, a little complacent from growing up in the Carraway house in a city where dwellings are still called through decades by a family’s name. I see now that this has been a story of the West, after all—Tom and Gatsby, Daisy and Jordan and I, were all Westerners, and perhaps we possessed some deficiency in common which made us subtly unadaptable to Eastern life.","sentences":[{"en":"That’s my Middle West—not the wheat or the prairies or the lost Swede towns, but the thrilling returning trains of my youth, and the street lamps and sleigh bells in the frosty dark and the shadows of holly wreaths thrown by lighted windows on the snow.","zh":"这就是我的中西部——不是麦田、原野或者那些荒凉的瑞典小城，而是年轻时返乡的列车，是寒冷黑夜中的街灯和圣诞的铃声，是明亮窗户上的圣诞花环投射在雪地上的影子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am part of that, a little solemn with the feel of those long winters, a little complacent from growing up in the Carraway house in a city where dwellings are still called through decades by a family’s name.","zh":"我是属于这里的，这些漫长的寒冬让我养成了严肃的性格。而我生活的城市很注重传统，世家故宅都是以屋主的姓氏命名的，自幼在卡拉威府邸长大的我难免有点骄傲自满。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I see now that this has been a story of the West, after all—Tom and Gatsby, Daisy and Jordan and I, were all Westerners, and perhaps we possessed some deficiency in common which made us subtly unadaptable to Eastern life.","zh":"现在我终于明白，这归根到底是个西部的故事——汤姆、盖茨比、黛熙、乔丹和我，大家都是西部人，也许我们拥有某些共同的缺点，无形中使得我们很难真正地适应东部的生活。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Even when the East excited me most, even when I was most keenly aware of its superiority to the bored, sprawling, swollen towns beyond the Ohio, with their interminable inquisitions which spared only the children and the very old—even then it had always for me a quality of distortion. West Egg, especially, still figures in my more fantastic dreams. I see it as a night scene by El Greco: a hundred houses, at once conventional and grotesque, crouching under a sullen, overhanging sky and a lustreless moon. In the foreground four solemn men in dress suits are walking along the sidewalk with a stretcher on which lies a drunken woman in a white evening dress. Her hand, which dangles over the side, sparkles cold with jewels. Gravely the men turn in at a house—the wrong house. But no one knows the woman’s name, and no one cares.","sentences":[{"en":"Even when the East excited me most, even when I was most keenly aware of its superiority to the bored, sprawling, swollen towns beyond the Ohio, with their interminable inquisitions which spared only the children and the very old—even then it had always for me a quality of distortion.","zh":"我曾为东部感到兴奋不已，也曾清楚地意识到，东部比俄亥俄州以西地区好得多。那里虽然不像西部地广人稀，但生活没那么沉闷乏味，哪怕你不是小孩或者老人，也不会整天被人缠着问东问西——可是即使在那个时候，我依然觉得东部的生活有点畸形。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"West Egg, especially, still figures in my more fantastic dreams.","zh":"尤其是西卵，它依然会出现在我怪诞的梦境里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I see it as a night scene by El Greco: a hundred houses, at once conventional and grotesque, crouching under a sullen, overhanging sky and a lustreless moon.","zh":"在我看来，它仿佛是艾尔·格列柯的夜景：上百座既传统又荒诞的房子匍匐在阴沉的天空和黯淡的月亮之下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the foreground four solemn men in dress suits are walking along the sidewalk with a stretcher on which lies a drunken woman in a white evening dress.","zh":"画面的前景是四个表情肃穆的男人，西装革履地抬着担架走在人行道上，而担架上躺着一位烂醉如泥、穿着白色晚礼服的女人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her hand, which dangles over the side, sparkles cold with jewels.","zh":"她的手垂在旁边，手腕上的珠宝闪烁着寒光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gravely the men turn in at a house—the wrong house.","zh":"那些男人沉重地走进一座房子——走错地方了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But no one knows the woman’s name, and no one cares.","zh":"但没有人知道那女人的名字，也没有人关心。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"After Gatsby’s death the East was haunted for me like that, distorted beyond my eyes’ power of correction. So when the blue smoke of brittle leaves was in the air and the wind blew the wet laundry stiff on the line I decided to come back home.","sentences":[{"en":"After Gatsby’s death the East was haunted for me like that, distorted beyond my eyes’ power of correction.","zh":"盖茨比死后，东部在我心目中就是这样阴森可怕，其畸形的程度超越了我的眼睛的矫正能力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So when the blue smoke of brittle leaves was in the air and the wind blew the wet laundry stiff on the line I decided to come back home.","zh":"所以等到空气中升起因燃烧枯叶而生的蓝烟，寒风将晾在绳子上的衣服吹得发硬，我就决定打道回府。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was one thing to be done before I left, an awkward, unpleasant thing that perhaps had better have been let alone. But I wanted to leave things in order and not just trust that obliging and indifferent sea to sweep my refuse away. I saw Jordan Baker and talked over and around what had happened to us together, and what had happened afterward to me, and she lay perfectly still, listening, in a big chair.","sentences":[{"en":"There was one thing to be done before I left, an awkward, unpleasant thing that perhaps had better have been let alone.","zh":"离开之前有件事需要先处理好，那件事说起来很尴尬，很不愉快，也许本来应该不去管它的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I wanted to leave things in order and not just trust that obliging and indifferent sea to sweep my refuse away.","zh":"但我喜欢把事情收拾得干干净净，而不是指望茫茫大海来把我的垃圾冲走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw Jordan Baker and talked over and around what had happened to us together, and what had happened afterward to me, and she lay perfectly still, listening, in a big chair.","zh":"于是我约见了乔丹·贝克，跟她聊起了发生在我们之间的事，以及后来我的遭遇，她坐在一张巨大的沙发椅上，纹丝不动地听着。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She was dressed to play golf, and I remember thinking she looked like a good illustration, her chin raised a little jauntily, her hair the colour of an autumn leaf, her face the same brown tint as the fingerless glove on her knee. When I had finished she told me without comment that she was engaged to another man. I doubted that, though there were several she could have married at a nod of her head, but I pretended to be surprised. For just a minute I wondered if I wasn’t making a mistake, then I thought it all over again quickly and got up to say goodbye.","sentences":[{"en":"She was dressed to play golf, and I remember thinking she looked like a good illustration, her chin raised a little jauntily, her hair the colour of an autumn leaf, her face the same brown tint as the fingerless glove on her knee.","zh":"她穿着高尔夫球服，我记得当时觉得她看上去漂亮得像插画，她的下巴微微翘起，一副满不在乎的神气，头发是秋叶的黄色，脸庞的颜色和膝盖上的无指手套相同，都是淡褐色的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When I had finished she told me without comment that she was engaged to another man.","zh":"我把话说完之后，她不动声色地说她已经和别人订婚了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I doubted that, though there were several she could have married at a nod of her head, but I pretended to be surprised.","zh":"我怀疑她是在骗我——尽管她不乏追求者，只要她点头随时都可以结婚——但我还是假装很惊讶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For just a minute I wondered if I wasn’t making a mistake, then I thought it all over again quickly and got up to say goodbye.","zh":"刹那间我在想就这样和她分手是不是错误，又赶紧从头考虑了一遍，然后站起来和她说再见。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Nevertheless you did throw me over,” said Jordan suddenly. “You threw me over on the telephone. I don’t give a damn about you now, but it was a new experience for me, and I felt a little dizzy for a while.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nevertheless you did throw me over,” said Jordan suddenly.","zh":"“反正是你甩掉我的，”乔丹突然说，“那天你在电话里甩掉我。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You threw me over on the telephone.","zh":"“反正是你甩掉我的，”乔丹突然说，“那天你在电话里甩掉我。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I don’t give a damn about you now, but it was a new experience for me, and I felt a little dizzy for a while.”","zh":"现在我不怪你，但我从来没有被人甩过，当时愣了好久才回过神来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"We shook hands.","sentences":[{"en":"We shook hands.","zh":"我们握了手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Oh, and do you remember”—she added—“a conversation we had once about driving a car?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, and do you remember”—she added—“a conversation we had once about driving a car?”","zh":"“喂，你记得吗，”她补充说，“有一次我们聊起了开车的事情。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Why—not exactly.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why—not exactly.”","zh":"“哦，不太记得了。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You said a bad driver was only safe until she met another bad driver? Well, I met another bad driver, didn’t I? I mean it was careless of me to make such a wrong guess. I thought you were rather an honest, straightforward person. I thought it was your secret pride.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You said a bad driver was only safe until she met another bad driver?","zh":"“你说烂司机只要不遇上别的烂司机，就不会出事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, I met another bad driver, didn’t I? I mean it was careless of me to make such a wrong guess.","zh":"哎，我遇到别的烂司机了，对吧？这只怪我自己不小心看错人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought you were rather an honest, straightforward person.","zh":"我原来以为你是个相当诚实、直爽的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought it was your secret pride.”","zh":"我以为那是你暗地里引以为豪的道德品质。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I’m thirty,” I said. “I’m five years too old to lie to myself and call it honour.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m thirty,” I said.","zh":"“我今年三十岁了，”我说，“五年前我会做违心的事情，并以此为荣，但现在我不会。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m five years too old to lie to myself and call it honour.”","zh":"“我今年三十岁了，”我说，“五年前我会做违心的事情，并以此为荣，但现在我不会。”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"She didn’t answer. Angry, and half in love with her, and tremendously sorry, I turned away.","sentences":[{"en":"She didn’t answer.","zh":"她没有回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Angry, and half in love with her, and tremendously sorry, I turned away.","zh":"我生气地转身走开，但对她还是有点不舍，也感到非常可惜。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"One afternoon late in October I saw Tom Buchanan. He was walking ahead of me along Fifth Avenue in his alert, aggressive way, his hands out a little from his body as if to fight off interference, his head moving sharply here and there, adapting itself to his restless eyes. Just as I slowed up to avoid overtaking him he stopped and began frowning into the windows of a jewellery store. Suddenly he saw me and walked back, holding out his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"One afternoon late in October I saw Tom Buchanan.","zh":"十月底的某个下午，我在第五大道看见了汤姆·布坎南。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was walking ahead of me along Fifth Avenue in his alert, aggressive way, his hands out a little from his body as if to fight off interference, his head moving sharply here and there, adapting itself to his restless eyes.","zh":"他走在我前面，步履轻快而急促，双手稍微向前抬起，随时准备推开阻碍的样子。他的头不停地扭来转去，眼睛滴溜溜地四处乱瞟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just as I slowed up to avoid overtaking him he stopped and began frowning into the windows of a jewellery store.","zh":"我正想放慢脚步以免超过他，他停了下来，开始眯着眼睛朝某家珠宝商店的橱窗里看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suddenly he saw me and walked back, holding out his hand.","zh":"他突然看到我了，于是往回走，伸出他的手。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“What’s the matter, Nick? Do you object to shaking hands with me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the matter, Nick?","zh":"“怎么回事，尼克？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you object to shaking hands with me?”","zh":"你拒绝跟我握手吗？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Yes. You know what I think of you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.","zh":"“是的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You know what I think of you.”","zh":"你知道我对你的看法。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“You’re crazy, Nick,” he said quickly. “Crazy as hell. I don’t know what’s the matter with you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You’re crazy, Nick,” he said quickly.","zh":"“你疯了，尼克，”他脱口而出，“彻底疯了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Crazy as hell.","zh":"“你疯了，尼克，”他脱口而出，“彻底疯了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I don’t know what’s the matter with you.”","zh":"我不知道你到底怎么回事。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“Tom,” I inquired, “what did you say to Wilson that afternoon?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Tom,” I inquired, “what did you say to Wilson that afternoon?”","zh":"“汤姆，”我问他，“那天下午你跟威尔逊说了什么？”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"He stared at me without a word, and I knew I had guessed right about those missing hours. I started to turn away, but he took a step after me and grabbed my arm.","sentences":[{"en":"He stared at me without a word, and I knew I had guessed right about those missing hours.","zh":"他哑口无言地望着我，我知道我猜对了，威尔逊在不知所踪的那几个小时果然是去找了他。我转身就走，但他跟上一步，拉住我的胳膊。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I started to turn away, but he took a step after me and grabbed my arm.","zh":"他哑口无言地望着我，我知道我猜对了，威尔逊在不知所踪的那几个小时果然是去找了他。我转身就走，但他跟上一步，拉住我的胳膊。","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“I told him the truth,” he said. “He came to the door while we were getting ready to leave, and when I sent down word that we weren’t in he tried to force his way upstairs. He was crazy enough to kill me if I hadn’t told him who owned the car. His hand was on a revolver in his pocket every minute he was in the house—” He broke off defiantly. “What if I did tell him? That fellow had it coming to him. He threw dust into your eyes just like he did in Daisy’s, but he was a tough one. He ran over Myrtle like you’d run over a dog and never even stopped his car.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I told him the truth,” he said.","zh":"“我跟他说了真话，”他说，“他到我家时，我们正准备出门，我派人去跟他说我们不在家，他想要强行闯到楼上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“He came to the door while we were getting ready to leave, and when I sent down word that we weren’t in he tried to force his way upstairs.","zh":"“我跟他说了真话，”他说，“他到我家时，我们正准备出门，我派人去跟他说我们不在家，他想要强行闯到楼上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was crazy enough to kill me if I hadn’t told him who owned the car.","zh":"他那时急疯了，我要是不说那辆车是谁的，他肯定会杀了我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His hand was on a revolver in his pocket every minute he was in the house—” He broke off defiantly.","zh":"走进我们家之后，他的手一直放在口袋里，拿着一把左轮…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“What if I did tell him?","zh":"”接着他又不服气地说，“我告诉他又怎样？","scope":"group"},{"en":"That fellow had it coming to him.","zh":"”接着他又不服气地说，“我告诉他又怎样？","scope":"group"},{"en":"He threw dust into your eyes just like he did in Daisy’s, but he was a tough one.","zh":"那家伙罪有应得。你的眼睛被他蒙蔽了，黛熙也是，但他是个狠角色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He ran over Myrtle like you’d run over a dog and never even stopped his car.”","zh":"他开车撞倒梅朵就像撞倒一条狗，停都不肯停下来。”","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"There was nothing I could say, except the one unutterable fact that it wasn’t true.","sentences":[{"en":"There was nothing I could say, except the one unutterable fact that it wasn’t true.","zh":"我不知道该说些什么，只能在心里默念着事实不是这样的。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"“And if you think I didn’t have my share of suffering—look here, when I went to give up that flat and saw that damn box of dog biscuits sitting there on the sideboard, I sat down and cried like a baby. By God it was awful—”","sentences":[{"en":"“And if you think I didn’t have my share of suffering—look here, when I went to give up that flat and saw that damn box of dog biscuits sitting there on the sideboard, I sat down and cried like a baby.","zh":"“你别以为我就没有受苦——告诉你吧，后来我去退掉那套公寓，看到那盒该死的狗粮还摆在橱柜里，我坐下来哭得像个婴儿。上帝作证，那真是太可怕了…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"By God it was awful—”","zh":"“你别以为我就没有受苦——告诉你吧，后来我去退掉那套公寓，看到那盒该死的狗粮还摆在橱柜里，我坐下来哭得像个婴儿。上帝作证，那真是太可怕了…”","scope":"group"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I couldn’t forgive him or like him, but I saw that what he had done was, to him, entirely justified. It was all very careless and confused. They were careless people, Tom and Daisy—they smashed up things and creatures and then retreated back into their money or their vast carelessness, or whatever it was that kept them together, and let other people clean up the mess they had made…","sentences":[{"en":"I couldn’t forgive him or like him, but I saw that what he had done was, to him, entirely justified.","zh":"我不能原谅他，也不能喜欢他，但我看得出来他所做的事情，在他自己眼中，是完全合情合理的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was all very careless and confused.","zh":"一切都是因为自私冷漠和思维混乱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were careless people, Tom and Daisy—they smashed up things and creatures and then retreated back into their money or their vast carelessness, or whatever it was that kept them together, and let other people clean up the mess they had made…","zh":"他们是自私冷漠的人，汤姆和黛熙——他们把东西打碎，毁掉别人的生活，然后龟缩到金钱、巨大的冷漠或者随便什么让他们蝇营狗苟地相处的东西里面，让别人来清理他们留下的残局…","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I shook hands with him; it seemed silly not to, for I felt suddenly as though I were talking to a child. Then he went into the jewellery store to buy a pearl necklace—or perhaps only a pair of cuff buttons—rid of my provincial squeamishness forever.","sentences":[{"en":"I shook hands with him; it seemed silly not to, for I felt suddenly as though I were talking to a child.","zh":"我终究和他握手了，否则显得很傻，因为我突然觉得我好像是在跟一个小孩说话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he went into the jewellery store to buy a pearl necklace—or perhaps only a pair of cuff buttons—rid of my provincial squeamishness forever.","zh":"然后他走进珠宝商店去买珍珠项链，或者也许只是买两个袖扣，永远地摆脱了我这个乡巴佬吹毛求疵的责难。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"type":"break"},{"en":"Gatsby’s house was still empty when I left—the grass on his lawn had grown as long as mine. One of the taxi drivers in the village never took a fare past the entrance gate without stopping for a minute and pointing inside; perhaps it was he who drove Daisy and Gatsby over to East Egg the night of the accident, and perhaps he had made a story about it all his own. I didn’t want to hear it and I avoided him when I got off the train.","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby’s house was still empty when I left—the grass on his lawn had grown as long as mine.","zh":"我离开时盖茨比的房子依然空着——他草坪里的草长得跟我的一样长了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One of the taxi drivers in the village never took a fare past the entrance gate without stopping for a minute and pointing inside; perhaps it was he who drove Daisy and Gatsby over to East Egg the night of the accident, and perhaps he had made a story about it all his own.","zh":"村里有个出租车司机每次载客经过大门总要停下来指指点点，也许车祸那晚正是他拉着黛熙和盖茨比去了东卵，也许他已经杜撰出一个别开生面的故事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I didn’t want to hear it and I avoided him when I got off the train.","zh":"但我不想听，每次下火车时我总是避开他。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"I spent my Saturday nights in New York because those gleaming, dazzling parties of his were with me so vividly that I could still hear the music and the laughter, faint and incessant, from his garden, and the cars going up and down his drive. One night I did hear a material car there, and saw its lights stop at his front steps. But I didn’t investigate. Probably it was some final guest who had been away at the ends of the earth and didn’t know that the party was over.","sentences":[{"en":"I spent my Saturday nights in New York because those gleaming, dazzling parties of his were with me so vividly that I could still hear the music and the laughter, faint and incessant, from his garden, and the cars going up and down his drive.","zh":"那几个星期六我都在纽约过夜，因为对我来说，他那些灯火辉煌、光彩夺目的宴会宛在眼前，我依然能听见音乐和笑声，轻轻地、不绝地从他的花园传出来，依然能听见轿车在他的车道驶进驶出。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One night I did hear a material car there, and saw its lights stop at his front steps.","zh":"某天夜里我真的听到有辆车停在那里，看见车灯停在他家前门的台阶下方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I didn’t investigate.","zh":"但我没有去看个究竟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Probably it was some final guest who had been away at the ends of the earth and didn’t know that the party was over.","zh":"也许是某个最后的客人，刚从遥远的地方归来，还不知道盖茨比的宴会早已曲终人散。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"On the last night, with my trunk packed and my car sold to the grocer, I went over and looked at that huge incoherent failure of a house once more. On the white steps an obscene word, scrawled by some boy with a piece of brick, stood out clearly in the moonlight, and I erased it, drawing my shoe raspingly along the stone. Then I wandered down to the beach and sprawled out on the sand.","sentences":[{"en":"On the last night, with my trunk packed and my car sold to the grocer, I went over and looked at that huge incoherent failure of a house once more.","zh":"临走那夜，我收拾好行李，把车卖给杂货店的老板，然后走过去，再次端详这座象征着失败的荒芜巨宅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the white steps an obscene word, scrawled by some boy with a piece of brick, stood out clearly in the moonlight, and I erased it, drawing my shoe raspingly along the stone.","zh":"白色的台阶上有个粗俗的字眼，不知道是哪个顽童用砖块涂上的，在月光下显得清清楚楚，我把它擦掉了，鞋底在石板上磨得沙沙响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then I wandered down to the beach and sprawled out on the sand.","zh":"接着我信步走到下面的海边，仰面躺在沙滩上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Most of the big shore places were closed now and there were hardly any lights except the shadowy, moving glow of a ferryboat across the Sound. And as the moon rose higher the inessential houses began to melt away until gradually I became aware of the old island here that flowered once for Dutch sailors’ eyes—a fresh, green breast of the new world. Its vanished trees, the trees that had made way for Gatsby’s house, had once pandered in whispers to the last and greatest of all human dreams; for a transitory enchanted moment man must have held his breath in the presence of this continent, compelled into an aesthetic contemplation he neither understood nor desired, face to face for the last time in history with something commensurate to his capacity for wonder.","sentences":[{"en":"Most of the big shore places were closed now and there were hardly any lights except the shadowy, moving glow of a ferryboat across the Sound.","zh":"这时海边的公馆多数已经闭门锁户，周围几乎没有灯火，只有一点黯淡的光芒在移动，那是横穿海湾的渡轮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as the moon rose higher the inessential houses began to melt away until gradually I became aware of the old island here that flowered once for Dutch sailors’ eyes—a fresh, green breast of the new world.","zh":"明月渐升渐高，那些微不足道的房子渐渐消失，我慢慢意识到这个古老的岛屿曾经鲜花遍地，曾经是当年那些荷兰水手眼里丰腴多汁的新世界。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Its vanished trees, the trees that had made way for Gatsby’s house, had once pandered in whispers to the last and greatest of all human dreams; for a transitory enchanted moment man must have held his breath in the presence of this continent, compelled into an aesthetic contemplation he neither understood nor desired, face to face for the last time in history with something commensurate to his capacity for wonder.","zh":"那些消失的树木，那些为盖茨比的豪宅让路的树木，已经呻吟着献身给全人类最后和最大的梦想。当初看到这片大陆，心醉神迷的人类肯定在刹那间屏住了呼吸，不由自主地陷入一种他既不理解也不渴望的美学沉思，有史以来最后一次面对某种他力所能及的惊喜。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"And as I sat there brooding on the old, unknown world, I thought of Gatsby’s wonder when he first picked out the green light at the end of Daisy’s dock. He had come a long way to this blue lawn, and his dream must have seemed so close that he could hardly fail to grasp it. He did not know that it was already behind him, somewhere back in that vast obscurity beyond the city, where the dark fields of the republic rolled on under the night.","sentences":[{"en":"And as I sat there brooding on the old, unknown world, I thought of Gatsby’s wonder when he first picked out the green light at the end of Daisy’s dock.","zh":"我坐在沙滩上遐想古老而未知的世界，忽而想起了盖茨比，他第一次见到黛熙家码头末端的绿灯时，肯定也感到万分惊喜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had come a long way to this blue lawn, and his dream must have seemed so close that he could hardly fail to grasp it.","zh":"他走过漫漫长路才来到这片蓝色的港湾，肯定觉得梦想已经离得非常近，几乎伸出手就能够抓得到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did not know that it was already behind him, somewhere back in that vast obscurity beyond the city, where the dark fields of the republic rolled on under the night.","zh":"他所不知道的是，梦想已经落在他身后，落在纽约以西那广袤无垠的大地上，落在黑暗夜幕下连绵不绝的美国原野上。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"Gatsby believed in the green light, the orgiastic future that year by year recedes before us. It eluded us then, but that’s no matter—tomorrow we will run faster, stretch out our arms further… And one fine morning—","sentences":[{"en":"Gatsby believed in the green light, the orgiastic future that year by year recedes before us.","zh":"盖茨比信奉的那盏绿灯，是年复一年在我们眼前渐渐消失的极乐未来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It eluded us then, but that’s no matter—tomorrow we will run faster, stretch out our arms further…","zh":"我们始终追它不上，但没有关系——明天我们会跑得更快，把手伸得更长…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And one fine morning—","zh":"等到某个美好的早晨——","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"},{"en":"So we beat on, boats against the current, borne back ceaselessly into the past.","sentences":[{"en":"So we beat on, boats against the current, borne back ceaselessly into the past.","zh":"于是我们奋力前进，却如同逆水行舟，注定要不停地退回过去。","scope":"sentence"}],"type":"text"}]}]};
